lsd:Entity_30310 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Balkan Cup was an international association football competition contested on and off from 1929 to 1980 by countries from the Balkans region. The first edition featured Romania, Greece, Yugoslavia and Bulgaria and was played over three years from 1929 to 1931. Romania won the first title with a game in hand after beating Yugoslavia 4–2. Greece dropped out of the tournament the same year, and was replaced by Albania, who went on to win the 1946 edition by defeating Romania 1–0 in the final game. Hungary were a world footballing power at the time and proved this with a 9–0 thrashing against Bulgaria. This time only four countries took part – Romania, Bulgaria, Turkey and Greece. Bulgaria won the final on away goals against Romania in 1976. Romania went on to win the last edition in 1980 by beating Yugoslavia 4–1 at home in the final." .

