lsd:Entity_7033 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The UEFA Cup Winners' Cup (abbreviated as CWC) was a association football club competition contested annually by the most recent winners of all European domestic cup competitions. The first competition was held in the 1960–61 season, but the Cup was not recognised by the governing body of European association football until October 1963. The tournament ran for 39 seasons with its final edition held in 1998–1999, after which it was absorbed into the Union of European Football Associations Cup. The Cup Winners' Cup was regarded by Union of European Football Associations as the second most prestigious European club competition, behind the European Cup and ahead of the Inter_Cities Fairs Cup (later the Union of European Football Associations Cup), although many association football writers and fans considered the Union of European Football Associations Cup as harder to win. Since the abolition of the UEFA Cup Winners' Cup, the Union of European Football Associations Super Cup place previously reserved for the Cup Winners' Cup winner has been taken by the winner of the Union of European Football Associations Cup, now the Union of European Football Associations Europa League." .

