lsd:Entity_10005 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "It takes place every year in the month of June in Bulgaria's capital Sofia since 2008. The first Sofia Pride parade was held on 2008, on the same date as the Stonewall riots in New York City that occurred in 1969. The first Sofia Pride parade, organized by the BGO Gemini, was held on 2008 and it was attended by some 120 people. However, the Bulgarian Orthodox Church (BOC) made an anti_parade statement (they also made one during the first held parade) since a few days earlier a young theologist from the Theologic Faculty of the University of Sofia made their anti_gay pride parade, for which they were vastly mocked." .

