    rdfs:label "The 1996 Intercontinental Cup was the 22nd edition of the FIBA Intercontinental Cup for men's professional basketball clubs and the 21st edition of the tournament being in the form of a true intercontinental tournament. It was contested between the winners of the 1995–96 season of the FIBA European League, Panathinaikos B.C., and Olimpia, the winners of the 1996 edition of the FIBA South American League. The first game of the 3 game series was held on 1996, at the Estadio Cubierto Newell's Old Boys, the home arena of Olimpia. The Olympic Indoor Hall hosted the last 2 games, on 1996, and 1996. Panathinaikos B.C. won the second and third games of the series, and became the 1996 world club champions. Panathinaikos B.C. won the series 2_1. Olimpia: Montecchia 6, Racca 25, Wilson 8, Jadlow 21, Uranga 7, Victoriano 12, Gutiérrez 2, Nocioni 2, Zulberti 6. Panathinaikos B.C.: Dinkins 7, Alvertis 21, Koch 0, Amaechi 23, Martínez 8, Oikonomou 8, Georgikopoulos 0, Sconochini 16. Panathinaikos B.C.: Dinkins 7, Sconochini 3, Alvertis 30, Oikonomou 16, Amaechi 19, Koch 8, Martínez 0. Panathinaikos B.C.: Dinkins 24, Sconochini 12, Alvertis 8, Oikonomou 9, Amaechi 18, Koch 9, Martínez 13, Georgikopoulos 5, Skoutaris 3." .

