    rdfs:label "The Art of the Motorcycle was an art exhibition that presented 114 motorcycles chosen for their historic importance or design excellence in a display designed by Frank Gehry in the curved rotunda of the Frank Lloyd Wright_designed Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum in New York City, running for three months in late 1998. It was in 1989 and 1990, one decade before The Art of the Motorcycle, that Mapplethorpe's The Perfect Moment art exhibition was hounded from one venue to another by outraged conservatives. A forthcoming art exhibition at the Bermuda National Gallery, inspired by The Art of the Motorcycle, will use the identical concept of the motorcycle as \"possible metaphor for the 20th century.\"" .

