lsd:Entity_14989 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Maryland Million Ladies is an American Thoroughbred horse race held annually in October since 1986 primarily at Laurel Park Racecourse in Laurel, Maryland or at Pimlico Race Course in Baltimore. To be eligible for the Maryland Million Ladies, a 3 year_old filly must be sired by a stallion who stands in Maryland. At its inception in 1986 through 1990 the Maryland Million Ladies was run at one and 1/16 mile on turf. The race itself has had many titles since 1986 due in large part to the aggressive marketing efforts of Maryland Million Limited, the series corporate founder. In its inaugural year (1986) the race was called the \"Eskimo Pie Maryland Ladies.\"" .

