lsd:Entity_15275 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jordan–Malaysia relations refers to bilateral foreign relations between the two countries, Jordan and Malaysia. Jordan has an embassy in Kuala Lumpur, and Malaysia has an embassy in Amman. In oil project, Malaysia YTL Power has acquired a 30% stake on oil shale project in Jordan. On the other side, Jordan has revive a regular flight service to Malaysia, and the country has invested for a construction of a new international financial district. Jordan also plans to set up a branch of Al al_Bayt University in Malaysia." .

