    rdfs:label "The United States of America, represented by the United States of America Olympic & Paralympic Committee (USOPC), is expected to compete at the United States at the 2020 Summer Olympics in Tokyo. U.S. athletes further achieved the entry standards, either by qualifying time or by world ranking, in the following track and field events (up to a maximum of 3 athletes in each event): The team will be selected based on the results of the 2020 United States of America Olympic Trials (June 18 to 27, 2021) to be held in Eugene, Oregon. Key: The United States of America women's soccer team qualified for the Olympics by reaching the finals of the 2020 CONCACAF Women's Olympic Qualifying Championship in Carson, California. U.S. swimmers further achieved qualifying standards in the following events (up to a maximum of 2 swimmers in each event at the Olympic Qualifying Time (OQT), and potentially 1 at the Olympic Selection Time (OST)): To assure their selection to the U.S. team, swimmers must finish in the top two of each individual pool event under the Olympic qualifying cut at the 2020 United States of America Olympic Trials (June 13 to 20, 2021) in Omaha, Nebraska." .

