    rdfs:label "The Valencia Marathon (also known as Marathon Valencia Trinidad Alfonso EDP for sponsorship reasons) is an annual marathon road running event hosted by Valencia, Spain, since 1981. The marathon was first held in 1981 as a popular race known as the Marató Popular de València. From 2011 to 2014, the marathon was known as the Divina Pastora Valencia Marathon. In 2015, the marathon was known as the Valencia Trinidad Alfonso Marathon. The course for the elite_only races in 2020 during the coronavirus pandemic used a modified version of the Valencia Half Marathon course, with marathon runners running two laps. Key: The 40th edition of the marathon, held during the coronavirus pandemic, was an elite_only event that also included a half marathon race." .

