lsd:Entity_18163 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Australia participated in the Australia in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016 which took place on 2016, in Valletta, Malta. Prior to the 2016 Contest, Australia had participated in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest once since its debut in 2015, with the song \"My Girls\" performed by Bella Paige. On 2016, it was announced that Alexa Curtis had been internally chosen by the broadcaster to represent Australia. Alexa Curtis (born 4 January 2004) is an Australian singer who won The Voice Kids Australia in 2014. In 2014, she performed with a small group of The Voice Kids at Vision Australia's Carols by Candlelight. In 2016, she sang the opening theme song for six episodes of The Powerpuff Girls on Cartoon Network Australia. \"We Are\" represented Australia during the Australia in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016. During the opening ceremony and the running order draw which took place on 2016, Australia was drawn to perform fourteenth on 2016, following Israel and preceding the Netherlands. During the press conference for the Australia in the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2016, held in Stockholm, the Reference Group announced several changes to the voting format for the 2016 contest." .

