lsd:Entity_18783 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 GEICO 500 was a NASCAR Sprint Cup Series 2015 Toyota Owners 400 held on 03 May 2015 at Talladega Superspeedway in Lincoln, Alabama. Contested over 188 laps on the 2.66 mile (4.28 km) asphalt superspeedway, it was the tenth 2015 Toyota Owners 400 of the 2015 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series. Dale Earnhardt Jr. won the 2015 Toyota Owners 400, his first win of the season and his sixth at Talladega Superspeedway and first at the racetrack since 2004. Jeff Gordon won the pole for the 2015 Toyota Owners 400, the 80th of his career and fourth at the track. Teammate Dale Earnhardt Jr. led a 2015 Toyota Owners 400 high of 67 laps. This was the 24th career victory for Dale Earnhardt Jr., sixth at Talladega Superspeedway and twelfth at the track for Hendrick Motorsports. The 2015 Toyota Owners 400 was scheduled to start at 1:20 p.m., but started a minute late at 1:21 p.m. when Jeff Gordon led the field to the green flag. Dale Earnhardt Jr. went underneath Jeff Gordon exiting turn 4 and took the lead with 64 laps to go. Jeff Gordon and Josh Wise were tagged for speeding on pit road and restarted the 2015 Toyota Owners 400 from the tail_end of the field. The 2015 Toyota Owners 400 stayed green after that and a wreck on the backstretch that collected Jeff Gordon, Casey Mears, Ricky Stenhouse Jr. and J.J. Yeley. Fox Sports covered their 15th 2015 Toyota Owners 400 at Talladega Superspeedway." .

