lsd:Entity_23476 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1971 Asheville 300 was a NASCAR Winston Cup Series racing event that took place on 1971, at New Asheville Speedway in Asheville. This race marked the Cup series' return to New Asheville Speedway after an absence of just under three years but it would be the series' final race here as the trimmed down schedule in 1972 eliminated this event. Like the 1959 Daytona 500, the 1969 Motor Trend 500 and the 1971 Space City 300, this race is considered to be one of NASCAR's infrequently occurring \"perfect games.\"" .

lsd:Entity_23478 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "TFcon is a Transformers fan convention held annually since 2002 in the Greater Toronto Area. Now the largest fan_run Transformers convention in the world, TFcon will be held for the 20th consecutive year in 2021 with events occurring in Toronto, Ontario, Canada in July and Baltimore, Maryland in October to celebrate the 37th Anniversary of the Transformers. The first TFcon was held in Hamilton, Ontario in 2002. In 2014 TFcon expanded to two shows a year, with one in Canada and one in the United States. TFcon was not held in 2020 for the first time since its inception in 2002 due to the COVID_19 pandemic." .

