    rdfs:label "The Ottawa Race Weekend (also known as Tamarack Ottawa Race Weekend for sponsorship reasons) is an annual weekend of road running events held the last weekend of May in the city of Ottawa, Ontario, Canada. The marathon was first held in 1975, and is categorized as a Gold Label Road Race by World Athletics. The Ottawa Race Weekend also includes Canada's largest health and fitness expo, which opens on the Thursday before the weekend. In addition, each year, participants in the Ottawa Race Weekend raise close to $1 million for approximately 25 local and national charities affiliated with the event. The race weekend includes seven races: a 1.2 km kids marathon, 2K, 5K, 10K, half marathon, wheelchair marathon, and marathon. The signature event of the weekend is the Ottawa Marathon, which was first held in 1975. Today it is the largest marathon event in Canada and is a qualifier for the Boston Marathon. The Ottawa Race Weekend was at one point the only road racing event in the world to host two World Athletics Silver Label events: the 10K and the Ottawa Marathon. In 2014 the 10k became the first World Athletics Gold Label road race in Canada." .

