lsd:Entity_24452 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1939 Poland vs Hungary football match, as it is known in Poland, was played on Sunday, 1939, at the Wojska Polskiego Stadium in Warsaw. In 1939, the Hungarian football team was widely regarded as one of the best in the world, and hardly anyone in Poland believed that their players in white and red uniforms, their national colours, were going to win over their opponents. On Sunday, 1939, in Warsaw, Poland was going to face Bulgaria. Then, on Wednesday, 1939, probably in Belgrade, Poland was scheduled to face Yugoslavia. On Friday, 1939, Germany invaded, World War II started, and Sunday's game was the last match of inter_war Poland." .

