lsd:Entity_28342 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "RavenCon is an annual United States of America science fiction convention founded in 2006 and held in Richmond. The name \"RavenCon\" was chosen as a tribute to author Edgar Allan Poe, who lived in Richmond for a time. RavenCon 2006 was held April 21–23, 2006, with Terry Brooks as author guest of honor, Tom Kidd as artist guest of honor, and Lee & Alexis Gilliland as fan guests of honor. In 2018 there was a RavenCon 13.5 that was held September 21–23, 2018 at the Four Points Sheraton Richmond, off of Midlothian Blvd." .

lsd:Entity_2835 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The unification (or re_unification) of East Timor, an independent state, and West Timor, a territory of Indonesia, both parts of the island of Timor, has been raised since the mid_20th century. Great Timor (Indonesia: Timor Raya) refers to the irredentism concept of a united and independent island of Timor, covering formerly Portuguese East Timor and formerly Dutch (now Indonesia) West Timor. During 1974–75, APODETI, an East Timorese party expressed its will to integrate East Timor and West Timor through an integration into the Republic of Indonesia. East Timor was invaded and occupied by Indonesia in 1975, which annexed the territory as its \"27th Province\" in 1976, but in a referendum held in 1999, the people of East Timor voted to end Indonesia occupation and become an independent state. In 2001 and 2002, before East Timor's independence, there were claims by the Indonesia military and some commentators, that this would inspire the secession of West Timor from Indonesia. After the Recovery of Independence in 2001, the government of East Timor fully recognises Indonesia's existing boundaries as inherited from the Netherlands East Indies." .

