lsd:Entity_28550 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Austin Marathon (also known as Ascension Seton Austin Marathon presented by Under Armour for sponsorship reasons) is an annual marathon held in Austin, Texas, since 1992. Due to the coronavirus pandemic, the 2021 edition of the Austin Marathon was postponed to April 25, 2021 and will not actually include a marathon. The Austin Marathon and Austin Half Marathon both start at 2nd St. and Congress Avenue. In addition to the marathon held on Sunday, the Austin Marathon weekend features the Manzano Mile presented by Dole on Saturday morning, and the half marathon and KXAN SimpleHealth 5K benefitting Paramount Theatre on Sunday morning. Austin Gives Miles, the marathon's official charity program, raised $702,500 in 2020. The Austin Marathon injected $48.5 million into the Austin economy during the 2019 race weekend." .

