lsd:Entity_3312 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Richardson fire (also known as the Richardson Backcountry Fire) was a 2011 wildfire in the Canadian province of Alberta. The Richardson fire was the largest fire in Alberta since the 1950 Chinchaga Fire, and the second largest recorded fire in the province's history. At a final size of approximately 700,000 hectares the Richardson fire would become the largest fire in Alberta's modern history, and the second largest recorded fire after the 1.5 million_hectare Chinchaga Fire of 1950. As the 1950 fire started in British Columbia and spread to Alberta, some sources classified the Richardson fire as the largest in Alberta history." .

