    rdfs:label "Ethiopia–Qatar relations are foreign relations between Ethiopia and Qatar. Ethiopia abruptly broke diplomatic ties with Qatar in April 2008, accusing \"the output of its media outlets\" of \"direct and indirect assistance to terrorist organizations,\" according to an Ethiopian Foreign Ministry statement. The statement further alleged that \"Qatar has left no stone unturned to cause harm to Ethiopia's national security\". The Qatar Foreign Ministry responded with a statement in which they \"expressed surprise\" at Ethiopia's actions, denying the accusations, and \"called on the Ethiopian Government to refrain from involving the State of Qatar in its rifts, recalling that the Ethiopian Government has previously made similar claims but the State of Qatar preferred not to reply out of the hope that the Ethiopian Government would stop such wrong behaviours.\"" .

lsd:Entity_34323 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2008 Texas's 22nd congressional district election was held on 2008. The 2008 presidential election, 2008 Senate election (for John Cornyn's seat), and 2008 Texas Legislature election occurred on the same date, as well as many local elections and ballot initiatives. He won the 2008 primary election, defeating foreign relations expert Joshua Kowert; businessman and NASCAR team owner Gene Christensen; and former Frisco mayor Kathy Seei. Barton won the 2008 primary, and faced Democratic winner Ludwig Otto in the general election, which Barton won 62.0–35.6%. The popular Fort Worth_based Granger was expected to win re_election in 2008 in this district comprising western areas of Fort Worth and surrounding areas. Paul was a Republican candidate in the 2008 presidential election (his second, following his run as Libertarian Party nominee in 1988), and ran un_opposed for re_election. Jackson Lee won the Democratic nomination and defeated Republican nominee John Faulk 77.3–20.3% in the 2008 November general election. Neugebauer won re_election over 2008 Democratic nominee Dwight Fullingim, 72.5 to 24.9%. Charlie defeated 2008 Republican nominee Robert Litoff 71.9–25.2% in the November general election. The 2008 election for Texas's 22nd congressional district was held on 2008, as part of the United States House of Representatives elections for the 111th United States Congress. Marchant defeated 2008 Democrat nominee Tom Love (campaign website) and 2008 Libertarian nominee David A. Casey 55.9–41.1% in the November election. Doggett defeated 2008 Republican nominee George Morovich 65.8–30.5% in the November election. Burgess defeated 2008 Democrat nominee Ken Leach (campaign website) 60.2–36.4% in the November election." .

