    rdfs:label "The 2012 United States presidential election in Indiana took place on 06 November 2012, as part of the 2012 United States presidential election in which all 50 states plus the District of Columbia participated. Indiana voters chose 11 electors to represent them in the Electoral College via a popular vote pitting incumbent Democratic President of the United States Barack Obama and his running mate, Vice President of the United States Joe Biden, against Republican challenger and former Massachusetts Governor Mitt Romney and his running mate, Congressman Paul Ryan. Incumbent Obama didn't visit Indiana although First Lady Michelle Obama, Vice President of the United States Joe Biden and former President of the United States Bill Clinton stumped in the state." .

