    rdfs:label "Kenya–Norway relations are bilateral relations between Kenya and Norway. In 1990, diplomatic relations between Kenya and Norway were severed due to Norway's criticism of the Kenyan government and its leadership. Norway's Trade Minister, Monica Mæland, led a delegation of 54 companies to Kenya in September 2015. Norway is cooperating with Kenya with a shift from aid to trade and investment. Kenya's main exports to Norway include: plants, flowers, coffee, tea and spices. 60% of Norway's exports to Kenya are made up of chemical fertiliser. Kenya's embassy in Stockholm is accredited to Norway." .

