lsd:Entity_37630 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Guatemala–India relations refers to the bilateral ties between India and Guatemala. According to the Ministry of Commerce of the Government of India, total trade between India and Guatemala was worth just $92 million in 2009–10, with India accounting for nearly $87 million worth of the trade or around 95%. Vice President of India, Venkaiah Naidu visited Guatemala in its first high level delegation visit to the country since establishing diplomatic relations in 1972. Diplomatic relations between Guatemala and India were established in 1972. India opened its embassy in Guatemala City on 2 May 2011. There is increased competition between in the production of cardamom between India and Guatemala, among other spices." .

