lsd:Entity_39787 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Algeria–Malaysia relations (Arabic: العلاقات الجزائرية الماليزية alealaqat aljazayiriat almalizia; French: Relations entre l'Algérie et la Malaisie; Malay: Hubungan Algeria–Malaysia; Jawi: هوبوڠن الجزائر–مليسيا) refers to bilateral foreign relations between Algeria and Malaysia. Algeria has an embassy in Kuala Lumpur, and Malaysia has an embassy in Algiers. In 2002, Algeria's exports to Malaysia were worth around $2.5 million, while Malaysia's exports to Algeria reached $113.6 million. Algeria's main exports to Malaysia include crude fertiliser and minerals, chemicals and chemical products while Malaysia's main exports to Algeria are palm oil, chemicals, chemical products, vegetable oil, wooden products, textiles and clothing." .

