lsd:Entity_41822 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Iceland–Palestine relations refers to the relations between Iceland and State of Palestine. Iceland was the first Western European country to recognise the independence of State of Palestine. Iceland's representative to State of Palestine is a non_resident based at the Ministry for Foreign Affairs in Reykjavík, while State of Palestine's ambassador to Iceland is also a non_resident based in Oslo, Norway. Iceland has had the NGO The Iceland_State of Palestine Association (Félagið Ísland_Palestína) since 1987. On 29 November 2011, the parliament of Iceland passed a resolution that authorized the government to officially recognize the state of State of Palestine within the 1967 borders. Össur Skarphéðinsson, Minister for Foreign Affairs of Iceland, formally declared Iceland's recognition of the state of State of Palestine on December 15, 2011. Riyad Al_Maliki, the Foreign Minister of State of Palestine, visited Iceland to receive the diplomatic note in person and noted on that occasion that Iceland's recognition was important as State of Palestine was now recognized for the first time by a Western and northern European country." .

lsd:Entity_41825 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tirreno–Adriatico, nicknamed the \"Race of the Two Seas\", is an elite road bicycle racing in Italy, run between the Tyrrhenian and Adriatic coasts. The Tirreno–Adriatico was created in 1966 by the Lazio_based cycling club Forze Sportive Romane. Since 2002 the Tirreno–Adriatico is raced over seven stages, starting on Italy's western, Tyrrhenian seashore and finishing in San Benedetto del Tronto on the Adriatic Sea. The route of the 2015 Tirreno–Adriatico is exemplary for the trend to suit stage race." .

