    rdfs:label "The French conquest of Morocco (Arabic: غزو فرنسا للمغرب \"French Invasion of Morocco\", French: Campagne du Maroc \"Morocco Campaign\" or pacification du Maroc \"Pacification of Morocco\") began in 1907 and continued until 1934. On 30 March 1912, Sultan Abd al_Hafid signed the Treaty of Fes, formally ceding Moroccan sovereignty to France, transforming Morocco into a protectorate of France and sparking the 1912 Fez riots. The Zaian confederation of Berber tribes in Morocco fought a war of opposition against the French between 1914 and 1921." .

