lsd:Entity_46643 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 AFC Asian Cup statistics was the 16th edition of the men's AFC Asian Cup, a quadrennial international association football tournament organised by the Asian Football Confederation (AFC). Considering the efforts of the Football Federation Australia in developing the game on their territory and considering also all the achievements that have been made towards the development of association football in Australia and to encourage Australia to take steps towards developing the game, I am happy and honoured to announce that the executive committee of the Asian Football Confederation has approved Australia as the host nation of the 2015 AFC Asian Cup statistics. The group stage of the 2015 AFC Asian Cup statistics took place from 2015–2015: each team played three games, with the winners and runners_up from each group advancing to the knockout stage. The 2015 Asian Cup achieved 26 consecutive matches without a draw, the most of any major association football tournament, breaking the previous record of 18 set at the 1930 FIFA World Cup in Uruguay. On 2015, after the defeat of Iraq and the United Arab Emirates during the 2015 AFC Asian Cup statistics, West Asian Football Federation members reportedly sought to remove Australia from the AFC primarily due to \"Australia benefiting hugely from Asian involvement without giving much in return\", the resentment grew in the aftermath of Australia's conquest of the tournament." .

