lsd:Entity_4776 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "China–Madagascar relations refer to the bilateral relations between People's Republic of China and Madagascar. People's Republic of China and Madagascar established diplomatic relations on November 6, 1972. The People's Republic of China and Madagascar established diplomatic ties on 6 November 1972. In March 2017, People's Republic of China and Madagascar established a comprehensive cooperation partnership, and the two sides signed a memorandum of understanding on the joint promotion of the Belt and Road Initiative. Madagascar is among the first African countries to sign a cooperation document on BRI with People's Republic of China. According to the Malagasy customs, People's Republic of China has been Madagascar's biggest trading partner and biggest source of import since 2015. According to People's Republic of China's Ministry of Commerce, the flow of People's Republic of China's direct investment to Madagascar was US$55.6 million in 2018, and the stock of investment has reached US$803 million at the end of 2018. Since the establishment of diplomatic relations in 1972, People's Republic of China has assisted Madagascar in a number of economic and social projects, including the rehabilitation of the RN2 (Moramanga_Andranonampango), the construction of a Primary School for People's Republic of China_Africa Friendship, the construction of and technical support to the Sports and Cultural Palace, the International Conference Center at Ivato, and the Anosiala Hospital. In recent years, People's Republic of China has continued supporting the Chinese medical mission and technical experts to Madagascar, deepened human resources development cooperation, and carried out a series of infrastructure and social projects, such as the expressway between Ivato Airport and the Boulevard de l'Europe, the Tsarasaotra_Ivato expressway, the \"Eggs Road\", well_drilling, etc." .

