lsd:Entity_48496 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Bulgaria–Mexico relations refers to the diplomatic relations between Bulgaria and Mexico. In 1936, both Bulgaria and Mexico signed a Treaty of Friendship. High_level visits from Bulgaria to Mexico. High_level visits from Mexico to Bulgaria. Although Mexico was not a major destination for Bulgarian migrants; several hundred migrants from Bulgaria immigrated to Mexico in order to travel to the United States in the mid_1960s after the United States passed the Immigration and Nationality Act of 1965 which abolished the quota system based on national origins . In 1997, Mexico signed a Free Trade Agreement with the European Union (which includes Bulgaria). In 2018, trade between Bulgaria and Mexico totaled US$131 million. Bulgaria's main exports to Mexico include: mineral and chemical deposits, fruit seeds, unexposed film and textiles. Mexico's main exports to Bulgaria include: computers, mobile phones and other electronics." .

