    rdfs:label "This was the nineteenth season for the Regal Trophy, known from this season onwards as the 1989–90 Regal Trophy for sponsorship reasons. The Regal Trophy was dropped due to \"fixture congestion\" when Rugby League became a summer sport The Rugby League season always (until the onset of \"Summer Rugby\" in 1996) ran from around August_time through to around May_time and this Regal Trophy always took place early in the season, in the Autumn, with the final usually taking place in late January The Regal Trophy was variably known, by its sponsorship name, as the Player's No.6 Trophy (1971–1977), the John Player Trophy (1977–1983), the John Player Special Trophy (1983–1989), and the 1989–90 Regal Trophy in 1989." .

