    rdfs:label "The 1978 Rangitikei by_election of 1978 was a by_election in the New Zealand electorate of Rangitikei, a predominantly rural district in the middle of New Zealand's North Island. The by_election occurred on 1978, and was precipitated by the death of sitting National Party member of parliament (and Speaker of the House) Sir Roy Jack in December 1977. This upset was extremely rare in the post_war political climate of New Zealand, especially in a rural electorate that traditionally voted National (although such voting is more likely in a by_election)." .

