    rdfs:label "The Munster GAA Hurling Under_20 Championship, known simply as the Munster Under_21 Hurling Championship, is an annual inter_county hurling competition organised by the Munster Council of the Gaelic Athletic Association (GAA). The championship was contested as the Munster Under_21 Championship between 1964 and 2018 before changing to an under_20 age category from 2019. The Munster Championship began in 1964 in response to a Congress motion put forward by the Kerry County Board for the introduction of a new championship grade. They won all bar one of the available championship titles between 1964 and 1985 and have won a combined total of 39 championship titles." .

