lsd:Entity_55492 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Supercoppa Italiana (English: Italian Super Cup) is an annual association football competition usually held the week before the season begins in Italy, or more recently in other countries during the winter. Inaugurated in 1988, 18 of the first 21 Supercoppa Italiana contested were played at the home of the Serie A champions, the exceptions being in 1993 and 2003, when it was held in the United States cities of Washington, D.C., and East Rutherford, New Jersey, and in 2002 when the game was played in the Libyan capital Tripoli." .

