lsd:Entity_61664 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Canada–Peru relations refers to the current and historical relations between Canada and the Peru. Canada and Peru established diplomatic relations on 21 October 1944. In 2016, Canada became an Associate member of the Pacific Alliance, which includes Peru, Chile, Colombia and Mexico. Martín Vizcarra was Ambassador of Peru to Canada and simultaneously was First Vice President of Peru. Upon the impeachment of President Kuczynski, Vizcarra left Canada and returned to Peru to take up the Presidency. High_level visits from Canada to Peru. High_level visits from Peru to Canada. In May 2008, Canada and Peru signed a Free Trade Agreement which took effect on 1 August 2009." .

