lsd:Entity_10034 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1960 Saskatchewan general election was the fourteenth provincial election held in the Canadian province of Saskatchewan. It was held on 1960, to elect members of the Legislative Assembly of Saskatchewan. The Co_operative Commonwealth Federation of Tommy Douglas campaigned promising Medicare, a public medical insurance and delivery plan for all of Saskatchewan, and it was re_elected with a slightly increased majority. A year later, Douglas passed legislation making Saskatchewan the first province in Canada to have Medicare. The Liberals were concerned that the economic development of Saskatchewan had lagged behind the rest of Canada during the Douglas era." .

