lsd:Entity_10593 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1949 Pelileo earthquake was the largest earthquake in the Western Hemisphere in more than five years. On 05 August 1949, it struck Ecuador's Tungurahua Province southeast of its capital Ambato and killed 5,050 people. At the time it struck the 1949 Pelileo earthquake was the second_worst earthquake in Ecuador's modern history topped only by the 1797 Riobamba earthquake, and the most devastating earthquake in the Western Hemisphere since the 1944 San Juan earthquake. Several major earthquakes have occurred throughout the country since 1949, including the 1987 Ecuador earthquakes and the 1997 Ecuador earthquake." .

