    rdfs:label "Black Ice World Tour was a 2008–2010 concert tour by Australian rock band AC/DC, in support of their fifteenth studio album Black Ice (2008). On September 30, 2020, AC/DC officially confirmed that Johnson and Rudd has rejoined the band for a new studio album and possibly tour, signaling that the “Black Ice” tour may not have been the last tour with Rudd, and the last full tour with Johnson. The tour ended up being the most successful by AC/DC, grossing roughly $441.1 million, making it the fourth highest_grossing concert tour of all_time." .

