lsd:Entity_11330 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Recopa Sudamericana (officially the 2013 Recopa Santander Sudamericana for sponsorship reasons) was the 21st edition of the Recopa Sudamericana, the association football competition organized by CONMEBOL between the winners of the previous season's two major South American club tournaments, the Copa Libertadores and the Copa Sudamericana. The competition was contested in two_legged home_and_away format between two Brazilian teams, S.C. Corinthians Paulista, the 2012 Copa Libertadores champion, and São Paulo FC, the 2012 Copa Sudamericana champion. The first leg was hosted by São Paulo FC at Estádio do Morumbi in São Paulo FC on 2013, while the second leg was hosted by S.C. Corinthians Paulista at Estádio do Pacaembu in São Paulo FC on 2013. S.C. Corinthians Paulista won both legs, the first leg by 2–1, and the second leg by 2–0, to win their first Recopa Sudamericana title." .

