lsd:Entity_12273 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Creole case was a slave rebellion aboard the American slave ship Creole in 01 November 1841, when the brig was seized by the enslaved persons onboard the ship, freeing 128 slaves who were aboard the ship when it reached Nassau in the British colony of the Bahamas where slavery was abolished. The Creole case generated diplomatic tension between the United Kingdom and the United States of America, and political rumblings within the United States of America." .

lsd:Entity_123 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sannin shogi (三人将棋 three_person chess), or in full kokusai sannin shōgi (国際三人将棋 international three_person chess), is a three_person Shogi variant invented circa 1930 by Tanigasaki Jisuke and recently revived. However, except for castling and the promoted king, which is reminiscent of the queen of Western chess (indeed, it moves like the queen in hexagonal chess), the pieces are fair analogues of their standard_shōgi counterparts." .

lsd:Entity_12306 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 34th Japan Academy Prize (第34回日本アカデミー賞) is the 34th edition of the Japan Academy Film Prize, an award presented by the Nippon Academy_Sho Association to award excellence in filmmaking. It awarded the best films of 2010 and it took place on 18 February 2011 at the Grand Prince Hotel New Takanawa in Tokyo, Japan." .

