lsd:Entity_12335 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009–10 NBA season was the 64th season of the National Basketball Association (National Basketball Association). During the National Basketball Association All_Star Weekend, Nate Robinson of the New York Knicks won the Sprite Slam Dunk Contest for the third time in his career; Kevin Durant, who also won the inaugural event, won this year's H.O.R.S.E Competition and Boston's Paul Pierce beat rookie Stephen Curry to win the Three_Point Shootout. The 2009–10 NBA season was broadcast in the United States by ABC, ESPN, TNT and National Basketball Association TV." .

