    rdfs:label "1875 Greek legislative election were held in Greece on 18 July 1875." .

lsd:Entity_12582 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 London Marathon was the 35th running of the annual marathon race in London, England, which took place on Sunday, 26 April 2015. It was the third time that McFadden had set a course record in London and it was her first global marathon title." .

lsd:Entity_12585 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013_14 Ukrainian Hockey Championship was the 22nd annual edition of the Ukrainian Hockey Championship." .

lsd:Entity_12588 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Queensland Cup season was the 13th season of Queensland's top_level statewide rugby league competition run by the Queensland Rugby League. Two new teams entered the Queensland Cup in 2008, as the competition expanded north with the Mackay Cutters and the Northern Pride. The 2008 Queensland Cup regular season featured 22 rounds, with one team receiving a bye in each round." .

lsd:Entity_12593 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Patagonian Expedition Race is an annual endurance adventure race that takes place in the remote wilderness of Chile Patagonia, run to help protect and raise awareness about the fragile environment in this region. Created by geologist Stjepan Pavicic, a pioneer of Chile Patagonia, the first race was run in 2004 and since then athletes from 26 different nations have taken part. Each edition takes place on a different course through the most remote and untouched regions of Chile Patagonia. The race is organized by NIGSA (Nómadas International Group S.A.), formerly known as, Nómadas Outdoor Services Ltda., an organization located in Punta Arenas, working for the goals of environmental protection and the advancement of eco_tourism in the region of Chile Patagonia. The mission of the race is to raise international awareness of the fragile environment of Chile Patagonia. Stjepan Pavicic, Race Director, explains: \"From the beginning, we have focused on creating an experience that is not only a physical and mental challenge, but one that sends a real message: we must protect and preserve this remote and pristine region of Chile Patagonia. Eventually the new trails will allow international tourists access to this region's unique features, increasing eco_tourism in Chile Patagonia. 2007: The longest race of its kind in history took the teams 1,112 km through the southern region of Chile Patagonia, from Torres del Paine National Park all the way to Puerto Williams on the Navarino Island. The race is also supported by the Chile Government, with the aim of promoting sustainable adventure travel in Chile Patagonia. The Patagonian Expedition Race entered an official partnership agreement with the Olympic Committee of Chile (Comité Olímpico de Chile, COCH) in October 2007." .

lsd:Entity_126 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 United States Women's Curling Championship took place on February 12–19 at the Scheels Arena in Fargo, North Dakota." .

lsd:Entity_12600 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 2021, the decennial United Kingdom Census 2021, called Census 2021, will occur throughout most of the United Kingdom, with the rest of the nation being enumerated in 2022. The United Kingdom Census 2011 was the first decennial census in the United Kingdom to include the option of completing the census documentation online. Although it is a Crown Dependency, and not part of the United Kingdom, Jersey will carry out a census on the same day as the 2021 UK census." .

lsd:Entity_12613 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988 Brabantse Pijl was the 28th edition of the Brabantse Pijl cycle race and was held on 27 March 1988." .

lsd:Entity_1265 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1932 Arizona gubernatorial election took place on 1932. Incumbent Governor George W. P. Hunt ran for the Democratic nomination, but lost in the primary to Benjamin Baker Moeur, whose pre_gubernatorial experience included service as the Secretary of the Board of Education for Arizona State Teacher's College, which would later become Arizona State University. Benjamin Baker Moeur defeated cattle rancher Jack Kinney in the general election, and was sworn in as Arizona's fourth Governor (excluding non_consecutive terms) on January 3, 1933. Incumbent Governor George W. P. Hunt, who was elected to his seventh (non_consecutive) term over then_incumbent Governor John Calhoun Phillips in 1930, was opposed in the primary by Benjamin Baker Moeur, who had served as Secretary of the Board of Education for Arizona State Teacher's College prior to running for the office of Governor, as well as Attorney General K. Berry Peterson, State Senator Fred Sutter, and Webster C. Reed." .

lsd:Entity_12651 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Panam GP Series season is the revival of Panam GP Series." .

lsd:Entity_12676 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Chang_Sat Bangkok Open was a professional tennis tournament played on hardcourt. It took place in Bangkok, Thailand between 13 September 2010 and 2010." .

lsd:Entity_12684 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kazakh famine of 1919–1922, also referred to as the Turkestan famine of 1919–1922, was a period of mass starvation and drought that took place in the Kirghiz ASSR (present_day Kazakhstan) and Turkestan Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic as a result of war communism policy, in which 400,000 to 750,000 peasants died. The event was part of the greater Russian famine of 1921–22 that affected other parts of the Soviet Union, in which up to 5,000,000 people died in total. The famine was caused by severe intermittent drought conditions, aggravated by the Russian Civil War and the policy of Prodrazvyorstka adopted by the Soviet Union government." .

lsd:Entity_12687 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 Constitution of Romania was drafted by a committee of the Great National Assembly (MAN) and approved by a plenary session of the Central Committee of the Romanian Communist Party on 1965. It was Romania's sixth constitution, and the third of the Communist era." .

lsd:Entity_12694 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1953 Yugoslav Cup was the 7th season of the top association football knockout competition in SFR Yugoslavia, the Yugoslav Cup (Serbo_Croatian: Kup Jugoslavije), also known as the \"Marshal Tito Cup\" (Kup Maršala Tita), since its establishment in 1946." .

lsd:Entity_12699 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lebanon competed at the Lebanon at the 2012 Summer Paralympics in London, United Kingdom from August 29 to 2012. Lebanese Paralympian, Edward Maalouf, who was sponsored by the British Embassy in Beirut, became the only qualified Paralympic athlete representing Lebanon at the London 2012 Paralympics." .

