lsd:Entity_12847 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Irish Professional Championship was a professional invitational snooker tournament which took place in 25 September 2007. The tournament was held at the Red Cow Exhibition Centre in Dublin, and featured sixteen exclusively Ireland and Northern Ireland players." .

lsd:Entity_12850 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Copa del Rey de Baloncesto 2011–12 was the 76th edition of the Copa del Rey de Baloncesto. It was managed by the ACB League and was held in Barcelona, in the Palau Sant Jordi on 16 February 2012–19." .

lsd:Entity_12862 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The September 1988 Haitian coup d'état took place on 18 September 1988, when a group of non_commissioned officers in the Haiti Presidential Guard overthrew General Henri Namphy and brought General Prosper Avril to power. Namphy had overthrown Manigat in the June 1988 Haiti coup d'état when Manigat sought to exercise his constitutional right to control military assignments." .

lsd:Entity_1287 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Qurna was a battle during the Iraq War between the Multinational force in Iraq and Iraqi insurgents. The battle took part in Al_Qurnah. In the battle, the insurgents tried to take the control of the city from the allies, mainly Danish, Lithuanian and United Kingdom soldiers." .

lsd:Entity_12873 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Tripoli occurred in 1551 when the Ottomans besieged and vanquished the Knights of Malta in the fortress of Tripoli, modern Libya. The siege culminated in a six_day bombardment and the surrender of the city on 15 August 1551. The Siege of Tripoli succeeded an earlier attack on Malta in July, which was repelled, and the successful invasion of Gozo, in which 5,000 Christian captives were taken and brought on galleys to the location of Tripoli. The French Ambassador to the Ottoman Empire, Gabriel d'Aramon, joined the Ottoman fleet at Tripoli, with two galleys and a galliot, The declared mission of the ambassador was to dissuade the Ottomans from capturing the city, at the request of the Grand Master of Malta, as Malta was not identified as an enemy in the Franco_Ottoman alliance against the Habsburgs." .

lsd:Entity_12899 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ram fighting is a blood sport between two rams (large_horned male sheep), held in a ring or open field." .

lsd:Entity_12928 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Jerusalem tractor attack was a terrorist ramming attack that occurred on 04 August 2014, when a man drove an excavator type of tractor out of a construction site, injuring several pedestrians and killing one man before ramming the tractor into a public bus, overturning the bus and then hitting it repeatedly. The attack took place following a month that had seen over 360 attacks on Jews, a spate that was thought by The Jerusalem Post to have \"peaked\" on 04 August 2014 with this attack and the shooting of a uniformed soldier in the French Hill neighborhood, leading to an increase in security in the city." .

lsd:Entity_12948 a lsd:Context_narration ;
