lsd:Entity_13486 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Aaron's 499 was the ninth race of the 2006 NASCAR Nextel Cup Series season. Elliott Sadler won the pole position, while Jimmie Johnson won the race." .

lsd:Entity_13511 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Beach Soccer World Cup 1997 was the third edition of the Beach Soccer World Championships, the most prestigious competition in international beach soccer contested by men's national teams until 2005, when the competition was then replaced by the second iteration of a world cup in beach soccer, the better known FIFA Beach Soccer World Cup. For the third consecutive time, the tournament took place at Copacabana Beach in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. Hosts Brazil won the tournament for the third time in a row by beating Uruguay 5–2 in what was a repeat of the final in the Beach Soccer World Cup 1996." .

lsd:Entity_13527 a lsd:Context_narration ;
