lsd:Entity_13533 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Montichiari (08 May 1373), is one of the most important episodes of the war waged by the papal league led by Gregory XI against the Visconti of Milan, preparing the return of the pope to Rome." .

lsd:Entity_13577 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1554, adopted unanimously on 29 July 2004, after reaffirming all United Nations Security Council resolution on Abkhazia and Georgia, particularly Resolution 1524 (2004), the Council extended the mandate of the United Nations Observer Mission in Georgia (UNOMIG) until 31 January 2005." .

lsd:Entity_13583 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The FIS Ski_Flying World Championships 1994 took place on 1994 in Planica, Slovenia for the record fourth time." .

lsd:Entity_13587 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The naval Battle of Palermo took place on 02 June 1676 during the Franco_Dutch War, between a French force sent to support a revolt in the city of Messina against the Spanish rule in Sicily, and a Spanish force supported by a Dutch maritime expedition force. As in the Franco_Spanish War of 1635_1659, in the Franco_Dutch War Spain retained its position in Italy and proved able to thwart French hopes of major gains." .

lsd:Entity_13592 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Teen USA 1986, the 4th Miss Teen USA pageant, was televised live from Ocean Center, Daytona Beach, Florida on 1986." .

lsd:Entity_13601 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1985 Guatemalan general election were held in Guatemala on 03 November 1985, with a second round of the presidential elections taking place on 8 December." .

lsd:Entity_13633 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Cyclone Beni was an intense tropical cyclone that affected four countries, on its 18_day journey across the South Pacific Ocean during January and 05 February 2003. Later that day RSMC Nadi reported that Beni had explosively developed and peaked as a Category 5 severe tropical cyclone on the Australian scale, with 10_minute sustained winds of 205 km/h (125 mph). The remnant low of Cyclone Beni made landfall near Mackay on 05 February 2003." .

lsd:Entity_13637 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dream 11 was a mixed martial arts event promoted by Fighting and Entertainment Group's mixed martial arts promotion Dream held on 06 October 2009." .

lsd:Entity_13642 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 Big Sky Conference Men's Basketball Tournament was the twelfth edition, held March 5–7 at the Walkup Skydome at Northern Arizona University in Flagstaff, Arizona." .

lsd:Entity_13656 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dau al Set (Catalan pronunciation: ), the first post_World War II artistic movement in Catalonia, was founded in Barcelona in 1948 by poet Joan Brossa. Dau al Set first began as an avant_garde artistic collective led by Joan Brossa, a Catalan poet, in 1948. In an attempt to revive the avant_garde scene in Spain Dau al Set was formed. In 1949, with help from Joan_Josep Tharrats's private printing press, Dau al Set published its first self_entitled magazine journal. The magazine journal was delivered throughout Barcelona to those with subscriptions and served a niche population at the time. During this time from 1953 till 1956 Dau al Set continued to be created and published by Joan_Josep Tharrats. Another influence on Dau al Set was Surrealism, a cultural movement greatly influenced by Dadaism, which began in the 1920s. Dau al Set has had a lasting impact throughout history the most notable being the continuation of the avant_garde in Spain throughout Francoist Spain. Moreover, Dau al Set contributed to the creation of the Informalist movement seen in Spain during the fifties. Also the magical and fantasy elements of Dau al Set was seen to later emerge again in Spain in the eighties." .

lsd:Entity_13660 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 603, adopted unanimously on 25 November 1987, considered a report by the Secretary_General regarding the United Nations Disengagement Observer Force." .

lsd:Entity_13666 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Elite One is the 57th season of the Cameroon top_tier association football league. Elite One consists of 18 teams for the 2017 season with three clubs relegated to Elite Two and three promoted." .

lsd:Entity_13679 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 WNBA All_Star Game was played on 12 July 2003 at Madison Square Garden in New York City, home of the New York Liberty." .

lsd:Entity_13687 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 FFA Cup Final was the 2nd final of the premier association football knockout cup competition in Australia. Perth Glory FC qualified for the FFA Cup Final on 2015, with a 3–1 victory over Melbourne City at Nib Stadium. Melbourne Victory qualified for the FFA Cup Final on 2015, with a 3–0 victory over Hume City at AAMI Park. On 2015, Football Federation Australia announced the 2015 FFA Cup Final would be held at either AAMI Park in Melbourne or Perth’s nib Stadium. The choice of venue depended on the result of the second semi_final match between Hume City and Melbourne Victory. If Melbourne Victory defeat Hume City, the 2015 Final would be held at AAMI Park. Melbourne Victory and Perth Glory FC were among 648 teams who entered the inaugural FFA Cup competition, and as A_League clubs, both entered the tournament in the Round of 32. Melbourne doubled the advantage seven minutes later with Carl Valeri playing a through_ball into the path of striker Besart Berisha, whose first touch took him past the final defender and then fired the ball across Perth Glory FC keeper Ante Covic and inside the left post." .

lsd:Entity_13699 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Aubervilliers Congress (French: congrès d'Aubervilliers) of the Socialist Party (PS) was held on 07 April 2018 and 08 April 2018 near the Front Populaire station of the Paris Métro in Aubervilliers, Seine_Saint_Denis. On 9 December 2017, the National Council of the Socialist Party (PS) agreed to hold the next party congress near the Front Populaire station of the Paris Métro in Aubervilliers, Seine_Sain7 07 April 2018_Deni8 07 April 2018 07 April 2018. The Aubervilliers Congress took place on 07 April 2018 and 08 April 2018, designating the national leadership of the party." .

lsd:Entity_13702 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 ITTF World Tour was the 21st season of the International Table Tennis Federation's professional table tennis world tour. The Super Series events offered the highest prize money and the most points towards the ITTF World Tour standings, which determined the qualifiers for the 2016 ITTF World Tour Grand Finals in December." .

lsd:Entity_1371 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 World Figure Skating Championships were held 29 March 2017 – 02 April 2017 in Helsinki, Finland. The following new ISU Judging System were set during this competition: Participants were required to have attained minimum technical element scores at an earlier senior international competition. The International Skating Union published a complete list on 2017." .

