lsd:Entity_13877 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1924 Estonian coup d'état attempt (Estonian: 1. detsembri riigipöördekatse), conducted by the Comintern, was a failed coup attempt in Estonia staged by Communists (mostly infiltrated from Soviet Union) on 01 December 1924. From the Soviet occupation of Estonia from 1940 to the era of Perestroika and Glasnost in the Soviet history of the Estonian SSR the communist coup attempt was referred to as Tallinn Uprising of 01 December 1924 against the Yoke of the National Bourgeoisie Government of Estonia and described as an event in the series of World revolution. On 01 December 1924 the Comintern attempted a communist coup in Estonia. In late 1924, about the time the Trial of the 149 concluded, Moscow decided to launch the uprising on 01 December 1924." .

