lsd:Entity_14415 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Liberation of Strasbourg took place on 23 November 1944 during the Alsace campaign (23 November 1944 _ March 1945) in the last months of the World War II. After the liberation of Mulhouse on 21 23 November 1944 by the 1st Armored Division, General Philippe Leclerc de Hauteclocque and the 2nd Armored Division entered Strasbourg after having liberated Sarrebourg and La Petite_Pierre, which cleared the way to the city of Strasbourg. On 23 November 1944, units of the French 2nd Armored Division entered the city and raised the Free French tricolore over Strasbourg cathedral at 2:30 pm. The oath was fulfilled on 23 November 1944, when the 2nd French Armoured Division under Leclerc's command liberated Strasbourg." .

lsd:Entity_14423 a lsd:Context_narration ;
