    rdfs:label "The Dawson Massacre, also called the Dawson expedition, was an incident in which 36 Texian militiamen were killed by Mexican soldiers on 17 September 1842 near San Antonio de Bexar (now the U.S. city of San Antonio, Texas). In late summer of 1848 (after Texas had become a U.S. state), a group of La Grange citizens retrieved the remains of the men killed in the Dawson Massacre from their burial site near Salado Creek." .

