lsd:Entity_14798 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "(Los Angeles Lakers) | television = NBC (U.S.) | announcers = Marv Albert and Doug Collins | HOFers = Lakers:Shaquille O'Neal (2016) Kobe Bryant (2020)76ers:Dikembe Mutombo (2015)Allen Iverson (2016)Coaches:Larry Brown (2002)Phil Jackson (2007)Officials:Dick Bavetta (2015) | radio_network = ESPN | radio_announcers = Brent Musburger and Jack Ramsay | referees_1 = Dick Bavetta, Ron Garretson, Joe Crawford | referees_2 = Steve Javie, Bernie Fryer, Ronnie Nunn | referees_3 = Bennett Salvatore, Bob Delaney, Dan Crawford | referees_4 = Hugh Evans, Jack Nies, Eddie F. Rush | referees_5 = Dick Bavetta, Bernie Fryer, Joe Crawford | ECF result = 76ers defeat Bucks, 4–3 | WCF result = Lakers defeat Spurs, 4–0 }} The 2001 NBA Finals was the NBA Finals of the National Basketball Association (NBA)'s 2000–01 season." .

lsd:Entity_14830 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Fernie is a city in the Elk Valley area of the East Kootenay region of southeastern British Columbia, Canada, located on BC Highway 3 on the eastern approaches to the Crowsnest Pass through the Rocky Mountains. Fernie lies on the Elk River, along Canada's southernmost east_west transportation corridor through the Rockies that crosses the range via the Crowsnest Pass, 40 kilometres (25 miles) to the east. Fernie is the only city_class municipality in Canada that is fully encircled by the Rocky Mountains. The Lizard Range is home to Fernie Alpine Resort, one of the largest ski resorts in Canada, and Island Lake Catskiing, a resort. The Flathead Valley avalanche were two avalanche that buried 11 snowmobilers near Fernie on December 28, 2008. On October 17, 2017, there was an ammonia leak at the Fernie Memorial Arena which killed three workers (two 2008 Flathead Valley avalanches employees and one CIMCO refrigeration employee from Calgary) during the Ghostriders' regular season. The 'Riders were relocated because of this to the Elk Valley Leisure Centre in Sparwood, British Columbia during the 2017–18 KIJHL season until the 2008 Flathead Valley avalanches decided what to do. The 2008 Flathead Valley avalanches decided to replace ammonia for a synthetic refrigerant prior to the 2018–19 KIJHL season and moved the team back to the Fernie Memorial Arena. Influenced by chinook winds and being to the west of the continent, Fernie's winters are mild for its latitude in North America, although the climate is a lot more continental than coastal British Columbia." .

lsd:Entity_14839 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The St Crispin Street Fair is a fair held periodically in the Market Square of Northampton, England." .

lsd:Entity_14844 a lsd:Context_narration ;
