lsd:Entity_15368 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The World Ports Classic was a European two_day road bicycle racing held between the port cities of Rotterdam and Antwerp, organized by Amaury Sport Organisation as a 2.1 event on the UCI Europe Tour. The riders started in Rotterdam, finishing the first day in Antwerp before riding in the opposite direction on the second and final day. The 2013 event was won by Nikolas Maes of Belgium, while Bos won in 2014 World Ports Classic." .

lsd:Entity_15371 a lsd:Context_narration ;
