lsd:Entity_15908 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The UEFA Euro 2016 qualifying tournament was a association football competition that was played from 07 September 2014 to 17 November 2015 to determine the 23 Union of European Football Associations member men's national teams joining the automatically qualified host team France in the Union of European Football Associations Euro 2016 final tournament. All Union of European Football Associations member associations were eligible to compete in the qualifying competition, with the host team France qualifying directly to the finals tournament. Union of European Football Associations also stated in their regulations that \"the teams drawn into the group of five teams will have France added to their group for the purpose of playing centralised friendlies\". The seedings were as follows: The first legs were pl12 Novembere14 NovemberNovember, and the second legs were played on 15–17 November 2015. Union of European Football Associations unveiled the branding for the qualifiers on 15." .

