lsd:Entity_16292 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Triplemanía XXVI was a professional wrestling event produced by the Mexican professional wrestling promotion Lucha Libre AAA Worldwide (AAA) or Triple A. It took place on 25 August 2018, in the Arena Ciudad de México in Mexico City, Mexico. 2018 marked the 26th year since 1993 that the Mexican professional wrestling company Lucha Libre AAA Worldwide (AAA) or Triple A held their annual Triplemanía show and the 31st Triplemanía show promoted by AAA, as they held multiple Triplemanía shows over the summers of 1994 to 1997. The 2018 event took place on 25 August 2018, at the Arena Ciudad de México (Mexico City Arena), an indoor arena in Azcapotzalco, Mexico City, Mexico that has a maximum capacity of 22,300 spectators. The Triplemanía XXVI show will feature an undetermined number of professional wrestling matches, with different wrestlers involved in pre_existing scripted feuds, plots and storylines." .

lsd:Entity_1631 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Damehåndboldligaen (known as the Boxer Dameligaen for sponsorship reasons) is the 79th season of the Danish Women's Handball League, Denmark's premier handball league. The following 12 clubs compete in the Danish Women's Handball League during the 2014–15 season: Following is the list of clubs competing in 2014–15 Damehåndboldligaen, with their manager, captain, kit manufacturer and shirt sponsor." .

lsd:Entity_16358 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Arts and Crafts movement was an international trend in the decorative arts and fine arts that developed earliest and most fully in the British Isles and subsequently spread across the British Empire and to the rest of Europe and America. Initiated in reaction against the perceived impoverishment of the decorative arts and the conditions in which they were produced, the movement flourished in Europe and North America between about 1880 and 1920. The terms American Craftsman or Craftsman style are often used to denote the style of architecture, interior design, and decorative arts that prevailed between the dominant eras of Art Nouveau and Art Deco in the US, or approximately the period from 1910 to 1925." .

