    rdfs:label "The first version of the modern The Price is Right format first aired in Australia on the 0_10 Network from 1973–1974; this version was hosted by Garry Meadows and announcer Keith Livingston. The Price is Right later aired on Seven Network from 1981–1985 with host Ian Turpie and announcer John Deeks as The New Price Is Right. The following pricing games were played on the Seven Network version from 1981 to 1985: The following pricing games were played on the Network Ten version in 1989: The Price is Right was revived again from 13 December 1993 until 2 October 1998 on Nine Network, hosted by Larry Emdur with announcer Shawn Cosgrove . Some of these models include: The Price is Right was revived again in 2012 on Seven Network, hosted by Larry Emdur with announcer Brodie Young." .

