lsd:Entity_1788 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Japan Expo is a convention on Japanese popular culture _ the largest of its kind in the world outside Japan _ taking place in Paris, France, although it has branched out into a partnership festival _ Kultima _ and expanded to include some European and US pop culture as well. It is held yearly at the beginning of July for four days (usually from Thursday to Sunday) in the Parc des Expositions de Villepinte (the second_largest convention center in France). The first exposition took place in 1999 at the ISC Paris Business School and welcomed 2,400 visitors, a number which has grown steadily. In 2002, Japan Expo was hosted at the Center of New Industries and Technologies (CNIT) in La Défense, Paris. Other than the main convention in Paris, Japan Expo has expanded to 4 cities in 3 countries on 2 continents:" .

lsd:Entity_17893 a lsd:Context_narration ;
