lsd:Entity_17985 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Saya (Turkish: Saya, Azeri Turkish: Saya) or Sayaqan (Turkish: Sayagan) is a summer feast and festival Turkic and Altai folklore. The Saya festival (literally it can be translated as abundance) is related to a cult of a solar deity, with a fertility cult." .

lsd:Entity_17992 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 United States Senate election in Colorado was held on 04 November 2014 to elect a member of the United States Senate to represent the Colorado, concurrently with the election of the Governor of Colorado, 2014 United States Senate elections to the United States Senate, elections to the United States House of Representatives, and various state and local elections. At the Republican state assembly on 2014, Cory Gardner received 73% of the votes of over 3,900 delegates." .

lsd:Entity_18000 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Daniels, et al. v. the City of New York was a class action lawsuit filed in 1999 against the New York Police Department (NYPD) and the City of New York, charging them with racial profiling and unlawful stop and frisk, and requesting the disbanding of the NYPD Street Crimes Unit." .

lsd:Entity_18036 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Scottish Open is a professional golf tournament in Scotland, and is one of eight tournaments that are part of the Rolex Series, which identifies it as one of the European Tour's premier events. The first Sunbeam Electric Scottish Open was part of the 1972 European Tour and was held at Downfield Golf Club near Dundee. From 1997 the Scottish Open's pre_Open place on the European Tour schedule was taken by the Loch Lomond World Invitational, which had been first held at Loch Lomond Golf Club in September 1996. From 2001, it was decided that the Loch Lomond event would be known as the Scottish Open and all prior editions, including the September 1996 event, would be granted Scottish Open status. The 2001 Scottish Open was run without a main sponsor but from 2002 it was known as the Barclays Scottish Open, and was played at Loch Lomond until 2010." .

lsd:Entity_1804 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 World Championships in Athletics, under the auspices of the World Athletics, were held in the Mercedes_Benz Arena, Stuttgart, Germany between 13 August 1993 and 22 August 1993 with the participation of 187 nations. At subsequent Championships the race was replaced by the longer 5000 m. 1987 | 1991 World Championships in Athletics | 1993 | 1995 World Championships in Athletics | 1997. 1987 | 1991 World Championships in Athletics | 1993 | 1995 World Championships in Athletics | 1997. 1987 |1991 World Championships in Athletics |1993 |1995 World Championships in Athletics |1997. 1987 |1991 World Championships in Athletics |1993 |1995 World Championships in Athletics |1997." .

