lsd:Entity_18231 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1928 United States presidential election in Texas took place on 06 November 1928, as part of the 1928 United States presidential election which was held throughout all contemporary forty_eight states. In the meantime, Texas continued to vote solidly Democratic: between 1904 and 1924 United States presidential election in Texas no Republican nominee reached 24% of the statewide vote total. However, with all other prominent Democrats sitting the election out, the party nominated Al Smith, four_term Governor of New York as its nominee for 1928, with little opposition, despite disagreement among Texas Democrats like Governor Moody, plus \"Pa\" and \"Ma\" Ferguson. The traditionally Republican Texas German counties of Comal and Guadalupe, along with the former 1920 Ferguson counties of Lee and Washington voted overwhelmingly for Smith in appreciation of his views on Prohibition: in Comal County, which had been Robert La Follette's strongest nationwide in 1924 United States presidential election in Texas, the Democratic vote rose from 13 to 78%, thus supporting La Follette's family's endorsement of Smith after he died." .

lsd:Entity_18236 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Fastlane (2018) was a professional wrestling pay_per_view (PPV) event and WWE Network event produced by WWE for the SmackDown brand division. It took place on 11 March 2018, at the Nationwide Arena in Columbus, Ohio. Storylines were produced on WWE's weekly television show WWE Friday Night SmackDown. During the match, there were tensions between Owens and Zayn as a result of General Manager Daniel Bryan scheduling them to face each other the following week to determine the number one contender for the WWE Championship at Fastlane (2018). Corbin and Ziggler won their respective matches, thus making it a fatal five_way for the WWE Championship at Fastlane (2018). Bryan gave him the opportunity to be added to the WWE Championship match at Fastlane (2018) if he could defeat Styles in a non_title match. Orton interrupted and said the U.S. title was the one title he had never held during his WWE career and would be taking it from Roode at Fastlane (2018)." .

lsd:Entity_18246 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Graham v. Richardson, 403 U.S. 365 (1971), was a Supreme Court of the United States case in which the Court determined that state restrictions on welfare benefits for legal aliens but not for citizens violated the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment. The 9_0 decision was written by Harry Blackmun." .

lsd:Entity_18255 a lsd:Context_narration ;
