lsd:Entity_18443 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "killing of Bernard Whitehurst was shot in the back and killed on 02 December 1975 by Donald Foster, a Montgomery police officer who said he thought Whitehurst was the suspect in the robbery of a neighborhood grocery store. From the date of the killing, the Montgomery Advertiser covered the shooting of killing of Bernard Whitehurst by police and later investigated the subsequent controversy, publishing news stories and editorials that questioned the original police reports." .

lsd:Entity_18458 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The King George Street bombing was a suicide bombing which occurred on 21 March 2002 outside a clothing store and toy shop on King George Street in Jerusalem. On Thursday afternoon, 21 March 2002, a Palestinian suicide bomber detonated the explosive device, hidden underneath his jacket, in the middle of Jerusalem's shopping district in the King George Street in downtown Jerusalem amongst a crowd of shoppers." .

