lsd:Entity_18503 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "This is the first season of 1921 Malaya Cup (later known as Malaysia Cup). The final were held at Selangor Club Padang on 1921 where the southern champ, Singapore Lions defeated the northern champ, Selangor FA with 2_1 scoreline. In 1921, the British Royal Navy battleship H. M. S. Malaya called at Port Swettenham (now Port Klang), Singapore Lions, Malacca, Penang and Port Dickson. A 1921 Malaya Cup committee was set up and it was decided to run the association football competition in northern and southern sections. Six teams participated the inaugural 1921 Malaya Cup, Malacca, Negeri Sembilan, Singapore Lions, Penang, Selangor and Perak. The first 1921 Malaya Cup match was played on 1921, with Selangor defeating Penang 5–1 in front of an estimated crowd of 5,000 in Kuala Lumpur. Singapore Lions and Selangor topped their respective sections, and met in the first 1921 Malaya Cup final on 1 October at the Selangor Club field (now Merdeka Square)." .

lsd:Entity_18518 a lsd:Context_narration ;
