lsd:Entity_18652 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2020 Venezuelan parliamentary election were held in Venezuela on 06 December 2020. In 2020, the Committee of Electoral Candidacies, in charge of appointing a new National Electoral Council of Venezuela (CNE), announced that it would suspend its meetings because of the pandemic. The United States sanctioned Alfonzo and three others on 2020, accusing them of facilitating the illegitimate Maduro regime’s efforts to undermine the independence and democratic order of Venezuela. As of 2020, during the COVID_19 pandemic, electoral organizations such as the Venezuelan Electoral Observatory and the Education Assembly Electoral Observation Network, assured that there were many obstacles in Venezuela left to surpass before an electoral process takes place by 06 December 2020, including conditions, technological problems and a lack of agreement between political factions, saying that having the elections in 2020 did not appear feasible." .

