lsd:Entity_19112 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2014–15 Croatian presidential election were held in Croatia on 28 December 2014 and 11 January 2015, the sixth such elections since independence in 1991. As no candidate received 50% of the vote in the first round in 28 December 2014, a run_off took place in January 2015 between the two candidates with the most votes; Josipović and Kolinda Grabar_Kitarović. The election of Grabar_Kitarović was the first victory for the Croatian Democratic Union (HDZ) in a presidential election since the death of Franjo Tuđman in December 1999, making her the first right_wing President of Croatia in 15 years." .

