lsd:Entity_19801 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Valencia from 3 November 1811 to 09 January 1812, saw Marshal Louis Gabriel Suchet's French Army of Aragon besiege Captain General Joaquín Blake y Joyes' forces in the city of Valencia during the Peninsular War. With a population of 100,000, a lack of food, and obsolete defenses, Valencia was in no condition to sustain a siege. As the bombardment intensified, Blake capitulated and handed over Valencia on 09 January 1812. Blake performed poorly throughout the siege and the citizens of Valencia despised him for his feeble efforts." .

lsd:Entity_19815 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 PBZ Zagreb Indoors was a tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts. It was the 2nd edition of the Zagreb Indoors event and was part of the ATP International Series of the 2007 ATP Tour. It took place at the ITC Stella Maris in Croatia from January 29 through 2007." .

lsd:Entity_19822 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Stripped Classicism (or \"Starved Classicism\" or \"Grecian Moderne\") is primarily a 20th_century classical architecture architectural style stripped of most or all ornamentation, frequently employed by governments while designing official buildings." .

lsd:Entity_1986 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 U.S. Open was the 99th U.S. Open, held June 17–20 at Pinehurst Resort Course No. Payne Stewart won his second U.S. Open and third major championship, one stroke ahead of runner_up Phil Mickelson. This was the first U.S. Open at Pinehurst, which returned in 2005 and 2014." .

lsd:Entity_19861 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "classical liberalism is a political ideology and a branch of liberalism that advocates civil liberties under the rule of law with an emphasis on economic freedom. As a term, classical liberalism was applied in retrospect to distinguish earlier 19th_century liberalism from social liberalism. The view that modern liberalism is a continuation of classical liberalism is not universally shared." .

lsd:Entity_19865 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Sparkassen Cup – doubles was the tennis doubles event of the thirteenth edition of the Sparkassen Cup; a WTA Tier II tournament held in Leipzig, Germany. Unseeded American pairing Alexandra Stevenson and Serena Williams won the title, defeating Janette Husárová and Paola Suárez in the final, 6–3, 7–5." .

lsd:Entity_19870 a lsd:Context_narration ;
