lsd:Entity_20115 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018–19 Top 14 season competition was the 120th season of the French domestic rugby union club competition operated by the National Rugby League (LNR). The Top 14 final was contested between the top two teams in the league stage – Stade Toulousain (1st) and Clermont (2nd) – who both won their semi_finals with relative ease. In terms of attendances, the Top 14 once again proved to be the most popular rugby union league in the world, with over 2.7 million supporters watching games that season. The team finishing in 13th place faces the runner_up of the Pro D2, with the winner of this match playing in the 2019–20 Top 14 season and the loser in the 2019–20 Pro D2." .

