lsd:Entity_20149 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Russia participated in the Russia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2015 with the song \"A Million Voices\", written by Gabriel Alares, Joakim Björnberg, Katrina Noorbergen, Leonid Gutkin and Vladimir Matetsky. The song was performed by Polina Gagarina, who was selected by Russian broadcaster Channel One Russia (C1R) in 2015 to represent the nation at the 2015 contest in Vienna, Austria. In Russia's Russia in the Eurovision Song Contest on 23 May, \"A Million Voices\" finished in second place, receiving 303 points and full marks from five countries. Prior to the 2015 Contest, Russia had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest eighteen times since its first entry in 1994. Since the introduction of the semi_finals to the contest in 2004, Russia has, up to Russia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016, managed to qualify to the final every year. The Russian broadcaster for the 2015 Contest, who broadcast the event in Russia and organised the selection process for its entry, was Channel One Russia (C1R). Since 2008, the Russian participation in the contest alternates between C1R and Russia_1 (RTR); with C1R in charge for 2015. On 2015, Russian media reported that C1R had internally selected Polina Gagarina to represent Russia in Vienna, which was later confirmed on 2015 during the C1R news program Vremya. The music video, directed by Konstantin Cherepkov, features Miss Universe Russia 2015 Vladislava Evtushenko. Russia was placed into the first semi_final, to be held on 2015, and was scheduled to perform in the second half of the show." .

