lsd:Entity_20349 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Siberian Baroque is an architectural style common for ambitious structures in 18th_century Siberia, where 115 stone churches in Siberia were recorded in 1803, most of which were built in this provincial variant of the baroque architecture, influenced by the Ukrainian Baroque and in some cases even incorporating lamaist motifs." .

lsd:Entity_20355 a lsd:Context_narration ;
