lsd:Entity_20412 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Davis v. Washington, 547 U.S. 813 (2006), was a case decided by the Supreme Court of the United States holding that hearsay statements made in a 911 call asking for aid were not \"testimonial\" in nature and thus their introduction at trial did not violate the Confrontation Clause as defined in Crawford v. Washington. In a decision authored by Justice Antonin Scalia, the Court ruled that the Confrontation Clause of the Sixth Amendment, as interpreted in Crawford v. Washington, does not apply to \"non_testimonial\" statements not intended to be used in a future criminal prosecution." .

lsd:Entity_20423 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1904 Missouri gubernatorial election was Missouri's 26th gubernatorial election. The election was held on 08 November 1904 and resulted in a victory for the Democratic nominee, Joseph W. Folk, over the Republican candidate, former Mayor of St. Louis Cyrus Walbridge, and several other candidates representing minor parties." .

lsd:Entity_20449 a lsd:Context_narration ;
