lsd:Entity_2147 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The World Conference on Women, 1980 or the Second World Conference on Women took place between 1980 and 1980 in Copenhagen, Denmark as the mid_decade assessment of progress and failure in implementing the goals established by the World Plan of Action at the 1975 inaugural conference on women. The 1980 Conference held from 14 July and 30 July in Copenhagen, Denmark was the direct result of the World Conference on Women, 1975, which had been held in Mexico City in 1975, establishing the World Plan of Action and Declaration of Mexico on the Equality of Women and Their Contribution to Development and Peace." .

