lsd:Entity_22037 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Axalta presents the Pocono 400 was a Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series Pocono 325 held on 11 June 2017 at Pocono Raceway in Long Pond, Pennsylvania. The Pocono 325 was contested over 160 laps on the 2.5_mile (4.0 km) triangular superspeedway, and was the 14th Pocono 325 of the 2017 Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series season. The Pocono 325 was held at Pocono Raceway, which is a three_turn superspeedway located in Long Pond, Pennsylvania. Kyle Busch scored the pole for the Pocono 325 with a time of 50.237 and a speed of 179.151 mph (288.316 km/h). Kyle Busch led the field to the green flag at 3:22 p.m. Aside from an unscheduled pit stop by Joey Logano for a flat left_rear tire on the sixth lap, nothing unusual happened in the early stage of the Pocono 325." .

