    rdfs:label "The 1942 Stanley Cup Finals was a best_of_seven series between the Toronto Maple Leafs and the Detroit Red Wings. Toronto came back from a 3–0 series deficit to win the best_of_seven Stanley Cup Final. Detroit's Don Grosso opened the scoring in the second minute before John McCreedy tied it for Toronto. Detroit took the second game in Toronto by a score of 4–2. After the goal, Toronto picked up the pace, eventually out_shooting Detroit 16–7 in the third. 1942 Toronto Maple Leafs." .

