lsd:Entity_23406 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1938 Stanley Cup Finals was a best_of_five series between the Chicago Blackhawks and the Toronto Maple Leafs. Chicago won the series 3–1 to win their second Stanley Cup. Chicago set a record with eight American players winning the Stanley Cup. It was the last time that the Hawks would win the Stanley Cup at home until 2015, and the last that a Chicago team would win a championship at Chicago Stadium until the Bulls won their second straight NBA championship in 1992. The NHL did not see fit to make sure that the Stanley Cup was in Chicago when they won the game and the series on April 12. 1938 Chicago Blackhawks." .

lsd:Entity_2344 a lsd:Context_narration ;
