lsd:Entity_23449 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Omaha Race Riot of 1919 occurred in Omaha, Nebraska, 28 September 1919–29, 1919. At about 2:00 p.m. on Sunday, 28 September 1919, a large group of white youths gathered near the Bancroft School in South Omaha and began a march to the Douglas County Courthouse, where Brown was being held. Meanwhile, Omaha officials requested assistance from the United States of America Army, which had been going on long before Brown was killed. Together with other riots in 1919, the Omaha riot prompted the United States of America Senate Committee on Judiciary in October 1919 to call for an investigation of urban, industrial and racial problems." .

