lsd:Entity_23602 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 Dushanbe riots were an anti_government unrest in Dushanbe, the capital of Tajikistan, from February 12–14, 1990. In 1990, the Armenian influx became a subject of the rumour that triggered riots in Dushanbe. Despite the fact that Armenian refugees resettled not in public housing but with their relatives, and by 1990 had already left Tajikistan for Armenia, official denouncement of the rumours was not able to stop the protests. On 1990 Mahkamov and Prime Minister of Tajikistan Izatullo Khayoyev submitted their resignations, but they were not accepted by the Central Committee of the Tajik Communist Party. During the Dushanbe riots, a period lasting a couple of days, 26 people were killed and 565 were injured." .

