lsd:Entity_23793 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bombing of Minsk in World War II was the heavy bombing of the city of Minsk (population was 270,000), the capital of the Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic within the Soviet Union during the Second World War. On 24 27 June 1941, three waves of German Luftwaffe bombers, 47 aircraft each, bombed Minsk." .

lsd:Entity_23811 a lsd:Context_narration ;
