lsd:Entity_23920 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Caesarea (260) took place when the Sasanian Empire under Shapur I besieged the Roman Empire city of Antioch in 260 after winning over the Romans in the Battle of Edessa. The siege took place during a Sassanid invasion of the Roman Empire east, Caesarea during that time had a large population (about 400,000 inhabitants). The Sasanian Empire were unable to take the city, and took a Roman Empire as captive and tortured him until he revealed another route they could use. The Sasanian Empire raided Caesarea during the night, killing every Roman Empire soldier." .

lsd:Entity_2393 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In software quality assurance, software performance testing is in general a software testing practice performed to determine how a system performs in terms of responsiveness and stability under a particular workload. Load software testing is the simplest form of software performance testing. Isolation software testing is not unique to software performance testing but involves repeating a test execution that resulted in a system problem. To ensure consistent results, the software performance testing environment should be isolated from other environments, such as user acceptance software testing (UAT) or development. This is true in the case of functional software testing, but even more so with software performance testing, due to the end_to_end nature of its scope. Performance software testing is mainly divided into two main categories: This part of software performance testing mainly deals with creating/scripting the work flows of key identified business processes." .

