lsd:Entity_24224 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Canberra Challenger was a professional tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It took place in Canberra, Australia between 2016 and 16 January 2016. The tournament attracted 10 of the world's top 100 singles players, and although the 2016 edition was described as a \"one_off\" due to a gap in the events with the draw sizes changing in Sydney and Auckland, Tennis ACT boss Ross Triffitt campaigned for it to become a permanent fixture in the tennis calendar, succeeding in getting the event a spot in the 2017 ATP Challenger Tour schedule." .

