lsd:Entity_24429 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Isani flat siege was a confrontation between the Georgia police and security forces and an armed group of four Chechen men, including the former ISIS officer Akhmed Chatayev, in and around a flat on Gabriel Salosi Street in the Isani district of Tbilisi, from 21 to 22 November 2017. A special operation, involving the Georgia police and State Security Service, to disarm an armed group entrenched in a rented flat in a block in Gabriel Salos Street in Tbilisi's Isani district began late on 21 November 2017 and escalated to a gunfight and explosions overnight after hours of futile attempts by the authorities to convince the men to surrender. According to the head of the Georgia State Security Service Vakhtang Gomelauri, Chatayev and his associates made their way to Georgia in 2017, bypassing a border checkpoint, but declined to specify the country from which they crossed into Georgia. Four more men, all Georgia nationals, detained from 2017 to January 2018, were found guilty of providing logistical support to the Chatayev group and sentenced from 10 to 12 years in prison." .

lsd:Entity_24441 a lsd:Context_narration ;
