lsd:Entity_24456 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Hurricane Jimena /hiˈmɛnə/ was the second_strongest hurricane of the 2009 Pacific hurricane season, and tied with Hurricane Norbert as the strongest tropical cyclone to make landfall on western portion of the Baja California Peninsula. By the evening of August 31, Hurricane hunters measured winds of 155 mph (250 km/h) and a pressure of 931 mbar (hPa; 27.49 inHg) while the powerful cyclone began to turn to the north due to nearby 2009 Pacific hurricane season and a low pressure area west of Baja California." .

