lsd:Entity_24634 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Antoinism is a healing and Christian_oriented new religious movement founded in 1910 by Louis_Joseph Antoine (1846–1912) in Jemeppe_sur_Meuse, Seraing in Belgium. Five years later, the family moved to Jemeppe_sur_Meuse (Belgium), where he built twenty houses for workers. Thus, after the death of Catherine, there were two forms of Antoinism, which still remain different today: one in Belgium, and one in France. As of 2011, Antoinism counts 64 temples: 32 in Belgium, 31 in France and 1 in the Principality of Monaco. Although it does not refer directly to the Gospel, Antoinism is often considered a Christian_based new religious movement." .

