lsd:Entity_26600 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Berlin–Palermo railway axis (German: Eisenbahnachse Berlin–Palermo, Italian: Asse ferroviario Berlino_Palermo) is project No. 1 of the Trans_European high_speed rail network (Trans_European Networks_R), which involves the creation of a 2,200_kilometre_long (1,400 mi) high_speed rail line between Berlin and Palermo. It appointed the Belgian Karel Van Miert to coordinate the Berlin–Palermo rail corridor, who upon his death in June 2009 was succeeded by the Irish Pat Cox." .

