lsd:Entity_28936 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1405, adopted unanimously on 19 April 2002, after recalling resolutions 242 (1967), 338 (1973), 1397 (2002), 1402 (2002) and 1403 (2002), the Council emphasised the necessity of humanitarian access to the Palestinian population." .

lsd:Entity_28960 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1961 European Cup Winners' Cup Final was an association football match contested between ACF Fiorentina of Italy and Rangers F.C. of Scotland. It was the final match of the 1960–61 European Cup Winners' Cup and the first European Cup Winners' Cup final. The first leg was played at Ibrox Park, Glasgow and the second leg at the Stadio Comunale in Florence. It was Rangers F.C. first European final and in doing so became the first British team to reach the final of a European football competition. It was ACF Fiorentina's second European final having previously reached the 1957 European Cup Final. ACF Fiorentina won the final 4–1 on aggregate. Rangers F.C. were required to play a preliminary round in the competition where they beat Ferencváros from Hungary 5_4 on aggregate. In the semi final Rangers F.C. were then required to play English team Wolverhampton Wanderers. Rangers F.C. won the tie 3_1 on aggregate to reach their first ever European final. ACF Fiorentina, who were managed by Hungarian Nándor Hidegkuti, were the recent Coppa Italia winners and had reached the final of the European Cup four years earlier. Rangers F.C. were managed by Scot Symon and had reached the semi_final of the European Cup the previous year." .

lsd:Entity_28967 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Dilam was a major battle of the Unification of Saudi Arabia between Rashidi and Saudi rebels." .

lsd:Entity_28979 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 197 was a mixed martial arts event held on 23 April 2016, at MGM Grand Garden Arena in Las Vegas. The event's number was initially planned for an event taking place on March 5, 2016 at HSBC Arena in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, before being cancelled on December 29, 2015 and moved to MGM Grand Garden Arena in Las Vegas, to take place on February 6, 2016; the February event became UFC Fight Night: Hendricks vs. Thompson rather than a numbered pay_per_view after Vitor Belfort declined to fight Anderson Silva, and the March show was renumbered as UFC 196." .

