lsd:Entity_29414 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "\"Day of Independence\") is the national day of Israel, commemorating the Israeli Declaration of Independence in 1948. Because Israel declared independence on 14 May 1948, which corresponded with the Hebrew date 5 Iyar in that year, Yom Ha'atzmaut was originally celebrated on that date. Independence Day (Israel) is founded on the declaration of the establishment of the Israel by the Jewish leadership headed by future Prime Minister David Ben_Gurion on 14 May 1948. In response to widespread public feeling, the Chief Rabbinate in Israel decided during 1950–51 that Independence Day (Israel) should be given the status of a minor Jewish holiday on which Hallel be recited. People affiliated to the Edah HaChareidis mourn the establishment of Israel on Independence Day (Israel), claiming that the establishment of a Jewish state before the coming of the Messiah is a sin and heresy. In 2015, Rabbi Shlomo Riskin of Efrat founded Day to Praise, a global initiative which calls on Christians around the world to join in reciting the Hallel (Psalms 113–118), with the Jewish people, on Israel's Independence Day (Israel)." .

lsd:Entity_29416 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kinburn was fought on 12 October 1787 (N.S." .

