lsd:Entity_29444 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In the Illinois state capitol referendum, 1834 voters in the state of Illinois were asked on 04 August 1834 to choose the next state capitol." .

lsd:Entity_2946 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Odisha Legislative Assembly election took place in 2009, concurrently with the general election. With the tenure of the Orissa Assembly scheduled to expire on 2009, the Election Commission of India announced on 2 March that year that the elections to the Assembly would be held alongside the general election. Naveen Patnaik then won a controversial trust vote on 2009, after the opposition Congress and BJP legislators walked out of the Assembly in protest in the manner the vote was being conducted." .

lsd:Entity_29486 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1904 United States presidential election in California took place on 08 November 1904 as part of the 1904 United States presidential election." .

lsd:Entity_29492 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Halberd was a British naval operation that took place on 27 September 1941, during the World War II. Nine merchant ships carrying 81,000 tons of military equipment and supplies sailed from Liverpool on 16 September and from the Clyde on 17 September as part of Malta Convoys WS (Winston Specials) 11X, passing Gibraltar on 24 27 September 1941, with a close escort under the command of Rear_Admiral Harold Burrough. Force H rejoined the Malta Convoys at 07:10 27 September 1941." .

lsd:Entity_29498 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1938 Norwegian Football Cup was the 37th season of the Norway annual knockout association football tournament. The tournament was open for all members of Norwegian Football Federation, except those from Northern Norway. The 1938 Norwegian Football Cup Final was played at Briskeby in Hamar on 1938, and was contested by the defending champions Mjøndalen and the three_time former winners Fredrikstad FK. Fredrikstad FK secured their fourth title with a 3_2 win after extra time in the 1938 Norwegian Football Cup Final. Fredrikstad FK's cup_victory completed the first Norway double, having also won the inaugural League of Norway." .

lsd:Entity_29517 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bliss_Leavitt Mark 9 torpedo was a Bliss_Leavitt torpedo developed and produced by the E. W. Bliss Company and the Naval Torpedo Station in Newport, Rhode Island in 1915." .

lsd:Entity_29526 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1986 British Columbia general election was the 34th general election in the Province of British Columbia, Canada. The governing British Columbia Social Credit Party (Socreds) had seen a leadership change just months before the election, with Bill Bennett standing down in favour of Bill Vander Zalm." .

lsd:Entity_29531 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Sejny took place in 01 September 1920 during the Polish–Soviet War and Polish–Lithuania War. The 1st Legions Infantry Division of Colonel Dab_Biernacki attacked Lithuania 2nd Infantry Division at Sejny, capturing the town after a six_hour battle." .

lsd:Entity_29539 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 South African Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held at Kyalami on 14 March 1993. The race, contested over 72 laps, was the first race of the 1993 Formula One season and was won from pole position by Alain Prost, driving a Williams_Renault, with Ayrton Senna second in a McLaren_Ford and Mark Blundell third in a Ligier_Renault." .

lsd:Entity_29550 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Edmonton bid for the 2022 Commonwealth Games was an attempt to bring the 2022 Commonwealth Games to the city of Edmonton, Alberta, Canada. On 10 February 2015, Edmonton withdrew its bid for the Games. On March 31, 2014, The City of Edmonton announced its intent to bid for 2022 Commonwealth Games. On July 1, 2014, The City of Edmonton, in partnership with the Government of Alberta and Commonwealth Games Canada, named former Edmonton Airports President and CEO Reg Milley as the Chair of the Bid Committee for the 2022 Commonwealth Games. The logo for the Edmonton bid was also unveiled during the Canada Day celebrations at City Hall. Edmonton is Canada's fifth_largest city and the second_largest city in as well as the capital of the Province of Alberta. On February 11, 2015, Edmonton announced it was withdrawing its bid to host the 2022 Commonwealth Games, citing financial reasons and a global fall in oil prices." .

lsd:Entity_2956 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 UAW_Ford 500 was the 30th stock car race of the 2007 NASCAR Nextel Cup Series and the fourth in the ten_race season_ending Chase for the Nextel Cup. It was held on 07 October 2007 at Talladega Superspeedway in Talladega, Alabama, before a crowd of 155,000. It was held on 07 October 2007 at Talladega Superspeedway in Talladega, Alabama, a superspeedway that holds NASCAR races. As Johnson went to block his teammate, Stewart bump_drafted Jeff Gordon to give the latter the lead, which he held to clinch his fifth victory of the season, the 80th of his career, and a season sweep of victories at Talladega Superspeedway." .

lsd:Entity_29566 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 144 was a mixed martial arts pay_per_view event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on 26 February 2012 at the Saitama Super Arena in Saitama, Japan. UFC 144 was held at the Saitama Super Arena in the Chūō_ku central ward of Saitama City in Saitama Prefecture. UFC 144 marked the UFC's fifth appearance in Japan, their first event in Japan since UFC 29 in 2000, and its first event in Japan since the 2007 purchase of Pride Fighting Championships, which held many of its cards at Saitama Super Arena." .

lsd:Entity_29573 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of the strait of Messina was fought in 276 BC when a Ancient Carthage fleet attacked the Sicilian fleet of Pyrrhus of Epirus, who was crossing the strait to Italy. Pyrrhus had left Italy for Sicily on the Autumn of 278 BC and scored several major victories against the Ancient Carthage armies, but Roman successes against Pyrrhus' Italian allies convinced him to return to Italy." .

lsd:Entity_29591 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 Dino Ferrari Grand Prix was a non_championship Formula One motorsport held at the Autodromo Dino Ferrari, Imola on 16 September 1979." .

lsd:Entity_29629 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 Lady Wigram Trophy was a motor race held at the Wigram Airfield Circuit on 1965. It was the fourteenth Lady Wigram Trophy to be held and was won by Jim Clark driving the Lotus 32B in what was the fastest race in the history of the Lady Wigram Trophy." .

lsd:Entity_29632 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The IWOCL (IWOCL – \"eye_wok_ul\") is an annual conference that brings together the community of OpenCL users, researchers, developers and suppliers to share OpenCL best practise and help advance the use of the Khronos OpenCL standard for the parallel programming of heterogeneous systems. Participation at IWOCL is open to anyone who is interested in contributing to, and participating in the OpenCL community including developers working with the many APIs, tools and libraries built on OpenCL, including the Khronos SPIR (Standard Portable Intermediate Representation) and SYCL (C++ abstraction layer). The IWOCL (IWOCL) is now in its 7th year with the first event taking place at Georgia Tech, USA on May 13–14, 2013." .

lsd:Entity_29647 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The San Diego Film Critics Society Awards 2006, honoring the best in film for 2006, were given in 2006 by the San Diego Film Critics Society Award." .

lsd:Entity_29649 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The group stage of the 2013 AFC Cup group stage was played from 26 February to 2013." .

lsd:Entity_29672 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Saskatchewan general election was held on 2007; the writ was dropped on 2007. The Saskatchewan New Democratic Party government of Premier Lorne Calvert was defeated by the Saskatchewan Party, led by Brad Wall. Lorne Calvert, Premier of Saskatchewan and leader of the New Democratic Party (NDP), advised the Lieutenant Governor of Saskatchewan to call an election for 2007. This strategy paid off; by the spring of 2007 the Saskatchewan Party was well ahead in most opinion polling. 1 Dan Harder, the Saskatchewan Party candidate in Regina Walsh Acres, withdrew his candidacy on 2007 after the party learned the details of a complaint of inappropriate conduct made against him by employees of Big Brothers of Regina in 2006 while he was executive director of the organization." .

lsd:Entity_29696 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1966 Xingtai earthquake (Chinese: 邢台大地震; pinyin: Xíngtái Dà Dìzhèn) was a sequence of major earthquakes that took place between 08 March 1966 and March 29, 1966, in the area administered by the prefecture_level city of Xingtai in southern Hebei province, People's Republic of China. The first earthquake with magnitude 6.0 on the Moment magnitude scale and epicenter in Longyao County occurred in the early morning of 08 March 1966." .

lsd:Entity_29703 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Formula Three, also called Formula 3, abbreviated as F3, is a third_tier class of open_wheel formula racing. (1213 kiB) Until the launch of the FIA Formula 3 Championship in 2019, there has never been a World Championship for Formula Three. In the 1970s and into the 1980s the European Formula Three Championship and British Formula 3 Championship (once one series had emerged from the competing British series in the 1970s) were the most prominent, with a number of future Formula One champions coming from them. France, Germany, and Italy also had important Formula Three series, but interest in these was originally subsidiary to national formulae – Formula Renault in France and Formula Super Vee in Germany. Brazil's SudAm Formula Three Championship, which now has the most powerful engine of all Formula Three series, was known for producing excellent drivers who polished their skills in the British Formula 3 championship." .

lsd:Entity_29710 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 2021 was unanimously adopted on 29 November 2011." .

lsd:Entity_29749 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "World Bee Day is celebrated on May 20." .

lsd:Entity_29778 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1947 ISSF World Shooting Championships was the contemporary name of the ISSF World Shooting Championship held in Stockholm, Sweden in the summer of 1947." .

lsd:Entity_29810 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Men's skeet event at the shooting at the 2016 Summer Olympics – men's skeet took place on 12 13 August 2016 and 13 August 2016 at the National Shooting Center." .

