lsd:Entity_30123 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Enschede fireworks disaster (Dutch: vuurwerkramp in Enschede) was a catastrophic fireworks explosion occurring at the S.E. A fire led to an enormous explosion which killed 23 people including four firefighters, and injured nearly 1,000. However, after the explosion, residents from the affected district of Roombeek—a poor, working_class neighbourhood—complained of government inaction and lack of interest, saying the whole disaster was just waiting to happen. Fireworks disaster led to intensified safety regulations in the Netherlands concerning the storage and sale of fireworks." .

