lsd:Entity_3073 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1989 Malawi earthquake occurred on 10 March 1989 in central Malawi, with a moment magnitude of 6.3 and a maximum Mercalli intensity of VII (Very strong). A field study conducted in October 1989 concluded that the 10 March 1989 earthquake \"should be treated as an eye opener, drawing attention to the potential of medium_size earthquakes hitting major cities in Malawi\"." .

lsd:Entity_30759 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Algeciras Campaign (sometimes known as the Battle or Battles of Algeciras) was an attempt by a French naval squadron from Toulon under Contre_Admiral Charles Linois to join a French and Spanish fleet at Cadiz during June and 14 July 1801 during the French Revolutionary War prior to a planned operation against either Egypt or Portugal. Saumarez ordered that the most damaged of the surviving ships, Pompée and Caesar, be laid up in dock and their crews distributed among the remaining ships to ensure that they could be repaired as rapidly as possible, a situation made necessary in part due to the seizure of many of Gibraltar's shipwrights in the Bay of Gibraltar when they were sent to aid Hannibal in the last stages of the battle." .

