lsd:Entity_32092 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "\"On the Navy\" or \"On the Symmories\" (Ancient Greek: Περὶ τῶν Συμμοριῶν) is the first surviving political oration of the prominent Athenian statesman and orator Demosthenes. A reference to the speech made in Demosthenes' later On the Liberty of the Rhodians proves that the speech was actually delivered to the Ecclesia, not just composed but never spoken. On the Navy is a speech of general interest, which provided Demosthenes an opportunity to be an advocate for common sense." .

