lsd:Entity_32371 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Christmas in Denmark (), the Denmark Jule and Christmas, is celebrated throughout December starting either at the beginning of Advent or on December 1 with a variety of traditions. Christmas Eve, Juleaften, the main event of Christmas in Denmark, is celebrated on the evening of December 24, the evening before the two Christmas holidays, December 25 and 26th. Celebrating on the eve before Christmas is also used for most other holidays in Denmark. Christmas in Denmark is originally an ancient old Norse tradition related to the Germanic Yule celebration of North Europe, but was mixed with the overlapping Christian tradition of Christmas when Denmark was christened during the 11th century. In Denmark, there is a tradition to go to Church on the afternoon of Christmas Eve, on the 24th." .

