lsd:Entity_3270 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Trinidad and Tobago League Cup, or commonly known as the First Citizens Cup for sponsorship reasons, is the league cup style association football competition open for Trinidad and Tobago teams competing in the country's TT Pro League. Unlike the FA Trophy, where 36 teams enter each season from the top three tiers of the Trinidad and Tobago association football league system and the Secondary Schools Football League, only teams from the TT Pro League compete in the league cup. Although the league cup is one of the three major domestic trophies attainable by Trinidad and Tobago league teams, it is perceived as a lower priority than the league championship and the FA Trophy. The competition began in 2000, under the name of the league cup, with San Juan Jabloteh winning the inaugural tournament by defeating Defence Force 1–0 at Marvin Lee Stadium. The Eastern Lions exacted revenge by defeating Defence Force 3–0 on penalties after the match ended 1–1 the following year in 2010 to claim their first league cup title." .

lsd:Entity_32705 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Handel Festival (in German: Händel_Festspiele) in Halle (Saale), Saxony_Anhalt, is an international music festival concentrating on the music of George Frideric Handel in the composer's birthplace. The first Handel Festival in Halle was conducted in 1922, three years after the Handel Festival in Göttingen." .

