    rdfs:label "The 2014 Ypres Rally was the 50th running of the event and the sixth round of the 2014 European Rally Championship season." .

lsd:Entity_32723 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Brest, sometimes called the battle of the River Penfeld, was an action in 1342 between an English squadron of converted merchant ships and that of a mercenary galley force from Genoa fighting for the Franco_Breton faction of Charles of Blois during the War of the Breton Succession, a side conflict of the Hundred Years War. A fleet of fourteen Genoese galleys was brought to Northern France from Italy by their commander Grimaldi four years before and had participated in the Channel campaign of 1338 against Portsmouth and Southampton as well as the defeat at the battle of Sluys; as such they were among the few escapees from the French fleet at that action. This disruption of Bloisian fortunes was compounded by the arrival of Robert III of Artois a few days later with 800 men and by King Philip VI who ordered the withdrawal of substantial numbers of French troops from Brittany and transferred them to Calais, where an English invasion was expected (the troops reported massing in Southern England by French spies were in fact destined for Brest too but were held up by a lack of ships)." .

lsd:Entity_32742 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1905–06 FA Cup was the 35th staging of the world's oldest association football competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup (more usually known as the FA Cup). Everton F.C. won the competition for the first time, beating Newcastle United 1–0 in the 1906 FA Cup Final at Crystal Palace. The format of the FA Cup for the season had a preliminary round, four qualifying rounds, four proper rounds, and the semi_finals and 1906 FA Cup Final. Everton F.C. and Newcastle United won to meet in the 1906 FA Cup Final." .

lsd:Entity_32745 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Pyzdry, one of many skirmishes of the January Uprising, took place on April 29, 1863, near the town of Pyzdry, which at that time belonged to Russian_controlled Congress Poland. Pyzdry, a town in historic Greater Poland, was at that time located in western part of Congress Poland, near the border with Kingdom of Prussia’s Province of Posen. On April 17, 1863, Taczanowski captured Pyzdry, the westernmost town of the Russian Empire, and forced Russian border guards into his unit." .

lsd:Entity_32747 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1963 Kinross and Western Perthshire by_election of 1963 was a by_election to the House of Commons. On 23 October, Home executed an instrument of disclaimer under the Peerage Act 1963, becoming Sir Alec Douglas_Home." .

lsd:Entity_32750 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Dream Theater is an American progressive metal band formed in 1985 under the name Images and Tour by John Petrucci, John Myung and Mike Portnoy while they attended Berklee College of Music in Boston, Massachusetts. With the stability that Dominici's appointment brought to Images and Tour, they began to increase the number of shows played in the New York City area, gaining a considerable amount of exposure. Mechanic ended up breaking the majority of the financial promises they had made to Dream Theater prior to signing their contract, so the band was restricted to playing around New York City. A little more than a month after Portnoy's departure, Dream Theater began auditioning for a new drummer in New York City. On November 27, 2020, Dream Theater released their ninth live album, Distant Memories – Live in London, recorded at Hammersmith Apollo prior the COVID_19 pandemic. Despite the band being forced to change their name, Dream Theater adopted a custom logo (known as the Images and Tour symbol) and wordmark which has appeared on the vast majority of their promotional material and on the front cover of every Dream Theater studio album. In September 2010, a fan of Dream Theater discovered that all of the letters of \"DOMINICI\" fit together perfectly into the Images and Tour symbol. Dream Theater won The Spirit of Prog Award at the Classic Rock Roll of Honour 2009 in London." .

lsd:Entity_32799 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Crimean parliamentary election were held on 31 October 2010 as a part of the general 2010 Ukrainian local elections. Early July 2010, the Verkhovna Rada (Ukraine's national parliament) supported by the Party of Regions’ initiative, announced local elections on the last day of 31 October 2010." .

lsd:Entity_32801 a lsd:Context_narration ;
