    rdfs:label "The Frankfurter Wachensturm (German: charge of the Frankfurt guard house) on 03 April 1833 was a failed attempt to start a revolution in Germany." .

lsd:Entity_33071 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "School of Paris (French: École de Paris) refers to the French and émigré artists who worked in Paris in the first half of the 20th century. The School of Paris was not a single art movement or institution, but refers to the importance of Paris as a center of Western art in the early decades of the 20th century." .

lsd:Entity_33074 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kellogg's Grove is either of two minor battles, or skirmishes, fought during the Black Hawk War in U.S. state of Illinois, in present_day Stephenson County at and near Kellogg's Grove. The second battle is known for playing a role in Abraham Lincoln's short career in the Illinois militia. The battle was the last on Illinois soil during the Black Hawk War. In the days preceding the second Battle of Kellogg's Grove a raid occurred on Bureau Creek, between the Rock and Illinois Rivers. The Second Battle of Kellogg's Grove occurred on 25 June 1832, after Major John Dement and his men, while camped at Kellogg's Grove on Sunday June 24, learned of a large group of Native Americans nearby. The 25 June 1832 battle was the last of the Black Hawk War on Illinois soil. Abraham Lincoln's service during the Black Hawk War has been a source of discrepancies and questioning, with two major battle sites being affiliated with Lincoln in the aftermath of combat. The marble facade at the monument, erected in 1901, commemorating the battle in Stillman Valley, Illinois includes the reference to Lincoln's, \"The presence of soldier, statesman, martyr, Abraham Lincoln assisting in the burial of these honored dead has made this spot more sacred.\" The Battle of Kellogg's Grove, like many of the battles and skirmishes during the Black Hawk War, had no real order or strategy." .

lsd:Entity_33079 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Andorran local elections were held on 04 December 2011." .

lsd:Entity_33089 a lsd:Context_narration ;
