lsd:Entity_33842 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Northern Steeplechase is New Zealand's richest steeplechase. It is run over 6,400 metres (21,000 ft) at Ellerslie Racecourse in Auckland, making it Australasia's longest horse race, and usually takes between eight and eight and a half minutes to complete." .

