lsd:Entity_34669 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Flight 19 was the designation of a group of five General Motors Eastern Aircraft Division TBM Avenger torpedo bombers that disappeared over the Bermuda Triangle on 05 December 1945, after losing contact during a United States Navy overwater navigation training flight from Naval Air Station Fort Lauderdale, Florida. By 17:50 several land_based radio stations had triangulated Flight 19's position as being within a 100 nmi (120 mi; 190 km) radius of 29°N 79°W; Flight 19 was north of the Bahamas and well off the coast of central Florida, but nobody transmitted this information on an open, repetitive basis. Had Flight 19 actually been where Taylor believed it to be, the flight would have made landfall with the Florida coastline within 20 minutes, depending on how far down they were. In 1991 a treasure_hunting expedition led by Graham Hawkes announced that the wreckage of five Avengers had been discovered off the coast of Florida, but that tail numbers revealed they were not Flight 19." .

lsd:Entity_34672 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 European Le Mans Series was the fifteenth season of the Automobile Club de l'Ouest's (ACO) European Le Mans Series. The six_event season began at Circuit Paul Ricard on 15 April 2018 and finished at Algarve International Circuit on 28 October 2018." .

lsd:Entity_34676 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Exorcising a boy possessed by a demon, or a boy with a mute spirit, is one of the miracles miracles of Jesus reported in the synoptic Gospels, involving the healing of a demonically possessed boy through exorcism. Mark's account (Mark 9:17–29) describes how Jesus is surrounded by a crowd, one of whom asks for help for his son, who 'has a spirit that makes him unable to speak'." .

lsd:Entity_34681 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Campeonato da Primeira Divisão de Futebol Profissional da FGF, better known as the 2013 Campeonato Gaúcho, was the 93rd season of Rio Grande do Sul's top_flight football league. The season began on 19 January 2013 and ended on 05 May 2013. The best placed team not playing in Campeonato Brasileiro Série A (Grêmio, S.C. Internacional), B or C (Caxias) will be \"promoted\" to 2013 Campeonato Brasileiro Série D. The best three teams not qualified to 2014 Copa Libertadores will qualify for 2014 Copa do Brasil." .

lsd:Entity_3469 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 UEFA Super Cup was a association football match between German team Bayern Munich and English team Liverpool F.C. on 2001 at Stade Louis II, the annual UEFA Super Cup contested between the winners of the UEFA Champions League and UEFA Cup. Bayern won the 2000–01 UEFA Champions League, defeating Valencia 5–4 in a penalty shoot_out after the match had finished 1–1. Liverpool F.C. won the 2000–01 UEFA Cup, beating Deportivo Alavés 5–4. Liverpool F.C. scored immediately after the start of the second half to lead the match 3–0 after Michael Owen scored. Hasan Salihamidžić and Carsten Jancker scored in the second half, but Liverpool F.C. held out until the end of the match to win 3–2, their second Super Cup win. They had won the 2000–01 UEFA Champions League beating Valencia 5–4 in a penalty shoot_out after the match had finished 1–1. Liverpool F.C. had played two legs in the third qualifying round of the 2001–02 UEFA Champions League. As winners of the 2000–01 FA Cup, Liverpool F.C. faced Manchester United in the 2001 FA Charity Shield, which they won 2–1. Liverpool F.C. had also played one match in the 2001–02 FA Premier League; a 2–1 win over West Ham United. Hamann passed the ball to Heskey on the edge of the Bayern penalty area, Heskey subsequently moved past Bayern defender's Thomas Linke and Kovač, and shot low beyond Kahn to give Liverpool F.C. a 2–0 lead. No further goals were scored and the referee blew for full_time with the final score 3–2 to Liverpool F.C.." .

