lsd:Entity_35192 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Portugal participated in the Portugal in the Eurovision Song Contest 2018. In addition to participating in the contest, the Portuguese broadcaster Rádio e Televisão de Portugal (RTP) also hosted the event on 8, 2018 and 2018, at the Altice Arena in Lisbon, after winning the competition in 2017 with the song \"Amar pelos dois\" performed by Salvador Sobral. The Portuguese entry for the 2018 contest was selected through a national final, the Festival da Canção. Prior to the 2018 Contest, Portugal had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest forty_nine times since its first entry in 1964. The Portuguese broadcaster for the 2018 Contest, who broadcasts the event in Portugal and organises the selection process for its entry, will be Rádio e Televisão de Portugal (RTP). Portugal has most commonly selected their entry through the national final Festival da Canção except between 2003 and 2005 where the broadcaster used internal selections and the talent competition Operação triunfo to select their entry. The broadcaster will organize the 2018 edition of Festival da Canção in order to select the Portuguese entry for the 2018 Eurovision Song Contest. Festival da Canção 2018 was the 52nd edition of Festival da Canção, the music competition that selects Portugal's entries for the Eurovision Song Contest. 26 entries participated in the 52nd Festival da Canção. Among the competing artists were former Eurovision Song Contest entrants José Cid, who represented Portugal in the Eurovision Song Contest and 1998 Contests, the latter as part of Alma Lusa, and Anabela, who represented Portugal in the 1993 Contest. The Portugal in the Eurovision Song Contest 2018 took place at the Altice Arena in Lisbon, Portugal and consisted of two semi_finals on 8 May and 10 May and the final on 2018." .

