lsd:Entity_37435 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Free Fair) in Bremen, Germany, first held in 1035, is one of the oldest fairs in Germany. 1793 Franz II is the last German Emperor who grants the Bremen merchants the right for the Freimarkt _ as of this time, they decide themselves when they want to celebrate. from 1830 The Bremer Freimarkt develops into an attractive event far beyond the borders of Bremen. 1936 The Freimarkt, which had taken place at differing locations (Grünenkamp, Domshof, Hohenstorsplatz), gets a fixed location in the heart of Bremen: on the Bürgerweide. Media related to Freimarkt Bremen at Wikimedia Commons." .

