lsd:Entity_37597 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1994 Gator Bowl was an American college football bowl game between the Virginia Tech Hokies and the Tennessee Volunteers at Ben Hill Griffin Stadium in Gainesville, Florida, on 1994. The game was moved to Gainesville in 1994 due to renovations to the Gator Bowl for the Jacksonville Jaguars. Instead of beginning in early 1995, work would have to begin in 1994, leaving the site of the 1994 Gator Bowl (played on Dec. 30) in doubt. The Hokies entered the 1994 college football season having finished the 1993 season with a win in the 1993 Independence Bowl, and hopes were high that they would return to a bowl game again in 1994. The 1994 Gator Bowl kicked off on 1994, at 8 p.m. EST at Ben Hill Griffin Stadium in Gainesville, Florida." .

lsd:Entity_37662 a lsd:Context_narration ;
