lsd:Entity_37698 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Rimsha Masih blasphemy case (Urdu: رمشا مسیح  — some early reports used the first name \"Rifta\" or \"Riftah\") is a Pakistan girl from Islamabad, who was arrested by the Pakistan police on blasphemy charges on August 2012 when she was 14 years old. The alleged charges included desecrating pages of the Quran (or a book containing verses from the Quran) by burning—a crime punishable by death under Pakistan's blasphemy law. France \"urged the Pakistan authorities to release this young girl\" and has reaffirmed that \"the very existence of the crime of blasphemy infringes upon fundamental freedoms, namely the freedom of religion or belief, as well as the freedom of expression. On September 7, Rimsha Masih blasphemy case was released on bail, on a surety of 1,000,000 Pakistan rupees (US$10,570 on that date). Paul Bhatti, the Pakistan Minister for National Harmony, who had earlier stated his hopes that the case might help end the widespread abuse of the blasphemy laws, expressed \"joy and satisfaction\" at the development. Despite the fact that the case against her was thrown out, people in Pakistan accused of blasphemy are often subject to vigilante justice." .

lsd:Entity_37700 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "artistic swimming at the 2018 Asian Games at the 2018 Asian Games was held at the Gelora Bung Karno Sports Complex, Jakarta, Indonesia from 27 August to 2018." .

lsd:Entity_37706 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Independence Day in the Niger is commemorated on August 3, marking the nation's independence from France in 1960. Independence Day is celebrated in Niger with official festivals and appearances of political leaders, an official broadcast by the President as well as the tradition (since 1975) that every Nigerien plant a tree." .

lsd:Entity_37709 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 Talladega 500 was a NASCAR Winston Cup Series event on 31 July 1983, at Talladega Superspeedway in Talladega, Alabama. Talladega Superspeedway, originally known as Alabama International Motor Superspeedway (AIMS), is a motorsports complex located north of Talladega, Alabama." .

lsd:Entity_37713 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kandy Esala Perahera (the Esala Perahera procession of Kandy) also known as The Festival of the Tooth is a festival held in July and August in Kandy, Sri Lanka. The festival ends with the traditional diya_kepeema ritual, a water cutting ceremony which is held at the Mahaweli River at Getambe, Kandy. It was also through the efforts of Upali Thera that the Kandy Esala Perahera came into being. The Kandy Esala Perahera begins with the Kap Situveema or Kappa, in which a sanctified young Jackfruit tree (Artocarpus integrifolia) is cut and planted in the premises of each of the four Devales dedicated to the four guardian gods Natha, Vishnu, Katharagama and the goddess Pattini. 2018 Kandy Esala Maha Perahera (Randoli Perahera) was held on August, the full moon poya day with the participation of hundreds thousands people. The following are some of the notable tusker elephants who participated as the main casket bearer of the Kandy Esala perehera festival." .

