lsd:Entity_39536 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Etruscan religion comprises a set of stories, beliefs, and religious practices of the Etruschi, originating in the 7th century BC from the preceding Iron Age Villanovan culture, heavily influenced by the mythology of ancient Greece and Phoenicia, and sharing similarities with concurrent Roman mythology and religion. As the Etruschi was assimilated into the Roman Republic in the 4th century BC, the Etruscan religion and mythology were partially incorporated into ancient Roman culture, following the Roman tendency to absorb some of the local gods and customs of conquered lands." .

