lsd:Entity_42892 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Boston Fashion Week is a week_long luxury clothing event that takes place annually in Boston, United States. The Boston Fashion Week was founded by Jay Calderin in 1995. Unlike other global fashion events such as the New York fashion week, Boston Fashion Week is a non_profit event with a low budget, that focuses on showcasing mainly local designers. Calderin founded Boston Fashion Week, and has served as the organization's Executive Director since 1995. Since the creation of Boston Fashion Week in 1995, the Tent only happened twice, in 2011 and 2012, although it was very well received by the general public." .

