lsd:Entity_43134 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 UEFA Cup Final was an association football match played on 2002, between Feyenoord of the Netherlands and Borussia Dortmund of Germany. It was the 31st UEFA Cup Final and was held in the De Kuip in Rotterdam, which is the home ground of Feyenoord. Both Feyenoord and Borussia Dortmund started off their European campaigns in the 2001–02 Champions League and entered the 2001–02 UEFA Cup in the third round, after finishing third in their respective Champions League groups. A huge party erupted both inside and outside De Kuip not only because of the title, but also because the final was held two days after Rotterdam's politician Pim Fortuyn was murdered." .

