    rdfs:label "Hurricane Kenna was the fourth_most intense tropical cyclone on record in the Eastern Pacific basin, and at the time the third_most intense Northeast Pacific tropical cyclone to strike the west coast of Mexico. A Reconnaissance Aircraft flight into the hurricane while it was near peak intensity recorded a pressure of 913 mbar (hPa), the fourth lowest recorded pressure for a Northeast Pacific tropical cyclone. Hurricane Kenna was at the time, the third most intense Northeast Pacific tropical cyclone to strike Mexico." .

