lsd:Entity_43194 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting 2011, commonly known as CHOGM 2011, was the twenty_second Meeting of the Heads of Government of the Commonwealth of Nations. Held in Perth, Western Australia, between 2011 and 2011 and hosted by the Prime Minister Julia Gillard. The summit failed to reach an agreement to endorse or even publish the Eminent Persons Group report; the United Kingdom, Australia and Canada urged the publication of the report but were opposed by India, Nigeria, Sri Lanka, South Africa and Namibia. Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh skipped the summit in protest against Australia's refusal to sell India uranium as it had not signed the Nuclear Nonproliferation Treaty. Australia later denied that Singh's pull out from the summit was over its refusal to sell uranium." .

