lsd:Entity_43923 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Summer Deaflympics, officially known as the 21st Summer Deaflympics, is an international multi_sport event that was celebrated from September 5 to 2009 in Taipei, Taiwan (Republic of China). The Chinese Taipei Sport Association for the Deaf expressed its intention to bid for the 2009 Summer Deaflympics following its participation at the 2001 Summer Deaflympics in Rome. Taipei was chosen to host the 21st Summer Deaflympics in a vote held at the 38th ICSD session, finishing ahead of Athens, Greece. The main stadium Taipei Stadium was completed on 2009, and was certified as a Class 1 Athletics Facility by the IAAF. The Organising Committee has designated 2009 as the \"Taipei Deaflympics Arts Month\", during which famous artists and art groups are invited to perform at the Taipei Arena, such as A_mei, Blue Man Group, Dynamic Yunnan, and Minghuayuan. The various sports offered at the 2009 Summer Deaflympics were held in 20 disciplines, including 15 individual sports and 5 team sports: The Games were held in 22 venues, most of which located in Taipei and Taipei County (now New Taipei). *   Host nation (Chinese Taipei) In the following calendar for the 2009 Summer Deaflympics, each blue box represents an event competition." .

