lsd:Entity_44211 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Relations between the European Union (EU) and the People's Republic of China (PRC) or China–European Union relations are bilateral relations that were established in 1975 between the PRC and the European Community. In March 2019, the European Union has referred to People's Republic of China as a \"systemic rival\". Relations between the European Union and People's Republic of China have experienced a cool down after People's Republic of China canceled the EU_People's Republic of China yearly summit in November 2008. The European Union representing its 28 Member States and People's Republic of China are both members of the World Trade Organisation (WTO) and participate in the ongoing discussions about the Trade in Services Agreement (TiSA). The SSTL project was launched in 2006 as a pilot project between the European Union and People's Republic of China as the first Asian country." .

