lsd:Entity_44384 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Little Blue River was fought on 21 October 1864, as part of Price's Raid during the American Civil War. At the start of the American Civil War in 1861, the state of Missouri was a slave state, but did not secede. The Confederates struck at about 07:00 on the morning of 21 October 1864, with the advance led by Company D of the 5th Missouri Cavalry Regiment." .

