lsd:Entity_44624 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Vilna offensive was a campaign of the Polish–Soviet War of 1919–1921. Vilnius, the historical capital of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, became part of the Lithuanian Soviet Socialist Republic and was soon proclaimed capital of the Lithuanian–Belorussian Soviet Socialist Republic (Lit_Bel) on February 27, 1919. In 1920, the Soviets recaptured Vilnius, followed by the Poles' establishment of the short_lived Republic of Central Lithuania. The Polish capture of Vilnius set the stage for further escalation of Polish conflicts with Soviet Russia and Lithuania." .

