lsd:Entity_44677 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Day's Gap, fought on April 30, 1863, was the first in a series of American Civil War skirmishes in Cullman County, Alabama, that lasted until May 2, known as Streight's Raid. These regiments participated in Streight's raid: The Civil War Trust, a division of the American Battlefield Trust, and its partners have saved 40 acres of the battlefield at Hog Mountain, an associated battle that occurred on the same day as the Battle of Day's Gap." .

