    rdfs:label "The Baku_Rostov highway bombing was an incident which occurred near the village of Shaami_Yurt in Chechen Republic, on 29 October 1999. The Government in their submission of 28 March 2003 explained that on 29 October 1999 the roadblock “Kavkaz_1” on the administrative border between Chechen Republic and Ingushetia had been closed, because it could not cope with the substantial number of refugees wishing to cross (see § 26 above)." .

lsd:Entity_44834 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle off Barbados was fought in 07 March 1778 during the American Revolutionary War. While escorting a fleet of United States of America ships in the West Indies, the frigate USS Randolph was attacked by the Great Britain ship_of_the_line HMS Yarmouth. However, after sailing out to meet the Great Britain off Charleston on February 14, the enemy was nowhere in sight, so the United States of America fleet headed for the West Indies where Biddle would raid commerce. Three days after that, at about 5:30 pm, on 07 March 1778, the Americans were sailing off the eastern coast of Barbados when lookouts spotted a large ship to the windward." .

