lsd:Entity_45031 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Iceland participated in the Iceland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017 with the song \"Paper\" written by Svala Björgvinsdóttir, Einar Egilsson, Lester Mendez and Lily Elise. Iceland was drawn to compete in the first semi_final of the Eurovision Song Contest which took place on 2017. Prior to the 2017 Contest, Iceland had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest thirty times since its first entry in 1986. In Iceland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016, Iceland failed to qualify to the final with the song \"Hear Them Calling\" performed by Greta Salóme. RÚV confirmed their intentions to participate at the 2017 Eurovision Song Contest on 22 August Iceland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016. Since 2006, Iceland has used a national final to select their entry for the Eurovision Song Contest, a method that has once again return for the selection of their 2017 participation. Söngvakeppnin 2017 was the twelfth edition of Söngvakeppnin, the music competition that selects Iceland's entries for the Eurovision Song Contest. The final took place on 2017 where the six entries that qualified from the preceding two semi_finals and an eliminated act who got a wildcard competed to become Iceland's Eurovision entry. Iceland was placed into the first semi_final, to be held on 2017, and was scheduled to perform in the second half of the show." .

