lsd:Entity_46911 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 European Dressage Championship was held between August 17 and 2011 in Rotterdam, Netherlands. At the 2008 International Federation for Equestrian Sports_General Assembly in Buenos Aires, the Netherlands was chosen as the country to host the 2011 European Dressage Championship. It was the second time in European Dressage Championship history _ after 1999 in Arnhem _ that the Netherlands was chosen to hold this sports event. Three days after the end of the European Dressage Championship the 2011 CHIO Rotterdam was held _ this year without dressage. As in years 1991, 1993, 2007 and 2009, in 2011 nine medals are awarded at the European Dressage Championship (three for the team competition, three in Grand Prix Spécial (individual) and also three in the Grand Prix Freestyle (individual). Great Britain, who was not credited with the 1963 Championships because of an International Federation for Equestrian Sports rule (see: European Dressage Championship), was in the lead after the end of the first day." .

lsd:Entity_46921 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Kenya–Russia relations (Swahili: Uhusiano wa Kenya_Urusi) (Russian: Российско_кенийские отношения) are bilateral relations between Kenya and Russia. Russia had established diplomatic relations with Kenya on December 14, 1963, and has since maintained good relations with the African Great Lakes country. Kenya and Russia agreed to form a business council which would oversee joint trade and investment programmes. Kenya exported goods worth Kes.12.85 billion (US$124 million) and Russia exported goods worth Kes.22.37 billion (US$216 million) to Kenya in 2018, according to the Russian Export Centre. The main goods Russia exports to Kenya are cereals, iron and steel, fertilizers and paper. In addition, Russia annually grants Kenya 30 scholarships from the federal budget. Additionally, Kenya is represented in Russia through its embassy in Moscow." .

