    rdfs:label "The 1958 South Carolina gubernatorial election was held on 1958 to select the Governor of South Carolina of the state of South Carolina. Ernest Hollings won the Democratic primary against rival Donald S. Russell and ran unopposed in the general election becoming the 106th Governor of South Carolina. The South Carolina Democratic Party held their primary for Governor of South Carolina in the summer of 1958 and it became a heated contest between Lieutenant Governor Ernest Hollings and the former president of the University of South Carolina, Donald S. Russell. The general election was held on 1958 and Ernest Hollings was elected the next Governor of South Carolina without opposition." .

