lsd:Entity_48112 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic–South Africa relations are the current and historical relations between the Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic (SADR) in Western Sahara and the South Africa. The relations between Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic (SADR) and South Africa, date back to the close bonds that were forged by the national liberation movements of both countries, namely the African National Congress (ANC) of South Africa and the Polisario Front of Western Sahara shortly after the formation of the Polisario Front in 1973. Shortly after the inauguration of the first South Africa post_apartheid government in 1994, the former South Africa President Nelson Mandela, announced a decision by the South Africa government of its intention to recognise and establish diplomatic relations with the Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic consistent with the earlier decisions of the OAU which South Africa formally joined in 1994." .

