lsd:Entity_4865 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2020 UEFA European Under_19 Championship (also known as Union of European Football Associations Under_19 Euro 2020) was scheduled to be the 19th edition of the UEFA European Under_19 Football Championship (69th edition if the Under_18 and Junior eras are included), the annual international youth association football championship organised by Union of European Football Associations for the men's under_19 national teams of Europe. Due to the COVID_19 pandemic, the tournament was initially postponed, rescheduled and was cancelled in 2020. Northern Ireland, which last hosted the tournament in 2005, was selected as host by Union of European Football Associations on 9 December 2016. The final tournament was originally scheduled to be played between 19 – 2020. Due to the COVID_19 pandemic, Union of European Football Associations announced on 2020 that the tournament had been postponed until further notice. On 2020, Union of European Football Associations announced that the final tournament had been rescheduled and would be played in two periods, with the group stage played between 2020–2020, and the knockout stage, which would consist of the semi_finals, the FIFA U_20 World Cup play_off and the final, pl11 November 2020ed be14 November 2020November 2020. Union of European Football Associations then announced on 2020 that after consultation with the 55 member associations, the final tournament had been further postponed, with the group stage played in 2020 and the knockout stage played in March 2021. On 2020, Union of European Football Associations announced that the tournament would be played in March 2021 in straight knock_out format, consisting of the quarter_finals, semi_finals, final, and play_off matches to decide the fifth team to qualify for the FIFA U_20 World Cup. Finally, the tournament was cancelled by Union of European Football Associations on 2020." .

lsd:Entity_48650 a lsd:Context_narration ;
