lsd:Entity_49374 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Elite 9 Hockey League (E9HL) is a youth ice hockey sports league composed of nine clubs: six charter members and three Boston Hockey League qualifiers. Headquartered in New England, the E9 is widely considered to be the premier youth ice hockey sports league in the region. The sports league was organized on 2014, in New England, after the suspension of operations of its predecessor organization, the New England Hockey League (NEHL), which had been founded in 2009. The sports league draws many highly skilled players from all over New England. The Elite 9 Hockey League originated in 2014 with four Massachusetts teams and two New Hampshire teams." .

