lsd:Entity_49484 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kiev (1918) of 1918 (Ukrainian: штурм Києва в січні 1918 року, romanized: shturm Kyieva v sichni 1918 roku, lit. 'the assault of Kyiv in 1918') was a Bolshevik military operation of Petrograd and Moscow Red Guard formations directed to capture the capital of Ukraine. The storming of Kiev (Kyiv) took place during the ongoing peace negotiations at Brest_Litovsk on 05 February 1918–8, 1918 (January 23–26, old style). On 1918 the government of Ukraine announced Kiev under a siege and appointed Mykhailo Kovenko as the military commandant of the city's defence. The Kiev garrison was greatly demoralized by Bolshevik propaganda and Soviet advances across the territory of Ukraine." .

lsd:Entity_49487 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "VELD Music Festival (commonly referred to as VELD) is an annual electronic dance music and hip_hop music festival held at Downsview Park in Toronto, Ontario. Due to the COVID_19 pandemic, the 2020 Veld Music Festival event scheduled for August 1 and 2, 2020 in Downsview Park in Toronto has been cancelled. In April 2012, a two_day electronic dance music (EDM) festival to be held at Downsview Park in the Toronto area on August 4–5 was announced. VELD 2019 ran from August 3rd to August 4th 2019 in Downsview Park, Toronto, Ontario. The overall praise of the festival was overwhelming with people demanding the festival to run 3 days for the year 2020 and to not longer invite performers who abuse the timings of the show such as Cardi B. VELD Music festival was expected to take place August 1–2, 2020, in Downsview Park, Toronto, ON. The 2021 edition of the VELD Music Festival is currently scheduled to take place on July 31 _ August 1 2021, at Toronto's Downsview Park." .

