lsd:Entity_50131 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1912–13 FA Cup was the 42nd season of the world's oldest association football competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup (more usually known as the FA Cup). Aston Villa F.C. won the competition for the fifth time, beating Sunderland 1–0 in the 1913 FA Cup Final at Crystal Palace, London. The format of the FA Cup for the season had two preliminary rounds, five qualifying rounds, four proper rounds, and the semi finals and 1913 FA Cup Final. The Burnley–Sunderland match went to a replay, which Sunderland won, going on to meet Aston Villa F.C. in the 1913 FA Cup Final. Wallace had earlier missed a penalty, something that would not occur again in FA Cup Final, until the 1988 1913 FA Cup Final between Wimbledon and Liverpool." .

