lsd:Entity_51082 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "America's Newsroom is an American television hard news program on Fox News currently hosted by Sandra Smith and a rotating co_anchor (most often, Trace Gallagher in Los Angeles) live from 9 a.m. _ noon on Monday through Friday. The show has been a part of the Fox News program lineup since 12 February 2007, and is the number one cable news broadcast in its time slot. On March 23, 2009, America's Newsroom began broadcasting in high definition and moved to Studio J, the Election Night 2008 set used by the Fox News. America's Newsroom is broadcast from Studio J at 1211 Avenue of the Americas (also known as the News Corp. Building), New York City." .

