    rdfs:label "Throughout the early Middle Ages, the Rurik dynasty knyazes of the Kievan Rus' used unique Symbols of the Rurikids to denote property rights over various items. In contrast to Western European heraldry, where coats of arms belonged to entire families, or were inherited without changes by firstborn sons, Rurik dynasty Symbols of the Rurikids were personal, with every knyaz devising an emblem of their own for themselves." .

