lsd:Entity_54664 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "net.art refers to a group of artists who have worked in the medium of Internet art since 1994. The term \"net.art\" is also used as a synonym for net art or Internet art and covers a much wider range of artistic practices. The net.art movement arose in the context of the wider development of Internet art. As such, net.art is more of a movement and a critical and political landmark in Internet art history, than a specific genre. Online social networks experiments, such as the Poietic Generator, which existed before the net.art movement, was involved in it, and still exist after it, may show that the fashion scheme of net.art may have forgetten some deep theoretical questions." .

