lsd:Entity_5621 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 Grand National (known as the Martell Grand National for sponsorship reasons) was the 151st official renewal of the world_famous Grand National steeplechase that took place at Aintree Racecourse near Liverpool, England, on 1998. The main race was seen by the smallest Grand National attendance at Aintree Racecourse since 1985, with a crowd of just 46,679, over 11,000 less than two years prior. His preparation for the National had included four victories, including the Peter Cazelet/Anthony Mildmay memorial chase at Sandown in January before finishing third in the Singer & Friedlander Grand National trial at Uttoxeter and second ahead of Earth Summit, who finished fifth in the Red Square Vodka Gold Cup at Haydock in February. Samlee was a nine_year_old who came to prominence after winning the Becher Chase over one circuit of the Aintree Racecourse Grand National course in November, having been second in the Scottish Grand National earlier in the year." .

