lsd:Entity_56725 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Formula E, officially the FIA Formula E Championship, is a single_seater motorsport championship that uses only electric cars. In 2011 it was conceived in Paris by Jean Todt at the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile, and the inaugural championship commenced in Beijing in 2014. The proposal for a city_based, single_seater electric car motor racing championship was conceived by Jean Todt, the president of the world governing body of motorsport, the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile (Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile), and presented to politicians Alejandro Agag and Antonio Tajani and the Italian actor Teo Teocoli at a dinner at a small Italian restaurant in the French capital Paris on 3 March 2011. Since 2014, the BMW i8 plug_in hybrid is employed as the Formula E safety car. The first Formula E race at the Beijing Olympic Green Circuit on 2014 was won by Lucas Di Grassi, after Nick Heidfeld and Nicolas Prost crashed out on the final corner. The 2016–17 Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile Formula E season was the third season of the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile Formula E championship. The 2017–18 Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile Formula E season was the fourth season of the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile Formula E championship. The 2019 Hong Kong ePrix was the 50th race of Formula E since its inception in 2014. Starting with the 2020–21 season, the Formula E Championship will be granted Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile World Championship status, due to it having met the criteria of having four manufacturer competitors and races on three continents since the 2015–16 season." .

lsd:Entity_56736 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Treaty of Pilar (in Spanish, Tratado del Pilar) was a pact signed among the rulers of the Argentine provinces of Santa Fe, Entre Ríos and Buenos Aires, which is recognized as the foundation of the federal organization of the country. The Treaty of Pilar was soon followed by the Treaty of Benegas, for the mutual defense of Santa Fe and Buenos Aires against the expansionist Entre Ríos and, two years later, by the Quadrilateral Treaty (including Pilar's signatories, plus Corrientes Province)." .

lsd:Entity_5674 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2007 Shinwar shooting, was the killing of a number of Afghan people on 04 March 2007, in the village of Spinpul, in the Shinwar of the Nangarhar Province of Afghanistan. United States Marines, fleeing the scene of a car bomb attack and ambush by Afghan militants, fired on people and vehicles surrounding them, according to initial reports killing as many as 19 civilians and injuring around 50 more." .

