lsd:Entity_57335 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Supercheap Auto Bathurst 1000 was an Australian touring car motor race for V8 Supercars, the twenty_first race of the 2012 International V8 Supercars Championship. It was held on Sunday, 2012 at the Mount Panorama Circuit on the outskirts of Bathurst, New South Wales, in Australia. The 2012 race was the sixteenth running of the Bathurst 1000 race, which was first held after the organisational split between the Australian Racing Drivers Club and V8 Supercars Australia that saw the Bathurst race run twice in 1997 and 1998, with one race open to V8 Supercar entries, and the other open to Super Touring cars. Waters, who won the 2011 Supercheap Auto Bathurst 1000 competition, was a late entry to the grid; the car was originally scheduled to be driven by Dixon, the 2012 winner, and Australian television personality Grant Denyer." .

