lsd:Entity_57527 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "If You Want Blood Tour You've Got It (written as just If You Want Blood Tour) is the first live album by Australian hard rock band AC/DC, and their only live album with Bon Scott as lead vocalist. If You Want Blood Tour reversed this tradition... it boasted a blunt ten tracks and, allowing nothing extraneous, got straight to the point, that being raging AC/DC rock and roll.\" Greg Prato of AllMusic notes, \"While most other rock bands of the era were busy experimenting with disco or creating studio_perfected epics, AC/DC was one of the few specializing in raw and bluesy hard rock, as evidenced by 1978's live set, If You Want Blood Tour You've Got It.\"" .

