lsd:Entity_62269 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Prosperous is the name given to a military engagement between the forces of the British Crown and the United Irishmen during the Irish Rebellion of 1798. Prosperous, a recently founded (1780) cotton_manufacturing village, was attacked shortly after the outbreak of the Irish Rebellion of 1798 at 2 a.m on 24 May 1798 by a rebel force about 20 strong under Dr. John Esmonde which targeted the British garrison consisting of Cork militia and a detachment of a Welsh regiment, the \"Ancient Britons\"." .

