lsd:Entity_6538 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1966 Australian Championships was a tennis tournament that took place on outdoor Grass courts at the White City Tennis Club, Sydney, Australia from 21 to 31 January 1966. It was the 54th edition of the Australian Championships (now known as the Australian Open), the 15th held in Sydney, and the first Grand Slam tournament of the year." .

lsd:Entity_6575 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 G_20 Toronto summit was the fourth meeting of the G20 heads of state/government, to discuss the global financial system and the world economy, which took place at the Metro Toronto Convention Centre in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, during 26 June 2010–27, 2010. Canada's largest banks, which are headquartered in Downtown Toronto, made plans to have employees work at alternate sites outside their downtown facilities, such as at home or in other branches. Nav Canada announced that it would place restrictions on the airspace in Toronto, making it limited to commercial flights only while all others would be restricted within a 30_nautical_mile (56 km) radius. However, the Canadian Parliamentary Budget Officer, Kevin Page, stated in his official report on the costs of the Huntsville and Toronto gatherings that other countries had not been as open about the full price for the similar meetings held there and that the $18 million figure for the 2009 G_20 Pittsburgh summit summit was merely for overtime pay for local police and the cost of law enforcement brought from other regions. It's Canada's turn, and it's necessary that we either don't take our turn or pay the appropriate price to have the security that is necessary so that everyone is safe here in Toronto.\" The Times of India and The Hindu commented on impacts on city life in Toronto due to the G20 summit and the \"unprecedented\" security measures taken in Canada." .

lsd:Entity_658 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Temalaca was a battle of the Mexican War of Independence that occurred on 05 November 1815 in the area around Temalaca, Puebla. At the end of the battle, Morelos was captured by Spanish forces under whose control he was soon after executed ending the second phase of the Mexican War of Independence." .

