lsd:Entity_8042 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "MLS Cup '97 was the second edition of the MLS Cup, the post_season championship match of Major League Soccer (MLS) in the United States. It was played on 1997, between D.C. United and the Colorado Rapids to determine the champion of the 1997 season. During a rainstorm that mirrored the previous final, D.C. repeated as MLS Cup champions by winning 2–1. Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium in Washington, D.C., the home of defending champions D.C. United, was selected as the host of the second MLS Cup on December 17, 1996. The MLS Cup is the post_season championship of Major League Soccer (MLS), a professional club association football league based in the United States that began play in 1996. The winners of the Conference Finals advanced to the single_match MLS Cup final, which would be held at a predetermined neutral venue. MLS Cup '97 was contested by defending champions and hosts D.C. United, who finished first in the regular season standings, and the Colorado Rapids, who finished fourth in the Western Conference. The MLS Cup final kicked off at 3:30 p.m. with an announced sellout crowd of 57,431 spectators at Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium, setting a new attendance record for a single playoff match. Three days after the MLS Cup final, D.C. United played the Dallas Burn in the U.S. Open Cup Final with a chance to earn the league's first \"treble\"." .

lsd:Entity_8078 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Al_Mina'a SC season will be Al_Mina'a SC 39th season in the Iraqi Premier League, having featured in all 41 editions of the competition except two." .

lsd:Entity_8085 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Ofira Air Battle was one of the first air battles of the Yom Kippur War. On 06 October 1973, Egypt launched a massive surprise attack on Israel that included over 200 Egyptian aircraft participating in an opening airstrike." .

lsd:Entity_8126 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Havana Jam was a three_day music festival that took place at the Karl Marx Theatre, in Havana, Cuba, on 2 March 1979–4 March 1979. With a real crisis in the music industry in the United States and the start of the salsa boom, in April 1978, CBS Records director, Bruce Lundvall, saw an open door to probe Cuban music and together with a group of the company's music enthusiasts made a four_day trip to Havana, where they were overwhelmed by the sound of Cuban music, but especially by Afro_Cuban jazz band Irakere, one of Cuba's most highly regarded and virtuoso musical acts." .

lsd:Entity_8134 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The tournament was contested in Nabeul city in Tunisia from 2017–15 October 2017. Unlike in the 2015 WMF World Cup, 24 teams from 5 continents are qualified for the final tournament: On 2017, the Executive bureau of the World Minifootball Federation had unanimously decided in Brno, Czech Republic that the 2017 World Cup will be organized from October 6 to 2017. On 2017, The final draw for 2017 WMF World Cup was made in Tunis." .

lsd:Entity_8143 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Capital Pride is an annual pride parade held in early June each year in Washington, D.C. It was founded as Gay Pride Day, a one_day block party and street festival, in 1975. The festival was the fourth_largest gay pride event in the United States of America in 2007. Capital Pride attracted more than 200,000 people in 2006, making it the fourth_largest gay pride event in the United States of America. On June 7, 2014, a United States of America Armed Forces color guard led the way and retired the colors in the Capital Pride parade. It was the first time in American history that an officially sanctioned United States of America Armed Forces color guard marched in a gay pride parade." .

