lsd:Entity_8763 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Kilkim Žaibu (from Lithuanian \"arise/soar with the lightning\") is an extreme metal festival in the Baltic region, Europe held annually since 1999. From 2010, the festival takes place at Lūkstas lake in the town of Varniai, Lithuania. Before that, it had been happening at \"Plūgo broliai\" in Joniškis, Lithuania. The festival took place in Varniai, Lithuania on 28 June 2018 _ 30 June 2018. The festival took place in Varniai, Lithuania on 29 June 2017 _ 1 July 2017. The festival took place in Varniai, Lit23 June 2016a25 2016 2016. The line_up: The festival in 20111 June 2010y12 June 2010me took place at lake Lukstas 11 June 12 June, Lithuania on 11–2010.12 June 2009h13 June 2009e festival took place at \"Plūgo Bro12 Junea13 Juneiškis, Lithuania on 12–2009. The line_up: The festival took place at \"Plūgo Broliai\", Joniškis, Lithuania on 7 June 2008." .

lsd:Entity_8773 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The White Lotus (traditional Chinese: 白蓮敎; simplified Chinese: 白莲敎; pinyin: Báiliánjiào; Wade–Giles: Pai_lien chiao) was a religious and political movement that appealed to many Han Chinese who found solace in worship of Wusheng Laomu (\"Unborn Venerable Mother\" (traditional Chinese: 無生老母; simplified Chinese: 无生老母)), who was foretold to gather all her children at the millennium into one family. This fear of secret societies carried on in the law; the Great Qing Legal Code, which was in effect until 1912, contained the following section: ll societies calling themselves at random White Lotus, communities of the Buddha Maitreya, or the Mingtsung religion (Manichaeans), or the school of the White Cloud, etc., together with all who carry out deviant and heretical practices, or who in secret places have prints and images, gather the people by burning incense, meeting at night and dispersing by day, thus stirring up and misleading people under the pretext of cultivating virtue, shall be sentenced. He took the title Hongwu Emperor and founded the Ming dynasty, whose name echoes the religious sentiment of the White Lotus. While traditional historiography has linked many Maitreyist and millenarian uprisings during the Ming and Qing dynasty as all related to the White Lotus, there are reasons to doubt that such connections existed." .

lsd:Entity_8808 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Gamaya is the fourth engineering educational institution established in Kerala, India. In addition to this, a 10% seats are provided for admission to the third semester classes for diploma holders (Lateral entry system) The alumni association has chapters in cities in India including Mumbai, Pune, Bangalore, Chennai, Kozhikode, Palakkad and Kochi." .

