lsd:Entity_8832 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Primera División de Fútbol Profesional – Apertura 1998 season (officially \"Copa Pilsener Apertura 1999\") started on 1998, and finished on 1998. The season saw Alianza Fútbol Club win its 7th league title after a 1_0 victory over C.D." .

lsd:Entity_8836 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of the Ruhr of 1943 was a 5_month British strategic bombing during World War II during the Second World War against the Ruhr in Nazi Germany, which had coke plants, steelworks, and 10 synthetic oil plants. Although not strictly part of the Ruhr area, the battle of the Ruhr included other cities such as Cologne which were within the Rhine_Ruhr region and considered part of the same \"industrial complex\". Even after this switch of focus to Hamburg, there would be further raids on the Ruhr area by the RAF—in part to keep German defences dispersed, just as there had been raids on areas other than the Ruhr during the battle. During the battle of the Ruhr, Bomber Command estimated about 70% of their aircraft losses were due to fighters." .

lsd:Entity_8839 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 592, adopted on 08 December 1986, having considered a letter from the representative of Zimbabwe in his capacity as Chairman of the Movement of Non_Aligned Countries, the Council reaffirmed the Geneva Conventions and condemned the opening of fire at a student demonstration by the Israel Defense Forces, in which two students were killed at Birzeit University." .

lsd:Entity_884 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Commando (Air Ministry serial number AL504) was a very long range Consolidated Liberator II aircraft adapted for passenger transport, to serve as the personal aircraft of Prime Minister Winston Churchill. On delivery Commando had a regular Liberator nose and tail configuration despite the internal modifications but was later converted to have a covered nose and also the same single tail fin used on the Consolidated PB4Y_2. After the second extended trip, Churchill never again flew in Commando, instead switching to Ascalon, an Avro York (a transport aircraft based on the Lancaster bomber, with a larger fuselage) with an all_British crew. Commando had served as Churchill's official aircraft during a critical period and later in the war was also used on occasion by other VIP's for their business in connection with the war effort. Commando was the second of 139 VLR (Very Long Range) Liberator II aircraft delivered to the RAF mostly to be used by RAF Coastal Command on maritime patrol duty and anti_submarine warfare, escorting the supply convoys of merchant vessels and attacking and sinking German U_boats. Winston Churchill's former personal transport Commando was assigned as the VIP aircraft. When Commando failed to arrive at Lagens Field emergency calls were made by radio and air_sea searches initiated once the aircraft was classified as overdue. Close to the flight path which Commando would have been following over the ocean in towards Lagens Field aircrew of the searching RAF Coastal Command aircraft spotted some yellow dinghies, a small amount of wreckage and an oil patch on the surface." .

lsd:Entity_8848 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The archery at the 1908 Summer Olympics – men's double York round was one of three archery events on the archery at the 1908 Summer Olympics programme." .

