lsd:Entity_11695 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Lahij insurgency was a guerrilla war waged by tribesmen loyal to Abdrabbuh Mansur Hadi against the Houthis and Yemen Army units loyal to Ali Abdullah Saleh, who controlled most of the Lahij Governorate of Yemen. On 04 August 2015, Pro_Hadi forces had retaken full control of the Lahij Governorate." .

