lsd:Entity_13109 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 WGC_Bridgestone Invitational was a professional golf tournament held July 31 – August 3 on the South Course of Firestone Country Club in Akron. It was the 16th WGC Invitational tournament, and the third of the World Golf Championships events in 2014." .

lsd:Entity_13122 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Siege of Al_Karak was a 17_day siege imposed by Ibrahim Pasha of Egypt on the Transjordanian town of Al Karak in 1834. The Pasha laid the siege on the town in pursuit of Qasim al_Ahmad, the leader of the 1834 Arab revolt in Palestine, who had fled from Nablus to take shelter in Al Karak. Afterward, Ibrahim Pasha's troops pursued and captured Qasim in Al Karak, which was under siege for 17 days. Ibrahim Pasha's troops pursued them and laid siege on Al Karak for 17 days." .

lsd:Entity_13132 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Nemesis is a hypothetical red dwarf or brown dwarf, originally postulated in 1984 to be orbiting the Sol at a distance of about 95,000 AU (1.5 light_years), somewhat beyond the Oort cloud, to explain a perceived cycle of mass extinctions in the geological record, which seem to occur more often at intervals of 26 million years. In a 2017 paper, Sarah Sadavoy and Steven Stahler argued that the Sol was likely part of a binary system at the time of its formation, leading them to suggest \"there probably was a Nemesis, a long time ago\". Such a star would have separated from this binary system over four billion years ago, meaning it could not be responsible for the more recent perceived cycle of mass extinctions, Douglas Vakoch told Business Insider, adding that \"If the sun really was part of a binary star system in its early days, its early twin deserves a benign name like Companion, rather than the threatening Nemesis.\" In 2011, Coryn Bailer_Jones analyzed craters on the surface of the Earth and reached the conclusion that the earlier findings of simple periodic patterns (implying periodic comet showers dislodged by a hypothetical Nemesis star) were statistical artifacts, and found that the crater record shows no evidence for Nemesis. Using newer and more powerful infrared telescope technology which is able to detect brown dwarfs as cool as 150 kelvins out to a distance of 10 light_years from the Sol, the Wide_field Infrared Survey Explorer (WISE survey) has not detected Nemesis. This hypothesis proposes that the Sol may have an undetected companion star in a highly elliptical orbit that periodically disturbs comets in the Oort cloud, causing a large increase of the number of comets visiting the inner Solar System with a consequential increase of impact events on Earth. If a red dwarf, it would exist in star catalogs, but it would only be confirmed by measuring its parallax; due to orbiting the Sol it would have a low proper motion and would escape detection by older proper motion surveys that have found stars like the 9th_magnitude Barnard's Star. In 2002, Muller speculated that Nemesis was perturbed 400 million years ago by a passing star from a circular orbit into an orbit with an eccentricity of 0.7. However, because Nemesis is so distant from the Sol, it is expected to be subject to perturbations by passing stars, and therefore its orbital period should shift by 15–30%. In particular, if Nemesis is a red dwarf or a brown dwarf, the WISE mission (an infrared sky survey that covered most of our Sol neighborhood in movement_verifying parallax measurements) was expected to be able to find it." .

lsd:Entity_13144 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1994 All_Ireland Senior Club Hurling Championship Final was a hurling match played at Croke Park on 1994 to determine the winners of the 1993–94 All_Ireland Senior Club Hurling Championship, the 24th season of the All_Ireland Senior Club Hurling Championship, a tournament organised by the Gaelic Athletic Association for the champion clubs of the four provinces of Ireland. The final was contested by Sarsfields GAA of Galway and Toomevara GAA of Tipperary, with Sarsfields GAA winning by 1_14 to 3_6. The All_Ireland final was a unique occasion as it was the first ever championship meeting between Sarsfields GAA and Toomevara GAA. Sarsfields GAA were hoping to become the first the first team to retain the title while Toomevara GAA were hoping to make their own history by winning their first All_Ireland title. Goals in the 13th, 29th and 44th minutes gave Toomevara GAA a three_point lead, however, Sarsfields GAA equalized with a 65th_minute goal from Michael Kenny after a Joe Cooney pass." .

lsd:Entity_13166 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Apamea was fought on 19 July 998 between the forces of the Byzantine Empire and the Fatimid Caliphate. Qalaat al_Madiq), surrounded by mountains and located near the Lake of Apamea, on 19 July 998. Arriving in Syria in mid_September, the emperor's army buried their fallen in the field of Apamea and then captured Shayzar, sacked the fortress of Masyaf and Rafaniya, torched Arqa, and raided the environs of Baalbek, Beirut, Tripoli and Jubayl." .

lsd:Entity_13195 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Search for Everything World Tour was a concert tour by American recording artist John Mayer in support of his seventh studio album The Search for Everything (2017)." .

lsd:Entity_13214 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Summis desiderantes affectibus (Latin for \"desiring with supreme ardor\"), sometimes abbreviated to Summis desiderantes was a papal bull regarding witchcraft issued by Innocent VIII on 5 14 December 1484." .

lsd:Entity_13236 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1975 World Table Tennis Championships were held in Kolkata, The entire tournament was held at the newly constructed Netaji Indoor Stadium, from 06 February 1975 to 16 February 1975." .

lsd:Entity_13277 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Vyborg took place in the spring of 1710 during the Great Northern War (1700–1721), as a second attempt by the Russians to capture the fortress port of Vyborg (Vyborg), near the modern border between Russia and Finland, after a failed attempt in 1706. Thirteen thousand troops under General_Admiral Fyodor Apraksin marched to Vyborg and laid siege on 22 01 March 1710. The selection of the command staff destined for the siege of Vyborg led to the main authority being given to General_Admiral Fyodor Apraksin, while his subordinates were Major_Generals Robert Bruce and Wilhelm Bergholtz. Russia had made a previous attempt to capture Vyborg; in October 1706, a siege corps was sent there under the command of Robert (Roman) Bruce. Peter's plan for the second siege of Vyborg involved a combination of land and sea forces, and the fort was to be taken by a prolonged siege. On 2 01 March 1710, General Apraksin received orders to attack Vyborg, and he planned to move out by 15 March. When the siege corps arrived at Vyborg on the 22nd, they occupied the town's outskirts and countryside, forcing the Swedes to regroup behind the town's inner stone wall. Thus, Myshlaevsky concluded that there were originally 12 cannon brought to Vyborg, but only ten of them were used in the siege, as two of them were disabled. However, other sources do not mention the truce_bearer or the naval battle; Fyodor Apraksin even wrote to the czar saying that he \"could not imagine\" how a Swedish fleet could be sent to Vyborg, although he did take precautions. Russia's occupation of Vyborg allowed the creation of a base to supply troops and build ships, and expanded the zone of action of the Baltic Fleet. Thus, in effect, the capture of Vyborg and Karelia served to determine the outcome of the Great Northern War by establishing a staging area for further military actions. Thus, after the Treaty of Nystad, Vyborg officially became incorporated into the Russian Empire as Vyborg." .

lsd:Entity_1331 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 Athens Trophy was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts in Athens in Greece. It was held from 05 October 1987 until 11 October 1987." .

lsd:Entity_13524 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1920 Summer Olympics – men's 3000 metres steeplechase event was part of the athletics at the 1920 Summer Olympics at the 1920 Summer Olympics. The competition was held on Wednesday, 18 August 1920 and on Friday, 20 August 1920." .

lsd:Entity_13567 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 AFC Champions League was the 34th edition of Asia's premier club association football tournament organized by the Asian Football Confederation (AFC), and the 13th under the current AFC Champions League title. Guangzhou Football Club won the tournament after defeating Al_Ahli in the 2015 AFC Champions League Final. The member associations are ranked based on their national team's and clubs' performance over the last four years in AFC competitions, with the allocation of slots for the 2015 and 2016 editions of the AFC club competitions determined by the 2014 rankings: The AFC Competitions Committee finalised the slot allocation for the 2015 and 2016 editions of the AFC Champions League based on the criteria, including AFC's MA rankings and the implementation of club licensing regulations, on 28 November 2014." .

lsd:Entity_13646 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1904 Cape Turnagain earthquake struck 10 kilometres (6.2 mi) north of Cape Turnagain on the morning of 09 August 1904 with a magnitude estimated at 6.8 Ms and 7.0–7.2 Mw It was felt throughout the North Island and upper South Island, with many communities within a 500 kilometres (310 mi) radius reporting noticeable ground shaking. It was the largest to strike New Zealand since the 7.0 Mw  North Canterbury earthquake in 1888. Seismograph data of the earthquake was held at stations in Melbourne and Honolulu, as well as various sites across New Zealand." .

lsd:Entity_13652 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Capture of Oaxaca was a battle during the Mexican War of Independence that occurred on 25 November 1812 at Oaxaca de Juárez, Oaxaca de Juárez. This army proceeded to march to Oaxaca de Juárez on 10 25 November 1812." .

lsd:Entity_13717 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Second Encirclement Campaign against Hubei_Henan_Anhui Soviet was an encirclement campaign launched by the Chinese Nationalist Government that was intended to destroy communist Hubei–Henan–Anhui Soviet and its Chinese Red Army in the local region. It was responded by the Communists' second counter_encirclement campaign at Hubei–Henan–Anhui Soviet (Chinese: 鄂豫皖苏区第二次苏区反围剿), also called by the communists as the second counter_encirclement campaign at Hubei–Henan–Anhui Revolutionary Base (Chinese: 鄂豫皖革命根据地第二次反围剿), in which the local Chinese Red Army successfully defended their soviet republic in the border region of Hubei, Henan, and Anhui provinces against the Nationalist attacks from 01 April 1931 to 01 July 1931." .

lsd:Entity_13722 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Derby County F.C. season is the 109th season in the Football League and 116th season overall of association football played by Derby County F.C., an English football club based in Derby County F.C., Derbyshire. Derby County F.C. retained 21 players from the 2013–14 Derby County F.C. season, these were players still under contract going into the new season. Several of Derby County F.C.'s players had come to the end of their contracts in the 2013–14 Derby County F.C. season and were therefore released by the club." .

lsd:Entity_13741 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Provisional Tungus Central National Government (PT_CNG; Russian: Временное Центральное Тунгусское Национальное Управление, Vremennoye Tsentral'noye Tungusskoye Natsional'noye Upravleniye), more commonly known as Tungus Republic (Russian: Тунгусская республика, Tungusskaya Respublika) was a short_lived unrecognized secessionist state covering mostly Okhotsk region and the eastern regions of the Yakut ASSR from 01 July 1924 to 01 May 1925." .

lsd:Entity_13802 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Bileća was fought in August 1388 between the forces of the Kingdom of Bosnia led by Grand Duke of the kingdom, Vlatko Vuković, and the Ottoman Turks under the leadership of Lala Şahin Pasha. King Tvrtko's army, led by his most capable and trusted general, Grand Duke of Bosnia, Vlatko Vuković, allowed the Turks to penetrate as far as the town of Bileća." .

lsd:Entity_13829 a lsd:Context_narration ;
