lsd:Entity_1394 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Asian Men's Club Volleyball Championship was the 19th edition of the Asian Men's Club Volleyball Championship, an annual international volleyball club tournament organised by the Asian Volleyball Confederation (AVC) with Myanmar Volleyball Federation (MVF). The tournament was held in Naypyidaw, Myanmar from 30 July 2018 to 06 August 2018. The 13 AVC member associations submitted their men's club to the 2018 Asian Club Championship." .

lsd:Entity_13948 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 5th edition of Miss Diva 2017 took place on 2017. At the finale held on 2017, Roshmitha Harimurthy along with the reigning Miss Universe 2016 Iris Mittenaere crowned Shraddha Shashidhar as Miss Diva , while Srinidhi Shetty crowned Peden Ongmu as Miss Diva and Aradhana Buragohain crowned Apeksha Porwal as Miss Diva 2017 2nd runner up. The two winners represented India at Miss Universe 2017, Miss Supranational 2017." .

lsd:Entity_13959 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lion Air Flight 904 was a scheduled domestic passenger flight from Husein Sastranegara International Airport in Bandung to Ngurah Rai International Airport in Bali, Indonesia. In January 2017, Budi Waseso, the chief of Indonesia's national narcotics agency, said that the pilot of Lion Air Flight 904 was under the influence of drugs at the time of the accident, and had hallucinated that the sea was part of the runway." .

lsd:Entity_13965 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1934 Air France Wibault 282T crash occurred on 09 May 1934 when Wibault 282T_12 F_AMHY of Air France crashed into the English Channel off Dungeness, Kent, United Kingdom while operating an international scheduled passenger flight from Paris–Le Bourget Airport, Paris, France to Croydon Airport, Surrey, United Kingdom. The aircraft was operating a scheduled international passenger flight from Paris–Le Bourget Airport, Paris, France to Croydon Airport, Surrey, United Kingdom." .

lsd:Entity_14015 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Supercoppa Italiana was the 27th edition of the Supercoppa Italiana, Italian football supercup, played on 22 December 2014 at the Jassim Bin Hamad Stadium in Doha, Qatar. It was held between 2013–14 Serie A champions, Juventus F.C., and the winners of the 2013–14 Coppa Italia, S.S.C. Napoli. The game was tentatively scheduled to be played on 2014, but due to S.S.C. Napoli's participation in the 2014–15 UEFA Champions League play_off round, the team asked that the game be rescheduled during Serie A's winter break. S.S.C. Napoli emerged as the victorious side 6–5 in a penalty shootout, following a 2–2 draw, to pick up their second trophy in the tournament. Qatar became the fifth different country to host a Supercoppa Italiana. Both of S.S.C. Napoli's prior appearances had been against Juventus F.C., beating them 5–1 in 1990 but losing 2–4 after extra time in 2012. Carlos Tevez put Juventus F.C. ahead in the fifth minute following defensive errors by S.S.C. Napoli." .

lsd:Entity_14080 a lsd:Context_narration ;
