lsd:Entity_14393 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Combined Bomber Offensive (CBO) was an Allied offensive of strategic bombing during World War II in Europe. The Combined Bomber Offensive began on 10 June 1943 during the British bombing campaign against German industry in the Ruhr area known as the \"Battle of the Ruhr\". After Arnold submitted the October 9, 1943 \"Plan to Assure the Most Effective Exploitation of the Combined Bomber Offensive\" on October 22 the \"Allied Joint Chiefs of Staff\" signed orders to raid \"the aircraft industries in the southern Germany and Austria regions\". Tedder's proposal to keep oil targets as the highest priority and place \"Germany's rail system in second priority was approved by the CSTC on November 1 On 12 April 1945, Strategic Bombing Directive No." .

