lsd:Entity_14481 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "According to some early medieval sources, the Siege of Exeter or Siege of Caer_Uisc was a military conflict that took place in or around 630 CE, between the Mercians, led by Penda of Mercia, and the Britons occupying Caer_Uisc (Exeter) in the kingdom of Dumnonia. The heathen Penda besieges Exeter in the year 634, and the siege is raised by the Briton Cadwalla." .

lsd:Entity_1453 a lsd:Context_narration ;
