lsd:Entity_14596 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A special election was held in 2006 California's 50th congressional district special election to choose a new member of the U.S. Representative to fill the vacancy caused by the resignation of Republican Randy Cunningham, who resigned November 28, 2005 after pleading guilty to bribery, wire fraud, mail fraud, and tax evasion charges. As no candidate won a simple majority, the top vote_getters in each party, Democrat Francine Busby and Republican Brian Bilbray, competed in a runoff special general election held on 06 June 2006, the same day that primaries were held for the November 2006 general election. In the 06 June 2006 primary election for the November 2006 election, both candidates won their party's nomination. The 06 June 2006 run_off was held at the same time as the primary election for the biennial November 7, 2006 general election. She faced the leading vote getter from the two other parties participating: Republican Brian Bilbray and Libertarian Paul King, as well as independent candidate William Griffith, in a 06 June 2006 runoff. For the new term beginning in 2007, the primaries were held on 06 June 2006, concurrent with the special election." .

lsd:Entity_14608 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The World Infestation Tour was a concert tour by American glam metal band Ratt in support of their latest album Invasion of Your Privacy." .

lsd:Entity_14633 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Singapore Open (officially known as the 2018 Singapore Open Badminton Championships) was a badminton tournament which took place at the Singapore Indoor Stadium in Singapore from 17 to 22 July 2018 and had a total purse of $355,000. The 2018 Singapore Open was the fourteenth tournament of the 2018 BWF World Tour and also part of the Singapore Open Badminton Championships championships, which had been held since 1987. This international tournament was held at Singapore Indoor Stadium in Singapore." .

lsd:Entity_14693 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The archery at the 2008 Summer Olympics – men's team at the 2008 Summer Olympics was part of the archery at the 2008 Summer Olympics and took place at the Olympic Green Archery Field. As the defending archery at the 2004 Summer Olympics – men's team, South Korea defended the title with two archers from the past Games, Im Dong_hyun and Park Kyung_Mo." .

lsd:Entity_14721 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Copa do Brasil Final was the final two_legged tie that decided the 2018 Copa do Brasil, the 30th season of the Copa do Brasil, Brazil's national cup association football tournament organised by the Brazilian Football Confederation. The finals were contested in a two_legged home_and_away format between the defending champions Cruzeiro E.C., from Minas Gerais, and S.C. Corinthians Paulista, from São Paulo. Cruzeiro E.C. and S.C. Corinthians Paulista reached the Copa do Brasil finals for the eighth and sixth time, respectively. The first leg was hosted by Cruzeiro E.C. at Mineirão in Belo Horizonte on 2018, while the second leg was hosted by S.C. Corinthians Paulista at Arena S.C. Corinthians Paulista in São Paulo on 2018. Cruzeiro E.C. defeated S.C. Corinthians Paulista 3–1 on aggregate in the finals to win their sixth title. In the finals, the teams played a single_elimination tournament with the following rules: In the second leg of the semi_finals, Douglas (S.C. Corinthians Paulista) picked up a yellow card and Sassá (Cruzeiro E.C.) was sent off which meant they were suspended for the first leg of the Finals. A goal from Thiago Neves gave Cruzeiro E.C. a 1–0 win over S.C. Corinthians Paulista in the first leg. Egídio (Cruzeiro E.C.), booked in the first leg, Ángelo Araos (S.C. Corinthians Paulista) sent off in the first leg, and Sassá (Cruzeiro E.C.), suspended six games, were ruled out of the second leg. In the second leg, Cruzeiro E.C. defeated S.C. Corinthians Paulista 1–2 to lift the Copa do Brasil." .

lsd:Entity_14817 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 Bombay bombings were a series of 13 terrorist bombings that took place in Mumbai, India, then known as Bombay, on 12 March 1993. After India's three_judge Supreme Court bench rejected his curative petition, saying the grounds raised by him do not fall within the principles laid down by the apex court in 2002, the Maharashtra state government executed Yakub Memon on 30 July 2015. On 9 12 March 1993, three days before the bombings took place, a small_time criminal from the Behrampada slum in Northeast Mumbai named Gul Noor Mohammad Sheikh (Gullu) was detained at the Nag Pada police station. The locations attacked: The official number of fatalities was 257 with 1,400 others injured (some sources reported that 317 people died; this misreport was due to a bomb which killed 69 in Calcutta on 16 March and was not part of 12 March 1993 Bombay bombings). On 10 July 2006, the Chief Minister of Maharashtra, Sharad Pawar, admitted that he had \"deliberately misled\" people following the 1993 Mumbai bombings by saying there were \"13 and not 12\" explosions and had added the name of a Muslim_dominated locality to show that people from both communities had been affected." .

lsd:Entity_14858 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Brookledge Follies is a variety show presented in a small theater located behind a historic Spanish_style mansion near Hancock Park in Los Angeles, California. Created by Erika Larsen in 2009, the invitation_only show was designed to showcase a wide range of variety talent on an occasional basis." .

lsd:Entity_14862 a lsd:Context_narration ;
