    rdfs:label "The judo at the 2016 Summer Olympics – women's 78 kg competition in judo at the 2016 Summer Olympics in Rio de Janeiro was held on 11 August 2016 at the Carioca Arena 2." .

lsd:Entity_15279 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Frontier Middle School shooting was a school shooting that occurred on 02 February 1996, at Frontier Middle School in Moses Lake, United States." .

lsd:Entity_15306 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Death of a Bachelor Tour was a concert tour by Panic! At The Disco, in support of the group's fifth studio album Death of a Bachelor (2016)." .

lsd:Entity_15324 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "black anarchism is a term applied to a group of people of African descent who identify with the principles of anarchism. black anarchism has had a major influence on the anarchist movement, black anarchists have a 100 year history in black led anti fascist and anti_racism history." .

lsd:Entity_15328 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Het Bijltjesoproer (\"Hatchet Riot\") or Kattenburgoproer (\"Kattenburg Riot\") of 30 May 1787 was an uprising of Dutch Orangist ship carpenters in the Kattenburg quarter of Amsterdam against the city's Patriots regenten. On the other hand, the Patriots movement was gaining strength since 1780, started arming themselves in 1783 and eventually seized control in several cities throughout the Netherlands, such as Utrecht. On 9 30 May 1787, the first pitched battle occurred near Jutphaas in the province of Utrecht, resulting in a Patriots victory." .

lsd:Entity_15359 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "taekwondo at the taekwondo at the 2016 Summer Olympics in Rio de Janeiro took place from 17 to 20 August 2016 at the Carioca Arena 3 inside the Barra Olympic Park in Barra da Tijuca. Around 128 taekwondo fighters competed in eight weight categories; four for men, and four for women. taekwondo competition at these Games featured a total of 128 athletes, 64 in each gender, and 16 in each of the eight weight categories. After finishing in third in taekwondo at the 2012 Summer Olympics, this Olympics marks South Korea's return to the top of the taekwondo medal standings." .

lsd:Entity_15383 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The \"The Keep Calm & Play Louder Tour\" was the second theatre tour undertaken by British pop_rock band McFly. The tour began on 07 March 2012 and ended on 21 April 2012." .

lsd:Entity_15400 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999–2000 Prva HNL was the ninth season of the Prva HNL, the national championship for men's association football teams in Croatia, since its establishment in 1992. The season started on 24 July 1999 and ended on 13 May 2000. GNK Dinamo Zagreb (Croatia Zagreb in fall season) were the defending champions, having won their ninth championship title the previous season, and they defended the title again, after a win against Rijeka on 6 13 May 2000." .

lsd:Entity_15438 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 Lexmark Indy 300 was the thirteenth and penultimate round of the 2004 Champ Car season, held on 24 October 2004 on the Surfers Paradise Street Circuit, Queensland, Australia. Paul Tracy won the pole and Bruno Junqueira won the race." .

lsd:Entity_15450 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Gijón International Film Festival (Asturian: Festival Internacional de Cine de Xixón or FICXixón) is an annual film festival held in Gijón, a city in northwest Spain. In the beginning it was an initiative of the City Council of Gijón in co_operation with Caja de Ahorros de Asturias (Cajastur)." .

lsd:Entity_15522 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Switzerland at the 2015 Summer Universiade participated at the 2015 Summer Universiade in Gwangju, South Korea." .

lsd:Entity_15534 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 German Grand Prix (formally the XXIV Grosser Mobil 1 Preis von Deutschland) was a Formula One motor race held on 30 July 1995 at the Hockenheimring, Hockenheim. The 45_lap race was won by Benetton driver Michael Schumacher after he started from second position. Damon Hill started the race from the pole position alongside Michael Schumacher." .

lsd:Entity_15545 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Tipton's Island was an engagement between a Shawnee war party and Indiana militia under command of John Tipton in 01 April 1813 on the White River near Seymour, Indiana. In 01 April 1813, during the War of 1812, a Shawnee war party killed two white settlers eight miles from Fort Vallonia." .

lsd:Entity_15607 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1970 Federation Cup was the eighth edition of what is now known as the Billie Jean King Cup. 22 nations participated in the tournament, which was held at the Freiburg Tennis Club in Freiburg, West Germany from 19 May 1970–24 May 1970. Australia Fed Cup team defeated West Germany in the final. West Germany vs. Australia Fed Cup team." .

lsd:Entity_15614 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 AFC Champions League was the 33rd edition of the top_level Asian club association football tournament organized by the Asian Football Confederation (AFC), and the 12th under the current AFC Champions League title. In the 2014 AFC Champions League Final, Western Sydney Wanderers FC of Australia defeated Al_Hilal of Saudi Arabia 1–0 on aggregate, to become the first Australian team to win the title, and in doing so qualified for the 2014 FIFA Club World Cup. The AFC laid out the procedure for deciding the participating associations and the allocation of slots, with inspection of the associations interested in participating in the AFC Champions League to be done in 2013, and the 2014 AFC Champions League Final decision to be made by the AFC on 26 November 2013. The AFC Competitions Committee proposed the following participating criteria for the 2014–2016 editions of the AFC Champions League on 12 March 2013: On 26 November 2013, the AFC Executive Committee approved the slots for the 2014 edition of the AFC Champions League." .

lsd:Entity_15681 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Execution of Louis XVI by guillotine, a major event of the French Revolution, took place on 21 January 1793 at the Place de la Révolution (\"Revolution Square\", formerly Place Louis XV, and renamed Place de la Concorde in 1795) in Paris. At Trial of Louis XVI on 17 21 January 1793, the National Convention had convicted the king of high treason in a near_unanimous vote; while no one voted \"not guilty\", several deputies abstained." .

lsd:Entity_15692 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Delaware Bay, or the Battle of Cape May, was a naval engagement fought between the Great Britain and United States of America during the American Revolutionary War. The ensuing combat in Delaware Bay, near Cape May, ended with an American victory over a superior British force." .

lsd:Entity_15706 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2011–12 Egyptian parliamentary election were held in Egypt held from 28 November 2011 to 11 January 2012, following the revolution that ousted President Hosni Mubarak, after which the Supreme Council of the Armed Forces (SCAF) dissolved Parliament. On 2011, an administrative court in Mansoura ruled that former NDP members were not allowed to stand in the election as independent candidates. The election for the upper house, the Shura Council (\"the Consultative Council\") are to follow on 2012, and will take place in 3 stages as well between 29 January and 22 February. Only then will presidential election be held, \"no later than 2012\" according to Hussein Tantawi's statement. The liberal New Wafd Party announced on 2011 that it would contest the election in an alliance with the Freedom and Justice Party. On 2012, the Supreme Constitutional Court of Egypt ruled that the election was unconstitutional, and one third of the winners were illegitimate. Mohamed Morsi, sworn as Egypt's new president on 30 June, has initially refrained from speaking publicly on that (crucial to the extent of his own real power) issue." .

lsd:Entity_15719 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 FA Trophy Final was the 29th final of The Football Association's cup competition for levels 5–8 of the English football league system. It was contested by Cheltenham Town F.C. and Southport F.C. on 1998 at Wembley Stadium, London." .

lsd:Entity_1572 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Lexmark Indy 300 was the eighteenth round of the 2003 CART season, held on 26 October 2003 on the Surfers Paradise Street Circuit, Queensland, Australia. The event was to have been the penultimate race of the 2003 season, but it later became the final round after the 2003 King Taco 500 was canceled because of a wildfire near to the California Speedway venue." .

lsd:Entity_15743 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Mrs. Carter Show World Tour was the fifth concert tour by American singer Beyoncé. It began in Belgrade, Serbia on 15 April 2013, and concluded in Lisbon, Portugal on 27 March 2014. The set list of the 2013 portion of the tour included approximately twenty five songs from Beyoncé's four solo studio albums: Dangerously in Love (2003), B'Day (2006), I Am... Sasha Fierce (2008), and 4 (2011). Tickets for Rock in Rio became available for general sale on April 4, 2013 and within two hours, the first day of the festival, in which Beyoncé was headlining, had sold out all 65,000 tickets. A video titled \"Goodbye to The Mrs. Carter Show World Tour\" was uploaded by the singer on her official YouTube channel on 27 March 2014 showing portions of live performances from the final leg of the tour, behind the scenes moments and visits to cities as \"XO\" was played in the background." .

lsd:Entity_15795 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The June 2015 Turkish general election took place on 07 June 2015 in all 85 electoral districts of Turkey to elect 550 members to the Grand National Assembly. In the end, no such initiative was taken and Supreme Electoral Council of Turkey (YSK) went on with the date 07 June 2015. The candidate lists were drawn up such that BBP candidates were placed top in electoral districts in which they won more votes than the SP in 2011 Turkish general election, while SP candidates were placed top in province of Turkey in which the SP had beaten the BBP in 2011 Turkish general election. On 5 January 2015, the Supreme Electoral Council of Turkey announced that the general election would take place on 07 June 2015 and also released a decision in regards to the process for standing as a candidate. The party's leader Masum Türker claimed that the abolition of the Presidency of Religious Affairs would cause division in Turkey and also predicted that an early election would occur after 07 June 2015 since no party would win a majority. The Supreme Electoral Council of Turkey announced the fully confirmed results on 18 07 June 2015. The 25th Parliament of Turkey was sworn in on 23 07 June 2015, chaired temporarily by the new parliament's oldest member Deniz Baykal." .

lsd:Entity_15803 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Maria Bueno and Darlene Hard defeated Robyn Ebbern and Margaret Smith in the final, 8–6, 9–7 to win the Ladies' Doubles tennis title at the 1963 Wimbledon Championships." .

lsd:Entity_15892 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1965 Rhodesian general election were held in Southern Rhodesia on 07 May 1965." .

lsd:Entity_15917 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1996 West Virginia gubernatorial election took place on 1996 to elect the Governor of West Virginia. Republican Cecil H. Underwood, who had previously been the Governor of West Virginia from 1957 to 1961, defeated Democratic State Senator Charlotte Pritt." .

lsd:Entity_15932 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1932 French Grand Prix (official name: XVIII Grand Prix de l'Automobile Club de France) was a Grand Prix motor race held at Reims_Gueux on 03 July 1932." .

lsd:Entity_15937 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Pro Bowl (branded as the 2017 Pro Bowl presented by Aquafina for sponsorship reasons) was the National Football League's all_star game for the 2016 NFL season, which was played at Camping World Stadium in Orlando on 29 January 2017. The game was the first in a three_year deal to host the Pro Bowl in Orlando, which also included cross_promotional events (such as a newly_established skills competition) held at the Walt Disney World Resort (which is owned by the primary parent company of the game's broadcaster, ESPN). On June 1, 2016, the NFL announced that it had awarded the next three Pro Bowl games to Orlando. The game format was nearly the same for 2017 as it had been in 2016, with some exceptions: at Camping World Stadium in Orlando." .

lsd:Entity_1594 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Racławice was one of the first battles of the Polish_Lithuanian Kościuszko Uprising against Russian Empire. It was fought on 04 April 1794 near the village of Racławice in Lesser Poland. The battle site is one of Poland's official national Historic Monuments (Pomnik historii), as designated May 1, 2004. After the battle, Kościuszko paraded before his troops in a sukmana, a traditional attire worn in Lesser Poland, in honour of the bravery of the peasants, whose charge ensured the quick capture of the Russian artillery He also praised Wojciech Bartosz Głowacki, a peasant who was the first to capture the cannon (he is visible in Matejko's painting, above). The victory was subsequently promoted in Poland as a major success and helped in spreading the Kościuszko Uprising to other areas of Poland and instigating the Warsaw Uprising of 1794." .

lsd:Entity_15940 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Copa Libertadores Finals was the final two_legged series that determined the 2010 Copa Libertadores champion. It was contested between Mexican club C.D. Guadalajara and Brazil club S.C. Internacional. The first leg was played on 11 August in C.D. Guadalajara's home field, while the second leg was played in S.C. Internacional's. S.C. Internacional, as the champions, played the winners of the 2010 Copa Sudamericana in the 2011 Recopa Sudamericana. S.C. Internacional, by virtue of being the last South American team in the competition, was predetermined to enter the semifinals of the 2010 FIFA Club World Cup before winning the finals. Prior to the 2010 final, Chivas and S.C. Internacional had previously met two times in South American competition. S.C. Internacional, on the other hand, are appearing on their third final after losing in 1980 to Nacional." .

lsd:Entity_15952 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "taekwondo at the 2004 Summer Olympics were held in the Sports Pavilion at the Faliro Coastal Zone Olympic Complex in Athens, Greece where 124 competitors competed in eight events, four each for men and women. A total of 124 taekwondo jins from 60 nations competed at the Athens Games:" .

lsd:Entity_15957 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hexham, 15 May 1464, marked the end of significant Lancastrian resistance in the north of England during the early part of the reign of Edward IV. The battle was fought near the town of Hexham in Northumberland. The two sides met outside Hexham on 14 15 May 1464. Neville showed little of Edward's conciliatory spirit, and had thirty leading Lancastrians executed in Hexham on the evening following the battle, including Henry Beaufort, 3rd Duke of Somerset, and Lord Roos. Following his defeat in the Battle of Hexham on 15 May 1464, Henry VI found refuge, sheltered by Lancastrian supporters, at houses across the north of England." .

lsd:Entity_16070 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A Egyptian constitutional referendum, 2014 was held in Egypt on 14 January 2014 and 15 January 2014 and with Egyptians abroad voting between 8 January and 12 January. The Freedom and Justice Party and the Islamic Bloc, which had won 65.3% of the vote in Egypt's parliamentary elections in 2011–2012, opposed the new Constitution and the referendum as being the fruits of an illegal military coup." .

lsd:Entity_16083 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Little Muddy Creek, also known as the Lame Deer Fight, was fought on 07 May 1877–8, 1877, by United States soldiers and scouts against a village of Miniconjou Lakota and Northern Cheyenne. The battle occurred near Little Muddy Creek in Montana Territory, near present_day Lame Deer, Rosebud County." .

lsd:Entity_16133 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1985 Israel Super Cup was the 15th Israel Super Cup (20th, including unofficial matches, as the competition wasn't played within the Israel Football Association in its first 5 editions, until 1969), an annual Israel football match played between the winners of the previous season's Top Division and Israel State Cup. The match was played between Maccabi Haifa F.C., champions of the 1984–85 Liga Leumit and Beitar Jerusalem F.C., winners of the 1984–85 Israel State Cup. This was Maccabi Haifa F.C.'s 3rd Israel Super Cup appearance (including unofficial matches) and Beitar's 4th. At the match, played at Thomas D'Alesandro Stadium, Maccabi Haifa F.C. won 5–2." .

lsd:Entity_1615 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The FIS Nordic World Ski Championships 1925 was the 1st official FIS Nordic World Ski Championships and took place between February 4–14, 1925 in Johannisbad (Janské Lázně), Czechoslovakia." .

lsd:Entity_16165 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siamese coup d'état of 1947 (Thailand: รัฐประหาร 8 พฤศจิกายน พ.ศ. 2490) was a Thailand coup d'état that took place on the evening of 07 November 1947, ending in the early morning hours of 08 November 1947." .

lsd:Entity_16192 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1963–64 Football League Cup was the fourth season of the EFL Cup, a knockout competition for England's top 92 football clubs. The competition began on 04 September 1963, and ended with the two_legged final on 15 22 April 1964 and 22 April 1964. Leicester City F.C. win 4–3 on aggregate." .

lsd:Entity_16207 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Universe 1976, the 25th Miss Universe pageant, was held on 11 July 1976 at the Lee Theatre in Hong Kong." .

lsd:Entity_16231 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Our Version of Events Tour was a debut global concert tour by Scottish singer Emeli Sandé, in support of her 2012 debut album, Our Version of Events." .

lsd:Entity_16280 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Sibiu Open was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Sibiu, Romania between 17 September 2018 and 23 September 2018." .

lsd:Entity_16312 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1952 Tour de Romandie was the sixth edition of the Tour de Romandie cycle race and was held from 17 April 1952 to 20 April 1952." .

lsd:Entity_16337 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The American Music Awards of 2016 took place on 20 November 2016, at the Microsoft Theater in Los Angeles. It was broadcast on American Broadcasting Company and was hosted by Gigi Hadid and Jay Pharoah." .

lsd:Entity_16405 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "LoveMusik is a musical written by Alfred Uhry, using a selection of music by Kurt Weill. The show was directed by Harold Prince with musical staging by Patricia Birch and starred Michael Cerveris as Kurt Weill, Donna Murphy as Lotte Lenya, David Pittu as Bertolt Brecht and John Scherer as George Davis. This bio_musical about the marital and professional relationship of the German_born composer Kurt Weill and the actress Lotte Lenya, directed by Harold Prince, is sluggish, tedious and (hold your breath) unmissable.\"" .

lsd:Entity_16415 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI) series of academic conferences is generally considered the most prestigious in the field of human–computer interaction and is one of the top_ranked conferences in computer science. CHI has been held annually since 1982 and attracts thousands of international attendees. The CHI conference series started with the Human Factors in Computer Systems conference in Gaithersburg, Maryland, US in 1982, organized by Bill Curtis and Ben Shneiderman. ACM SIGCHI became the sponsor of the Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems." .

lsd:Entity_16467 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 BMW Championships was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor grass courts at Devonshire Park in Eastbourne in the United Kingdom that was part of the Toyota Series category of the 1981 WTA Tour. It was the eighth edition of the tournament and was held from 15 June 1981 through 21 June 1981." .

lsd:Entity_16488 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 52nd Guldbagge Awards ceremony, presented by the Swedish Film Institute, honoring the best Swedish films of 2016 and took place on 2017 at Cirkus in Stockholm. The nominees for the 52nd Guldbagge Awards were announced on 2017 in Stockholm, by the Swedish Film Institute." .

lsd:Entity_1649 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Prague Cup is an international, multi_level synchronized skating competition, held in Prague, Czech Republic. Prague Cup is organized by the Czech Figure Skating Association and sanctioned by the International Skating Union." .

lsd:Entity_16537 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sandown 500 was an annual endurance motor race which was staged at the Sandown Raceway, near Melbourne, Victoria, Australia from 1964 to 2019. The second hiatus in the history of the race commenced in 1999 when a Queensland government_supported bid saw the Sandown 500 replaced on the Supercars calendar by the Queensland 500, held at Queensland Raceway. By 2003, new owners of Queensland Raceway had tired of the relative expense of the 500 kilometre endurance race format, resulting in the Sandown 500 again being contested by V8 Supercars. After a change of promoter of Sandown Raceway's motorsport activities, a changed V8 Supercars calendar resulted in the 500 kilometre event moving to the Phillip Island Grand Prix Circuit for the 2008 season, while Sandown reverted to hosting a sprint round, an event which became known as the Sandown Challenge. The Sandown 500 returned to the V8 Supercars calendar in 2012, replacing the Phillip Island 500 to again become the traditional lead_in race to the Bathurst 1000. 2015 saw Winterbottom win the Sandown 500 for a second time, having first tasted success in 2006, leading home a Prodrive Racing Australia one_two finish. It was also announced in the months leading up to the event that the Sandown 500 would not return in 2020, to be replaced by The Bend 500 at The Bend Motorsport Park." .

lsd:Entity_16552 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Día internacional de darileidy cortorreal (French: Journée internationale de la Francophonie) is observed within the Organisation internationale de la Francophonie's 77 member states every 20 March 1988 to celebrate the French language and Francophone culture. According to the Canadian then_minister for La Francophonie Steven Blaney's speech in 2013, the Día internacional de darileidy cortorreal is to \"celebrate our commitment to not only the French language and the rich and diverse francophone culture but also the values of peace, democracy and respect for human rights that unite all members of the Organisation internationale de la Francophonie\"." .

lsd:Entity_16556 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 ECM Prague Open was a tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts. It was the 13th edition of the Prague Open, and was part of the Tier IV Series of the 2008 WTA Tour and of the 2008 ATP Challenger Tretorn Serie+. It took place at the I. Czech Lawn Tennis Club in Prague, Czech Republic, from April 28 through 04 May 2008." .

lsd:Entity_16601 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Indian vice_presidential election was held on 16 August 1997 to elect Vice President of India. Krishan Kant defeated Surjit Singh Barnala to become 10th Vice President of India." .

lsd:Entity_16644 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Fort Lauderdale–Tampa Bay rivalry, also known as the Florida Derby, refers to the suspended association football rivalry that most recently involved the Fort Lauderdale Strikers and the Tampa Bay Rowdies, both of whom played in the North American Soccer League through the 2016 season." .

lsd:Entity_16659 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 Budweiser NASCAR 400 was a NASCAR Winston Cup Series racing event that took place on 1981, at Texas World Speedway in College Station, Texas." .

lsd:Entity_1666 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The second World Youth Day 1987 took place on 06 April 1987 and 12 April 1987 in Buenos Aires, Argentina and was presided by John Paul II. The headquarters of the 2nd edition of World Youth Day was made official by John Paul II on June 8, 1986. The World Youth Day of 1987 took place as part of the John Paul's apostolic trip to Uruguay and Argentina which took place from March 31 to 12 April 1987. The Pope arrived in Argentina on 06 April 1987. The Cross of the World Youth Day was a wooden crucifix of 3.8 m height given to young Catholics by John Paul II at the end of the Holy Year of 1984 with the words \"Take it for the world as a sign of the love of the Lord Jesus.\" For the first time since its institution, the Cross out of Rome to be one of the main symbols of World Youth Day in Buenos Aires 1987. The World Youth Day Hymn of Buenos Aires 1987, popularly known as \"Un Nuevo Sol\" was composed by Alberto Croce and Eugenio Perpetua." .

lsd:Entity_16693 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Tro_Bro Leon was the 24th edition of the Tro Bro Leon cycle race and was held on 22 April 2007." .

lsd:Entity_16699 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Buttevant Rail Disaster was a train crash that occurred at Buttevant Railway Station, County Cork in Ireland, 220 kilometres (137 mi) on the Dublin to Cork main line on 1 August 1980." .

lsd:Entity_16831 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In May 2005, an unregistered editor posted a hoax article onto Wikipedia about journalist John Seigenthaler. In 2013, the hoax article was archived to Wikipedia:List of hoaxes on Wikipedia." .

lsd:Entity_16840 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The fifty_sixth edition of the 2014 Caribbean Series (Serie del Caribe) was played in 2014. It was held from February 1 through 08 February 2014 of 2014 with the champion baseball teams of Cuba, Naranjas de Villa Clara; Dominican Republic, Tigres del Licey; Mexico, Naranjeros de Hermosillo; Puerto Rico, Indios de Mayagüez, and Venezuela, Navegantes del Magallanes." .

lsd:Entity_16843 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Cheriyal scroll painting is a stylized version of Nakashi art, rich in the local motifs peculiar to the Telangana. They are at present made only in Hyderabad, Telangana, India. In the same way, Cheriyal scrolls must have been popular across Telangana in earlier times, though with the advent of television, cinemas and computers it has been fenced into its last outpost, the Cheriyal town. While the above_mentioned traditions could have significantly influenced the Cheriyal scroll paintings and artists, the Cheriyal paintings were and continue to be a distinctly local invention, peculiar to the Telangana region, drawing mainly on local traditions. It can safely be said that the local temple art traditions and the Kalamkari tradition across Telangana in particular, and the graphic art traditions of the Deccan and South India in general were the major influences that shaped and guided the art of scroll paintings." .

lsd:Entity_16857 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 2016 Summer Olympics – women's hammer throw competition at the 2016 Summer Olympics in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. The event was held at the Olympic Stadium on 12 August 2016–15 August 2016. Anita Włodarczyk, the reigning World Champion and European Champion, was one of the stand_out gold medal favourites in the Olympic athletics programme, given that she held all ten of the best throws that year and a season's best of 80.26 m – the third best ever." .

lsd:Entity_16883 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 European Figure Skating Championships was a senior international figure skating competition in the 1999–2000 season. The event was held at the Wiener Stadthalle in Vienna, Austria from 06 February 2000 to 13, 2000." .

lsd:Entity_16896 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1941 Colima earthquake occurred on 15 April 1941 at 19:09 UTC (13:09 local time). The intensities were X (Extreme) in Colima, VIII (Severe) in Manzanillo, and V (Moderate) in Mexico City. This earthquake was very close to where the 1973 Colima earthquake occurred." .

lsd:Entity_16964 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 355, adopted on 01 August 1974, recalled its resolutions 186, 353 and United Nations Security Council Resolution 354, noted that all States have declared their respect for Cyprus' sovereignty, independence and territorial integrity and requested the Secretary_General take appropriate action with regard to a possible cease_fire and report back to the Council." .

lsd:Entity_17046 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 Castilian_Leonese regional election was held on Sunday, 28 May 1995, to elect the 4th Cortes of the autonomous community of Castile and León. The 1991 Castilian_Leonese regional election was held on 26 May 1991, setting the election date for the Cortes on Sunday, 28 May 1995." .

lsd:Entity_17063 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 13 July 2011, Noar Linhas Aéreas Flight 4896, a Let L_410 Turbolet passenger aircraft on a domestic service from Recife to Mossoró, Brazil, crashed shortly after take_off in the Boa Viagem neighbourhood of Recife, after suffering an engine failure. The aircraft took off from Recife/Guararapes–Gilberto Freyre International Airport's runway 18 at 06:50 local time (09:50 UTC) bound for Augusto Severo International Airport, Natal and then Mossoró Airport, its final destination." .

lsd:Entity_17069 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Taeyunkak Hotel Fire was a skyscraper fire in Seoul, South Korea on 25 December 1971, that killed 164 people and injured 63 people." .

lsd:Entity_17073 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Second Battle of the Corunna Road (Spanish: Batalla de la Carretera de Coruña) was a battle of the Spanish Civil War that took place from 13 December 1936 to 15 January 1937, northwest of Madrid. In 13 December 1936, the Nationalists launched an offensive in order to cut the Corunna Road and isolate Madrid, but a Republican counter_offensive stopped the Nationalist advance. However, by 15 January 1937 both sides were exhausted and the battle ceased. After the Third Battle of the Corunna Road in 15 January 1937 with similar results, the next Nationalist attempt to encircle Madrid was the Battle of Jarama, taking place between 6 February and 27 February." .

lsd:Entity_17133 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Novara was a battle of the War of the League of Cambrai fought on 06 June 1513, near Novara, in Northern Italy. Nevertheless, the French under King Louis XII were driven out of the city of Milan the following month by the War of the League of Cambrai. In 06 June 1513, the French army, consisting of more than 20,000 under Louis de la Trémoille, besieged the city of Novara, which was held by Swiss mercenaries. By 06 June 1513, most of the western part of the duchy of Milan had been occupied by the French. The French defeat forced Louis XII to withdraw from Milan and Italy." .

lsd:Entity_17137 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Estepona was a naval battle that occurred in the year 1342 between the armada of the Crown of Aragon, commanded by Admiral Pere de Montcada, against the fleet of the Marinid Dynasty. The battle took place in the Bay of Estepona (Málaga) in the Strait of Gibraltar and resulted in an Aragonese victory and a rout of the Marinid fleet." .

lsd:Entity_17143 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Upton was fought on 28 August 1651 when a New Model Army detachment under the command of Colonel John Lambert made a surprise attack on Royalists defending the river Severn crossing at Upton_upon_Severn, 6 miles (9.7 km) below Worcester. To do this, on the next day, 28 August 1651, a strong detachment, both horse (cavalry) and foot (infantry), under the command of Colonel John Lambert, was ordered to march from Evesham to Upton_upon_Severn and drive Major General Edward Massey from there, by taking possession of the bridge and occupying the town (which is located on the west bank of the Severn)." .

lsd:Entity_17147 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2007 Senegalese parliamentary election were held in Senegal on 03 June 2007. In the 2007 presidential elections, turnout had been 70%; in the 2001 Senegalese parliamentary election it had been 67.4%." .

lsd:Entity_17194 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Next Generation Adelaide International was a men's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It was the 31st edition of the event known that year as the Australian Hard Court Championships, and was part of the International Series of the 2008 ATP Tour. It took place at the Memorial Drive Park in Australian Hard Court Championships, Australia, from 31 December 2007 through 06 January 2008." .

lsd:Entity_1721 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1976 United States presidential election in Utah took place on 02 November 1976. Utah was won by incumbent Republican President Gerald Ford over the Democratic nominee, Jimmy Carter. Ronald Reagan would repeat Nixon’s 1972 United States presidential election in Utah clean sweep in 1980 United States presidential election in Utah his elections, and no county in Utah except Carbon and Tooele would ever vote against a Republican until 2008." .

lsd:Entity_17220 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 Coca_Cola 600, the 45th running of the Coca_Cola 600, was a NASCAR Nextel Cup Series Coca_Cola 600 held on 30 May 2004 at Charlotte Motor Speedway in Charlotte, North Carolina. Contested at 400 laps on the 1.5 mile (2.4 km) speedway, it was the twelfth Coca_Cola 600 of the 2004 NASCAR Nextel Cup Series season. Jimmie Johnson of Hendrick Motorsports won the Coca_Cola 600, his second win of the season and also at Charlotte. 80) Charlotte Motor Speedway is a motorsports complex located in Concord, North Carolina, United States 13 miles from Charlotte, North Carolina." .

lsd:Entity_17267 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 NHK Trophy was the final event of six in the 2000–01 ISU Grand Prix of Figure Skating, a senior_level international invitational competition series. It was held at the Asahikawa Taisetsu Ice Arena in Asahikawa on 30 November 2000 – 03 December 2000." .

lsd:Entity_1730 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Guangzhou International Women's Open (also known as the Landsky Lighting Guangzhou International Women's Open for sponsorship reasons) was a tennis tournament on outdoor hard courts. It was the 7th edition of the Guangzhou International Women's Open, and part of the WTA International tournaments of the 2010 WTA Tour. It took place in Guangzhou, People's Republic of China, from September 13 through 19 September 2010." .

lsd:Entity_17324 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Grand Prix Cycliste de Québec was the second edition of the Grand Prix Cycliste de Québec, a single_day professional bicycle road race. It was held on 09 September 2011, over a distance of 201.6 km (125.3 mi), starting and finishing in Quebec City, Quebec, Canada." .

lsd:Entity_17338 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "New Democrats, also known as centrism Democrats, Clinton Democrats, or moderate Democrats, are a centrism ideological faction within the Democratic Party in the United States. Bill Clinton is the Democratic politician most identified with the New Democrats due to his promise of welfare reform in the 1992 United States presidential campaign and its subsequent enactment, his 1992 promise of a middle_class tax cut and his 1993 expansion of the Earned Income Tax Credit for the working poor. Clinton presented himself as a centrism candidate to draw White middle_class voters who had left the Democratic Party for the Republican Party. Columnist Michael Lind argued that neoliberalism for New Democrats was the \"highest stage\" of left liberalism. Many leading New Democrats, including Bill Clinton, started out in the George McGovern wing of the Democratic Party and gradually moved toward the right on economic and military policy." .

lsd:Entity_17345 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Mascot was an unsuccessful British carrier air raid conducted against the German battleship Tirpitz at her anchorage in Kåfjorden, Norway, on 17 July 1944. The improved defences in place by the time of Operation Mascot included a cliff_top observation post near Kåfjorden, which was capable of directing the battleship's anti_aircraft guns if necessary." .

lsd:Entity_17349 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Northern Ireland Football League Cup (BetMcLean League Cup for sponsorship purposes), also known as the Irish League Cup, is a national association football knock_out cup competition in Northern Ireland open to the 36 Northern Ireland Football League clubs. The cup is operated by the Northern Ireland Football League, who in 2013 took over the administration from the Irish Football Association (IFA) for the 2013–14 season onwards, after which the cup was renamed as the Northern Ireland Football League (NIFL) Cup." .

lsd:Entity_17357 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Agram Trial or Zagreb Trial (known as the \"High treason trial\" in Serbo_Croatian, veleizdajnički proces) was the trial of 53 Serbs in Austria_Hungary, who were accused of conspiracy to overthrow the state and place Croatia_Slavonia under Serbian rule." .

lsd:Entity_17368 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The debut season of One in a Million, season 1 premiered on 26 May 2006 and was aired on 8TV." .

lsd:Entity_17424 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2002–03 Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup was the ninth season of the Bosnia and Herzegovina's annual association football cup, and a third season of the unified competition. The competition started on 06 November 2002 with the First Round and concluded on 27 May 2003 with the Final." .

lsd:Entity_17467 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1901 Argentine Primera División was the tenth season of top_flight football in Argentina. The season began on 19 May 1901 and ended on 30 August 1901." .

lsd:Entity_17476 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 581, adopted on 13 February 1986, after hearing representations from Sudan and the front_line states and reaffirming resolutions 567 (1985), 568 (1985), 571 (1985), 572 (1985) and United Nations Security Council Resolution 580 (1985), the Council strongly condemned \"racist South Africa\" for its recent threats to perpetrate acts of aggression against neighbouring countries in southern Africa." .

lsd:Entity_17488 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011–12 Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup is the seventieth season of Bosnia and Herzegovina's annual association football cup, and a twelfth season of the unified competition. The competition started on 14 September 2011 and concluded on 16 May 2012. The following 32 teams competed in Round 1: (Team in bold is the winner) 1 Of the 32 participants, the Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina has 20 clubs, while the Republika of Srpska has 11. The draws for the round of 32 was conducted in Sarajevo at 12:00 (CEST) on 6 14 September 2011 in hotel \"Art\". All 32 clubs entered the competition from this round, while the matches were played on 14 September 2011." .

lsd:Entity_17531 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bulgarian coup d'état of 1934, also known as the 1934 Bulgarian coup d'état (Bulgarian: Деветнадесетомайски преврат, Devetnadesetomayski prevrat), was a coup d'état in the Kingdom of Bulgaria carried out by the Zveno military organization and the Military Union with the aid of the Bulgarian Army. Taking advantage of the discord in the Popular Bloc in the spring of 1934, the Zveno activists carried out the coup on the eve of 19 May 1934, ahead of Aleksandar Tsankov's supporters, who had planned a coup for 20 May. In foreign policy, the Zveno's most notable act was to establish diplomatic relations with the USSR on 23 July 1934 and steer Bulgaria towards France." .

lsd:Entity_17550 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Murder of Ofir Rahum was a shooting attack which occurred on 17 January 2001, in which Palestinian militants from the Tanzim faction of Fatah killed 16_year_old Israeli high school student Ofir Rahum on the outskirts of Ramallah." .

lsd:Entity_17567 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Skirmish of Arisaig took place on 16 17 May 1746 at Arisaig, Scotland and was the last armed conflict of the Jacobite rising of 1745." .

lsd:Entity_17579 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1842 United States House of Representatives elections for the 28th Congress were held during President John Tyler's term at various dates in different states between 1842 and February 1844. Maryland's elections to the next Congress were 1844 United States House of Representatives elections, after the 1842–1843 election cycle was passed and almost after the next Congress completed." .

lsd:Entity_17630 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Artscape Nordland (Skulpturlandskap Nordland) is an international art project that aims to bring art to people where they live, art museums being few and far apart in the sparsely populated county of Nordland. The project has been celebrated by the composers Kari Beate Tandberg and Karsten Brustad who working together wrote «Skulpturlandskap Nordland – en musikalsk dialog» (\"Artscape Nordland: a musical dialogue\")." .

lsd:Entity_17638 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Malacca occurred in 1568, when the Sultan of Aceh Alauddin attacked the Portuguese_held city of Portuguese Malacca." .

lsd:Entity_17674 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 KNVB Cup Final was a association football match between AZ Alkmaar and AFC Ajax on 2007 at De Kuip, Rotterdam. It was the final match of the 2006–07 KNVB Cup competition. AFC Ajax beat AZ Alkmaar on penalties after the match finished 1–1 after extra time." .

lsd:Entity_17716 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010–11 Taça de Portugal, also known as Taca de Portugal Millennium for sponsorship reasons, was the 71st season of the Taca de Portugal. A total of 172 clubs from all four tiers of Portugal association football took part in this tournament." .

lsd:Entity_17791 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "symbiogenesis, or endosymbiotic theory, is the leading evolutionary theory of the origin of eukaryotic cells from prokaryotic organisms. Essay on the Theory of symbiogenesis, he wrote, \"The theory of symbiogenesis is a theory of selection relying on the phenomenon of symbiosis.\"" .

lsd:Entity_17816 a lsd:Context_narration ;
