lsd:Entity_17914 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Fourteenth Ordinary General Assembly of the Synod of Bishops, popularly referred to as the Synod on the Family, took place from 4 to 25 October 2015 with the theme of \"the vocation and mission of the family in the Church and in the contemporary world.\" On Sunday, 18 04 October 2015 Francis canonized Louis and Marie_Azélie Guérin Martin." .

lsd:Entity_17921 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1959 Volta a Catalunya was the 39th edition of the Volta a Catalunya cycle race and was held from 06 September 1959 to 13 September 1959." .

lsd:Entity_17928 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1970 European Rowing Championships were rowing championships held on Lake Öreg in Tata, Hungary." .

lsd:Entity_17942 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1840 United States presidential election in Pennsylvania took place between October 30 and 1840, as part of the 1840 United States presidential election. Pennsylvania voted for Whig challenger William Henry Harrison over Democratic incumbent Martin Van Buren by just 334 votes, a margin of 0.12%. It is the narrowest margin of victory in a presidential election in Pennsylvania history, with Donald Trump's 2016 win following close behind at 0.72%." .

lsd:Entity_17949 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Guangzhou Uprising, Canton Uprising or Canton Riots of 1927 was a failed communist uprising in the city of Guangzhou (Canton) in southern China. On 11 December 1927, the political leadership of the CPC ordered about 20,000 communist_leaning soldiers and armed workers to organize a \"Red Guard\" and take over Guangzhou." .

lsd:Entity_17973 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1994 Australian FAI Indycar Grand Prix was the opening round of the 1994 IndyCar season, held on 20 March 1994 on the Surfers Paradise Street Circuit, Australia." .

lsd:Entity_17978 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Tomaszów Mazowiecki (Polish: Bitwa pod Tomaszowem Mazowieckim) refers to the battle on 06 September 1939 near the town of Tomaszów Mazowiecki, Second Polish Republic, during the Invasion of Poland." .

lsd:Entity_17995 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Council of Constantinople was convened in late 1094 by the Byzantine emperor Alexios I Komnenos and held in Constantinople at Palace of Blachernae in order to resolve the case of Leo of Chalcedon." .

lsd:Entity_18047 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Denmark participated in the Denmark in the Eurovision Song Contest 2017. Prior to the 2017 contest, Denmark had participated in the Eurovision Song Contest forty_five times since their first entry in 1957. In the Denmark in the Eurovision Song Contest 2016, \"Soldiers of Love\" performed by Lighthouse X failed to qualify Denmark to the final, making it the second consecutive year that Denmark missed out on qualification. Dansk Melodi Grand Prix 2017 was the 47th edition of Dansk Melodi Grand Prix, the music competition that selects Denmark's entries for the Eurovision Song Contest. Denmark was placed into the second semi_final, to be held on 2017, and was scheduled to perform in the first half of the show." .

lsd:Entity_18072 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Myanmar National League (known as the Ooredoo Myanmar National League for sponsorship reasons) is the 6th season of the Myanmar National League, the top Burmese professional league for association football clubs. The Myanmar National League will be temporarily suspended for three months from 8 March to 22 June due to the 2015 Southeast Asian Games held in Singapore. The 2015 transfer window for Myanmar National League clubs will open from 2015 to 2015. This season will be the first Myanmar National League season to have Ooredoo as the title sponsor, after penning a deal worth US $1.5 million per year on 2015. A total of 12 teams will compete in the league: 10 sides from the 2014 season and two promoted teams from the 2014 Myanmar National League 2. Fixtures and Results of the Myanmar National League 2015 season." .

lsd:Entity_18076 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Illinois–Missouri football rivalry, also known as the Arch Rivalry, is an American college football rivalry between the Illinois Fighting Illini football team of the University of Illinois and Missouri Tigers football team of the University of Missouri." .

lsd:Entity_18124 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Tushino bombing was a terrorist attack that occurred on 05 July 2003, at Tushino airfield in Moscow, Russia, killing 15 people and injuring up to 60 more. Only a few meters away from where Elikhadzhiyeva had detonated, 26_year_old Zinaida Aliyeva detonated her explosives 15 minutes later, killing 11 people on the spot while at least 60 people were injured, with four of them later dying in hospital. The Tushino bombing was part of a string of suicide attacks in Russia that had occurred within the previous four months, killing 165 people in total, in the context of the Second Chechen War." .

lsd:Entity_18199 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sinhalese–Portuguese War was a series of conflicts waged from 1527 to 1658 during the Transitional and Kandyan periods in Sri Lanka between the Sinhalese kingdoms and their allies, against the Portuguese Empire. The last Portuguese forces were expelled from Sri Lanka entirely in 1658." .

lsd:Entity_18221 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Drakenburg (German: Schlacht bei Drakenburg) took place on 23 May 1547 to the north of Nienburg, between the Protestant army of the Schmalkaldic League and the Holy Roman Empire troops of Eric II, Duke of Brunswick_Lüneburg, Prince of Calenberg. After Eric was informed of the approach of the enemy near Drakenburg, he ordered his soldiers to get into battle formation. The units under the command of Wrisberg reached the battlefield on 23 May 1547, but the battle was already over." .

lsd:Entity_18227 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The papal bull Aeterni regis was issued on 21 June 1481 by Sixtus IV." .

lsd:Entity_18278 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Norwegian Premier League was the 61st completed season of top division association football in Norway. The season began on 09 April 2006 and ended on 05 November 2006." .

lsd:Entity_183 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "July 2009 Moldovan parliamentary election were held in Moldova on 29 July 2009. The Party of Communists of the Republic of Moldova won 48 of the 101 seats, but lost the majority they had won in the April 2009 Moldovan parliamentary election." .

lsd:Entity_18303 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Korea National League, also known as the Incheon International Airport Korea National League due to sponsorship reasons, was the 14th season of the Korea National League, the third tier of South Korea's football league system. The 2016 season operated in the same system as in 2015 Korea National League, with the ten member clubs playing each other a total of three times each before the top four sides compete in the post_season championship playoff series." .

lsd:Entity_18315 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bangka Island massacre (also spelled Banka Island massacre) was committed during World War II in the Pacific, on Bangka Island, east of Sumatra in the Indonesian archipelago. On 16 February 1942, Imperial Japanese soldiers machine_gunned 22 Australian Army nurses and 60 Australian and British soldiers and crew members who had survived the sinking of Vyner Brooke by Japanese bombers. About 100 survivors reunited near Radji Beach at Bangka Island in the Dutch East Indies (now Indonesia), including 22 of the original 65 nurses." .

lsd:Entity_18322 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Carmen de Patagones school shooting occurred on 28 September 2004 at the \"Islas Malvinas\" Institute in Carmen de Patagones, Buenos Aires Province, Argentina. The morning of Tuesday 28 September 2004, in the middle school N°202 \"Islas Malvinas\" in Carmen de Patagones, a 15_year_old student named Rafael Solich, known as \"Junior\", opened fire upon his classmates in their classroom." .

lsd:Entity_18377 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 ATP Challenger China International – Nanchang was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in Nanchang, China between 12 September 2016 and 17 September 2016." .

lsd:Entity_18381 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The football (soccer) 2001 Campeonato Brasileiro Série B, the second level of Brazilian National League, was played from August 11 to 2001. The competition had 28 clubs and two of them were promoted to Série A and six were relegated to Campeonato Brasileiro Série C. Paysandu S.C. finished the final phase group with the most points, and was declared 2001 Campeonato Brasileiro Série B champions, claiming the promotion to the 2002 Série A along with Figueirense, the runners_up." .

lsd:Entity_1840 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 World Baseball Classic was the inaugural tournament between national baseball teams that included players from Major League Baseball. It was held from March 3 to 20 in stadiums that are in and around Tokyo; San Juan, Puerto Rico; Lake Buena Vista, Florida; Phoenix, Arizona; Scottsdale, Arizona; Anaheim, California; and San Diego. The first World Baseball Classic featured 16 teams in a round_robin. Seven stadiums were used during the tournament: The teams selected for the inaugural World Baseball Classic were chosen because they were judged to be the \"best baseball_playing nations in the world and provide global representation for the event.\"" .

lsd:Entity_18418 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Solheim Cup was the 13th edition of the Solheim Cup matches, held on August 16–18 at the Colorado Golf Club in Parker, Colorado, southeast of Denver. Points were earned beginning with the 2011 Solheim Cup LPGA Hana Bank Championship and concluding with the 2013 Women's British Open. 1Age at the start of the 2013 Solheim Cup matches on 2013 (Pepper turned 48 during the matches). 1Age at the start of the 2013 Solheim Cup matches on 2013." .

lsd:Entity_18426 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Versailles rail accident occurred on 08 May 1842 in the cutting between Meudon and Bellevue stations on the railway between Versailles and Paris following celebrations at the Palace of Versailles marking King Louis Philippe's saint's day." .

lsd:Entity_18454 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Arkansas–Texas A&M football rivalry is an American college football rivalry between the Arkansas Razorbacks football and Texas A&M Aggies football, which started in 1903." .

lsd:Entity_18491 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 British Academy Scotland New Talent Awards were held on 25 March 2014 at The Arches." .

lsd:Entity_18496 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Cap de la Roque was a naval battle that took place on 22 May 1703 between a Dutch convoy protected by captain Roemer Vlack and a French squadron under Alain Emmanuel de Coëtlogon, during the War of the Spanish Succession. This battle is sometimes called \"The Battle of the Bay of Biscay\", but this is geographical not correct, as Cabo da Roca is situated in the southern part of Portugal." .

lsd:Entity_18552 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Mount Dhaulagiri avalanches occurred in central Nepal during the month of October and resulted in the deaths of at least 43 people of various nationalities, including at least 21 trekkers. On 14 October 2014, a snowstorm and series of avalanche occurred on and around Annapurna and Dhaulagiri in the Manang District and Mustang District of Nepal within the Himalaya range. Twenty_one trekkers and guides from Nepal, Slovakia and Germany were rescued on 15 October after the avalanche the previous day. When search and rescue operations ceased on 19 October, up to 400 people had been rescued from various areas including Thorong La, the Manang District and Mustang District areas and the Tukuche basecamp of Mustang District." .

lsd:Entity_18565 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC Fight Night: Lewis vs. Abdurakhimov (also known as UFC Fight Night 102) was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on 09 December 2016, at Times Union Center in Albany, New York." .

lsd:Entity_18637 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Nietjärvi (15 July 1944–17 July 1944) was part of the Continuation War between Finland and the Soviet Union, which occurred during World War II. Finnish field artillery fired in U_line during five days period (11 July _15 July 1944) more rounds than in any other battle during summer 1944, total 54,300, while mortars fired 24,400." .

lsd:Entity_18649 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Anqing (安慶之戰) was a prolonged siege of the prefecture_level city of Anqing in Anhui, China, initiated by Hunan Army forces loyal to the Qing Dynasty against the Taiping Rebellion of the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom." .

lsd:Entity_1871 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Continental Airlines Flight 1713 was a commercial airline flight that crashed while taking off in a snowstorm from Stapleton International Airport in Denver, Colorado on 15 November 1987." .

lsd:Entity_18722 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Invercargill mayoral election finished on Saturday, 09 October 2010 and was conducted under the First Past the Post system using the postal voting system. The candidates for mayor included the incumbent Tim Shadbolt who contested a sixth consecutive term. Tim Shadbolt won the mayoral election and won a sixth term as Mayor of Invercargill, making him one of the longest_serving mayors in New Zealand." .

lsd:Entity_18751 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Armenian Cup was the tenth edition of the Armenian Independence Cup, a football competition. In 2001, the tournament had 16 participants, none of which were reserve teams. The first legs were played on 07 April 2001 and 2001. The firs3 27 May 2001 legs4 May 2001ed on 3 May and 2001." .

lsd:Entity_18764 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1989 Irish Professional Championship was a professional invitational snooker tournament, which took place in 01 February 1989 at the Antrim Forum in Antrim, Northern Ireland." .

lsd:Entity_18814 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A 1946 Albury state by_election was held for the New South Wales Legislative Assembly seat of Albury on Saturday, 1946. The seat was subsequently won by John Hurley of the Australian Labor Party (New South Wales Branch). At the 1946 federal election held on 28 September, Mair was unsuccessful with the Australian Labor Party (New South Wales Branch) winning all three NSW seats." .

lsd:Entity_18834 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's 400 metre individual medley competition at the 1999 Pan Pacific Swimming Championships – men's 400 metre individual medley took place on August 23 at the Sydney Olympic Park Aquatic Centre. The 1997 Pan Pacific Swimming Championships – men's 400 metre individual medley champion was Matthew Dunn of Australia." .

lsd:Entity_18864 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Pure Michigan 400 was a NASCAR Sprint Cup Series stock car Consumers Energy 400 held on 28 August 2016 at Michigan International Speedway in Brooklyn, Michigan. Contested over 200 laps on the two_mile (3.2 km) D_shaped oval, it was the 24th Consumers Energy 400 of the 2016 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series season. Kyle Larson won his first career Cup Series Consumers Energy 400, the Consumers Energy 400 had thirteen lead changes among different drivers and four cautions for 17 laps. Michigan International Speedway (MIS) is a two_mile (3.2 km) moderate_banked D_shaped speedway located off U.S. Highway 12 on more than 1,400 acres (5.7 km2) approximately four miles (6.4 km) south of the village of Brooklyn, in the scenic Irish Hills area of southeastern Michigan. Joey Logano scored the pole for the Consumers Energy 400 with a time of 35.697 and a speed of 201.698 mph (324.601 km/h)." .

lsd:Entity_18894 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1958 Ugandan general election were held in Uganda between 20 October 1958 and 24 October 1958." .

lsd:Entity_19013 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Edict of Restitution, passed eleven years into the Thirty Years' War on 06 March 1629, in the city of Vienna, following Catholic successes at arms, was a belated attempt by Ferdinand II to restore the religious and territorial situations reached in the Peace of Augsburg (1555), whose \"Ecclesiastical Reservation\" had impeded the secularization of Catholic church lands after 1555, as no further Catholic church lands could legally be transferred to Protestant control. With that principle confirmed by the Treaty at Augsburg, the violence of that earlier day between the Lutherans and the Catholics in Germany ended—at least for the generation, until renewed tensions brought about the Thirty Years' War. Behind all this were the inheritance practices in Europe as a whole and in particular the German states within the Holy Roman Empire." .

lsd:Entity_19027 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 Women's EuroHockey Nations Championship was the fourth edition of the field hockey championship organised by the European Hockey Federation. It was held in Amstelveen, Netherlands from 14 June 1995 to 25 June 1995." .

lsd:Entity_19050 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sama (Turkish: Sema, Persian, Urdu and Arabic: سَمَاع _ samā‘un) is a Sufi ceremony performed as dhikr." .

lsd:Entity_1912 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In Catholicism, the Miracle of Lanciano is a Eucharistic miracle which is alleged to have occurred in the eighth century in the city of Lanciano, Italy. The alleged miracle is usually described roughly as follows: In the city of Lanciano, Italy, then known as Anxanum, some time in the 700s, a Basilian hieromonk was assigned to celebrate Mass at the monastery of St. Longinus." .

lsd:Entity_19138 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1997 Papua New Guinean general election were held in Papua New Guinea between 14 June 1997 and 28 June 1997." .

lsd:Entity_19194 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1953 World Table Tennis Championships were held at the Floreasca and Dynamo Halls in Bucharest from 20 March 1953 to 29 March 1953." .

lsd:Entity_19202 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 Critérium du Dauphiné Libéré was the 43rd edition of the cycle race and was held from 03 June 1991 to 10 03 June 1991. The race started in Chamonix_Mont_Blanc and finished in Aix_les_Bains." .

lsd:Entity_19212 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1928 Tour of the Basque Country was the fifth edition of the Itzulia Basque Country cycle race and was held from 01 August 1928 to 05 August 1928. The race started in Bilbao and finished in Getxo." .

lsd:Entity_19217 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Turkish Cup Final was a association football match between Beşiktaş J.K. and Kayseri Erciyesspor. Beşiktaş won 1–0 after extra time. Beşiktaş beat Vestel Manisaspor 4_0 at home, and lost 0–2 away. In the Semi Finals Beşiktaş faced off, with one of their Istanbul rivals, Fenerbahçe S.K.. At home, Beşiktaş won 1–0. Away Beşiktaş ended the match down 1–0. In extra time though, Mert Nobre scored a goal for Beşiktaş making it 1–1. The 1st match ended 0–0 at home, and away 1_1. The results were a 1–0 win away and a 1–1 draw at home." .

lsd:Entity_1937 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Welwyn Tunnel rail crash took place in Welwyn North Tunnel, north of Welwyn (now Welwyn North) station on the Great Northern Railway, on 09 June 1866." .

lsd:Entity_19444 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "West Germany vs France was a FIFA World Cup semi_final match that took place in the Estadio Ramón Sánchez Pigone stadium in Seville, Spain on 08 July 1982 and is in both countries known as Night of Seville (German: Nacht von Sevilla, France national association football team: Nuit de Séville). Four minutes later, Germany national association football team began their comeback, with Rummenigge flicking home an outside_of_the_foot volley from six yards that cut France's lead to 3–2. The penalty shootout began with Giresse converting the first kick for France, which was answered by Germany national association football team's Manfred Kaltz. Amoros for France and Paul Breitner for Germany national association football team both converted, but in the third round, Uli Stielike's shot was blocked by Ettori, following Rocheteau's successful strike, giving France a 3–2 lead. However, in the fourth round, France failed to capitalise: Schumacher blocked Didier Six's shot, and Littbarski scored for Germany national association football team." .

lsd:Entity_19472 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 AFC Champions League Finals was the final match of the 2013 AFC Champions League, the thirty_second round of the top grade Asian club association football tournament. The first leg was hosted by FC Seoul at the Seoul World Cup Stadium in Seoul on 2013, while the second leg was hosted by Guangzhou Evergrande at the Tianhe Stadium in Guangzhou on 2013." .

lsd:Entity_19479 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Philippsburg was a siege of the fortress of Philippsburg during the Franco_Dutch War. This made it a constant threat to the Holy Roman Empire's west flank and at the outbreak of the Franco_Dutch War it became the jumping off point for several French incursions into the Palatinate and Neckar area. Charles V, Duke of Lorraine began the siege with a 40,000 strong imperial force on 01 May 1676." .

lsd:Entity_19495 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1896 United States presidential election in New York took place on 03 November 1896. New York was won by the Republican nominees, former Governor William McKinley of Ohio and his running mate corporate lawyer Garret Hobart of New Jersey. McKinley would lose New York City to Bryan in their 1900 United States presidential election in New York rematch four years later and Bryan would later win the city again against William Howard Taft in 1908." .

lsd:Entity_19537 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Tientsin, or the Relief of Tianjin, occurred on 13 July 1900–14 July 1900, during the Boxer Rebellion in Northern China. On 13 July 1900, the allied force to assault the walled city of Tianjin consisted of about 6,900 soldiers: 2,500 Russians, 2,000 Japanese, 900 Americans, 800 British, 600 French, and 100 Germans and Austrians. For the Eight_Nation Alliance, Tianjin was the bloodiest battle of the Boxer Rebellion. In the Nankai District of Tianjin in present_day China, a \"Nie Shicheng Martyrs Monument\" is in the area, to General Nie Shicheng who died in battle at the Battle of Tientsin." .

lsd:Entity_19545 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sexual abuse scandal in the Catholic archdiocese of Boston was part of a series of Catholic Church sexual abuse cases in the United States that revealed widespread crimes in the American Roman Catholic Church. The events in the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Boston exploded into a national Catholic Church sexual abuse cases. In June 2004, much of the land around the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Boston headquarters was sold to Boston College, in part to raise money for legal costs associated with the scandal. Ward was suspended by the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Boston in 2002 and dismissed by the Vatican in 2005." .

lsd:Entity_19559 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Earth México 2012, the 11th annual national beauty pageant of Miss Earth México, will be held late summer of 2012. The winner of Miss Earth México 2012 will represent Mexico in the international Miss Earth 2012 pageant which will be held on 2012 in Philippines. Special awards were given during the Miss Earth México 2012 coronation night as follows: The following is the list of delegates that represented the 32 States of Mexico as listed in the Miss Earth Mexico 2012 website including their height and age during the pageant:" .

lsd:Entity_19628 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Prison Fatal (Spanish for \"Deadly Prison\") was a major lucha libre event produced and scripted by the Mexican International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) professional wrestling promotion on 03 February 2000. The Prison Fatal show was the first confirmed IWRG show that used the name, with it becoming a regular event with the 2012 Prisión Fatal show. The main event was the eponymous Prisión Fatal Steel cage match where the last person remaining in the cage was forced to unmasked per the match stipulation. The Prison Fatal show was the first time that IWRG promoted a show under that name, and it was not used again until the 2012 Prisión Fatal show. The event featured at least two, and most likely more, professional wrestling matches with different wrestlers involved in pre_existing scripted feuds, plots and storylines. The main event Prisión Fatal steel cage match included 12 wrestlers in total and had a 10_minute time limit, where all wrestlers had to remain in the ring before they would be allowed to climb over the top of the cage to safety." .

lsd:Entity_19649 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Witch's Cradle (1944), sometimes billed as Witches' Cradle, is an unfinished, silent, experimental short film written and directed by Maya Deren, featuring Marcel Duchamp, and filmed in Peggy Guggenheim's Art of This Century gallery. The Witch's Cradle was written and directed by experimental filmmaker Maya Deren." .

lsd:Entity_19687 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Trani Cup was a professional tennis tournament played on clay court. It took place in Trani, Italy between 09 August 2010 and 15 August 2010." .

lsd:Entity_19717 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Asian Junior Badminton Championships is an Asia continental junior championships to crown the best U_19 badminton players across Asia. This tournament were held in Tennis Indoor Senayan, Gelora Bung Karno Sports Complex, Jakarta, Indonesia from 11 July 2005–17 July 2005." .

lsd:Entity_19759 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The September 2010 Quetta bombing occurred on 03 September 2010 in Quetta, Pakistan." .

lsd:Entity_19765 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Stampex is a twice yearly British Philatelic exhibition held at the Business Design Centre (BDC) at Islington, London, every Spring and Autumn." .

lsd:Entity_19771 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1969–70 FIBA European Cup Winner's Cup was the fourth edition of FIBA Europe's 2nd_tier level European_wide professional club basketball competition, contested between national domestic cup champions, running from 04 December 1969, to 26 April 1970." .

lsd:Entity_19798 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Anthony Joshua vs. Joseph Parker, billed as Road to Undisputed, was a professional boxing heavyweight unification match contested between Anthony Joshua and Joseph Parker. The event took place on 31 March 2018 at Millennium Stadium in Cardiff, Wales, with Joshua's WBA (Super), IBF, and IBO titles and Parker's WBO title on the line." .

lsd:Entity_19827 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Relief of Montgomery Castle took place during the First English Civil War of 1642–1646. On 17 18 September 1644, a Parliamentarian force commanded by Sir John Meldrum advanced to engage a Royalist army led by Lord Byron which was besieging Montgomery Castle in mid Wales." .

lsd:Entity_19850 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "South Korea at the 2012 Asian Beach Games participated in the 2012 Asian Beach Games in Haiyang, China on 2012–2012." .

lsd:Entity_19858 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Tughlaqabad (also known as the Battle of Delhi) was a notable battle fought on 07 October 1556 between Hem Chandra Vikramaditya, also known as Hemu and the forces of the Mughal emperor Akbar led by Tardi Beg Khan at Tughlaqabad Fort near Delhi. The battle ended in a victory for Hem Chandra who took possession of Delhi and claimed royal status, assuming the title of Raja Vikramaditya. Hemu, who had set off in pursuit of Agra's governor, reached Tughlaqabad Fort, a village just outside Delhi where he ran into Tardi Beg Khan's forces. He took possession of Delhi after a day's battle on 07 October 1556." .

lsd:Entity_19900 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Jaji occurred in 17 April 1987, during the first stage of withdrawal of Soviet forces from Soviet–Afghan War. Remaining Soviet troops supported the Democratic Republic of Afghanistan's operations in Paktia against the Mujahideen, hoping to relieve a besieged garrison at Ali Sher, and cut off supply lines to the Mujahideen from Pakistan." .

lsd:Entity_19907 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1976 VFL Grand Final was an Australian rules football game contested between the Hawthorn Football Club and North Melbourne Football Club at the Melbourne Cricket Ground on 25 September 1976. It was the 80th annual VFL/AFL Grand Final of the Victorian Football League, staged to determine the premiers for the 1976 VFL season." .

lsd:Entity_1994 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Lathen train collision occurred on 22 September 2006 when a Transrapid magnetic levitation (or \"maglev\") train collided with a maintenance vehicle near Lathen, Germany, killing 23 people." .

lsd:Entity_19949 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 DFB_Ligapokal Final decided the winner of the 2004 DFB_Ligapokal, the 8th edition of the reiterated DFB_Ligapokal, a knockout association football cup competition. The match was played on 2004 at the Stadion am Bruchweg in Mainz. FC Bayern Munich won the match 3–2 against SV Werder Bremen for their 5th title." .

lsd:Entity_19978 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 Cup of Russia was the fifth event of six in the 1998–99 ISU Grand Prix of Figure Skating, a senior_level international invitational competition series. It was held in Moscow on 26 November 1998–29." .

lsd:Entity_19983 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Irish presidential election, 1959 was held on 17 June 1959. Éamon de Valera, then Taoiseach, was elected as President of Ireland." .

lsd:Entity_20006 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Democratic Party (Italy) leadership election was an open primary election held in November–08 December 2013. After having come first in the vote by party members, Matteo Renzi was elected by a landslide 68% in a three_way primary on 08 December 2013." .

lsd:Entity_20015 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Minolta A_mount camera system was a line of photographic equipment from Minolta introduced in 1985 with the world's first integrated autofocus system in the camera body with interchangeable lenses. In Europe, early Minolta A_mount cameras were initially identified by a 4 digit number followed by Minolta AF. The last film_based Minolta AF SLRs produced by Minolta were the Maxxum 50 (a.k.a." .

lsd:Entity_20018 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2000 Northern Cyprus presidential election were held in Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus on 15 April 2000." .

lsd:Entity_20025 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Ironman World Championship was a long distance triathlon competition held on 2012 in Kailua_Kona, Hawaii. The Ironman 2012 series consisted of 28 Ironman races plus the 2011 Ironman World Championship which was itself a qualifier for the 2012 Championship." .

lsd:Entity_20037 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2009–10 Eurocup Basketball was the eighth edition of Europe's second_tier level transnational competition for men's professional basketball clubs, the EuroCup Basketball. The competition was won by Spanish club Valencia BC, who won their second EuroCup Basketball title, and also secured a place in the 2010–11 edition of the EuroCup Basketball's parent competition, the EuroLeague." .

lsd:Entity_20054 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 EBSA European Under_21 Snooker Championships took place in Bucharest, Romania between 18 March 2014_23 March 2014. For winning the tournament, Oliver Lines was rewarded with a place in the 2014/15 snooker season." .

lsd:Entity_20124 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In version control systems, a commit is an operation which sends the latest changes to the source code to the repository, making these changes part of the head revision of the repository. In this context, a commit within a version control system is protected as it is easily rolled back, even after the commit has been applied. To commit a change in git on the command line, assuming git is installed, the following command is run: git commit _m 'commit message' This is also assuming that the files within the current directory have been staged as such: git add . The above command adds all of the files in the working directory to be staged for the git commit. Also, a shortcut to add all the unstaged files and make a commit at the same time is: git commit _a _m 'commit message' To commit a change in Mercurial on the command line, assuming hg is installed, the following command is used: hg commit __message 'Commit Message' This is also assuming that the files within the current directory have been staged as such: hg add. The above command adds all of the files in the working directory to be staged for the Mercurial commit." .

lsd:Entity_20153 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Women's Pan American Cup was the fifth edition of the Women's Pan American Cup, the quadrennial international women's field hockey championship of the Americas organised by the Pan American Hockey Federation. It was held between 2017 and 2017 in Lancaster, Pennsylvania, United States, simultaneously with the men's tournament." .

lsd:Entity_20173 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Candomblé Jejé, also known as Brazilian Vodum, is one of the major branches (nations) of Candomblé." .

lsd:Entity_20198 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 All_Ireland Senior Club Hurling Championship Final was a hurling match played at Croke Park, Dublin, the headquarters of the Gaelic Athletic Association, on Wednesday, 2010, to determine the winners of the 2009–10 All_Ireland Senior Club Hurling Championship. The match was won by Ballyhale Shamrocks GAA of Kilkenny, who beat Portumna GAA of Galway by 1_19 to 0_17. Prior to the 2010 final, Ballyhale Shamrocks GAA and Portumna GAA had previously met only once in the All_Ireland championship." .

lsd:Entity_2027 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1966 Daytona 500, the 8th running of the Daytona 500, was won by Richard Petty driving a 1966 Plymouth on 27 February 1966. The 1966 Daytona 500 was the fifth Daytona 500 of 49 in the 1966 NASCAR Grand National Series, which included the two qualifying races for the 500. The 1966 NASCAR Grand National Series opened in Augusta with Petty taking the win in the season inaugural Daytona 500. Dan Gurney followed with a win in Riverside before the drivers and their teams ventured to Daytona International Speedway for the 500_mile (800 km) Daytona 500. David Pearson won the NASCAR Grand National Series Championship after winning 15 events while 168 drivers competed in at least one Daytona 500 during the 1966 NASCAR Grand National Series. Richard Petty captured the pole position for the Daytona 500 with a speed of 175.165 miles per hour (281.901 km/h). After starting on the 1966 Daytona 500 pole, Petty went on to lead the first six laps of the Daytona 500, before relinquishing the lead to Paul Goldsmith, who had started in the third position. The victory by Petty was his second at the Daytona International Speedway, having won the Daytona 500 in 1964. Richard Petty's victory at the 1966 Daytona 500 was the first and only time that he captured the pole position, despite winning the Daytona 500 a record seven times? As of 2009, Richard Petty is the only driver to win the Daytona 500 seven times: 1964, 1966, 1971, 1973, 1974, 1979, and 1981. The 1966 Daytona 500 was the first time that a driver won the Daytona 500 for a second time." .

lsd:Entity_20318 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "KotoriCon was an annual two_day anime convention held during January at Rowan College at Gloucester County (formerly known as Gloucester County College) in Sewell, New Jersey. The convention in 2010 started under the name Gloucester County Anime Convention. The third KotoriCon was in two locations, Pitman High School and Gloucester County College; in the first location, a concert by Eyeshine took place on January 6, 2012." .

lsd:Entity_20322 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Typhoon Longwang, known in the Philippines as Typhoon Maring, was the deadliest tropical cyclone to impact China during the 2005 Pacific typhoon season. Typhoon Longwang, weakened from its passage of Taiwan, struck mainland China late on October 2 as a low_end typhoon." .

lsd:Entity_2033 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "AAA When Worlds Collide (Spanish: Cuando Los Mundos Chocan) was a professional wrestling pay_per_view (PPV) event that took place on 06 November 1994, at the Los Angeles Memorial Sports Arena in Los Angeles. For the match, Hijo del Santo and Octagón would \"bet\" their masks against the hair of Barr and Guerrero, a challenge that La Pareja del Terror eagerly accepted, and the match was set for the AAA When Worlds Collide show in Los Angeles. After Triplemanía III_A, Aguayo began teaming with his son Perro Aguayo Jr. as the latter began his professional wrestling career." .

lsd:Entity_20333 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 33rd Grey Cup was played on 01 December 1945, before 18,660 fans at Varsity Stadium at Toronto. The Toronto Argonauts defeated the Winnipeg Blue Bombers 35 to 0." .

lsd:Entity_20337 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In the 2008 Agartala bombings at least 4 people were killed and a 100 injured on 01 October 2008 in a series of 5 blasts set off in Agartala, capital of the Indian state of Tripura, within 45 minutes, while two unexploded bombs were defused." .

lsd:Entity_20368 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jürgen Melzer and Philipp Petzschner won the title, defeating the Polish team of Mariusz Fyrstenberg and Marcin Matkowski in the final, 6–2, 6–2." .

lsd:Entity_20387 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Ladies Tour of Qatar was the 8th edition of the Ladies Tour of Qatar. It took place from 02 February 2016 until 05 February 2016 and consisted of 4 stages. A year after her last stage win, also at Al Shamal, Ellen van Dijk made the best of her time_trialling skills to conquer her third success in Qatar." .

lsd:Entity_20471 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1950 Wimbledon Championships took place on the outdoor grass courts at the All England Lawn Tennis and Croquet Club in Wimbledon, United Kingdom. The tournament was held from Monday 26 June 1950 until Saturday 08 July 1950. It was the 64th staging of the Wimbledon Championships, and the third Grand Slam tennis event of 1950." .

lsd:Entity_20506 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In 03 November 2015, Turkish Security Forces launched the Siege of Silvan (2015) _ an operation and a curfew in the city of Silvan, directed against the PKK_affiliated group YDG_H. The curfew was started on 03 November 2015 and lifted on 14 November 2015, during the time the military and police forces held anti_terror operations in the three neighborhoods of Konak, Mescit and Tekel." .

lsd:Entity_20512 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 58th Edition of Vuelta a España (Tour of Spain), a long_distance bicycle stage race and one of the three grand tours, was held from 6 September to 28 September 2003. It consisted of 21 stages covering a total of 2,957 km (1,837 mi), and was won by Roberto Heras of the US Postal cycling team. Isidro Nozal lead the general classification for much of the race until succumbing to the pressure posed by Roberto Heras who closed the gap to Nozal over the final days and took the jersey in the final time trial. The points classification was won by Erik Zabel from Germany, the mountains classification was won by Félix Cárdenas from Colombia and the combination classification was won by Alejandro Valverde." .

lsd:Entity_2059 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992 WTA Tour Championships were held in New York City, United States of America between 16 November 1992 and 22 November 1992." .

lsd:Entity_20626 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Greater Poland Civil War (Polish: Wojna domowa w Wielkopolsce) refers to the conflict that took place during 1382–1385 in the Greater Poland province of the Kingdom of Poland during the interregnum period following the transition of power between the Piast dynasty, Angevin dynasty and the Jagiellon dynasty." .

lsd:Entity_2067 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 BET Hip Hop Awards are a recognition ceremony held on 2009 at the Atlanta Civic Center in Atlanta, Georgia. The 2009 show was hosted by Mike Epps. Kanye West led the BET Hip_Hop Awards 2009 with nine nominations, followed by Jay_Z and Lil Wayne with seven and T.I." .

lsd:Entity_20695 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1917–18 Austrian football championship season was the seventh season of top_tier football in Austria. It was won by Floridsdorfer AC who would finish ahead of SK Rapid Wien by goal difference." .

lsd:Entity_207 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1973 World Series was the World Series of Major League Baseball's (MLB) 1973 Major League Baseball season. The 70th edition of the World Series, it was a best_of_seven playoff played between the American League (AL) champion (and defending World Series champion) Oakland Athletics and the National League (NL) champion New York Mets. Starting in 1974 World Series, MLB printed an official World Series program that was sold in both stadiums. The 1973 Mets' .509 season winning percentage is the lowest posted by any pennant winner in Major League Baseball history. The final standings: At 82–79, the 1973 New York Mets had the worst record of any team to play in a World Series. In four World Series (1951, 1954, 1962, and 1973), Mays did not hit a single home run. AL Oakland A's (4) vs. NL New York Mets (3) The Mets and A's opened the Series in Oakland with Jon Matlack and Ken Holtzman as the Game 1 starters (Matlack, with a 14–16 record during the 1973 Major League Baseball season, is one of only four pitchers in history to start Game 1 of a World Series after a regular season losing record). Along with blinding sunshine \"turn every fly ball into adventure\" (especially for a 42_year_old Willie Mays), Curt Gowdy described the contest in the official MLB 1973 Fall Classic highlight film as one of the \"longest and weirdest games in World Series history\". Vern Hoscheit, a coach with the A's in 1973, would win a World Series with the Mets as a coach in 1986." .

lsd:Entity_20703 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 CAF Confederation Cup Final was the final of 2012 CAF Confederation Cup, the 9th edition of the CAF Confederation Cup, Africa's secondary club association football competition organized by the Confederation of African Football (CAF). The final was played between Djoliba AC from Mali and AC Léopards from the Republic of the Congo. As the winner of the 2012 CAF Confederation Cup, they qualified to participate in the 2013 CAF Super Cup against the winner of the 2012 CAF Champions League." .

lsd:Entity_20710 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Russian Cup Final decided the winner of the 2014–15 Russian Cup, the 23rd season of Russia's main football cup. It was played on 21 May 2015 at the Central Stadium in Astrakhan, between FC Lokomotiv Moscow and FC Kuban Krasnodar. FC Lokomotiv Moscow came back from behind and emerged victorious with a 3_1 win in extra time. The Russian Cup final was held for the first time ever at Central Stadium in Astrakhan. Kuban Stadium in Krasnodar and Otkrytie Arena in Moscow were touted to be other potential alternatives but ultimately the stadium was announced by the Russian Football Union as the venue of the final through an official statement on Twitter on 2015. FC Lokomotiv Moscow played their 7th Russian Cup final, second only to CSKA's 10. Prior to the 2015 final, they have won five, against the seven won by their cross town rivals. As a side note, Leonid Kuchuk, the current manager of Kuban, faced FC Lokomotiv Moscow in the final after he was sacked from the same position earlier this season following a disappointing start at the helm of the Muscovite club." .

lsd:Entity_20715 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2019 ASB Classic (sponsored by ASB Bank) was a joint ATP and WTA tennis tournament, played on outdoor hard courts. It took place at the ASB Tennis Centre in Auckland, New Zealand, from 31 December 2018 to 2019 for the women, and from 7 to 12 January 2019 for the men." .

lsd:Entity_2076 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Babang (12 July 1965) was the fourth and last in a series of successful ambushes conducted between in May and 12 July 1965 by Australian troops from 3rd Battalion, Royal Australian Regiment (3 RAR), this time at Babang in Kalimantan (Indonesian Borneo), during the Indonesia–Malaysia confrontation." .

lsd:Entity_20773 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Heineken Open was a men's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It was the 33rd edition of the event known that year as the Heineken Open, and was part of the ATP International Series of the 2008 ATP Tour. It took place at the ASB Tennis Centre in Auckland, New Zealand, from 5 January through 13 January 2008." .

lsd:Entity_20786 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1947 Open Championship was the 76th The Open Championship, held 2 July–4 July at Royal Liverpool Golf Club in Hoylake. Fred Daly became the first Irish winner of the The Open Championship, one stroke ahead of runners_up Reg Horne and amateur Frank Stranahan." .

lsd:Entity_20796 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Paris_Tours was the 96th edition of the Paris–Tours cycle race and was held on 06 October 2002. The race started in Saint_Arnoult_en_Yvelines and finished in Tours." .

lsd:Entity_20820 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1869 Cachar earthquake occurred on 10 January 1869 with an estimated moment magnitude of 7.4 and a maximum EMS_98 intensity of VII (Damaging). The earthquake was felt in Upper Burma, Bihar, Jharkhand, Bengal and Northeast India." .

lsd:Entity_20824 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Turkish presidential election refers to two attempts to elect the country's President of Turkey, to succeed Ahmet Necdet Sezer. Turkey President of Turkey office is regarded as the guardian of the country's secular system; the fact that Gül's wife wears the Islamic headscarf, as well as his own history in political Islam, turned the elections into a political crisis. Abdullah Gül's candidacy was announced by Erdoğan on 2007 while calling Gül as his brother. He was the official candidate of the Justice and Development Party, thus making him the strongest candidate to be the President of Turkey of Turkey. On 2007, Foreign Minister Abdullah Gül withdrew his candidacy after the Parliament failed to achieve a quorum for a second time. On 2007, two days before the start of the nominations announcement for the President of Turkey elections, over one million protesters marched in the centre of Ankara, chanting slogans such as \"Turkey is secular, and it will remain secular\", and \"We do not want an imam for President\" to protest against the possibility of Prime Minister Erdoğan or another member of the Justice and Development Party standing in the President of Turkey elections. A second rally was organised for 2007 opposing the candidacy of Abdullah Gül from the Justice and Development Party, which has its roots in political Islam. On 2007, the Turkish Armed Forces issued a statement of its interests on its official website, later termed the \"e_memorandum\" by Ural Akbulut: \"...The problem that emerged in the President of Turkey election process is focused on arguments over secularism. The first round of voting took place on 2007, which resulted in Abdullah Gül, the Minister of Foreign Affairs and the official candidate of the Justice and Development Party, achieving 357 votes. As of 2007 and 2007, the following parties were represented in the Turkish Grand National Assembly and therefore could vote: Votes taken by Abdullah Gül was below the two_thirds of the vote needed, and so, there would be another round of voting in the following days. On 2007, the President of Turkey elections were postponed due to the lack of a candidate after the pullout of Abdullah Gül." .

lsd:Entity_20856 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Welsh Open was a professional ranking snooker tournament that took place between 24 January 1997–01 February 1997 at the Newport Centre in Newport, Wales. Stephen Hendry defeated Mark King 9–2 in the final to win his second Welsh Open title." .

lsd:Entity_20877 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The December 2011 Jabal al_Zawiya massacres took place on 19 20 December 2011–20 December 2011, in the Idlib province of Syria during the 2011_2012 Idlib Governorate clashes between the Syrian Army and opposition forces, within the larger scope of the 2011_2012 Syrian uprising." .

lsd:Entity_20881 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Cavalese cable car disaster of 1998, also known as the Strage del Cermis (Italy: Massacre of Cermis), occurred on 03 February 1998, near the Italy town of Cavalese, a ski resort in the Dolomites some 25 miles (40 km) northeast of Trento." .

lsd:Entity_20910 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Prince of Ning rebellion or rebellion of the Prince of Ning (Chinese: 寧王之亂) was a rebellion that took place in China between 10 July 1519 and 20 August 1519 during the Ming dynasty." .

lsd:Entity_20921 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Weber Cup, named after bowling legend Dick Weber, is a men's ten_pin bowling competition between Team Europe and Team USA. The Weber Cup is the annual Europe vs United States ten_pin bowling championships and is currently broadcast live from start to finish on Sky Sports in the UK and in many other international channels around the world. The 2008 Weber Cup took place once again at the Barnsley Metrodome, from 3 to 5 October 2008." .

lsd:Entity_20958 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 Goodwrench 500, was a NASCAR Winston Cup Series race held on 26 February 1995 at Rockingham Speedway in Richmond County, North Carolina." .

lsd:Entity_20969 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Myall Creek Massacre involved the killing of at least twenty_eight unarmed Indigenous Australians by twelve colonists on 10 June 1838 at the Myall Creek near the Gwydir River, in northern New South Wales. The poem expresses Dunlop's sorrow over the massacre and expresses sympathy for the Aboriginals of Australia. The Myall Creek Massacre is often cited as the only massacre of its kind in colonial Australia for which white people were subsequently executed. A memorial to the victims of the massacre was unveiled on 10 June 1838 2000, consisting of a granite rock and plaque overlooking the site of the massacre. The Myall Creek Massacre and Memorial Site was included on the Australian National Heritage List on 7 June 2008 and the New South Wales State Heritage Register on 12 November 2010." .

lsd:Entity_20975 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 Asian Men's Volleyball Championship was the 6th Asian Volleyball Championship, which took place from 11 August 1991 to 1991, in Perth, Western Australia." .

lsd:Entity_20979 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Garowe Principles were a set of agreements between the Transitional Federal Government (TFG) of Somalia and various Somali stakeholders outlining a framework for the interim administration's scheduled political transition in August 2012 to a permanent, representative government. The agreements were signed during the Somali National Consultative Constitutional Conference held in Garoowe, the administrative capital of the autonomous Puntland region." .

lsd:Entity_21028 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss Teen USA 2016 was the 34th Miss Teen USA pageant, was held at The Venetian in Las Vegas, Nevada on 2016." .

lsd:Entity_21040 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Scottish Women's Premier League (SWPL) was the fourteenth season of the Scottish Women's Premier League, the highest division of women's association football in Scotland since its inception in 2002. After 12 games the top two clubs, Glasgow City F.C. and Hibernian had moved 12 points clear of third placed Aberdeen." .

lsd:Entity_21090 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "401 (1791), was the first United States Supreme Court decision and the earliest case calling for oral argument. Van Staphorst v. Maryland (1791) was docketed prior to West v. Barnes but settled before the Court heard the case: West was argued on 1791 and decided on 1791. Despite lack of formal training, West represented himself pro se in the circuit court in 1791 before Chief Justice John Jay, Associate Justice William Cushing, and Henry Marchant. The court's opinion was extensively covered by period newspapers as no official court reporter was yet published in 1791, and the seriatim opinions were republished in the newspapers and are currently accessible in James R. Perry's The Documentary History of the Supreme Court of the United States, 1789_1800, Volume 6, \"West v. Barnes,\" pp." .

lsd:Entity_21098 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Loncomilla was the decisive battle of the 1851 Chilean Revolution between conservative government and liberal rebel forces on 08 December 1851." .

lsd:Entity_21141 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In the Netherlands, the Boekenweek (Dutch pronunciation: (listen); English: Book Week) is an annual \"week\" of ten days dedicated to Dutch literature. The beginning of the Boekenweek is marked by the Boekenbal (book ball), a gathering that is attended by writers and publishers. Since 2002, the Boekenweekgeschenk can be used as a ticket to travel for free by train with the Nederlandse Spoorwegen on the final Sunday of the Boekenweek. The curriculum vitae of the author of the Boekenweekgeschenk – called the Boekenweek_cv – is distributed by public libraries among their members. In 1932, the first Boekenweek was held and the first Boekenweekgeschenk was published. Despite competition from other media, including new technology since 1932, the Boekenweekgeschenk has grown in popularity over the years. In 2010, during the 75th Boekenweek, 958.000 copies of the Boekenweekgeschenk were produced." .

lsd:Entity_21151 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Kufra conflict started in the aftermath of the Libyan civil war, and involved armed clashes between the Tobu and Zuwayya tribes in the Kufra area of Cyrenaica, Libya." .

lsd:Entity_21199 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of the Vozha River (Russian Битва на реке Воже) was a battle fought between the Grand Duchy of Moscow and the Golden Horde on 11 August 1378." .

lsd:Entity_21299 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 British Virgin Islands general election was held in the British Virgin Islands on 07 November 2011. On 2011 Governor Boyd McCleary officially appointed Orlando Smith as the Premier under section 52(1) the constitution." .

lsd:Entity_21304 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The National Defence revolt (Greek: Κίνημα της Εθνικής Αμύνης) was a military uprising in Thessaloniki on 17 August 1916, by Greek Army officers opposed to the neutrality followed by the royal government in Athens during World War I, and sympathetic to former Prime Minister Eleftherios Venizelos and the Entente Powers." .

lsd:Entity_21316 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "dudum siquidem (Latin for \"A short while ago\") is a papal bull issued by Pope Alexander VI on 26 September 1493, one of the Bulls of Donation addressed to the Catholic Monarchs Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II of Aragon which supplemented the bull Inter caetera and purported to grant to them \"all islands and mainlands whatsoever, found and to be found, discovered and to be discovered, that are or may be or may seem to be in the route of navigation or travel towards the west or south, whether they be in western parts, or in the regions of the south and east and of India\". In August 1493 the Portuguese ambassadors Pêro Dias and Rui de Pina were in Barcelona negotiating with the Spanish over several issues, including the Portuguese intention to send a fleet to the New World to capture the islands discovered by Columbus, when Ferdinand and Isabella sent an appeal to the pope which resulted in the granting of dudum siquidem, dated 26 September 1493." .

lsd:Entity_21322 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Jaipur Literature Festival, or JLF, is an annual literary festival which takes place in the India city of Jaipur each January. The Festival is an Initiative of the Jaipur Virasat Foundation (JVF) founded by Faith Singh, originally as a segment of the Jaipur Heritage International Festival in 2006, and developed into a free_standing festival of literature standing on its own feet in 2008. The 2006 inaugural Jaipur Literature Festival featured 18 writers, including Hari Kunzru, William Dalrymple, Shobhaa De and Namita Gokhale and 14 others. Police said that Ruchir Joshi, Jeet Thayil, Hari Kunzru and Amitava Kumar fled Jaipur on the advice of officials at the Jaipur Literature Festival after reading excerpts from The Satanic Verses, which is banned in India. Rushdie expressed disappointment \"on behalf of India\", \"an India in which religious extremists can prevent free expression of ideas at a literary festival, in which the politicians are too, let's say, in bed with those groups...for narrow electoral reasons, in which the police forces are unable to secure venues against demonstrators even when they know the demonstration is on its way\". The festival also expanded beyond the four walls of Diggi Palace, holding more than 300 events in 10 venues, including the Music Stage at Clarks Amer, the Jaipur BookMark at Narain Niwas, and two special sessions at Amer Fort and Hawa Mahal to focus on heritage and culture, supported by Rajasthan Tourism. Notable sessions of the festival in 2015 included two packed sessions each for Nobel Laureate Sir V. S. Naipaul and former President of India, Dr APJ Abdul Kalam, who drew a 5,000_strong crowd to the Front Lawns of Diggi Palace. The Jaipur Lit Fest 2016 began at the Diggi Palace as scheduled, with Gair dance from Barmer, Rajasthan accompanied by a crowd that had been waiting since early morning. The 2018 Jaipur Literature Festival was organised from 25 to 29 January at the Diggi Palace in Jaipur. The Jaipur literature festival 2019 was organised in royal Diggi Palace Jaipur from 24 to 28 January 2019. Around 300 speakers were expected to visit Jaipur literature festival 2018–2019, including prominent writers such as Shobha de (known for her bold writing style), Anuradha Roy (India novelist, journalist), Chitra Banerjee (best known for her novel The palace of illusions). Here are few more names of Jaipur literature festival 2018–2019 are: The Jaipur Literature Festival 2020 took place at the royal Diggi Palace from 23 to 27 January 2020." .

lsd:Entity_21329 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Gavinana was a battle in the War of the League of Cognac. It was fought on 03 August 1530 between the city of Florence and the army of the Holy Roman Empire." .

lsd:Entity_21356 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Elwood Cooke and Bobby Riggs defeated Charles Hare and Frank Wilde in the final, 6–3, 3–6, 6–3, 9–7 to win the Gentlemen' Doubles tennis title at the 1939 Wimbledon Championship." .

lsd:Entity_21364 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992 Yukon general election (32nd general election) was held on 19 October 1992 to elect members of the 28th Legislative Assembly of the territory of Yukon, Canada." .

lsd:Entity_21384 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Canadian Open Badminton Championships was the eighth grand prix gold and grand prix tournament of the 2012 BWF Grand Prix Gold and Grand Prix. The tournament was held in Richmond Olympic Oval, Richmond, British Columbia, Canada 10 July 2012 until 15 July 2012 and had a total purse of $50,000." .

lsd:Entity_21404 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Glasgow (1544) was fought on 16 March 1544, between Matthew Stewart, 4th Earl of Lennox and the Scottish Regent James Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Arran, and their adherents, during the minority of Mary, Queen of Scots. There was a second battle at Glasgow Muir in May 1544 between Arran and the Earl of Glencairn. According to an English messenger, Edward Storye, it was reported that Hamilton then took the town of Glasgow and laid siege to Bishop's Castle on Wednesday 26 March 1544. Around 24 May 1544, Hamilton fought another battle on Glasgow Moor with the Earl of Glencairn." .

lsd:Entity_21420 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 UEFA Champions League Final was the 40th edition and took place in Vienna between AFC Ajax and A.C. Milan. It was A.C. Milan's third consecutive UEFA Champions League final, a feat which has since been matched in the Champions League era by Juventus between 1996 UEFA Champions League Final and 1998 and Real Madrid between 2016 and 2018, A.C. Milan was also aiming to tie Real Madrid's record of having won the European Cup/UEFA Champions League six times." .

lsd:Entity_21443 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Born and raised in Reykjavík, Björk began her music career at the age of 11 and first gained international recognition as the lead singer of the alternative rock band the Sugarcubes, whose 1987 single \"Birthday\" was a hit on UK and US indie stations and a favourite among music critics. Björk was born on 21 November 1965 in Reykjavík, where she grew up. At six, Björk enrolled at Reykjavík school Barnamúsíkskóli, where she studied classical piano and flute. The group was featured in the documentary Rokk í Reykjavík, with Björk being featured on the cover of the VHS release. Björk was featured on two tracks of the soundtrack for the 1992 film Remote Control (known as Sódóma Reykjavík in Iceland). Björk's former band, the Sugarcubes, reunited for a one_night_only concert in Reykjavík on 17 November 2006. Björk is currently set to embark on her eleventh concert tour, called Björk Orkestral, in which she will perform orchestral arrangements of songs from her career so far. On 21 May 2010, Björk wrote an open letter in The Reykjavík Grapevine, calling on the Icelandic government to \"do everything in its power to revoke the contracts with Magma Energy\", the Canadian company which now has complete ownership of Icelandic geothermal company HS Orka. In 1998, Björk invited Stína to perform as her support act on the Homogenic Tour, and in 2004 Stína contributed to the production of Medúlla." .

lsd:Entity_21478 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 China Open was a professional ranking snooker tournament that took place between 24 February 2002 – 03 March 2002 at the International Gymnastic Centre in Shanghai, People's Republic of China." .

lsd:Entity_21502 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 European Athletics Championships – women's 1500 metres at the 2006 European Athletics Championships were held at the Ullevi on August 11 and August 13." .

lsd:Entity_21517 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Kaiserswerth (18 April 1702 – 15 June 1702), was a siege of the War of the Spanish Succession." .

lsd:Entity_21541 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Grand Prix was a professional snooker tournament and the first of eight WPBSA ranking events in the Snooker season 1997/1998 season, preceding the UK Championship. It was held from 14 to 26 October 1997 at the Bournemouth International Centre in Bournemouth, England." .

lsd:Entity_21587 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 European Youth Summer Olympic Days was the fifth edition of multi_sport event for European youths between the ages of 12 and 18. It was held in Esbjerg, Denmark from 10 to 16 July 1999." .

lsd:Entity_21617 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Maryland gubernatorial election was held on 2018. The date included the election of the Governor of Maryland, lieutenant Governor of Maryland, and all members of the Maryland General Assembly. Hogan thus became the second Republican Governor of Maryland of Maryland to win reelection, the first since 1954. Hogan was elected Governor of Maryland in 2014 Maryland gubernatorial election, defeating then_lieutenant Governor of Maryland Anthony G. Brown by a margin of 52–47; the result was considered one of the biggest election upsets that year. In 2018, Hogan had a 68% approval rating, the second_highest approval of any Governor of Maryland in the country, only behind Governor Charlie Baker of Massachusetts, who had a 71% approval rating. Following the Maryland Green Party's nominating procedure, the delegates of the Coordinating Council, which is the party's State Central Committee, made the decision to nominate the gubernatorial ticket as no other candidate had filed by the party's 2018 deadline." .

lsd:Entity_21645 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Alberta Winter Games is a multi_sport event that was hosted in Banff and Canmore, Alberta on February 6–9, 2014." .

lsd:Entity_21654 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Zieleńce was a battle in the Polish–Russian War of 1792, in defence of the Polish Constitution of 3 May 1791. The battle took place on 18 June 1792, between the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth Army of Józef Poniatowski and an Imperial Russian Army group under the command of General Irakly Morkov, which was a part of General Mikhail Krechetnikov's Russian forces invading the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth from the south." .

lsd:Entity_21728 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1963 Men's European Volleyball Championship was the sixth edition of the event, organized by Europe's governing volleyball body, the European Volleyball Confederation. It was hosted in various cities in Romania from 21 October 1963 to 02 November 1963, with the final taking place in Bucharest." .

lsd:Entity_21736 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Blumenau or Battle of Lamač was the last battle fought in the Austro_Prussian War, on 22 July 1866 (on the day of the conclusion of peace), with the Austrians defending against the Kingdom of Prussia army. Kingdom of Prussia scout patrols were in Malacky on 19 22 July 1866, and in two days the Kingdom of Prussia army occupied Stomfa (Stupava). On Sunday, the morning of 22 July 1866, the Kingdom of Prussia army began the attack on Lamacs." .

lsd:Entity_21810 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 Taça de Portugal Final was the final match of the 1992–93 Taça de Portugal, the 53rd season of the Taça de Portugal, the premier Portuguese association football cup competition organized by the Portuguese Football Federation (FPF). The match was played on 10 June 1993 at the Estádio Nacional in Oeiras, and opposed two Primeira Liga sides: S.L. Benfica and Boavista F.C.. S.L. Benfica defeated Boavista F.C. 5–2 to claim the Taça de Portugal for a twenty_second time in their history. In Portugal, the final was televised live on RTP. As a result of S.L. Benfica winning the Taça de Portugal, they qualified for the 1993 Supertaça Cândido de Oliveira where they took on 1992–93 Primeira Divisão winners Porto." .

lsd:Entity_21822 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Grito de Dolores (Spanish: Grito de Dolores) occurred in Dolores Hidalgo Municipality, Mexico, on 16 September 1810, when Roman Catholic priest Miguel Hidalgo y Costilla rang his church bell and gave the call to arms that triggered the Mexican War of Independence. His speech became known as the \"Grito de Dolores\". Mexico's independence from Spain took a decade of Mexican War of Independence. The President then recites a shout of patriotism (a Grito Mexicano) based upon the \"Grito de Dolores\", with the names of the important heroes of the Mexican War of Independence who were there on that historic day. On the morning of 16 September 1810, or Independence Day, the national military parade in honor of the holiday starts in the Zócalo and its outskirts, passes the Hidalgo Memorial and ends on the Paseo de la Reforma, Mexico City’s main boulevard, passing \"El Ángel de la Independencia\" memorial column and other places along the way. President Felipe Calderón made an exception by re_enacting the Grito in Dolores Hidalgo Municipality Hidalgo as part of the bicentennial celebrations on 16 September 1810 2010, even though he had already done so the night before from the National Palace balcony to launch the celebrations. Similar celebrations to the Presidential one occur in cities and towns throughout Mexico, and in Mexican embassies and consulates worldwide on 15 or 16 September 1810." .

lsd:Entity_21832 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Festival de Gramado (Portuguese: Festival de Gramado) is an international film festival held annually in the Brazil city of Gramado, Rio Grande do Sul, since 1973. Formed by the National Cinema Institute (Instituto Nacional de Cinema _ INC) in 1973, the Festival de Gramado was originally launched at the Hydrangeas Festivity (Festa das Hortênsias), where film exhibitions were promoted between 1969 and 1971. By the 1980s, it was already the most important film festival of Brazil." .

lsd:Entity_21870 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018–19 Big Bash League season or BBL|08 was the eighth season of the KFC Big Bash League, the professional men's Twenty20 domestic cricket competition in Australia. The title was won by Melbourne Renegades, who defeated Melbourne Stars at the Marvel Stadium. This was the first BBL season featuring the new cricket broadcasting rights deal made between Cricket Australia, Fox Sports Australia and Seven Network." .

lsd:Entity_21878 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1895 European Rowing Championships were rowing championships held on the Bruges_Ostend Canal in the Belgian city of Ostend on 15 September 1895. At the World Rowing Federation Congress held on 14 September and 15 September 1895, five nations were represented." .

lsd:Entity_21948 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Oregon–Oregon State rivalry (known as the Civil War until 2020) is a college rivalry between the University of Oregon and Oregon State University. The football rivalry is the seventh longest running rivalry in the United States of America, being first contested in 1894." .

lsd:Entity_21964 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Wimbledon Championships was a tennis tournament played on grass courts at the All England Lawn Tennis and Croquet Club in Wimbledon, London in the United Kingdom. It was the 113th edition of the Wimbledon Championships and were held from 21 June 1999 to 04 July 1999." .

lsd:Entity_21975 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 World Amateur Boxing Championships was held at the Heydar Aliyev Sports and Exhibition Complex in Baku, Azerbaijan from 2011 to 2011. The competition ran under the supervision of the world's governing body for amateur boxing, the International Boxing Association, and followed on from the biggest World Championships in International Boxing Association history which was held in Milan, Italy in 2009." .

lsd:Entity_22001 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Glinsky's Rebellion was a revolt in 1508 in the Grand Duchy of Lithuania by a group of aristocrats led by Prince Michael Glinski in 1508. In the early 16th century, the Grand Duchy of Lithuania lost about one third of its territory as a result of the Russian–Lithuanian Wars from 1500 to 1503. Historians Volodymyr Antonovych, Matvey Liubavsky, Mykhailo Hrushevsky and Mitrofan Dovnar_Zapol'skiy while noting the rebellion's narrowness, described it as a struggle between those of \"Russian\" and \"Lithuanian origins\" in the Grand Duchy of Lithuania and as an Orthodox Christian struggle against Catholic proselytism. Meanwhile, Polish historians Ludwik Finkel, Oskar Halecki, Ludwik Kolankowski, and the Russian historian Alexander Presnyakov denied that the rebellion had ethnic and religious aspects and considered Michael Glinski a shady dealer, supported only by his dependents." .

lsd:Entity_22016 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pinkpop Festival or PINKPOP is a large, annual music festival held at Landgraaf, Netherlands. Starting in 1970, at Burgemeester Damen Sportpark in the city of Geleen, Pinkpop is the oldest and longest running annual dedicated pop and rock music festival in the world. Pinkpop 2008 was held May 30 – June 1 in the Landgraaf Megaland Park." .

lsd:Entity_22067 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Africa One Antonov An_26 crash occurred on 26 July 2002 when an Africa One Antonov An_26 (9Q_CMC) faced a rejected takeoff at Kinshasa_N'Djili Airport in Kinshasa, Democratic Republic of the Congo." .

lsd:Entity_22071 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Borgo was a battle between Corsican and French forces over control of the town of Borgo on 8 10 October 1768. In 10 October 1768, Pasquale Paoli tried to recapture U Borgu (Borgo), where a French force of 700 men under De Ludre was entrenched awaiting reinforcements." .

lsd:Entity_22085 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Eurovision Young Dancers (French: L'Eurovision des Jeunes Danseurs), often shortened to EYD, or Young Dancers, was a biennial dance competition, organised by the European Broadcasting Union (EBU) and is broadcast on television throughout Europe. Performers between the ages of 16 and 21, from member countries of the European Broadcasting Union, compete as solo of couples to dance routines of their choice. The inaugural Eurovision Young Dancers contest, then known as Eurovision Competition for Young Dancers, took place in Reggio Emilia, Italy, on 1985. Eurovision Young Dancers is also the only Eurovision event to feature a country whose broadcaster is neither a full nor European Broadcasting Union of the EBU, as Kosovo made their sole appearance in 2011 (although they have broadcast other Eurovision events for many years). Florence Clerc, Irek Mukhamedow, Christopher Bruce and Piotr Nardelli were the dance teachers selected to work with the participants and tasked to select the 10 finalists out of the 13 participating countries. In addition, several transcontinental countries with only part of their territory in Europe have competed: Russia, since 1995; Canada in the North America continent, despite only being an European Broadcasting Union of the EBU, have competed twice, in 1987 and 1989. Sixteen performances have won the Eurovision Young Dancers competition, a biennial dance contest organised by member countries of the European Broadcasting Union." .

lsd:Entity_221 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Uncle Tobys Hardcourts was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It was the ninth edition of the event then known as the Uncle Tobys Hardcourts, and was a WTA Tier III tournaments event on the 2005 WTA Tour. It took place in Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia, from 02 January 2005 through 08 January 2005." .

lsd:Entity_2215 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1989 World Snooker Championship (also referred to as the 1989 Embassy World Snooker Championship for the purposes of sponsorship) was a professional ranking snooker tournament that took place between 15 15 April 1989 and 1 01 May 1989 at the Crucible Theatre in Sheffield, England." .

lsd:Entity_22184 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Groenlo was a siege of Groenlo during the Eighty Years' War and the Anglo–Spanish War by a Dutch and English army led by Maurice of Nassau after it had followed an unsuccessful siege by Maurice in 1595. The siege lasted from 11 to 28 September 1597 and ended in the town's capture from its Spanish garrison. Groenlo was then held by the States until a siege in 1606 by Ambrosio Spinola." .

lsd:Entity_22194 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The badminton competition at the badminton at the 2006 Central American and Caribbean Games was held in the Pavilion of Parque del Este in Santo Domingo as a sub_cities for Cartagena, Colombia. The tournament was scheduled to be held from 15 July 2006–30 July 2006." .

lsd:Entity_22197 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1996–97 Slovenian PrvaLiga season started on 04 August 1996 and ended on 01 June 1997." .

lsd:Entity_22248 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998–99 Danish Superliga season was the 9th season of the Danish Superliga league championship, governed by the Danish Football Union. It took place from the first match on 26 July 1998, to final match on 16 June 1999." .

lsd:Entity_22275 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1913 Asmara earthquake took place outside Asmara, Eritrea on 27 February 1913. The data as to the magnitude of the earthquake is imprecise due to the frequency and magnitude of aftershocks, but a maximum felt intensity of VI (Strong) on the Mercalli intensity scale was recorded at Asmara. The earthquake caused significant damage in Asmara (VI), Keren (IV), Massawa (V) and Adi Ugri (V)." .

lsd:Entity_22278 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1986 Alaska gubernatorial election took place on November 4, 1986, for the post of Governor of Alaska. In the general election, Democratic state Representative Steve Cowper defeated Republican candidate Arliss Sturgulewski and Alaska Independence candidate Joe Vogler." .

lsd:Entity_2228 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 World Junior Figure Skating Championships was an international figure skating competition in the 2014–2015 figure skating season. The event was held on 02 March 2015–08 March 2015 at the newly constructed Tallinn Arena in Tallinn, Estonia." .

lsd:Entity_22328 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Global Observer is a concept for a high_altitude, long endurance unmanned aerial vehicle, designed by AeroVironment (AV) to operate as a stratospheric geosynchronous satellite system with regional coverage. In 05 August 2010, Aerovironment announced that the full_sized Global Observer wing had passed wing load testing. The Global Observer performed its first flight on 05 August 2010, taking off from Edwards AFB and reaching an altitude of 4,000 ft (1,200 m) for one hour. AeroVironment is currently in possession of the second prototype Global Observer. On 6 February 2014, AeroVironment announced that it had teamed with Lockheed Martin to sell the Global Observer to international customers." .

lsd:Entity_22334 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992 Roermond earthquake occurred on 13 April 1992, around 3:20 AM (1:20 UTC) with a moment magnitude of 5.3 and a maximum Mercalli intensity of VII (Very strong). Striking on the Peel Boundary Fault, a normal fault near Roermond, it was the strongest recorded earthquake in the Netherlands and in Northwestern Europe, and caused substantial damage to older buildings in the Netherlands and adjacent countries of Belgium and Germany. The earthquake was recorded as 5.8 on the Richter magnitude scale (5.3 on the moment magnitude scale) and a maximum intensity of VII (Very strong) on the Mercalli intensity scale. The economic cost of the earthquake was estimated to be around 275 million guilders (around 125 million euros), of which 170 million guilders (around 77 million euros) of damage in the Netherlands." .

lsd:Entity_22373 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Zirve Publishing House massacre, called the missionary massacres by Turkish media, took place on 18 April 2007, in Zirve Publishing House, Malatya, Turkey." .

lsd:Entity_22378 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 World Netball Series was the inaugural tournament of the Fast5 Netball World Series. The 2009 World Netball Series was a new and exciting opportunity for those that have wanted to support netball to assist in making the series a success. The following were the sponsors for the 2009 World Netball Series: _The Co_operative Group who assists with the netball development in the UK. It is sometimes described as the ‘voice of Manchester’ for anything that is occurring there, like the 2009 world netball series." .

lsd:Entity_22382 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Robin White and Shelby Cannon won in the final 3–6, 6–2, 7–5 against Meredith McGrath and Rick Leach." .

lsd:Entity_2239 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Second Battle of Zurich (25 September 1799–26 September 1799) was a key victory by the Republican French army in Switzerland led by André Masséna over an Austrian and Russian force commanded by Alexander Korsakov near Zürich. The French troops which took part in the battle included: On 22 August Korsakov and Hotze agreed that the Russians with 22,000 men would line the lower reaches of the River Limmat (Aare), and Hotze with 20,000 men would occupy the Obersee region below Lake Zürich from the Linth to Glarus. Korsakov himself arrived in Zürich the following day, quickly displaying a vain over_confidence in the capabilities of his troops and disregard both for the French and his allies the Austrians: The presumption and arrogance of Korsakoff were carried to such a pitch, that in a conference with the Archduke Charles, shortly before the battle , when that great general was pointing out the positions which should in an especial manner be guarded, and said, pointing to the map, \"Here you should place a battalion.\" Shortly before the battle Korsakov detached Sacken's 5,000 man Reserve Division to Rapperswil to reinforce Hotze in anticipation of Suvorov's approach, consequently weakening his defensive line along the Limmat before Zürich and exposing his line of communications. The War of the Second Coalition War had greatly weakened the Helvetic Republic, the consequent loss of popular support led ultimately to the 1803 Act of Mediation." .

lsd:Entity_22421 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Ladeira da Velha was fought on 03 August 1831, between Portuguese Liberal and Miguelite forces on São Miguel Island in the Azores, as part of the Liberal Wars." .

lsd:Entity_22427 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 IMSA SportsCar Championship season was the third season of the United SportsCar Championship and first to be under the name as the IMSA SportsCar Championship organized by the International Motor Sports Association (IMSA)." .

lsd:Entity_22451 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bulgarian–Serbian wars of 917–924 (Bulgarian: Българо–сръбски войни от 917–924) were a series of conflicts fought between the Bulgarian Empire and the Principality of Serbia as a part of the greater Byzantine–Bulgarian war of 913–927. On 20 August 917 the Byzantines suffered a devastating defeat at the hands of the Bulgarian army in the Battle of Achelous which de facto brought the Balkans under Bulgarian control." .

lsd:Entity_225 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Paso de Cuevas was fought on 12 August 1865 during the Paraguayan invasion of the Argentine province of Corrientes." .

lsd:Entity_22522 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kharkiv Operation (November 24 _ 12 December 1919) was an offensive during the Russian Civil War by the Southern Front of the Red Army under command of Alexander Yegorov, against the White Guard troops of Anton Denikin. In the night of 12 December 1919, the Latvian and 8th Cavalry divisions entered the outskirts of Kharkiv, and in the afternoon the remaining White troops encircled in the city capitulated." .

lsd:Entity_22526 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 NBA All_Star Game was an exhibition basketball game which was played on 13 February 2000 at Oakland Arena in Oakland, home of the Golden State Warriors." .

lsd:Entity_2255 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Cravant was fought on 31 July 1423, during the Hundred Years' War between English and French forces at the village of Cravant in Burgundy, at a bridge and ford on the banks of the river Yonne, a left_bank tributary of the Seine, southeast of Auxerre." .

lsd:Entity_22555 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Mexican Grand Prix (formally known as the Formula 1 Gran Premio de México 2018) was a Formula One motor race held on 28 October 2018 at the Autódromo Hermanos Rodríguez in Mexico City. The race was the nineteenth round of the 2018 Formula One World Championship and marked the 20th running of the Mexican Grand Prix, and the 19th time that the race had been run as a World Championship event since the inaugural season in 1950. Daniel Ricciardo took pole position from team mate Max Verstappen and with Hamilton in third." .

lsd:Entity_22610 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "pwn symbols, especially the number 1337, are Internet meme that have spilled over into popular culture. pwn has its owned colloquialisms, many of which originated as jokes based on common typing errors, habits of new computer users, or knowledge of cyberculture and history." .

lsd:Entity_22618 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "On 11 February 2016, 2016 Ohio machete attack, a native of Guinea who was a permanent resident in the United States and had been working in computer programming and information technology, entered the Nazareth Restaurant in Columbus, Ohio, and began to attack customers with a machete, injuring four. In November 2016, following a car ramming and stabbing attack at Ohio State University, Columbus Police Deputy Chief Michael Woods compared it to the restaurant attack committed by Barry as also a potential act of terrorism." .

lsd:Entity_22648 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kilvenmani massacre (or Keezhvenmani massacre) was an incident in Kizhavenmani village, Tamil Nadu on 25 December 1968 in which a group of around 44 people, the families of striking Dalit (oppressed community) village labourers, were murdered by a gang, allegedly led by their landlords. The massacre resulted in death of 44, including 5 aged men, 16 women and 23 children. The Communist Party of India (Marxist) organises an annual \"Venmani Martyrs Day\" to commemorate the massacre." .

lsd:Entity_22659 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Łódź took place from 11 November 1914 to 06 December 1914, near the city of Łódź in Poland. The Scheidemann's Russian Empire Second army was deployed around Łódź, with his IV, I and XXIII Corps on the Warta, and his II Corps at Łęczyca. The enlarged Ninth Army would then attack the Russian Empire right flank, cutting Łódź off from Warsaw, and eliminating any troops thus encircled. On 15 November, the Germans captured Kutno, and on 16 November, crossed the Bzura, while Scheidemann ordered his Russian Empire I and IV Corps to retreat towards Łódź. It was Plehve's Russian Empire Fifth Army which prevented German encirclement of Łódź from the south. On 16 November he ordered Wenzel von Plehve's Russian Empire Fifth Army to abandon the proposed offensive into Silesia and to move northward towards Łódź; they marched 116 km (72 mi) in only two days. By 19 November, the Germans were facing a numerically superior Russian Empire force, with the intention of the Russians to attack the German penetration east of Łódź on 21 November. Yet, Mackensen still ordered his XX and XXV Reserve Corps to continue their effort to outflank the Russian Empire Łódź defenses. For the Russian Empire Army, Łódź became the furthest point of advance towards Germany's heartland." .

lsd:Entity_22672 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 ITF Women's Circuit UBS Thurgau was a professional tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts. It took place in Kreuzlingen, Switzerland, on 22 February 2016–28 February 2016." .

lsd:Entity_22685 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 20th 1965 Vuelta a España (Tour of Spain), a long_distance bicycle stage race and one of the three grand tours, was held from 29 April 1965 to 16 May 1965." .

lsd:Entity_2272 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 ITM Auckland SuperSprint was a motor racing event for Supercars, held on the weekend of 4 to 2016. The event was held at Pukekohe Park Raceway near Pukekohe, New Zealand, and consisted of four races at 100 kilometres in length." .

lsd:Entity_22738 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In the Battle of al_Buqaia in 1163, the Crusaders and their allies inflicted a rare defeat on Nur ad_Din Zangi, the Emir of Aleppo and Damascus. King Amalric I led the army of the Kingdom of Jerusalem, together with contingents from the northern Latin states, a substantial body of pilgrims who had just arrived from France, and a force brought by the Byzantine Empire governor of Cilicia. Nur ad_Din was no match for such a formidable combination of enemies and his army suffered a defeat near al_Buqaia (located between Krak des Chevaliers and Beqaa Valley, in modern_day Akkar District, Lebanon)." .

lsd:Entity_22743 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Eastern China smog was a severe air pollution episode that affected East China, including all or parts of the municipalities of Shanghai and Tianjin, and the provinces of Hebei, Shandong, Jiangsu, Anhui, Henan, and Zhejiang, during 01 December 2013." .

lsd:Entity_22778 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Soy Luna In Concert was the debut concert tour by the cast of the popular Disney Channel television series Soy Luna, in support of the soundtracks Soy Luna (2016), Música en ti (2016) and La vida es un sueño (2017). The tour began on 24 March 2017 in Buenos Aires at Tecnopolis Arena. For the first leg, the cast of Soy Luna performed on forty two shows across nineteen cities of Latin America, finishing on 2017 in Guayaquil." .

lsd:Entity_2281 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Reichenberg was a battle of the Third Silesian War (part of the Seven Years War), fought on 21 April 1757 near the town of Liberec (Czech: Liberec) in Bohemia. At Liberec he encountered Königsegg's Austria corps. The full Austria corps consisted of 18,000 infantry and 4,900 cavalry, but only about 14,000 of them had been concentrated at Liberec. Austria Forces during the battle were: Prussian Forces during the battle were (cavalry maintained 4 sqns and infantry had 2 battalions):" .

lsd:Entity_22835 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Theyyam (Teyyam, Theyam, Theyyattam) is a popular ritual form of dance worship in Kerala and Karnataka, India. The Devakoothu is the only Theyyam ritual performed by women.It is performed only on the Thekkumbad Kulom temple. Briefly, Theyyam provides a good example for the religious evolution of, and the subsequent different stages in modern Hinduism, with the overall understanding that within Hindu syncretism lay propitiation as ancient practices and rituals of ancient worship intended for the blessings of the supernatural not unlike, \"in Indus Valley and other ancient civilizations, mother goddess had been invoked for fertility and prosperity\"." .

lsd:Entity_22846 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Chilembwe uprising was a rebellion against British colonial rule in Nyasaland (modern_day Malawi) which took place in 31 January 1915. The rebellion had lasting effects on the British system of administration in Nyasaland, and some reform was enacted in its aftermath." .

lsd:Entity_2285 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Grand Paris Express is a group of new rapid transit lines being built in the Île_de_France region of France." .

lsd:Entity_22870 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 23rd Miss Chinese International, Miss Chinese International Pageant 2012 was held on 2012. Miss Chinese International Pageant 2010 Eliza Sam of Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada crowned her successor, Kelly Cheung of Chicago, USA at the end of the pageant. Cheung represented Hong Kong, China at Miss World 2012, becoming the first Miss Chinese International titleholder to represent the region in a Miss World Pageant that is not a Miss Hong Kong Pageant titleholder." .

lsd:Entity_22886 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The football at the 1976 Summer Olympics started on 18 July 1976 and ended on 31 July 1976. The following 13 teams qualified for the 1976 Olympics association football tournament: With six goals, Andrzej Szarmach of Poland is the top scorer in the tournament." .

lsd:Entity_22917 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Starmus Festival is an international gathering focused on celebrating astronomy, space exploration, music, art, and allied sciences such as biology and chemistry. It was founded by Garik Israelian, an astronomer at the Institute for Astrophysics in Tenerife, Canary Islands, Spain. The festival has occurred in 2011, 2014 and 2016 in Tenerife. The first Starmus Festival took place June 20–25, 2011, on Tenerife, and La Palma, Canary Islands. The second Starmus Festival occurred September 22–27, 2014, again on Tenerife, and La Palma, Canary Islands. The Government of Tenerife has announced that the equivalent publicity value from Starmus Festival II (2014) exceeds 170 Mln. The third STARMUS festival took place in 2016 in the Canary Islands, on Tenerife and La Palma from June 27 to July 2. In addition to the scientists in attendance the festival also featured a vast array of musical talent including: keynote speaker Brian Eno, Hans Zimmer, Brian May, Sarah Brightman, Anathema, the Symphonic Orchestra of Tenerife, and MC Hawking. The festival closed with the Sonic Universe Concert featuring Sarah Brightman singing with the Symphonic Orchestra of Tenerife as conducted by Hans Zimmer. Open to the general public at large as well as the Starmus Festival delegates, the two Sonic Universe Concerts were held at the Magma Arte & Congresos, an arena in Tenerife. It is the result of the unique Starmus meeting in 2011 on Tenerife, where the legendary Russian and American pioneers of the space age met up for the first time to share the moments that electrified the human race." .

lsd:Entity_22924 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Romanian Navy during World War II was the main Axis naval force in the Black Sea campaigns and fought against the Soviet Union's Black Sea Fleet from 1941 to 1944. The naval war in the Black Sea commenced with the Raid on Constanța on 26 June 1941, the only encounter between major warships during the entire campaign." .

lsd:Entity_23002 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1995 Hong Kong legislative election for members of the Legislative Council of Hong Kong (LegCo) was held on 17 September 1995. It was the first, and only, fully elected legislative election in the British Hong Kong before transferring Hong Kong's sovereignty to China two years later." .

lsd:Entity_23006 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Victoria's Secret Fashion Show is an annual promotional event sponsored by and featuring Victoria's Secret, a brand of lingerie. From 1995 to 2018, Victoria's Secret uses the show to market its goods in high_profile settings. The first fashion show, introduced by Stephanie Seymour, was held at the Plaza Hotel in New York City in 1995. In 1999, during Super Bowl XXXIII, Victoria's Secret announced a 72_hour countdown to the webcast of their fashion show, which resulted in over 2 million viewers. In place of the fashion show, the company sent the Victoria's Secret (Tyra Banks, Heidi Klum, Gisele Bündchen, Adriana Lima, and Alessandra Ambrosio) on an Victoria's Secret Across America Tour in 2004 to promote the brand through visit to four major cities: New York City, Miami, Las Vegas, and Los Angeles. Victoria's Secret sister brand PINK made its debut on the fashion show starting in 2006 and was regularly featured in a segment of the fashion show each year afterward. In 2009, the fashion show returned to the Lexington Avenue Armory and featured the “Victoria's Secret Model Search”, a competition to find a new fashion show Angel with the winner announced as Kylie Bisutti. On November 21, 2019, L Brands CFO Stuart Burgdoerfer officially confirmed that the 2019 fashion show had been canceled, citing its declining viewership and lack of immediate \"material impact\" on Victoria's Secret sales post_broadcast. The same models who were featured in the campaigns for the \"Angel\"_bra line, with the exception of Chandra North filling in the spot for Christensen, walked the fashion show with Angel wings on.. Over the years, the show featured various forms and sizes of wings, such as butterfly, peacock, or devil wings, which have become emblematic of the Victoria's Secret brand. Prior to each fashion show, Victoria's Secret contracts a renowned jewelry designer to craft the bra to be used as a focal point for promoting the fashion show and as a centerpiece within it. Victoria's Secret had worked with Swarovski for 9 years prior to the Swarovski items worn on the fashion show in 2011." .

lsd:Entity_23034 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Malaysia Super Series Premier was the third super series tournament of the 2016 BWF Super Series. The tournament took place in Shah Alam, Malaysia from 05 April 2016–10 April 2016 and had a total purse of $550,000." .

lsd:Entity_23091 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 European Cup Winter Throwing was held on 16 March and 17 March at the Pista de Atletismo Universitat Jaume I and Complejo Deportivo Gaetà Huguet in Castelló de la Plana, Spain. It was the thirteenth edition of the athletics competition in throwing events and was jointly organised by the European Athletic Association and the Real Federación Española de Atletismo." .

lsd:Entity_23147 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1852 United States presidential election in Delaware took place on 02 November 1852, as part of the 1852 United States presidential election." .

lsd:Entity_23153 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1950 Tour de Suisse was the 14th edition of the Tour de Suisse cycle race and was held from 24 June 1950 to 01 July 1950." .

lsd:Entity_23166 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Typhoon Damrey was a compact tropical cyclone, which became the strongest to affect the area north of the Yangtze River since 1949. It was the tenth named storm and the fifth typhoon of the 2012 Pacific typhoon season. Damrey finally intensified into a typhoon early on August 2, a half of day before it made landfall over the northern Jiangsu. According to JTWC Best Track Data, Damrey became a typhoon at 12Z. Based on RSMC Best Track Data, Damrey intensified into a typhoon west of Jeju at 00Z on August 2, when it just arrived at the Yellow Sea. Unlike JTWC analyses that Damrey began to gradually weaken after 00Z on August 2, JMA analyses that the typhoon reached peak intensity at 06Z, with ten_minute maximum sustained winds at 70 knots (130 km/h, 80 mph) and the atmospheric pressure at 965 hPa (14.00 psi). After slightly weakening, Damrey made landfall as a minimal typhoon over Xiangshui County in Jiangsu, China at 13:30 UTC (21:30 CST)." .

lsd:Entity_23223 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pink Friday Tour is the debut concert tour by Trinidadian singer/songwriter Nicki Minaj. The tour then continued on to Europe and North America in June, July, and 14 August 2012. The tour came to a close on 14 August 2012 in New York City at the Roseland Ballroom. Alexis Petridis from The Guardian attended the show at the HMV Hammersmith Apollo in London, he gave the Pink Friday Tour an average score with 3 out of 5 stars, saying \"It seems a strange thing to say about a performance that opens with a woman rapping \"I'm a bad bitch, I'm a cunt\", but there's something oddly restrained about Nicki Minaj's live show." .

lsd:Entity_23231 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "ofo (/ˈoʊfoʊ/), stylised as ofo, is a Beijing_based bicycle_sharing system company founded in 2014. The company was founded in 2014 by five members of the Peking University cycling club as a project that initially focused on bicycle tourism before deciding on bicycle_sharing system. ofo was launched in June 2015 in Beijing, gaining 20,000 users and 2,000 bicycles by October with investment funding from a Peking University alumnus. After missing the opportunity to merge with Mobike and failing to reach an acquisition deal with Didi, ofo now suffers from consistently high operational costs and lack of additional funding to expand its business. It was reported in January 2019 that ofo had dissolved its international division and offered its 50 remaining employees the option to leave immediately or take a 50% pay cut and transfer to the Chinese business." .

lsd:Entity_23334 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Whitby Gothic Weekend, abbreviated to WGW or nicknamed Whitby, is a twice_yearly music festival for the gothic subculture, in Whitby, North Yorkshire, England, organised by Jo Hampshire. Whitby Gothic Weekend is an alternative music festival held in Whitby. The term \"Whitby Gothic Weekend\" is sometimes used as a generic term to describe events during the week in Whitby as a whole, although the name of the event and its associated logo are registered trademarks of Jo Hampshire of Top Mum Promotions." .

lsd:Entity_23341 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1919 VFL Grand Final was an Australian rules football game contested between the Collingwood Football Club and Richmond Football Club, held at the Melbourne Cricket Ground in Melbourne on 11 October 1919. It was the 22nd annual VFL/AFL Grand Final of the Victorian Football League, staged to determine the premiers for the 1919 VFL season." .

lsd:Entity_2338 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Big Revival Tour was the fourteenth headlining concert tour by American country music artist Kenny Chesney, in support of his sixteenth studio album The Big Revival (2014)." .

lsd:Entity_23388 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Fine Air Flight 101 was a scheduled cargo flight from Miami International Airport to Las Américas International Airport, operated by McDonnell Douglas DC_8_61F N27UA, that crashed after take_off on 07 August 1997, at Miami International Airport." .

lsd:Entity_23392 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Bin Jawad was a battle in the 2011 Libyan Civil War between forces loyal to Libya leader Muammar Gaddafi and anti_Gaddafi forces for control of the town of Bin Jawad. On 5 06 March 2011, following the Battle of Ra's Lanuf, rebel forces advanced along the Mediterranean coast and captured the town of Bin Jawad. On the morning of 06 March 2011, the rebels were on the move again and were passing through Bin Jawad, when they realized that loyalist forces had entered the town the previous night and taken up positions in houses and on rooftops in preparation for an ambush." .

lsd:Entity_23440 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 Challenge Bell was a tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts at the Club Avantage Multi_Sports in Quebec City in Canada that was part of Tier III of the 1993 WTA Tour. It was the 1st edition of the National Bank Cup, and was held from 01 November 1993 through 07 November 1993." .

lsd:Entity_23455 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 Amstel Gold Race was the 14th edition of the annual road bicycle racing \"Amstel Gold Race\", held on Sunday 14 April 1979, in the Dutch province of Limburg. The race stretched 237 kilometres, with the start in Heerlen and the finish in Meerssen. There were a total of 137 competitors, and 32 cyclists finished the race." .

lsd:Entity_23489 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Fort Henry (1777) was an attack on American militiamen during the American Revolutionary War near the Virginia outpost known as Fort Henry by a mixed band of Indians in 21 September 1777. The battle is reported in some sources to have taken place on 01 September 1777, and in others on 21 September 1777." .

lsd:Entity_23540 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The shell game (also known as thimblerig, three shells and a pea, the old army game) is portrayed as a gambling game, but in reality, when a wager for money is made, it is almost always a confidence trick used to perpetrate fraud. In practice, however, the shell game is notorious for its use by confidence tricksters who will typically rig the game using sleight of hand to move or hide the ball during play and replace it as required." .

lsd:Entity_23589 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tan_Sahsa Flight 414 was a scheduled flight from Juan Santamaría International Airport, San José, Costa Rica to Toncontin Airport in Tegucigalpa, Honduras, with a stopover at Augusto C. Sandino Airport in Managua, Nicaragua on 21 October 1989. Flown with a Boeing 727_200, the flight crashed into a hill of the mountain range after the pilots failed to follow a special landing procedure required for the arrival to the airport, killing 131 passengers, leaving 15 survivors." .

lsd:Entity_23628 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A panel discussion, or simply a panel, involves a group of people gathered to discuss a topic in front of an audience, typically at scientific, business, or academic conferences, fan conventions, and on television shows. The typical format for a discussion panel includes a moderator in front of an audience. Television shows in the English_speaking world that feature a discussion panel format include Real Time with Bill Maher, Loose Women, The Nightly Show with Larry Wilmore, as well as segments of the long_running Meet the Press." .

lsd:Entity_2363 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1961 Monaco Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 14 May 1961 on the Circuit de Monaco in Monte Carlo, Monaco. It was race 1 of 8 in both the 1961 World Championship of Drivers and the 1961 Formula One season." .

lsd:Entity_23651 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tatiana Golovin and Richard Gasquet won the title, defeating Cara Black and Wayne Black in the final." .

lsd:Entity_23656 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Credit Agricole Friuladria Tennis Cup was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Cordenons, Italy between 12 August 2013 and 18 August 2013." .

lsd:Entity_23677 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Asia Tour was planned to be the eleventh concert tour by Canadian singer Celine Dion. The tour was organized to support the English language album Loved Me Back to Life, and was scheduled to take place in October and 29 November 2014. The tour was organized to support the English language album Loved Me Back to Life, and was scheduled to take place in October and 29 November 2014." .

lsd:Entity_23688 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 GP Miguel Induráin was the 59th edition of the GP Miguel Indurain cycle race and was held on 31 March 2012." .

lsd:Entity_23706 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 World Horticultural Exposition (昆明世博会) was an A1 category international garden festival recognised by the Bureau International des Expositions (BIE). Organised under the auspices of the International Association of Horticultural Producers, the event was held in Kunming, People's Republic of China." .

lsd:Entity_23715 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1880 United States presidential election in New York took place on 02 November 1880. New York was won by the Republican nominees, Congressman James A. Garfield of Ohio and his running mate former Collector of the Port of New York Chester A. Arthur of New York." .

lsd:Entity_2373 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ashleigh Barty and Demi Schuurs won the title, defeating Makarova and Latisha Chan in the final, 4–6, 6–3, ." .

lsd:Entity_23818 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Güstow, also known as the Battle of Tornow, was a battle during the Pomeranian War in the Seven Years' War fought between Prussia and Sweden near the village Güstow in Germany on 18 November 1758." .

lsd:Entity_23826 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Gideon v. Wainwright, 372 U.S. 335 (1963), is a landmark Supreme Court of the United States case in which the Court unanimously held that in criminal cases states are required under the Sixth Amendment of the U.S. Constitution to provide an attorney to defendants who are unable to afford their own attorneys. The Supreme Court's decision was announced on 18 March 1963, and delivered by Justice Hugo Black." .

lsd:Entity_23866 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Salses (1639–1640) was a double siege during the Franco_Spanish War (1635_1659), starting with a French success, but ending with a Spanish victory. Now Salses_le_Château was alone and hunger forced the French to surrender on 06 January 1640. The presence of a large number of troops in Catalonia contributed to the outbreak of the Catalan Revolt a few months later and the murder of Dalmau de Queralt, Count of Santa Coloma, second in command at the siege of Salses_le_Château." .

lsd:Entity_23886 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Imam Abbas Mosque bombing occurred on 28 April 2007 when a suicide car bomb exploded in front of the al_‘Abbās Mosque in Karbala, Iraq. Karbala is considered the second most important shrine city for the Shia Islam." .

lsd:Entity_23896 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Delray Beach International Tennis Championships is an Association of Tennis Professionals World Tour 250 series men's professional tennis tournament held each year in Delray Beach, Florida, United States of America, and played on hard courts. The event was held in Coral Springs from 1993–1998; in 1999, it was relocated to the Delray Beach Tennis Center." .

lsd:Entity_23924 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Revelation of John describes a War in Heaven between angels led by the Archangel Michael against those led by \"the dragon\", identified as the devil or Satan, who will be defeated and thrown down to the earth. 7 Then war broke out in heaven. As a result of linking this motif with the cited passage of the Revelation of John, the casting of Satan down from heaven, which other versions of the motif present as an action of God himself, has become attributed to the archangel Michael at the conclusion of a war between two groups of angels, of whom (because of the mention of the dragon's tail casting a third of the stars of heaven to the earth) one third are supposed to have been on the side of Satan, in spite of the fact that the casting down of the stars (Revelation 12:4) is recounted as occurring before the start of the \"War in Heaven\" (Revelation 12:7). He added that Michael's name \"was the war_cry of the good angels in the battle fought in heaven against the enemy and his followers\". The concept of a War in Heaven at the end of time became an addendum to the story of Satan's fall at the genesis of time—a narrative which included Satan and a third of all of heaven's angels." .

lsd:Entity_24020 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 IIHF World U18 Championships was the 15th IIHF World U18 Championship and was hosted in Sochi, Russia. The IIHF selected 12 referees and 10 linesmen to work the 2013 IIHF World U18 Championships. The Division I A tournament was played in Asiago, Italy, from 7 to 2013." .

lsd:Entity_24100 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Silje Case (26 June 1989 – 15 October 1994) was a Norwegian girl who was killed by two boys in the village of Rosten near Trondheim on 15 October 1994." .

lsd:Entity_24137 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Danish Figure Skating Championships (Danish: Danmarks Mesterskaberne 2007) was held in Frederikshavn from 01 December 2006 through 3, 2006." .

lsd:Entity_2417 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Toray Pan Pacific Open was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts. It was the 25th edition of the Pan Pacific Open, and was part of the WTA Tier I tournaments of the 2008 WTA Tour. It took place at the Ariake Coliseum in Tokyo, Japan, from 15 September 2008 through 21 September 2008." .

lsd:Entity_24229 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "OTI Festival 1977 was the sixth edition of the OTI Song Festival that was held in Madrid on November 12, the same city where the inaugural edition of the Latin_American song contest was held back in 1972. The construction of this building started in 1973 and was finished in 1977 few months before the OTI Song Festival was held again in this city. Guayo González, the Nicaraguan contestant, sang \"Quincho Barrilete\", a song addressing poverty, composed by the renowned Carlos Mejía Godoy." .

lsd:Entity_24239 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The wrestling at the 1992 Summer Olympics – men's freestyle 130 kg as part of the wrestling at the 1992 Summer Olympics were held at the Institut National d'Educació Física de Catalunya from August 4 to August 6." .

lsd:Entity_24257 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992 Irish Professional Championship was a professional invitational snooker tournament, which took place in 18 May 1992 at Jury's Hotel in Cork, Ireland." .

lsd:Entity_24294 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006–07 La Liga season, the 76th since its establishment, started on 27 August 2006 and finished on 17 June 2007. Real Madrid CF won La Liga on the better head to head against Barcelona in one of its most thrilling seasons to date." .

lsd:Entity_24395 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 Russian Figure Skating Championships (Russian: Чемпионат России по фигурному катанию на коньках 1998) were held in Moscow on 11 December 1997–14 December 1997." .

lsd:Entity_2445 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 La Flèche Wallonne was the 43rd edition of La Flèche Wallonne cycle race and was held on 10 April 1979. The race started in Esneux and finished in Marcinelle." .

lsd:Entity_24450 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1992–93 Umaglesi Liga was the fourth season of top_tier football in Georgia. It began on 09 August 1992 and ended on 21 June 1993." .

lsd:Entity_24528 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 25th Congress of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union met in Moscow from 24 February 1976 to 05 March 1976." .

lsd:Entity_24551 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Indiana gubernatorial election took place on 2012. The Republican candidate, Congressman Mike Pence; the Democratic candidate, former Speaker of the Indiana House of Representatives John R. Gregg; and the Libertarian candidate, youth mentor, small business owner and reality TV personality, Rupert Boneham, were all unopposed in their respective primaries or conventions and contested the general election. This is the first open Indiana gubernatorial election since 1996 and the first gubernatorial election since 1972 without the Governor of Indiana or LT. Governor of Indiana as a nominee. The Indiana Debate Commission organized three televised debates between Indiana Gubernatorial candidates Republican Mike Pence, Democrat John R. Gregg and Libertarian Rupert Boneham. The first debate was held on Wednesday, 2012 at the Zionsville Performing Arts Center in Zionsville, Indiana and was moderated by former Indianapolis Star editor Dennis Ryerson. The second debate was held on Wednesday, 2012 at the DeBartolo Performing Arts Center in South Bend, Indiana and was moderated by Indiana Fiscal Policy Institute president John Ketzenberger. The third debate was held on Thursday, 2012 at the WFWA PBS 39 studio in Fort Wayne, Indiana and was moderated by DePauw University Executive Director of Media Relations Ken Owen." .

lsd:Entity_24557 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Big Week or Operation Argument was a sequence of raids by the United States Army Air Forces and RAF Bomber Command from 20 to 25 February 1944, as part of the European strategic bombing campaign against Nazi Germany. Prior to the Big Week, throughout 1943, the US 8th Air Force had been growing in size and experience and started pressing attacks deeper into Germany." .

lsd:Entity_24605 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1998 WDF Europe Cup was the 11th edition of the WDF Europe Cup darts tournament, organised by the World Darts Federation. It was held in Oslo, Norway from August 6 to 9." .

lsd:Entity_24611 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Asian Players Tour Championship 2012/2013 – Event 2 was a professional minor_ranking snooker tournament that took place between 23 September 2012–27 September 2012 at the Yixing Sports Centre in Yixing, People's Republic of China." .

lsd:Entity_24678 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Barcelona (09 June 1359–11, 1359) was a naval engagement fought in the coastal region of Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain, between the navies of the Crowns of Aragon and Castile, during the War of the Two Peters. Consisting of 128 warships including royal vessels, ships from the King of Castile's vassals, and several others that had been sent by the Castilian_allied monarchs of Kingdom of Portugal and Emirate of Granada, this large fleet had been entrusted to the Genoese admiral, Egidio Boccanegra, who was seconded by two of his relatives, Ambrogio and Bartolome. Traversing the coast of Valencia and forcing the surrender of the Castle of Guardamar, it appeared before Barcelona on 09 June 1359. The king, Peter I of Kingdom of Portugal, and Muhammed V, Sultan of Emirate of Granada, also contributed ships to the increase in Peter's fleet. On 09 June 1359 it was within sight of Barcelona." .

lsd:Entity_24684 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1883 Ontario general election was the fifth general election held in the Province of Ontario, Canada, to elect the 88 Members of the 5th Legislative Assembly of Ontario (\"MLAs\"). Held on 27 February 1883, the fifth Ontario provincial election was the only one ever contested in the month of February. The Ontario Liberal Party, led by Oliver Mowat, won a fourth consecutive term in government, despite losing nine seats in the Legislature." .

lsd:Entity_24705 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bowling Green massacre is a fictitious incident of terrorism mentioned by Kellyanne Conway, U.S. A day later, on January 31, two days before the Hardball interview with Conway, Kentucky senator Rand Paul referenced the 2011 case in an interview with MSNBC by mentioning \"the possibility or the attempted bombing in Bowling Green, where I live\". On 29 January 2017, in an interview with Cosmopolitan, Conway said that Obama had limited Iraqi immigration because \"two Iraqi nationals came to this country, joined ISIS, traveled back to the Middle East to get trained and refine their terrorism skills, and come back here, and were the masterminds behind the Bowling Green massacre of taking innocent soldiers' lives away\". On February 3, the day after her MSNBC interview, Conway said she misspoke and that she meant to use the term \"Bowling Green terrorists\" instead of \"Bowling Green massacre\", referring to the two Iraqi men arrested in 2011. In a March 2017 interview with New York, Conway said she intended to say \"Bowling Green masterminds\" rather than \"Bowling Green massacre\", in reference to \"would_be terrorists who were apprehended before they staged an attack\"." .

lsd:Entity_24725 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of the Echinades was fought in 1427 among the Echinades islands off western Greece between the fleets of Carlo I Tocco and the Byzantine Empire." .

lsd:Entity_24728 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Oulu International Children's and Youth Film Festival (Finnish: Oulun kansainvälinen lasten_ ja nuortenelokuvien festivaali) is an annual children's film festival held in November in Oulu, Finland. The festival has been founded in 1982 by the Oulu Film Centre. Other awards are the ECFA Award for the best European film, the For Tomorrow Award to the best youth film and a prize of the Media Foundation of the Evangelical Lutheran Church of Finland for a Finnish feature or short film at the film festival." .

lsd:Entity_24736 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Thirty_second Amendment of the Constitution Bill 2013 was a proposal to amend the Constitution of Ireland to abolish Seanad Éireann, the upper house of the Irish parliament, the Oireachtas. The next day, the Local Government Minister Phil Hogan made the necessary order establishing 04 October 2013 as the date for the referendum on the Seanad bill, and for a separate referendum on Thirty_third Amendment of the Constitution of Ireland to establish a Court of Appeal." .

lsd:Entity_24741 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Netflix Prize was an open competition for the best collaborative filtering algorithm to predict user ratings for films, based on previous ratings without any other information about the users or films, i.e. The competition was held by Netflix, an online DVD_rental and video streaming service, and was open to anyone who is neither connected with Netflix (current and former employees, agents, close relatives of Netflix employees, etc.) On 21 September 2009, the grand prize of US$1,000,000 was given to the BellKor's Pragmatic Chaos team which bested Netflix's own algorithm for predicting ratings by 10.06%. The competition began on 02 October 2006. The Netflix Prize competition then entered the \"last call\" period for the Grand Prize. On July 26, 2009, Netflix stopped gathering submissions for the Netflix Prize contest. On September 18, 2009, Netflix announced team \"BellKor's Pragmatic Chaos\" as the prize winner (a Test RMSE of 0.8567), and the prize was awarded to the team in a ceremony on 21 September 2009. On March 12, 2010, Netflix announced that it would not pursue a second Prize competition that it had announced the previous August." .

lsd:Entity_24744 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC Live: Vera vs. Jones (also known as UFC on Versus 1) was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on 21 March 2010 in Broomfield, Colorado, United States of America at the 1stBank Center." .

lsd:Entity_24748 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 Guilin Airport collision was a ground collision between a People's Liberation Army Air Force (PLAAF) Harbin H_5 bomber and a CAAC Hawker_Siddeley Trident at the military – civilian Guilin Qifengling Airport, killing 11 passengers. On 14 September 1983, a military aircraft collided into a CAAC Hawker_Siddeley Trident at the Guilin Qifengling Airport." .

lsd:Entity_24791 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 Halloween blizzard was a powerful storm that caused a period of heavy snowfall and ice accumulation, which affected parts of the Upper Midwest of the United States, from 31 October 1991 to 03 November 1991. By the time the precipitation stopped falling, many cities in the eastern half of Minnesota and northwestern Wisconsin had witnessed record early_season snowfall accumulations, while parts of southern Minnesota and northern Iowa were crippled by a large ice storm. The precipitation from this system began falling as snow in Iowa late on October 30, and by the morning of 31 October 1991 it had changed over to ice and spread northward across southeast Minnesota. The heavy snow began falling across east central Minnesota and northwest Wisconsin during the late afternoon hours of 31 October 1991. As the storm system pushed its way northward, more communities in eastern Minnesota and northwestern Wisconsin began to experience similar conditions; and thundersnow occurred as far north as Duluth. By the time the snow ended on 03 November 1991 the storm had dropped 36.9 in (93.7 cm) on Duluth, the largest single snow storm total in Minnesota history at that time. In all, at least one foot (30 cm) of snow fell in a swath approximately 100 mi (160 km) wide from south central Minnesota, northeastward into northwestern Wisconsin and into the Minnesota Arrowhead. Areas of southern Minnesota and Iowa along and south of the I_90 corridor did not see as much snow, but instead saw a major ice storm. Most of Minnesota, western Wisconsin and northern Iowa were heavily impacted by the storm. Eleven counties in southern Minnesota were declared federal disaster areas, and 52 counties in Iowa were declared disaster areas. Many roads were closed both from the snow and ice, including long stretches of I_90, I_35 and I_29 in Iowa, Minnesota and South Dakota. November 1 saw similar daily records fall, but with a more wide reaching area from most of central Minnesota eastward to La Crosse and Eau Claire, Wisconsin." .

lsd:Entity_24840 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013–14 Eredivisie was the 58th season of Eredivisie since its establishment in 1955. It began on 02 August 2013 with the first match of the season and ended on 18 May 2014 with the returns of the finals of the European competition and relegation playoffs. A total of 18 teams took part in the league: The best fifteen teams from the 2012–13 Eredivisie, two promotion/relegation playoff winners and the 2012–13 Eerste Divisie champions." .

lsd:Entity_24844 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1975 Davis Cup was the 64th edition of the Davis Cup, the most important tournament between national teams in men's tennis. Sweden Davis Cup team then defeated Czechoslovakia in the final to win their first title and become the sixth nation to win the Davis Cup. The final was held at the Kungliga tennishallen in Stockholm, Sweden Davis Cup team on 19 December–21 December 1975." .

lsd:Entity_2488 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 RFU Championship, known for sponsorship reasons as the Greene King IPA Championship, is the sixth season of the professionalised format of the RFU Championship, the second tier of the English rugby union league system run by the Rugby Football Union. Ten of the teams that competed in the 2013–14 RFU Championship remain in the competition for the 2014–15 RFU Championship." .

lsd:Entity_24902 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Rolling Stones' The Rolling Stones US Tour 1978 was a concert tour of the United States that took place during June and 26 July 1978, immediately following the release of the group's 1978 album Some Girls." .

lsd:Entity_24939 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Huntsville bus crash involved a school bus carrying 40 students from Lee High School to the Huntsville Center for Technology and occurred on 20 November 2006, on an elevated portion of Interstate 565 in Huntsville. On 20 November 2006, around 10 AM, a school bus carrying forty students from Lee High School to the Huntsville Center for Technology was traveling in the left lane on the elevated two_lane I_565." .

lsd:Entity_24960 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Ma'arra, or Ma'arra, occurred in late 1098 in the city of Maarrat al_Nu'man, in what is modern_day Syria, during the First Crusade." .

lsd:Entity_25048 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 Winter Universiade, the XIII Winter Universiade, took place in Štrbské pleso, Czechoslovakia." .

lsd:Entity_25058 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The national commemorative Exhibition of the centenary of the opening of the Ports of Brazil, also known as Brazilian National Exposition of 1908 or the National Exposition of Brazil at Rio de Janeiro, marked a hundred years since the opening of the Brazilian ports acelebrated Brazil's trade and development. It opened in Urca, Rio de Janeiro on 11 August 1908, stayed open for 3 months and received over 1 million visitors." .

lsd:Entity_25125 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Turkish Airlines Flight 1951 (also known as the Poldercrash or the Schiphol Polderbaan incident) was a passenger flight that crashed during landing at Amsterdam Schiphol Airport, Netherlands, on 25 February 2009, resulting in the deaths of nine passengers and crew, including all three pilots. The aircraft, a Turkish Airlines Boeing 737_800, crashed into a field approximately 1.5 kilometres (0.9 mi) north of the Amsterdam Airport Schiphol (18R), prior to crossing the A9 motorway inbound, at 09:26 UTC (10:26 CET), having flown from Istanbul, Turkey." .

lsd:Entity_25177 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Canucks–Flames rivalry is a rivalry that takes place in the Pacific Division of the National Hockey League between the Vancouver Canucks and the Calgary Flames. The Vancouver Canucks started play in the 1970–71 season as an expansion team and the Calgary Flames started play during the 1980–81 season as a relocated team from Atlanta (Atlanta Flames)." .

lsd:Entity_25208 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Keep Moving Tour is a cancelled concert tour by Australian hard rock musician Andrew Stockdale in support of his debut solo album Keep Moving. In July 2013, it was announced that all Andrew Stockdale Keep Moving tour dates had been cancelled, and that his old band Wolfmother would reunite to perform a number of shows in the United States. As of 21 July 2013, it is not yet known whether any of the Keep Moving shows will be rescheduled, either as Andrew Stockdale or as Wolfmother." .

lsd:Entity_25231 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The triathlon at the 2000 Summer Olympics – men's was part of the triathlon at the 2000 Summer Olympics programme. The competition was held on Sunday, 2000 at the Sydney Opera House in Sydney. 52 athletes competed in triathlon at the 2000 Summer Olympics – men's; only four of them dropped out of the cycling phase." .

lsd:Entity_25243 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1938 Kyeema crash occurred on 25 October 1938 when the Australian National Airways Douglas DC_2 Kyeema, tail number VH_UYC, flying from Adelaide to Melbourne, commenced final approach to Essendon Airport through heavy fog and crashed into the western slopes of Mount Dandenong, also known as Mount Corhanwarrabul, killing all 18 on board instantly." .

lsd:Entity_25261 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017–18 Northern Kentucky Norse men's basketball team represented Northern Kentucky University (NKU) during the 2017–18 NCAA Division I men's basketball season. The 2016–17 Northern Kentucky Norse men's basketball team, led by third_year head coach John Brannen, played their home games at BB&T Arena in Highland Heights, Kentucky as members of the Horizon League. The 2016–17 Northern Kentucky Norse men's basketball team shared their home arena, BB&T Arena, with the University of Cincinnati's men's basketball team during the season while Cincinnati's home arena, Fifth Third Arena, underwent renovations during the season." .

lsd:Entity_25267 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Natural Bridge was fought during the American Civil War in what is now Woodville, Florida near Tallahassee on 06 March 1865. As people in Tallahassee tell the story, handed down since the civil war, a small band of Confederate troops and volunteers, mostly composed of teenagers from the nearby Florida Military and Collegiate Institute that would later become Florida State University, and the elderly, protected by breastworks, prevented a detachment of United States Colored Troops from crossing the Woodville on the St. Marks River. The Union Army force, however, had advanced and, after finding one bridge destroyed, started before dawn on 06 March 1865 to attempt to cross the river at Woodville. Based on the involvement of the students from the Florida Military and Collegiate Institute, the Florida State University Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) program is one of only four Army ROTC programs to have a battle streamer for their actions in the Civil War. The site of the battle is now Woodville Battlefield State Historic Site, a Florida State Park, and contains a monument with the inscription: This monument erected under authority of an act of the legislature of Florida of 1921 as a just tribute of the people of Florida to commemorate the victory of the battle of Woodville. A ceremony honoring the combatants on both sides of the Battle of Natural Bridge, followed by a reenactment of the battle featuring Union, Confederate, and civilian reenactors, is held at the park the first weekend of March every year." .

lsd:Entity_2527 a lsd:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "3" ;
    lsd:appears_in lsd:Entity_63671 .

lsd:Entity_25294 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Sunoco Red Cross Pennsylvania 500 was a NASCAR Sprint Cup Series stock car race held on 01 August 2010 at Pocono Raceway in Long Pond, Pennsylvania. Greg Biffle, driving for Roush Fenway Racing, won the race while Tony Stewart finished second, and Carl Edwards, who started twenty_fifth, clinched third." .

lsd:Entity_25321 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Swedish Open Championships, also known as the Swedish Open Championships (SOC), is an annual table tennis tournament in Sweden, run by the International Table Tennis Federation (ITTF)." .

lsd:Entity_25332 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 World Series of Poker Europe (WSOPE) took place from 19 October 2017 to 10 November 2017 at King's Casino Rozvadov in Rozvadov, Czech Republic. Source: Final standings as of 10 November 2017 (end of WSOPE): The 2017 World Series of Poker Europe Main Event began on November 4 and finished 10 November 2017." .

lsd:Entity_25373 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1908–09 FA Cup was the 38th staging of the world's oldest association football competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup (more usually known as the FA Cup). Manchester United F.C. won the competition for the first time, beating Bristol City 1–0 in the 1909 FA Cup Final at Crystal Palace, through a goal from Sandy Turnbull. The format of the FA Cup for the season had two preliminary rounds, five qualifying rounds, four proper rounds, and the semi finals and 1909 FA Cup Final. Bristol City won this tie, and so went on to meet the other semi_1909 FA Cup Final winner, Manchester United F.C., in the 1909 FA Cup Final. The Final was played on 24 April 1909 at Crystal Palace, and was contested by Manchester United F.C. and Bristol City, both of the First Division." .

lsd:Entity_25445 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1957 Stanley Cup Finals was the championship series of the National Hockey League's (NHL) 1956–57 season, and the culmination of the 1957 Stanley Cup playoffs. It was contested between the defending champion Montreal Canadiens and the Boston Bruins. The Canadiens were making their seventh consecutive Final appearance, while Boston was making their first appearance since their 1953 loss to Montreal. 1957 Montreal Canadiens." .

lsd:Entity_25528 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 Paris–Roubaix was ultimately settled in a 6_man sprint on the velodrome in Roubaix with Bernard Hinault prevailing in front of former four times winner Roger De Vlaeminck and reigning three times winner Francesco Moser. With about 8 kilometres to go, Bernard Hinault attempted to break away, but was hauled in by Hennie Kuiper acting for Roger De Vlaeminck. In the end, he was able to resist the charge from Roger De Vlaeminck, and became the first French winner of the Paris–Roubaix for 25 years." .

lsd:Entity_25571 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Take Us Alive World Tour was a concert tour by hard rock band Extreme, taking place in from mid to late 2008, in support of Saudades de Rock, their first album of original material in 13 years, and the first since their reunion in 2007." .

lsd:Entity_2559 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Zimbabwe Premier Soccer League season (known as the Castle Larger Zimbabwe Premier Soccer League for sponsorship reasons) will be the thirty second season of the Zimbabwe Premier Soccer League since its establishment in 1980. Dynamos F.C. are the defending champions, having won the previous 2011 Zimbabwe Premier Soccer League season." .

lsd:Entity_25624 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1957 Saint Lucian general election were held in Saint Lucia on 18 September 1957." .

lsd:Entity_25668 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Berlin ePrix (formally the 2018 BMW i Berlin E_Prix) was a Formula E electric car race held at the Tempelhof Airport Street Circuit at Tempelhof Airport in the outskirts of Berlin on 19 May 2018. It was the ninth round of the 2017–18 Formula E season and the fourth edition of the Berlin ePrix as part of the championship. Daniel Abt won the pole position by recording the fastest lap in qualifying and he maintained his start line advantage for virtually the entire race, with teammate di Grassi in second at Audi's home ePrix despite Abt having a slow mandatory mid_Berlin ePrix pit stop to switch into a second car as he had to let e.Dams_Renault's Sébastien Buemi enter his pitbox. The ePrix was held at the 2.375 km (1.476 mi) clockwise ten_turn Tempelhof Airport Street Circuit at Berlin Tempelhof Airport on 19 May 2018." .

lsd:Entity_2567 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Papillon was a large scale air and ground assault on the Viet Minh at Hòa Bình by the French Army and Air Force in 01 April 1947, during the early stages of the First Indochina War." .

lsd:Entity_25713 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Elephant Point was an airborne operation at the mouth of the Yangon River conducted by a composite Gurkha airborne battalion that took place on 01 May 1945. At 02:30 on 01 May 1945, a C_47 of 317 Tactical Control Squadron USAAF departed for Yangon carrying a twenty_man pathfinder team, followed by a CCG plane carrying a pair of VCP, to mark and defend the landing zone at Tawhai. Operation Dracula was a complete success, as Japanese forces had actually vacated Yangon several days prior to the amphibious landing; 36th Indian Infantry Brigade was able to occupy the city without encountering any Japanese opposition." .

lsd:Entity_25732 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sasun Uprising or Sason rebellion of 1904 (Armenian: Սասունի երկրորդ ապստամբութիւնը, Sasuni yerkrord apstambut'yunĕ, literally Second Sassoun resistance) was an uprising by Armenian fedayees against the Ottoman Empire in Turkey's Sason region in 1904. The first Sason resistance was led by the Armenian national movement's Armenian fedayees, which belonged to Hunchak. In May 1903, a Armenian fedayees led by Gorgos \"Marrik\" arrived in Sason. Andranik suggested inciting a general revolt in Armenia which would disperse the Turkish forces; Hrayr objected that an Armenian revolt, unsupported by other factions of the Ottoman Empire, would be doomed and suggested concentrating on the defense of Sason." .

lsd:Entity_25746 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sinjar offensive was a combination of operations of Kurdish Peshmerga, PKK and People's Protection Units forces in 17 December 2014, to recapture regions formerly lost to the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant in their August offensive. In August 2014, the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant launched an offensive in Northern Iraq and pushed into Kurdish held areas of the Nineveh Governorate, capturing the city of Sinjar, among others." .

lsd:Entity_25762 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United States v. Manning was the court_martial of former United States Army Private First Class Bradley E. Manning, known now as Chelsea Manning." .

lsd:Entity_25783 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1986 Miller High Life 400 was a NASCAR Winston Cup Series race that was held on 23 February 1986, at Richmond Raceway (now Richmond Raceway) in Richmond, Virginia. Kyle Petty would defeat Joe Ruttman in his 1986 Ford Thunderbird, finishing under caution in front of twenty_five thousand fans." .

lsd:Entity_25813 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The fencing at the 2016 Summer Olympics – women's épée competition in fencing at the 2016 Summer Olympics in Rio de Janeiro was held on 06 August 2016 at the Carioca Arena 3." .

lsd:Entity_25868 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1966 Syrian coup d'état refers to events between 21 February 1966 and 23 February 1966 during which the government of the Syria was overthrown and replaced." .

lsd:Entity_2588 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1951 edition of Mitropa Cup was unofficial and only for this tournament was named Zentropacup. The tournament crushed by the contemporary and most prestigious Latin Cup and Rio Cup, which eluded the national champions club, was won by the Austrians of SK Rapid Wien. 03 July 1951, Praterstadion, Vienna. 05 July 1951, Praterstadion, Vienna. 05 July 1951, Praterstadion, Vienna." .

lsd:Entity_25880 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Go Bowling 400 is a Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series Kansas 400 held on 13 May 2017, at Kansas Speedway in Kansas City, Kansas. Contested over 267 laps on the 1.5 mile (2.4 km) asphalt speedway, it was the 11th Kansas 400 of the 2017 Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series season. Kansas Speedway is a 1.5_mile (2.4 km) tri_oval Kansas 400 track in Kansas City, Kansas. Ryan Blaney scored the pole for the Kansas 400 with a time of 28.481 and a speed of 189.600 mph (305.132 km/h). Ryan Blaney led the field to the green flag at 7:53 p.m. Martin Truex Jr. shot past his outside exiting Turn 2 to take the lead on lap 11. Fox Sports covered their seventh Kansas 400 at the Kansas Speedway." .

lsd:Entity_25905 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The short track speed skating at the 2006 Winter Olympics – men's 5000 metre relay in short track speed skating at the 2006 Winter Olympics began with the semifinals, on 15 February, and concluded with the final on 25 February, at the Torino Palavela." .

lsd:Entity_26036 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015–16 Top 14 season competition was a France domestic rugby union club competition operated by the National Rugby League (LNR). Having defeated Toulouse and table_topping Clermont en route to the final, Racing 92 won their sixth France championship title, and first since 1990, with a 29–21 win over Toulon, despite playing over three_quarters of the game with 14 men after scrum_half Maxime Machenaud was sent off for a dangerous tackle on Matt Giteau. The winners then face the top two teams in the semi_finals, with the winners meeting in the final, held this season at Camp Nou because the traditional site of Stade de France was not available in 2015–16 due to conflict with UEFA Euro 2016." .

lsd:Entity_26043 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 123 was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on 20 November 2010 at the The Palace of Auburn Hills in Auburn Hills. It was the first Ultimate Fighting Championship event in the Metro Detroit area since Ultimate Fighting Championship 9." .

lsd:Entity_26129 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Colombian Championship 1962 was the 15th season of Colombia's top_flight football league. Millonarios won the league for the 7th time in its history, defending successfully the title won in Colombian Championship 1961. Source: RSSSF.com Colombia 1962." .

lsd:Entity_26137 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "murder of Jenna Lepomäki was an 18_year_old Finnish woman, who was found dead in Fuengirola, Spain, on 06 October 2011." .

lsd:Entity_26148 a lsd:Context_narration ;
