lsd:Entity_35428 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Knockshinnoch Disaster was a mining accident that occurred in September 1950 in the village of New Cumnock, Ayrshire, Scotland." .

lsd:Entity_3547 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 Monaco Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 27 May 1990 at Circuit de Monaco. It was the fourth race of the 1990 Formula One season and the 48th Monaco Grand Prix." .

lsd:Entity_35487 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Atlanta Open (known for sponsorship reasons as the Truist Atlanta Open), is a professional men's tennis tournament that has been played in the Atlanta area in the United States of America since 2010, usually during July or August. The event was previously held in Indianapolis from 1988 until it was moved to Atlanta after 2009. The Atlanta Open was known as the Atlanta Tennis Championships for its first two years before signing BB&T as a title sponsor in 2012. In December 2009 it was announced that the ATP had sold the license to a group in Atlanta, Georgia, where it would be held at the Atlanta Athletic Club. Prior to 2010 Atlanta had previously held a tennis tournament known as the Verizon Tennis Challenge from 1992 to 2001. In 2012, the tournament gained BB&T as title sponsor and changed its name to the BB&T Atlanta Open. The 2012 and later editions have been held in Atlantic Station in midtown Atlanta." .

lsd:Entity_35507 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2015 Vincentian general election were held in Saint Vincent and the Grenadines on 09 December 2015." .

lsd:Entity_3551 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 London Marathon was the 34th running of the annual marathon race in London, England, which took place on Sunday, 13 April 2014. The 2014 London Marathon was held on 13 April 2014. The men's elite race featured a particularly strong field, including marathon world_record holder Wilson Kipsang, reigning Olympic and world marathon champion Stephen Kiprotich, 2013 London Marathon champion Tsegaye Kebede, and London course_record holder Emmanuel Kipchirchir Mutai." .

lsd:Entity_35553 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Monterrey Challenger was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in Monterrey, Mexico from 26 to 31 of 26 October 2015." .

lsd:Entity_35567 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label ": ‘Η Ἁγία καὶ Μεγάλη Σύνοδος τῆς ’Ορθοδόξου ’Εκκλησίας) (also sometimes called the Council of Crete), was a synod of set representative bishops of the universally recognised autocephalous local churches of Eastern Orthodox Christianity held in Kolymvari, Crete. On 27 19 June 2016, the Synod of the Church of Antioch issued a statement concerning the Crete Council that stated that the documents adopted by in Crete were not binding for the Patriarchate of Antioch; the Church of Antioch recognized the Synod as \"a preliminary gathering on the way to a Pan_Orthodox Council\", while the documents it adopted as not final and open for discussion." .

lsd:Entity_35571 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 MTV Millennial Awards were held on 2017 at the Palacio de los Deportes in Mexico City, and was broadcast on 2017 through MTV Latin America." .

lsd:Entity_35579 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Summer Tour was a co_headlining tour by American bands Matchbox Twenty and the Goo Goo Dolls. Beginning in 2013, the tour supported the band's albums, North and Magnetic respectively." .

lsd:Entity_35598 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Linea Aeropostal Venezolana Flight 253 (November 1956) was being operated by a Lockheed L_749 Constellation, registration YV_C_AMA and named Jose Marti, on an international scheduled Passenger flight that took off from Idlewild International Airport (modern John F. Kennedy International Airport) bound for Caracas International Airport on 27 November 1956." .

lsd:Entity_356 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Apertura 2015 Copa MX Final was the final of the Apertura 2015 Copa MX, the seventh edition of the Copa MX under its current format and 74th overall organized by the Mexican Football Federation, the governing body of association football in Mexico. The final was contested in a single leg format between Liga MX clubs, Club León and C.D. Guadalajara. Club León has won the tournament five times which makes them tied with América and Puebla for most of all time, while C.D. Guadalajara has won it twice. C.D. Guadalajara last reached a final of the most previous edition of Copa MX, losing 4–2 to Puebla." .

lsd:Entity_35618 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 6 Hours of Spa_Francorchamps, formally the WEC 6 Heures de Spa_Francorchamps, was an endurance sports car racing 6 Hours of Spa_Francorchamps held at the Circuit de Spa_Francorchamps, Stavelot, Belgium on 2017–2017. It was the second race of the 2017 FIA World Endurance Championship, and was the sixth running of the 6 Hours of Spa_Francorchamps as part of the championship." .

lsd:Entity_35707 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Clásica de Almería was the 16th edition of the Clásica de Almería cycle race and was held on 04 March 2001. The race started in Vícar and finished in Vera." .

lsd:Entity_35780 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "'the Green Mountain War' or Arabic: حرب عمان, romanized: Ḥarb ʻumān), also known as Jebel Akhdar rebellion broke out in 1954 and again in 1957 in Oman, as an effort by the local Omanis in the interior of Oman led by their elected Imam, Ghalib Alhinai, to protect the Imamate of Oman from the occupation plans of sultan Said bin Taimur, backed by the British government, who were eager to gain access to the oil wells in the interior lands of Oman. On 1954, the Muscat and Oman Field Force (MOFF), later renamed Sultan of Oman's Armed Forces (SAF), which had eight British officers among its troops, marched from Fahud to Adam and occupied it. On 29 July 1957, the House of Commons debated the Jebel Akhdar War under the title \"Muscat and Oman\"." .

lsd:Entity_35849 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1932 Jalisco earthquake began on 03 June 1932 at 10:36 UTC with a megathrust event that registered 8.1 on the moment magnitude scale. With a maximum perceived intensity of X (Extreme) on the Mercalli intensity scale, at least 400 deaths were caused in Mexico and neighboring Guatemala. It was the first of a series of seismic events that affected parts of western Mexico during the month of 03 June 1932, all reaching magnitude 7 or greater. Carlos Valdez, director of the National Seismology Center at the National Autonomous University of Mexico, called the earthquake the most powerful quake in modern Mexican history. The initial earthquake of 03 June 1932 off of the coast of Colima and Jalisco caused extensive damage along western Mexico, with much of the deaths and injuries concentrated in the area of Guadalajara." .

lsd:Entity_35871 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Stångebro, or the Battle of Linköping, took place at Linköping, Sweden, on 25 September 1598 (O.S.) In the battle, an army of c. 8, 000–12,000 commanded by Duke Charles defeated a mixed force of c. 5,000–8,000 consisting of an invading army of mercenaries in the king's employ and diverse but poorly co_ordinated supporting Swedish noblemen's forces commanded by King of both Sweden and the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth Sigismund III Vasa, who was acting to maintain and restore his personal union against anti_Catholic forces in Lutheran Sweden. The force won a battle against the troops of Duke Charles at Stegeborg but soon found itself encircled and retired to Linköping." .

lsd:Entity_35934 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1979 European Competition for Women's Football was a women's association football tournament contested by European nations. It took place in Italy from 19 to 27 July 1979. Denmark women's national football team won the tournament, beating hosts Italy 2–0 in the final at Stadio San Paolo. The European Confederation, Union of European Football Associations (UEFA), displayed little enthusiasm for women's association football and were particularly hostile to Italy's independent women's association football federation." .

lsd:Entity_35948 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss World 2001, the 51st edition of the Miss World pageant, was held on 16 November 2001 at the Super Bowl of Sun City, North West Entertainment Centre in Sun City, North West, South Africa. The Miss World 2001 contest was originally set to be held in Durban, but later changed the venue to Sun City, North West." .

lsd:Entity_35970 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Trois_Rivières was fought on 08 June 1776, during the American Revolutionary War. A site near the Le Jeune bridge was designated a National Historic Site of Canada in 1920 in order to commemorate the battle. There are three plaques in the city of Trois_Rivières commemorating aspects of the battle. During the American retreat from Quebec, and in this battle, wounded soldiers were treated at the Ursuline convent in Trois_Rivières." .

lsd:Entity_3598 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1834 Hebron pogrom occurred in early 01 August 1834, when the forces of Ibrahim Pasha launched an assault against Hebron to crush the last pocket of significant resistance in Palestine during the Peasants' revolt in Palestine." .

lsd:Entity_35984 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "luge at the 1992 Winter Olympics consisted of three events at La Plagne bobsleigh, luge, and skeleton track. Twenty_three nations participated in luge at the Albertville Games." .

lsd:Entity_35998 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1935–36 Palestine League was the fourth season of league football in the Mandatory Palestine. It began on 07 December 1935 and ended on 18 19 December 1936." .

lsd:Entity_36003 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 683, adopted on 22 December 1990, after recalling Resolution 21 (1947) which approved the Trusteeship Territory of the Japanese Mandated Islands (since known as the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands) as well as Chapter XII of the United Nations Charter which established the United Nations Trusteeship system, the Council determined that, in the light of entry into force of new status agreements for Micronesia, the Marshall Islands and the Northern Mariana Islands, the objectives of the Trusteeship Agreement had been completed and therefore ended the Trusteeship Agreement with those entities." .

lsd:Entity_36027 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Winter Universiade, the XXI Winter Universiade, took place in Tarvisio, Italy." .

lsd:Entity_36030 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1941 Iraqi coup d'état (Arabic: ثورة رشيد عالي الكيلاني, Thawrah Rašīd ʿAlī al_Kaylānī), also called the Rashid Ali Al_Gaylani coup or the Golden Square coup, was a nationalist and pro_Nazi coup d'état in Iraq on 01 April 1941 that overthrew the pro_British regime of Regent 'Abd al_Ilah and his Prime Minister Nuri al_Said and installed Rashid Ali al_Gaylani as Prime Minister." .

lsd:Entity_36037 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1980 Svenska Cupen Final took place on 20 June 1984 at Råsunda Stadium in Solna. The match was contested by Allsvenskan sides Malmö FF and IK Brage. Brage played their first cup final ever, Malmö FF played their first final since 1978 and their 13th final in total." .

lsd:Entity_36055 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1926 Horta earthquake (Portugal: Sismo da Horta de 1926/Terramoto da Horta), occurred at 8:42 a.m. (local time) on 31 August 1926. It caused the destruction of many of the buildings located in the city of Horta, the central group of the Portugal autonomous region of the Azores, resulting in the death of nine and the partial or complete destruction of 4,138 buildings. On 31 August 1926, at about 8:40 in the morning, the islands were raised by a violent earthquake with its epicentre centralized in the Faial_Pico Channel, at a depth of 1.6–4 kilometres (0.99–2.49 mi) and with a body wave magnitude of 5.3–5.9. The earthquake progressed to a Mercalli Intensity of X (Extreme) in the northern part of Horta (around Conceição)." .

lsd:Entity_36070 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ovid's exile is related by the poet himself, and also in brief references to the event by Pliny the Elder and Statius. Ovid wrote that the cause of his exile was carmen et error: \"a poem and an error\", probably the Ars Amatoria and a personal indiscretion or mistake. Ovid's poems in exile have been seen as of fundamental importance for the study of Roman aristocracy under Augustus and Tiberius, furnishing \"precious pieces of information about events and persons\". In modern times, classicists have questioned whether the exile was merely a farce, a misrepresentation by Ovid, or a rhetorical and literary device. Ovid wrote later that the reason for his exile was carmen et error – \"a poem and a mistake\", claiming that what he did was nothing illegal, but nevertheless worse than murder, more harmful than poetry. The carmen to which Ovid referred has been identified as Ars Amatoria (The Art of Love), written some seven years before his exile, although Ovid expresses surprise that only he has been exiled for such a reason, though many others also wrote obscene verse, seemingly with the emperor's approval. A more recent thesis has been that Ovid's exile was not real. Early in the 20th century, J. J. Hartman argued that Ovid never left Rome for exile, and that all of his works referring to it are an imaginative and humorous fiction. In a 1985 article, A.D. Fitton Brown also argued that Ovid's exile was fictional. According to Pliny the Elder, Ovid wrote another poem about fishing while in exile. In his works from exile, principally the Tristia and the Epistulae, Ovid tried to do three things that he hoped would help convince the emperor to end his exile: Much has been written suggesting that what Ovid wrote during this period is entirely different from his earlier works. According to Ovid himself, his exile ruined his former poetic genius." .

lsd:Entity_36109 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 Copa Sudamericana Finals was a two_legged football match_up to determine the 2004 Copa Sudamericana champion. It was contested by Bolivian club Club Bolívar and Argentinian club Club Atlético Boca Juniors." .

lsd:Entity_36151 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Honda Indy Toronto was the second running of the Honda Indy Toronto (it had been conducted for 22 previous years under different sponsorship) and the tenth round of the 2010 IndyCar Series season." .

lsd:Entity_36244 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Tian Shan (simplified Chinese: 天山之战; traditional Chinese: 天山之戰; pinyin: Tiānshān zhī zhàn) was a battle fought in Tian Shan (in modern_day Xinjiang) in 99 BC during the Han–Xiongnu War." .

lsd:Entity_3626 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 53rd running of the 1969 Tour of Flanders cycling race in Belgium was held on Sunday 30 March 1969. Belgian cycling legend Eddy Merckx won ahead of Italians Felice Gimondi and Marino Basso, winning his first of two in the Flemish classic. Eddy Merckx won practically every major cycling event in 1969, including the 1969 Tour of Flanders. He arrived in Gentbrugge with a 5' 36\" lead over runner_up Felice Gimondi, the biggest margin in the history of the 1969 Tour of Flanders." .

lsd:Entity_36284 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1984 Virginia Slims of Los Angeles was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts at the Manhattan Country Club in Manhattan Beach, California in the United States that was part of the 1984 Virginia Slims World Championship Series. The tournament was held from 01 October 1984 through 07 October 1984." .

lsd:Entity_36292 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 California lieutenant gubernatorial election was held on 02 November 2010 to choose the Lieutenant Governor of California. Incumbent Republican Lieutenant Governor of California Abel Maldonado, who was appointed to the office, ran for election to a full term and was defeated by Democratic Mayor Gavin Newsom of San Francisco." .

lsd:Entity_36300 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 English Badminton Championships was held in University of Derby Sports Centre, from 05 February 2016 to 07 February 2016." .

lsd:Entity_36361 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 WGC_Dell Match Play Championship was the 18th WGC Match Play, played March 23–27 at Austin Country Club in Austin." .

lsd:Entity_3639 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1995 Empress's Cup Final was the 17th final of the Empress's Cup competition. The final was played at Nishigaoka Soccer Stadium in Tokyo on March 3, 1996. Fujita SC Mercury won their 1st title, by defeating Nippon TV Beleza 3–2." .

lsd:Entity_36391 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015–16 Austrian Cup (German: ÖFB_Samsung_Cup) was the 82nd season of Austria's nationwide football cup competition. It began with the matches of the First Round on 17 July 2015 and ended on 20 19 May 2016 with the final at Wörthersee Stadion in Klagenfurt." .

lsd:Entity_36395 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1962 Tour de Suisse was the 26th edition of the Tour de Suisse cycle race and was held from 14 June 1962 to 20 June 1962." .

lsd:Entity_36452 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The women's curling tournament of the curling at the 2018 Winter Olympics – women's tournament was held between 2018 and 2018 at the Gangneung Indoor Ice Rink." .

lsd:Entity_36464 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Orange Open Guadeloupe was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in Le Gosier, Guadeloupe between 2012 – 01 April 2012." .

lsd:Entity_36473 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Hillary Clinton presidential campaign, 2008, then junior United States Senator from New York, was announced on her website on 20 January 2007. On the final day of primaries on 2008, Obama had gained enough pledged_ and super_delegates to become the presumptive nominee; she then suspended her campaign on 07 June 2008, and endorsed Barack Obama. On 2008, Solis Doyle ceased duties as campaign manager, and become a senior adviser, traveling with Clinton. Maggie Williams was appointed campaign manager; she had been Clinton's chief of staff at the White House. A 2008, NPR article stated (with regard to mailing lists) that \"Last year, New York Sen. Hillary Clinton took the unusual step of renting out some of her lists.\" Later in 2008, Clinton backed out of a cover photo shoot with Vogue over concerns by the Clinton camp that she would appear \"too feminine,\" which prompted the magazine's editor_in_chief, Anna Wintour, to write, \"Imagine my amazement, then, when I learned that Hillary Clinton, our only female presidential hopeful, had decided to steer clear of our pages at this point in her campaign for fear of looking too feminine. In mid 2008, a flurry of articles circulated announcing that \"Hillary Clinton and Sarah Palin plan to appear next week at the same rally in New York City – perhaps the closest the two history_making women will be to each other before Election Day.\"" .

lsd:Entity_36500 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Stirling Castle took place from 8 January to 01 February 1746, during the Jacobite rising of 1745, when a Jacobite force besieged Stirling Castle, held by a government garrison under William Blakeney. Despite defeating a relief force under Henry Hawley at Falkirk Muir on 17 January, the siege made little progress; when Cumberland's army began advancing north from Edinburgh, it was abandoned and on 01 February 1746 the Jacobites withdrew to Inverness. One of the strongest fortifications in Scotland, Stirling Castle controlled access between the Highlands and the Lowlands. De Gordon arrived at Stirling on 6 January to supervise siege operations, but his artillery did not arrive until 14 January and in the end never saw action. Charles reluctantly complied, but this destroyed the last remnants of trust between the two parties; on 01 February 1746, the siege was abandoned, and the Jacobite army withdrew." .

lsd:Entity_36514 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The two_man women's bobsleigh competition at the bobsleigh at the 2018 Winter Olympics – two_woman was held on 20 February 2018 and 21 February 2018 at the Alpensia Sliding Centre near Pyeongchang, South Korea. The first two runs were held on 20 February 2018 and the last runs on 21 February 2018." .

lsd:Entity_36535 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The FIS Freestyle World Ski Championships 2003 were held between January 31 and February 2 at the Deer Valley ski resort in northern Utah near Park City, United States of America." .

lsd:Entity_36601 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Wisniowiec (also known as the Battle of Lopuszno) took place on 28 April 1512. The battle was fought in Lopushne near Vyshnivets." .

lsd:Entity_36607 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 LPGA Championship was the 36th Women's PGA Championship, played July 26–29 at Bethesda Country Club in Bethesda, a suburb northwest of Washington, D.C. Five strokes back, Beth Daniel shot a final round 66 (−5) for 280 (−4) to win her sole major title, a stroke ahead of runner_up Rosie Jones, the third round leader." .

lsd:Entity_36631 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Action of 15 July 1805 was a small naval action that took place off Chausey, on the coast of Normandy, involving two British gun_brigs on one side, and vessels on the other. In 1805 Plumper, together with her sister_ship Teazer, were part of the Royal Navy force blockading the coat of northern France." .

lsd:Entity_36635 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1981 Chengdu_Kunming Railway Train Crash occurred on 09 July 1981, when train number 442 passed the failed Liziyida bridge near Ganluo County, Sichuan province." .

lsd:Entity_36639 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The naval Battle of Matapan took place on 19 July 1717 off the Cape Matapan, on the coast of the Mani Peninsula in southern Greece, between the Armada Grossa of the Republic of Venice, supported by a mixed squadron of allied ships from Portugal, the Papal States and Malta, and the Ottoman fleet, under Kapudan Pasha Eğribozlu İbrahim Pasha. The 24 Republic of Venice sailing ships under Marcantonio Diedo, commander of the Republic of Venice fleet, met up with another Republic of Venice squadron of 24 galleys under the Capitano generale da Mar Andrea Pisani and a small squadron of 9 mixed Portugal_Malta ships under the Malta knight Bellefontaine near Cape Matapan on 2 July. As a result of the battle, the Republic of Venice attempt to recapture the Morea was foiled and the Ottoman reconquest of the peninsula was confirmed. 13 Republic of Venice 5 Malta 4 Papal 2 Tuscan." .

lsd:Entity_36664 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 6 Hours of Donington was an auto racing held at the Donington Park, Leicestershire, United Kingdom on 13–2012. It was the second round of the 2012 European Le Mans Series season, and the first time that the European Le Mans Series held the 6 Hours of Donington since 2006." .

lsd:Entity_36687 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990 WTA Tour Championships was the season_ending women's tennis held at the Madison Square Garden in New York City, United States between 12 November 1990 and 18 November 1990." .

lsd:Entity_36701 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988 Taiwan Open was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts in Taipei, Taiwan and was part of the Category 1 tier of the 1988 Virginia Slims World Championship Series. It was the third edition of the tournament and was held from 18 April 1988 through 24 April 1988." .

lsd:Entity_36707 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Carbisdale (also known as Invercarron) took place close to the village of Culrain, Sutherland, Scotland on 27 April 1650 and was part of the Wars of the Three Kingdoms. Although Carbisdale is the name of the nearest farm to the site of the battle, Culrain is the nearest village." .

lsd:Entity_36711 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Blockade of Veracruz was a conflict during the Mexican_American War. The blockade of Veracruz was extremely important in the Mexican_American War in stopping the trade of contraband. On 1846, Conner proclaimed Veracruz, Alvarado, Tampico and Matamoros under blockade Conner sent the sloop_of_war St. Mary's to Tampico, the paddle frigate Mississippi to Veracruz, and the sloop_of_war Falmouth to Alvarado." .

lsd:Entity_36723 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Martinair Flight 138 was a chartered flight from Surabaya, Indonesia, to Colombo, Sri Lanka. On 04 December 1974, the aircraft, a McDonnell Douglas DC_8_55CF, crashed into a mountain shortly before landing, killing all 191 people aboard – 182 Indonesian hajj pilgrims bound for Mecca, and 9 crew members. Sri Lanka aviation authorities later took the blame for their poor communication with the tech crew of the flight \" The aircraft took off from Juanda International Airport Indonesia at approximately 1200 hours on 04 December 1974 to proceed to Jeddah, Saudi_Arabia with a programmed stop at Bandaranaike Airport, near Colombo." .

lsd:Entity_36763 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "wrestling at the 2015 European Games – men's Greco_Roman 75 kg competition at the wrestling at the 2015 European Games in Baku, Azerbaijan, took place on 14 June at the Heydar Aliyev Sports and Exhibition Complex." .

lsd:Entity_36769 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1973_74 Cypriot Cup was the 32nd edition of the Cypriot Cup. It began on 06 March 1974 with the preliminary round and concluded on 23 June 1974 with the final which was held at GSP Stadium. AC Omonia won their 3rd Cypriot Cup trophy after beating Enosis Neon Paralimni FC 2–0 in the final." .

lsd:Entity_36805 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Erzurum Offensive (Russian: Эрзурумское сражение Erzurumskoe srazhenie, Turkish: Erzurum Taarruzu) or Battle of Erzurum (Turkish: Erzurum Muharebesi) was a major winter offensive by the Imperial Russian Army on the Caucasus Campaign, during the World War I that led to the capture of the strategic city of Erzurum. As of 10 January 1916, Ottoman Empire forces were 126,000 men, only 50,539 of whom were combat soldiers. On January 17, at Battle of Koprukoy The forces at Köprüköy, the main town on the road to Erzurum, were forced to leave. On the same day, Russian forces captured Muş after the Battle of Mush, 70 mi from Erzurum. Erzurum was considered as the second best_defended town in the Ottoman Empire. The Ottoman Empire units began to retreat from the fortified zones at the front and to evacuate the town of Erzurum. The Ottoman Empire did not have a chance to enjoy its victory at the Battle of Gallipoli since its loss of Erzurum changed the atmosphere in an instant. The Battle of Erzurum forms the climax of John Buchan's novel Greenmantle." .

lsd:Entity_36830 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Wielkopolska Chronicle (or Chronicle of Greater Kingdom of Poland, Polish: Kronika wielkopolska) is an anonymous medieval chronicle describing supposed history of Kingdom of Poland from legendary times up to the year 1273. The chronicle was written from the point of view of the region of Wielkopolska (Greater Kingdom of Poland)." .

lsd:Entity_36836 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 FIBA Intercontinental Cup was the 23rd edition of the FIBA Intercontinental Cup for men's professional basketball clubs and the 22nd edition of the tournament being in the form of a true intercontinental tournament for clubs. The 2 game aggregate score tournament took place at the Ginásio José Corrêa arena in Barueri, São Paulo, Brazil, on October 4 and 2013, in order to determine the world club champion. The tournament was contested between the 2012–13 season EuroLeague champions, Olympiacos B.C., and the 2013 FIBA Americas League champions, Pinheiros Sky. Olympiacos B.C. won the series 2_0." .

lsd:Entity_36934 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "During the 2002–03 Leicester City F.C. season English football season, Leicester City F.C. competed in the Football League First Division after being relegated from the FA Premier League 2001–02 Leicester City F.C. season." .

lsd:Entity_3695 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Hurricane Cleo was the strongest hurricane of the 1964 North Atlantic tropical cyclone season. Early on 21 August 1964 hurricane warnings were in effect for Barbados and the Windward Islands." .

lsd:Entity_37013 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Ottoman conquest of Adrianople, a major Byzantine Empire city in Thrace, was conquered by the Ottoman Empire sometime in the 1360s, and eventually became the Ottoman capital, until the Fall of Constantinople in 1453. The main target of the advance was Ottoman conquest of Adrianople, which was the third most important Byzantine Empire city (after Constantinople and Thessalonica). The date of Ottoman conquest of Adrianople's fall to the Turks has been disputed among scholars due to the differing accounts in the source material, with the years 1361 to 1362, 1367 and 1371 variously proposed. Following sources dating from long after the events, earlier scholarship generally placed the conquest between 1361 and 1363, in accordance with the report in Ottoman sources that a solar eclipse occurred in the year of Ottoman conquest of Adrianople's fall. Thus later Turkish sources report that Lala Shahin Pasha defeated the Byzantine Empire ruler (tekfur) of the city at a battle in Sazlıdere southeast of the city, forcing him to flee secretly by boat. Based on Elisabeth Zachariadou's examination of previously unregarded Byzantine Empire sources, most modern scholars have moved to the view that the city was captured in 1369. Thus a poem from the city's metropolitan bishop to Emperor John V Palaiologos shows Ottoman conquest of Adrianople to have still been in Byzantine Empire hands in Christmas 1366, while a series of Byzantine Empire short chronicles place the date of its capture in 1369. Edirne did not immediately become the Ottoman Empire' capital; Murad's court continued to reside in Bursa and in nearby Demotika, as well as Edirne. The conquest of Ottoman conquest of Adrianople was a turning point in the history of the Ottoman Empire in Europe: prior to this the Balkan peoples had regarded them as transient raiders, like so many that came before them in centuries prior. Instead, the transformation of Ottoman conquest of Adrianople into the new Ottoman capital of Edirne signalled to the local populace that the Ottoman Empire intended to settle permanently in Europe." .

lsd:Entity_37019 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Maryland gubernatorial election was held on 07 November 2006. Elected to his first term in 2002 Maryland gubernatorial election, incumbent Republican Governor Bob Ehrlich ran for a second term as governor, opposed by the Democratic nominee, Martin O'Malley, the Mayor of Baltimore." .

lsd:Entity_37028 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 32 was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship at the Meadowlands Arena in East Rutherford on 29 June 2001." .

lsd:Entity_37069 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Türk Telecom İzmir Cup was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in İzmir, Turkey between 19 September 2011 and 25 September 2011." .

lsd:Entity_37073 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1991 Indian general election were held in India in 1991 to elect the members of the 10th Lok Sabha. The remaining election days were postponed until mid_June and voting finally took place on 12 June 1991 and 15 June 1991." .

lsd:Entity_37082 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Kentucky Cup Turf Stakes is a Grade III American Thoroughbred horse race for three years olds and older, over a distance of 1 1⁄2 miles on the turf held annually in September at Kentucky Downs racetrack in Franklin, Kentucky during their short turf meeting." .

lsd:Entity_37104 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Michelob Championship at Kingsmill was a golf tournament on the PGA Tour from 1968 to 2002. It was played in Virginia at the River Course of Kingsmill Golf Club outside of Williamsburg, from 1981 to 2002. The event was founded in 1968 as the Kaiser International Open Invitational, which was played in northern California at Silverado Country Club in Napa through 1980." .

lsd:Entity_37121 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Nutuk (Modern Turkish: Söylev; The Speech) was a speech delivered by Mustafa Kemal Atatürk from 15 to 20 01 October 1927, at the second congress of Cumhuriyet Halk Partisi." .

lsd:Entity_37207 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1921 Copa del Rey was the 21st staging of the Copa del Rey, the Spanish association football cup competition. The competition started on 09 April 1921, and concluded on 08 May 1921, with the Final, held at the San Mamés in Bilbao, in which Athletic Club lifted the trophy for the 8th time ever with a 4–1 victory over Athletic Madrid." .

lsd:Entity_37218 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1987 UK Championship (also known as the 1987 Tennent's UK Championship for sponsorship reasons) was a professional ranking snooker tournament that took place at the Preston Guild Hall in Preston, England. The event started on 13 13 November 1987 and the televised stages were shown on BBC between 21 1987 and 29 13 November 1987." .

lsd:Entity_37232 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1996 United States presidential election in Kansas took place on 05 November 1996, as part of the 1996 United States presidential election. Kansas was won by former home state Senator Bob Dole (R_Kansas) over President of the United States Bill Clinton (D), with Dole winning 54.29% to 36.08% by a margin of 18.21%. Billionaire businessman Ross Perot (Reform Party of the United States of America_TX) finished in third, with 8.62% of the popular vote, a sharp decline from 1992 United States presidential election in Kansas, when Perot captured 27% of the state’s votes and held George H.W." .

lsd:Entity_37236 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Badminton at the All_Africa Games at the badminton at the 2011 All_Africa Games in Maputo was held between 06 September 2011–12, 2011." .

lsd:Entity_37242 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Japan Open Tennis Championships – Women's Doubles was the women's doubles event of the twenty_fifth edition of the Japan Open; a WTA Tier III tournament held in Tokyo, Japan. Corina Morariu and Kimberly Po won in the final 6–3, 6–2 against Catherine Barclay and Kerry_Anne Guse." .

lsd:Entity_37248 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Dolinskoye (Dolinskoe, Dolinsky), which took place 25 kilometers northwest of the Chechen Republic capital of Grozny, was the first major ground engagement of the First Chechen War. The battle began on 12 01 December 1994, when six officers (including two colonels) and 13 enlisted men of the Russian Airborne Troops died in a surprise 9K51 Grad multiple rocket launcher attack on an advancing column of armored vehicles of the 106th Airborne Division and 56th Airborne Brigade. The Russians lost 21 soldiers killed in the initial attack and admitted losing up to 200 men in the overall battle., According to the Chechen Republic commander Hussein Ikshanov." .

lsd:Entity_37254 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1925 Australian federal election was held in Australia on 1925. The incumbent Nationalist–Country coalition, led by Prime Minister of Australia Stanley Bruce, defeated the opposition Labor Party led by Matthew Charlton in a landslide. Prime Minister of Australia Stanley Bruce was a supporter of the White Australia Policy, and made it an issue in his campaign for the 1925 Australian Federal election." .

lsd:Entity_37272 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1991 DFB_Pokal Final decided the winner of the 1990–91 DFB_Pokal, the 48th season of Germany's premier knockout association football cup competition. It was played on 22 June 1991 at the Olympiastadion Berlin in Berlin. SV Werder Bremen won the match 4–3 on penalties against 1. FC Köln, following a 1–1 draw after extra time, to claim their second cup title." .

lsd:Entity_3730 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Clonfin Ambush was an ambush carried out by the Irish Republican Army (IRA) on 02 February 1921, during the Irish War of Independence." .

lsd:Entity_37338 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Indonesia Open Badminton Championships in badminton was held in Jakarta, from 25 July 2001 to 29 July 2001." .

lsd:Entity_37382 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1943 Paris–Roubaix was the 41st edition of the Paris–Roubaix, a classic one_day cycle race in France. The single day event was held on 25 April 1943 and stretched 250 km (155 mi) from Paris to the finish at Roubaix Velodrome." .

lsd:Entity_37421 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Monte Carlo Rally (formally known as the 81ème Rallye Automobile Monte_Carlo) was a motor racing event for rally cars that was held over four days between 16 January and 19 January, and marked the eighty_first running of the Monte Carlo Rally. Thirteen World Rally Car crews were entered in the event, including the defending World Drivers' Champion Sébastien Loeb, prior to the start a six_time winner of the Monte Carlo Rally. The rally was won by Sébastien Loeb, the seventy_seventh of his career and his seventh victory on the Monte Carlo Rally. The itinerary for the 2013 rally remained relatively unchanged from 2012 Monte Carlo Rally. With the cars running in the order that they finished the 2012 Monte Carlo Rally season, Sébastien Loeb was the first driver through the stages, and on his arrival at the end of Le Moulinon—Antraigues it was observed that the dry conditions had torn the studs free of his front tyres." .

lsd:Entity_37461 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 CAF Confederation Cup Final was the final of the 2014 CAF Confederation Cup, the 11th edition of the CAF Confederation Cup, Africa's secondary club association football competition organized by the Confederation of African Football (CAF). The final was contested in two_legged home_and_away format between Pedro Sangome of Côte d'Ivoire and Al Ahly SC of Egypt. The first leg was hosted by Pedro Sangome at the Stade Robert Champroux in Abidjan on 2014, while the second leg was hosted by Al Ahly SC at the Cairo International Stadium in Cairo on 2014. This was the first African final for Pedro Sangome. While Al Ahly SC had reached the finals of the African Champions Cup/CAF Champions League ten times and the African Cup Winners' Cup four times respectively, this was their first final in the CAF Confederation Cup. In their head_to_head meetings, the home match of Pedro Sangome finished in a 1–1 draw, while Al Ahly SC won their home match 1–0. Both teams finished with nine points, and Al Ahly SC won the group over Pedro Sangome on head_to_head record." .

lsd:Entity_37511 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Deir Yassin massacre took place on 09 April 1948, when around 130 fighters from the Far_right wing Zionist paramilitary groups Irgun and Lehi killed at least 107 Palestinian Arabs, including women and children, in Deir Yassin, a village of roughly 600 people near Jerusalem. Israeli military historian Uri Milstein alleged in 1998 that Pa'il was not in Deir Yassin on 09 April 1948. Pa'il, who died in 2015, defended himself in an interview in 2007: \"What the Lehi and Etzel people did in Deir Yassin in 09 April 1948 was a despicable act." .

lsd:Entity_37547 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Quart Festival was an annual popular music festival that took place in Kristiansand, Norway in the beginning of July. It was the most visited music festival in Norway. It was first named Qvadradurmusivalen in 1991, but changed into the more ear_catching Quart Festival the following year. For several years Quart was the largest music festival in Norway, but went bankrupt in 2008 in part due to tough competition from the Hovefestivalen in Arendal and some Oslo_based festivals. The Quart Festival was revived by one of the original organisers and was held on 30 June to 2009." .

lsd:Entity_37553 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss America 1939, the 13th Miss America pageant, was the last pageant to be held at the famed Steel Pier in Atlantic City, New Jersey. The finals were held on Saturday, 1939, and Miss Michigan, Patricia Donnelly, was crowned Miss America 1939." .

lsd:Entity_37562 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Europe Cup in Badminton was the 33rd edition of the Europe Cup in badminton. It was held between June 23–27, 2010, in the ZBC_Hal, in Zwolle, Netherlands. The draw was held on 2010 at Zwolle, Netherlands." .

lsd:Entity_37621 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Singapore Grand Prix, formally known as the 2008 Formula 1 SingTel Singapore Grand Prix, was a Formula One race held on 28 September 2008 at 20:00 SST at the newly built Marina Bay Street Circuit in Marina Bay, Singapore. This was also the first time Singapore hosted a Formula One race, as the last Singapore Grand Prix was a Formula Libre event in 1973. The 61_lap race was won by Fernando Alonso for the Renault team from 15th on the grid, after his teammate deliberately crashed on lap 14 to bring out the safety car after his first pit stop." .

lsd:Entity_37653 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The battle of Kolding (Slaget ved Kolding) on 09 January 1644 was the opening engagement of the Torstenson War between the Swedish Empire and Denmark_Norway. The battle was primarily a cavalry engagement between Swedish and Danish cavalry near the Danish seaport of Kolding." .

lsd:Entity_37682 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Schwyz occurred on 14 August 1799–15 August 1799 between French forces commanded by General of Division André Masséna and Major General von Franz Jellachich's brigade." .

lsd:Entity_37688 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Una (Croatian: Operacija Una) was a military offensive conducted by the Croatian Army (Hrvatska vojska – HV) against the Army of Republika Srpska (Vojska Republike Srpske – VRS) in western Bosnia and Herzegovina on 18 September 1995–19 September 1995, during the Bosnian War. The ARBiH drive towards Sanski Most and Novi Grad, where one of the bridgeheads had been established by the HV, came to a halt on 18 September 1995–19 September 1995, as the ARBiH encountered 14,000 previously undetected VRS troops in the area, supported by 2,000 troops that had arrived from Serbia. On 20 19 September 1995, Červenko submitted his report on Operation Una to Tuđman, divorcing responsibility from himself, and blaming Vrbanac and Defence Minister Gojko Šušak." .

lsd:Entity_3770 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 8th Golden Horse Film Awards (Mandarin:第8屆金馬獎) took place on 30 October 1970 at Zhongshan Hall in Taipei, Taiwan." .

lsd:Entity_37719 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Tripoli airport clashes occurred on 04 June 2012, after members of the Al_Awfea militia stormed the Tripoli International Airport as a measure to prompt the government's release of its jailed leader, Abu Oegeila al_Hebshi." .

lsd:Entity_37733 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1983 WTA German Open, also known by its sponsored name Fila German Open, was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts at the Rot_Weiss Tennis Club Berlin in West Berlin in West Germany that was part of the 1983 Virginia Slims World Championship Series. The tournament was held from 16 May 1983 through 22 May 1983." .

lsd:Entity_37849 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1975 Virginia Slims of Houston was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet court at the Sam Houston Coliseum and Music Hall in Houston, Texas in the United States that was part of the 1975 WTA Tour." .

lsd:Entity_37862 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1976 U.S. Open was the 76th U.S. Open, held June 17–20 at the Highlands Course of the Atlanta Athletic Club in Duluth, Georgia, a suburb northeast of Atlanta." .

lsd:Entity_3792 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1930 German football championship, the 23rd edition of the competition, was won by Hertha BSC, defeating Holstein Kiel 5–4 in the final. The teams qualified through the regional championships: The round of 16, played on 18 May 1930: The quarter_finals, played on 1 22 June 1930, with the replay held on 9 June: The semi_finals, played on 15 22 June 1930: The final, played on 22 June 1930:" .

lsd:Entity_37958 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle on Vrtijeljka (Serbian: бој на Вртијељци, romanized: boj na Vrtijeljci) was fought on the hill of Vrtijeljka near Cetinje between a Venetian irregular force and an advancing Ottoman force on 07 May 1685 at the start of the Morean War. The two met at the hill of Vrtijeljka on 07 May 1685." .

lsd:Entity_37968 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Indy Japan: The Final was the ninth and final running of the Indy Japan 300 and the sixteenth round of the 2011 IndyCar Series season. The race was contested over 63 laps at the 2.983_mile (4.801 km) Twin Ring Motegi road course in Motegi, Tochigi, Japan." .

lsd:Entity_37988 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Istria Cup was the fourth edition of the Istria Cup, an invitational women's association football tournament held annually in Istria, Croatia. It took place from 02 March 2016–07 March 2016; at the same time as the 2016 Algarve Cup, 2016 SheBelieves Cup and 2016 Cyprus Cup." .

lsd:Entity_38017 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Commission of Inquiry into the Crimes and Misappropriations Committed by Ex_President Habré, His Accomplices and/or Accessories (French: Commission d'Enquête du Ministère Chadien de la Justice sur les Crimes du Régime de Hissène Habré) was established on 29 December 1990 by the President of Chad, Idriss Déby. Habré began a programme of widespread repression including torture and killings, until he was himself overthrown by one of his former generals, the Libyan_backed Idriss Déby, in 29 December 1990." .

lsd:Entity_38032 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Miss World 1981, the 31st edition of the Miss World pageant, was held on 1981 at the Royal Albert Hall in London, UK. Another Venezuelan, Irene Sáez, had been crowned Miss Universe 1981 in July, making Venezuela one of the few countries to hold both major international titles (Miss Universe and Miss World) in the same year." .

lsd:Entity_38069 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1996 Ukrainian Cup Final is a association football match that took place at the Olimpiyskiy National Sports Complex on 26 May 1996. The match was the 5th Ukraine Cup Final and it was contested by FC Dynamo Kyiv and PFC Nyva Vinnytsia. The 1996 Ukrainian Cup Final was the fifth to be held in the Ukraine capital Kiev." .

lsd:Entity_38100 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Bandy World Championship 2009 was held between 18 January 2009 and 25 January 2009 in Västerås, Sweden. Men's teams from 13 countries participated in the 2009 competition: Belarus, Finland, Kazakhstan, Norway, Russia, Sweden (group A) and Canada, Estonia, Hungary, Latvia, Mongolia, the Netherlands and the United States (group B). The main venues were ABB Arena Syd in Västerås, Sweden's largest indoor arena for bandy, and Hakonplan, an outdoor stadium. Statistics for goalscorers during Bandy World Championships 2009." .

lsd:Entity_38111 a lsd:Context_narration ;
