lsd:Entity_38145 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Tour Down Under was the seventh edition of the Tour Down Under stage race. It took place from 18 January 2005 to 23 January 2005 in and around Adelaide, South Australia. 18 January 2005 – Adelaide _ Adelaide, 50 km. 23 January 2005 – Adelaide to Adelaide, 81 km." .

lsd:Entity_38157 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Government Pension Fund Global comprises two entirely separate sovereign wealth fund owned by the government of Norway. Its name changed in 2006 from the Petroleum Fund of Norway. Norway's sovereign wealth fund is taking steps to become more active in company governance. Norway's Government Pension Fund Global (GPFG) has the potential to influence the corporate governance market in Europe, and possibly China as well, greatly. As a result of the large size of the fund relative to the low number of people living in Norway (5.2 million people in 2017), the Oil Fund has become a hot political issue, dominated by three main issues: There are diverse concerns and predicted effects of sovereign wealth fund on international financial markets and the global economy as a whole, with experts expressing strong fears regarding destabilization and protectionism stemming from sovereign wealth fund. The Ministry of Finance in Norway stated that it would not withdraw investing in these companies or discuss an eventual exclusion of surveillance industry companies from its investments." .

lsd:Entity_38164 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Zacatecas was a military action of the Mexican War of Independence fought on 15 April 1811 at Zacatecas, Zacatecas. The victory was not decisive and the Royalist army continued to harass the insurgents until they were defeated again at Zacatecas on 15 April 1811." .

lsd:Entity_38208 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Miss Paraguay 2007 pageant was won by María José Maldonado. In took place on 2007 at the Municipal Theatre Ignacio A. Pane in Asunción, Paraguay." .

lsd:Entity_38240 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "World Festival of Animated Film Zagreb (Croatian: Svjetski festival animiranog filma), also known as Animafest Zagreb, is a film festival entirely dedicated to animated film held annually in Zagreb, Croatia. Zagreb's candidacy for holding a permanent animated film festival was accepted at the 1969 ASIFA meeting in London." .

lsd:Entity_38254 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Cotagaita was fought on 27 October 1810 during the Campaign of Upper Peru in the Argentine War of Independence when the troops of the Army of the North were sent by the Primera Junta government in Buenos Aires to the Alto Perú to fight the Royalists. The battle was fought near the town of Santiago de Cotagaita, nowadays in Potosí Department in Bolivia." .

lsd:Entity_38277 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Noahidism (/ˈnoʊə.haɪd.ɪsm/) or Noachidism (/ˈnoʊə.xaɪd.ɪsm/) is a monotheistic Jewish religious movement based upon the Noahide laws and their traditional interpretations within Orthodox Judaism." .

lsd:Entity_38311 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Rakshasbhuvan was fought on 10 August 1763. However, the Marathas were being led by Peshwa Madhavrao (until the skirmish of Chambhar Gonda, Senasahebsubha Janoji Bhonsle and Raghunathrao, uncle of Peshwa were also in the camp), who was assisted by Visaji Tryambak, Sardar Naro Shankar Dani, Babuji Naik (A Chief of Senasahebsubha's Nagpur Army who, prior to battle a few months before, had made a friendship treaty with Nizam),Sardar Yashwantrao Wable (Kopergaon) and Sardar Malojiraje III Ghorpade of Mudhol trounced the Nizam's forces at Rakshasbhuvan after the battle was fought for five to six months." .

lsd:Entity_38327 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1969 Georgia 500 was a NASCAR Grand National Series event that was held on November 17, 1968, at Middle Georgia Raceway in Byron, Georgia. It is not to be confused with another running of the 1969 Georgia 500 which actually took place in 1969." .

lsd:Entity_38366 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup Final will be the 17th final of the Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup, the highest association football cup competition in Bosnia and Herzegovina. The date of both 2012 Final matches, as in all the recent years, is set so that it avoids clashes with Premier League of Bosnia and Herzegovina fixtures. That goal, as proved later, will be the only one F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo concede on his route to final. F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo met Borac, a team they faced also in the last two season of this competition (once in final). Krajišnik got in lead in 38_minute over Šaban Pehilj, Željezničars footballer on loan, but Hrvoje Mišić scored the equalizer for NK Široki Brijeg in 86_minute of the game for the final 1–1. In the last hurdle before the final, NK Široki Brijeg faced Velež. Mario Kvesić scored for 0–1 in the 69_minute, sealing the fate of Velež and securing his team the final of the Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup for the fourth time. This final marked the eight appearance in final of Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup for F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo and ninth final in domestic cups, since they were once in final of Yugoslav Cup. On the other side, this will be the fourth final for NK Široki Brijeg and they won it once (in 2007), with two finals lost (in 2005 and 2006). On 2012, a draw to decide who will be the first host was held with F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo hosting the first_leg on 25 April and NK Široki Brijeg the rematch three weeks later on 17 May, with both matches aired on BHT1. Before the match, F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo was in a more than a 3_year unbeaten streak in national cup, with the last lost match dating to 24 September 2008 against Zvijezda in the first round of 2008–09 Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup. They won two of the last three national cups, since they lost the final in 2009–10 Bosnia and Herzegovina Football Cup to Borac on an aggregate score of 3:3 after two draw matches. Nevertheless, manager of NK Široki Brijeg, Marijan Bloudek, admitted that F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo is the better side at the moment, with the many records and the league position proving that, but with his team very close behind and with realistic chances to win. Many managers and sport workers came to the final, not only from Bosnia and Herzegovina but also from the region. While NK Široki Brijeg didn't have any problems with suspended or injured players, Patrick Nyema Gerhardt, F.K. Željezničar Sarajevo's standard player, would miss the game because of booking." .

lsd:Entity_38391 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Mitzvah Day International is an annual day of faith_based social action that takes place in November each year, primarily in the United Kingdom. Mitzvah Day International was founded by Laura Marks in 2005, who, upon returning to her native UK from a period spent in Los Angeles, decided to bring the 'Mitzvah Day' concept she became familiar with through the Temple Israel of Hollywood synagogue back to the UK. Mitzvah Day was originally associated with the Jewish Community Centre for London, and became registered as an independent charity in the United Kingdom in 2008. Mitzvah Day has been publicly endorsed by many public figures in the United Kingdom, including former UK Prime Minister David Cameron, Deputy Prime Minister and Leader of the Liberal Democrats Nick Clegg, Leader of the Labour Party Ed Miliband Former UK Prime Minister Tony Blair, UK Prime Minister Boris Johnson, Chief Rabbi of the United Kingdom Jonathan Sacks, and The Archbishop of Canterbury. In 2012, the name of the organization officially changed from 'Mitzvah Day' to 'Mitzvah Day International' to reflect the growing participation of community groups outside the UK." .

lsd:Entity_38396 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Tyrepower Tasmania SuperSprint was a motor racing event for V8 Supercars, held on the weekend of 1 to 2016. The event was held at Symmons Plains Raceway in Launceston, Tasmania, and consisted of one race of 120 kilometres and one race of 200 km in length." .

lsd:Entity_38428 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1901–02 FA Cup was the thirty_first staging of the world's oldest association football competition, the Football Association Challenge Cup (more usually known as the FA Cup). Sheffield United F.C. won the competition for the second time, beating Southampton 2–1 in the replay of the 1902 FA Cup Final at Crystal Palace. The format of the FA Cup for the season had a preliminary round, five qualifying rounds, an intermediate round, three proper rounds, and the semi finals and 1902 FA Cup Final. Sheffield United F.C. eventually won and went on to meet Southampton in the 1902 FA Cup Final." .

lsd:Entity_38435 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hancock, also called the Romney Campaign, was a battle fought during the Romney Expedition, occurred January 5–6, 1862, in Washington County, and Morgan County, West Virginia, as part of Maj. Gen. Thomas J." .

lsd:Entity_38470 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Power Horse Cup was a men's tennis tournament played on clay courts. It was the first edition of the Power Horse Cup as an ATP World Tour 250 series event on the 2013 ATP World Tour and replaced the World Team Cup, a team event previously held at the same venue. It took place at the Rochusclub in Düsseldorf, Germany, from May 19 through 25 May 2013." .

lsd:Entity_38485 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Access All Areas Tour (advertised as the Access All Areas: North American Tour) was the second concert tour by supergroup, The AAA Girls." .

lsd:Entity_38489 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Budapest_Bamako or Great African Run is a charity car race in Africa, and the largest amateur rally in the world. It is a low_budget version of the Dakar Rally, and goes from Budapest, Hungary to Bamako, Mali through the Sahara. On 2005, forty_two teams lined up in Budapest's Hősök tere for the inaugural run of the Budapest_Bamako. The Budapest–Bamako is primarily a charity event, that brings direct donations to communities in Mali and Mauritania." .

lsd:Entity_38492 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "UFC 202 was a mixed martial arts event produced by the Ultimate Fighting Championship that was held on 20 August 2016, at T_Mobile Arena in Paradise, Nevada, part of the Las Vegas metropolitan area." .

lsd:Entity_38497 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Campeonato Ecuatoriano de Fútbol Serie A (officially known as the Copa Banco del Pacífico Ecuadorian Liga Pro for sponsorship reasons) is the 58th season of the Ecuadorian Liga Pro. Twelve teams are competing in the 2016 Ecuadorian Liga Pro season, ten of whom remain from the previous season. LDU Loja and Deportivo Quito were relegated from the Ecuadorian Liga Pro after accumulating the fewest points during the 2015 Campeonato Ecuatoriano de Fútbol Serie A." .

lsd:Entity_38522 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1994 Dutch Open was an ATP tennis tournament held in Hilversum, Netherlands and played on outdoor clay court. It was the 36th edition of the tournament and was held from 25 July 1994 to 01 August 1994." .

