lsd:Entity_3883 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Edict of Potsdam (German: Edikt von Potsdam) was a proclamation issued by Frederick William and Duke of Prussia, in Potsdam on 29 October 1685, as a response to the revocation of the Edict of Nantes by the Edict of Fontainebleau. Kein Neid ward wach, Nicht Eifersucht, _ man öffnete die Thür Und hieß als Glaubensbrüder uns willkommen...... Theodor Fontane, 1885, ' Encouraged by the French theologian_philosopher Jakob Abbadie, on 29 October 1685, Frederick William issued the Edict of Potsdam." .

lsd:Entity_38860 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Aanayoottu (feeding of elephants) is a festival held in the precincts of the Vadakkunnathan temple in City of Thrissur, in Kerala. Elephants are an integral part of Kerala culture, and elephants are integral to all festivals, including the Aanayoottu." .

lsd:Entity_38878 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 UNCAF Nations Cup was a Copa Centroamericana held in San Jose, Costa Rica in 17 March 1999." .

lsd:Entity_38882 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Cranston Fire was a wildfire that burned in southwest Riverside County, in the United States. The Cranston Fire allegedly was started on 25 July 2018, around noon, by Brandon M. McGlover, who allegedly started numerous fires in the region that day. On 25 July 2018, the same day the fire was reported, CAL FIRE arrested Brandon N. McGlover for setting multiple fires in Riverside County." .

lsd:Entity_38949 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Opening on 05 February 1989 at the National Art Museum of China (previously called the National Art Gallery), this exhibition included over 186 artists and approximately 300 artworks from all over China. China/Avant_Garde Exhibition — Exhibition Information, 1989." .

