lsd:Entity_46304 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Abukir (1801) of 08 March 1801 was the second pitched battle of the French campaign in Egypt and Syria to be fought at Abu Qir on the Mediterranean coast, near the Nile Delta." .

lsd:Entity_46326 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 48th Japan Record Awards took place at the New National Theatre Tokyo in Shibuya, Tokyo, on 2006, starting at 6:30PM JST. The primary ceremonies were televised in Japan on TBS Holdings." .

lsd:Entity_46330 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Oral Fixation Tour (known as Tour Fijación Oral in hispanophone countries) was the fourth concert tour by Colombian singer and songwriter, Shakira. It began on 14 01 June 2006 at the Feria De Muestras in Zaragoza, Spain. The tour concluded on 9 01 July 2007 at the Turkcell Kuruçeşme Arena in Istanbul, Turkey." .

lsd:Entity_46356 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 1373, adopted unanimously on 28 September 2001, is a counter_terrorism measure passed following the 11 September terrorist attacks on the United States. UN United Nations Security Council resolution 1566 picked up loose ends from 1373 by actually spelling out what the Security Council sees as terrorism: criminal acts, including against civilians, committed with the intent to cause death or serious bodily injury, or taking of hostages, with the purpose to provoke a state of terror in the general public or in a group of persons or particular persons, intimidate a population or compel a government or an international organization to do or to abstain from doing any act." .

lsd:Entity_46360 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Backlash was a professional wrestling pay_per_view (PPV) event produced by the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE) promotion. It took place on 2000, at the Capital One Arena in Washington, D.C. The first show was originally titled Backlash: In Your House, but the promotion dropped the \"In Your House\" name (previously a series of shows for the promotion) to establish monthly pay_per_views, in which Backlash was the first. The WWF brought back Backlash as the post_WrestleMania 2000 pay_per_view, thus establishing Backlash as an annual event for the promotion, as well as the annual post_WrestleMania event. prior to Backlash, Austin made his first WWF appearance in 6 months, where he dropped a concrete barrier from a crane onto the \"DX Express\" bus, causing it to explode." .

lsd:Entity_46364 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The North African Cup of Champions is a tournament designed by the Union of North African Football Federations (UNAF) that puts together the winners of the domestic leagues around North Africa." .

lsd:Entity_4637 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2019 Bolivian general election were held in Bolivia on 20 October 2019. As a result, the second vice president of Bolivia of the Senate, Jeanine Áñez of the opposition Democrat Social Movement, assumed the interim presidency of Bolivia on 2019. On 2019 the TSE cancelled the redo session after neither MAS nor 'Bolivia Dice No' protested the inclusion of the annulled ballots. The day after the election the vice_president of Bolivia of the TSE Antonio Costas resigned, citing his disagreement with the decision to stop transmitting results." .

lsd:Entity_46402 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 UCI Cyclo_cross World Championships were held in Tábor, Czech Republic on Saturday February 3 and Sunday 04 February 2001." .

lsd:Entity_46427 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 28th People's Choice Awards, honoring the best in American popular culture for 2001, were held on 13 January 2002 at the Shrine Auditorium in Los Angeles, California. They were hosted by Kevin James, and broadcast on CBS." .

lsd:Entity_46429 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 Hong Kong Chief Executive election was to select the second term of the Chief Executive of Hong Kong (CE) of the Hong Kong (HKSAR). Incumbent Chief Executive of Hong Kong Tung Chee Hwa was supported by Chinese leaders for his re_election as early as 2001." .

lsd:Entity_46462 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Fulton County Fair is located in Dover Township, Fulton County on Ohio State Route 108, just north the Ohio Turnpike Exit 34 near Wauseon." .

lsd:Entity_46493 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Adana massacre (Armenian: Ադանայի կոտորած, Turkish: Adana İğtişaşı) occurred in the Adana Vilayet of the Ottoman Empire in 01 April 1909. The government of Turkey, as well as some Turkish writers and nationalists, deny the massacre happened, claiming that the events of 01 April 1909 were in fact an Armenian \"rampage of pillaging and death\" targeting the Muslim population that \"ended up with about 17,000 Armenian and 1,850 Turkish deaths.\"" .

lsd:Entity_46505 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1926 World Series, the 23rd playing of Major League Baseball's championship series, pitted the National League champion St. Louis Cardinals against the American League champion New York Yankees. (p146) In early 1926, thousands of Cleveland fans, confident that their Indians would win the pennant even when they trailed the Yankees by six games, made World Series ticket reservations. This was Hoyt's fourth World Series with the Yankees, and he entered the 1926 Series with over 35 innings of pitching experience in the championship series. The 1926 World Series produced one of the most famous anecdotes in baseball history, involving Babe Ruth and Johnny Sylvester. (p119) Ruth's failed attempt to steal second base ended the 1926 World Series; it is the only time a World Series has ended with a runner being caught stealing. The Bronx Bombers would go on to sweep their next three World Series, 1927 World Series, 1928, and 1932." .

lsd:Entity_46510 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Uijeongbu was a battle fought in Uijeongbu during the Korean War from 25 to 26 June 1950, during the North Korean invasion of South Korea." .

