lsd:Entity_48067 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1980 Avon Championships of Cincinnati was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts at the Riverfront Coliseum in Cincinnati, Ohio in the United States that was part of the 1980 Avon Championships Circuit. It was the inaugural edition of the tournament and was held from 07 January 1980 through 13 January 1980." .

lsd:Entity_48074 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Islamic Solidarity Games is an international sporting event held in Palembang, Indonesia from 22 September 2013 to 01 October 2013." .

lsd:Entity_48121 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Constantinople by the Sasanian Empire Persians and Avars, aided by large numbers of Sclaveni, ended in a strategic victory for the Byzantine Empire. The new emperor's mismanagement left the Byzantine Empire vulnerable and unstable when the Sasanian Empire king Khosrau II (r. 590–628) invaded, using the coup as a pretext for war as Khosrau II was personally close to Maurice, who helped him return his throne after Bahram Chobin's revolt. Initially, the Sasanian Empire invasion was successful, with the Byzantine Empire being driven into the Anatolian heartland. Despite continuous bombardment for a month, morale was high inside the walls of Constantinople because of Patriarch Sergius' religious fervor and his processions along the wall with an icon, which could be the icon of the Virgin Mary, inspiring the belief that the Byzantine Empire were under divine protection. Though the Persians were experts in siege, the walls of Constantinople proved to defend easily against the siege towers and engines, amongst the reasons being that the former could not move their siege equipment to the European side of the Bosphorus (which was heavily guarded), where their Avar and Slavic allies were initially stationed." .

lsd:Entity_4813 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Copa del Rey de Baloncesto was the 63rd edition of the Copa del Rey de Baloncesto. It was organized by the ACB and was held in Valencia at the Pabellón Municipal Fuente de San Luis between 29 January 1999 and 01 February 1999." .

lsd:Entity_48150 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Hawaii gubernatorial election took place on 2014, to elect the Governor of Hawaii, concurrently with a special election to Hawaii's Class III Senate Seat, as well as other elections to the United States Senate in other states and elections to the United States House of Representatives and various state and local elections. Incumbent Democratic governor Neil Abercrombie ran for re_election to a second term in office, but was defeated by State Senator David Ige in the Democratic primary, making Abercrombie the first incumbent governor to lose renomination in Hawaii history." .

lsd:Entity_48181 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 2012 Summer Olympics – women's triple jump competition at the 2012 Summer Olympics in London, United Kingdom. The event was held at the London Stadium on 03 August 2012–05 August 2012." .

lsd:Entity_48193 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Gary Johnson presidential campaign, 2016, the 29th Governor of New Mexico, was announced on 2016, for the nomination of the Libertarian Party for President of the United States of America. Balanced Rebellion is a campaign advertisement and campaign project launched by AlternativePAC, the political action committee supporting Gary Johnson for President of the United States of America in the 2016 United States presidential election." .

lsd:Entity_48198 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Sejdić and Finci v. Bosnia and Herzegovina (27996/06 and 34836/06) was a case (merged from two) decided by the Grand Chamber of the European Court of Human Rights in 22 December 2009, in the first judgment finding a violation of Article 14 of the European Convention on Human Rights taken in conjunction with Article 3 of Protocol No. In November 2014, the UK and German foreign ministers, Philip Hammond and Frank_Walter Steinmeier, sent an \"open letter\" to the people of Bosnia and Herzegovina, which pledged substantive progress towards Bosnia's EU membership if Bosnia's politicians gave a written commitment to implement a package of reforms, including compliance with the Sejdic and Finci ruling of the European Court of Human Rights." .

lsd:Entity_4820 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Virginia gubernatorial election was held on 06 November 2001. Incumbent Republican Governor Jim Gilmore was barred from seeking a second term; Democratic nominee Mark Warner, the 1996 Democratic nominee for the U.S. Senate, defeated Republican nominee Mark Earley, the Attorney General of Virginia." .

lsd:Entity_48230 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Bangkusay Channel (Filipino: Labanan sa Ilog Bangkusay; Spanish: Batalla de Bangkusay), on 03 June 1571, was a naval engagement that marked the last resistance by locals to the Spanish Empire's occupation and colonization of the Pasig River delta, which had been the site of the indigenous polities of Rajahnate of Maynila and Tondo. On 03 June 1571, Tarik Sulayman, supported by Rajah Sulayman, led his troops down the Pampanga River and fought the battle in the bay of Bangkusay, off the port of Tondo. Legazpi was able to establish a municipal government for Manila on June 24, 1571, which eventually became the capital of the entire Spanish East Indies colony and subsequently the capital of the Philippines." .

lsd:Entity_48244 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 World Rowing Championships were World Rowing Championships that were held from 22 to 27 July 2008 in conjunction with the World Junior Rowing Championships in Ottensheim near Linz, Austria. Since 2008 was an Olympic year for rowing, the World Championships did not include Olympic events scheduled for the 2008 Summer Olympics, or the adaptive rowing events at the 2008 Summer Paralympics." .

lsd:Entity_48282 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Erzurum was a military engagement fought between the Ottoman Empire and the Russian Empire, during the Russo_Turkish War of 1877–78. The battle was fought on 08 November 1877_09 November 1877 on the Ottoman territory and ended with the Russians withdrawing to instead besiege Kars, which fell afterwards. On 4 09 November 1877 the Russian army achieved a victory at Uzunahmet, having inflicted heavy casualties on the Turks, which included 3,000 killed and wounded, 1,000 prisoners and 42 artillery pieces left by the panicked gunners, with a loss of only 1,200 men Although the Turkish troops ceased resistance and were fleeing in disarray, with 4,000 of them deserting the army, a part of their infantry maintained order and retreated to the well_fortified position in Erzurum with 14 guns The Russians, being miles away and exhausted by the battle, did not chase them and therefore missed a chance to capture Erzurum on the heels of the fleeing enemy Having developed a plan of assault on the stronghold, the Russian army advanced under the cover of night, but had difficulties of movement control in the dark. A part of their troops from the 153th Infantry Regiment mistook their direction and captured one of the redoubts, Azizieh, all by themselves, without help from the rest of the army, but had to leave it due to the lack of support All the three Turkish battalions stationed in the Azizieh redoubt were routed, numbering 1,600, whereas the Russians lost 400:399 or 600 men in this battle After the Russians left Azizieh, the Turks made an attempt to counterattack them, but were successfully driven back As the works of Erzurum were too strong to be taken by assault, the siege park was needed at Kars:198 and in the following days the weather set in with a snowstorm the Russians decided to withdraw their army and instead attack Kars, which they succeeded in capturing–210 Ahmed Muhtar Pasha, the Ottoman commander during the siege, requested reinforcements from Istanbul and was receiving them all through November After epidemics broke out, he withdrew his forces to Bayburt for the remainder of the war Muhtar Pasha was awarded the title Ghazi for his role in the defence of Erzurum, Gedikler and Yahniler." .

lsd:Entity_48295 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Deeg, fought on 13 November 1804, took place outside Deeg, now in the Bharatpur district of Rajasthan, India." .

lsd:Entity_48311 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Lovebox Festival is a three_day music festival. The move came after London Borough of Tower Hamlets turned down its application to continue in Victoria Park and Lambeth residents objected to its move to Brockwell Park. The event has been running since 2002 and was founded by DJs Groove Armada. Groove Armada began Lovebox Festival as a resident club night at London venue 93 Feet East in 2002. In 2003 to celebrate the first anniversary of the night, the pair hosted the first outdoor Lovebox Festival event. In 2005, Lovebox Festival moved to Victoria Park in London Borough of Tower Hamlets. Lovebox Festival has also hosted nights at The End, Turnmills, Neighbourhood, Canvas, The Key and The Ministry of Sound in London and elsewhere in Brighton, Dublin, Belfast, Edinburgh, Newcastle and Ibiza, as well as an annual summer boat party, which ran until 2008. In 2014, Lovebox Festival launched After Dark, a series of parties held after both the Friday and Saturday nights of the festival across a selection of East London club spaces, including Oval Space, The Laundry and Village Underground. Being based in central London, yet still encompassing many of the features of country_set events such as Glastonbury and Secret Garden Party, Lovebox Festival has developed a reputation for being an “urban_based_yet_rural_feeling, multi_dimensional festival – without the camping or the endless tramping about.”." .

lsd:Entity_48343 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Euroleague Final Four is the final four format championship of the European_wide top_tier level EuroLeague professional club basketball competition. The Euroleague Basketball Company used the final four format for the first time in 2002, following the 2001 FIBA SuproLeague Final four, which was the last final four held by FIBA Europe. The first time the EuroLeague used a Final four format to decide its league champion, was at the conclusion of the 1965–66 and 1966–67 seasons, when it held the 1966 FIBA European Champions Cup Final four, and the 1967 FIBA European Champions Cup Final four. The Euroleague Final Four has been held every year since, with FIBA Europe organizing it until 2001, and the Euroleague Basketball Company organizing it since 2002. The SuproLeague, which was organized by FIBA, and the EuroLeague, which was organized by Euroleague Basketball Company. Euroleague Basketball Company's EuroLeague competition, in its inaugural year, used a playoff format, with the two professional teams from Bologna (Virtus and Fortitudo), AEK, and TAU reaching the tournament's semifinals. That season's Euroleague Basketball tournament, the Euroleague 2000–01 season, did not end with a Final four tournament. The EuroLeague now officially recognizes both the 2001 FIBA SuproLeague Final four, and the 2001 Euroleague Semifinals, as Final Fours. * The 2000–01 season was a transition year, with the best European teams splitting into two different major leagues: The SuproLeague, held by FIBA, and the EuroLeague, held by Euroleague Basketball. That season's EuroLeague Basketball tournament did not end with a Final four tournament." .

lsd:Entity_48411 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Miller Lite 200 was a Championship Auto Racing Teams (CART) motor race held on 12 August 2001 at Mid_Ohio Sports Car Course in Lexington, Ohio, United States of America. Team Penske dominated the event, with Gil de Ferran taking pole position and Hélio Castroneves finishing ahead of de Ferran in the race itself." .

lsd:Entity_48439 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The American Basketball League, often abbreviated to the ABL of 1996 was the first independent professional basketball league for women in the United States. The ABL began league competition in the Fall of 1996, while the WNBA launched its first game in June 1997. Both organizations came into existence during a surge in popularity for women's basketball in the United States that followed the perfect 35–0 national championship season for the Connecticut Huskies in 1995 and the undefeated, gold medal_winning performance of the United States Women's basketball team at the 1996 Summer Olympics. The ABL lasted two full seasons: 1996–97 and 1997–98. On 22 December 1998; with almost no warning, the ABL declared Chapter 11 bankruptcy and suspended operations. The 1996–97 ABL All_Star Game was played on 1996, at the Hartford Civic Center. The 1998–99 ABL All_Star Game was scheduled to be played on January 24, 1999, in San Jose, California, but was canceled when the league ceased operations in 22 December 1998." .

lsd:Entity_48473 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tropical Storm Lowell was a moderate tropical storm that developed during the 2008 Pacific hurricane season. It quickly intensified into Tropical Storm Lowell, peaking as a moderate tropical storm." .

lsd:Entity_48500 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Alaska Airlines Flight 779 was a contract cargo flight operated on 21 July 1961 by an Alaska Airlines Douglas DC_6A that crashed short of the runway at Shemya Air Force Base with the loss of all six crew members on board." .

lsd:Entity_48524 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Badminton World Championships – Women's Doubles took place in Honda Center in Anaheim, United States of America, between 15 August 2005 and 21 August 2005." .

lsd:Entity_48527 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council election took place on 04 May 2000 to elect members of Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council in South Yorkshire, England." .

lsd:Entity_48545 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Big Lightning (also sometimes The Great Lightning, Russian: Большая молния, Bolshaya molniya) is an unfinished opera sketched in 1932 by Dmitri Shostakovich." .

lsd:Entity_48554 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1962 Dwars door Vlaanderen was the 18th edition of the Dwars door Vlaanderen cycle race and was held on 21 April 1962–22 April 1962." .

lsd:Entity_48566 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1985 Porsche Classic was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor hard courts in Filderstadt, West Germany that was part of the 1985 WTA Tour. It was the eighth edition of the tournament and was held from 14 October 1985 through 20 October 1985." .

lsd:Entity_48702 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Great Bakersfield Fire of 1889 was a conflagration in Bakersfield, California." .

lsd:Entity_48707 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Latin Grammy Awards of 2000 were held in Los Angeles at the Staples Center on Wednesday, 2000. On 2000 the Latin Academy of Recording Arts & Sciences announced that the inaugural Latin Grammy Award were going to take place on 2000 in Los Angeles and the awards ceremony would be broadcast in the United States by CBS, which will also distribute it to other countries. The list of nominees for the Latin Grammy Awards of 2000, slated for 2000 in Los Angeles, was unveiled on Friday, 2000 in a Miami ceremony hosted by Michael Greene, President of the National Academy of Recording Arts & Sciences. The list of hosts for the first_ever Latin Grammy Award, included Gloria Estefan, Antonio Banderas, Jimmy Smits, Andy García and Jennifer Lopez, who also was announced to perform her hit single \"No Me Ames\" with Marc Anthony, but Anthony (with six nominations that night) did not attend the show citing complications with his (then) wife's pregnancy. On 2000 Sony Discos released the first \"Latin Grammy Nominees CD\" to coincide with the inaugural awards with nominees from three categories, Latin Grammy Award for Record of the Year, Best Female Pop Vocal Performance and Best Tropical Song, with a portion of the proceeds to support the Latin Academy Of Recording Arts and Sciences for community_outreach efforts." .

lsd:Entity_48719 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Armenian First League season began on 05 April 2011, and ended on 10 October 2011." .

lsd:Entity_48722 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Belarusian Super Cup was held on 2017 between the 2016 Belarusian Premier League champions FC BATE Borisov and the 2015–16 Belarusian Cup winners FC Torpedo_BelAZ Zhodino." .

lsd:Entity_48764 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A Credit default swap (CDS) is a swap agreement that the seller of the CDS will compensate the buyer in the event of a debt default (by the debtor) or other credit event. A \"Credit default swap\" (CDS) is a Credit derivative contract between two counterparties. J.P. Morgan & Co. is widely credited with creating the modern Credit default swap in 1994. Under the Duffie construct, the price of a Credit default swap can also be derived by calculating the asset swap spread of a bond. A new type of default swap is the \"loan only\" Credit default swap (LCDS)." .

lsd:Entity_48779 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1993 European Amateur Boxing Championships were held in Bursa from September 6 to September 12. The 30th edition of the normally bi_annual competition, in which 197 fighters from 32 countries participated this time, was organised by the European governing body for amateur boxing, EABA." .

lsd:Entity_48792 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Hirak movement in the Rif or The Rif Movement (Berber: ⴰⵎⵓⵙⵙⵓ ⵏ ⴰⵕⵉⴼ, Arabic: حراك الريف Movement of the Rif) is a popular mass protest movement that took place in the Berber Rif region in northern Morocco between 28 October 2016 and June 2017 as a result of the death of Mohcine Fikri, a fishmonger who was crushed to death after jumping into the back of a garbage truck, following the confiscation by local authorities of the fish which he was selling on the local market. Macron also reported that the king said to him, that \"he inaugurated the practice of spending vacations in Al Hoceima\", and the king claimed to Macron, that \"contrary to other countries, people in the Rif were free to protest\"." .

lsd:Entity_48812 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Gwangbokjeol is a holiday celebrated annually on 15 August in both South Korea and North Korea. It is notable for being the only Korean public holiday celebrated by both South Korea and North Korea. In South Korea it is known as Gwangbokjeol (광복절; literally, \"the day the light returned\"), and is one of the public holidays in South Korea. After the Korean Peninsula was liberated by the Allies in 1945, independent Korean governments were created three years later, on 15 August 1948, when the pro_U.S. Syngman Rhee was elected first President of South Korea and pro_Soviet Kim Il_sung was made first Leader of North Korea. Gwangbokjeol was officially designated a public holiday on 1 October 1949 in South Korea and is known as Chogukhaebangŭi nal (조국해방의 날; literally \"Liberation of Fatherland Day\") in North Korea. North Korea currently celebrates this holiday separately from South Korea. At 10:23 a.m., 15 August 1974, Mun Se_gwang, a Zainichi Korean and North Korea sympathizer, attempted to assassinate President Park Chung_hee at the National Theater of Korea in Seoul during a Gwangbokjeol ceremony; Park was unharmed but his wife Yuk Young_soo, First Lady of South Korea, was killed." .

lsd:Entity_4883 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Asian Junior Badminton Championships – women's singles tournament of the 2013 Asian Junior Badminton Championships was held from July 10–14 in Kota Kinabalu, Malaysia." .

lsd:Entity_48843 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Copa Libertadores was the 49th edition of the Copa Libertadores, CONMEBOL's premier annual international club tournament. Liga Deportiva Universitaria de Quito earned a berth in the 2008 FIFA Club World Cup and 2009 Recopa Sudamericana." .

lsd:Entity_48929 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 FIM Motocross World Championship season was the 60th International Motorcycling Federation Motocross World Championship season. A 19_round calendar for the 2016 season was announced on 14 October 2015 FIM Motocross World Championship season." .

lsd:Entity_48980 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tour des Fjords (earlier known as Rogaland Grand Prix until 2012) is a road bicycle racing held annually between Stavanger and Bergen, in the region of western Norway, Norway. From the 2019 season the race will merge with Tour of Norway to form a new six day stage race that will cover all of the southern counties of Norway. The first edition will be held from May 28th until June 2nd 2019." .

lsd:Entity_48998 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 UEFA European Under_17 Football Championship was the twelfth edition of Union of European Football Associations's UEFA European Under_17 Football Championship since the re_organising of age group competitions in 2002. Slovakia were hosts of the tournament with games taking place at four venues between 05 May 2013–17 May 2013." .

lsd:Entity_49001 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Copa América Group C was one of the three groups of competing nations in the 2015 Copa lola. Group play began on 2015 and ended on 21 June 2015." .

lsd:Entity_49022 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1994 Skate Canada International was held in Red Deer, Alberta on 03 November 1994–6." .

lsd:Entity_4905 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The First Moscow Conference (Codename: Caviar) of World War II took place from 29 September 1941 to 01 October 1941. The initial contact with the Soviet Union came with Presidential Envoy and Director of the Lend_Lease programme Harry Hopkins with Soviet leader Joseph Stalin in Moscow. The Moscow conference was proposed following the meeting between British Prime Minister Winston Churchill and US President Franklin D. Roosevelt at Placentia Bay. An announcement on Radio Moscow said _ Comrade Stalin requested the American Ambassador (Laurence Steinhardt) and the British Ambassador (Sir Stafford Cripps) to convey to President Roosevelt and Mr. Churchill respectively the heartfelt thanks of the peoples of the Soviet Union and of the Soviet Government for their readiness to aid the U.S.S.R. in its war of liberation against Hitlerite Germany. W. Averell Harriman representing the United States of America and Lord Beaverbrook representing the United Kingdom met with Vyacheslav Molotov (Soviet Minister of Foreign Affairs) presiding. In a speech of 1941 to mark the 24th anniversary of the October Revolution Joseph Stalin stated _ ... the three power conference in Moscow with the participation of Mr. Beaverbrook, the representative of Great Britain, and Mr. Harriman, representative of the United States of America, decided upon systematic assistance to our country with tanks and airplanes. If to this is added the fact that a few days ago the United States of America decided to grant a loan of one billion dollars to the Soviet Union, one can say with assurance that the coalition of the United States of America, Great Britain and the U. S. S. R., is a reality (stormy applause) which is increasing and will increase for the good of our common cause." .

lsd:Entity_49109 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008–09 Montenegrin First League was the third season of the top_tier football in Montenegro. The season began on 09 August 2008 and ended on 30 May 2009." .

lsd:Entity_49133 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "El Porteñazo (02 June 1962 – 06 June 1962) was a short_lived military rebellion against the government of Rómulo Betancourt in Venezuela, in which rebels attempted to take over the city of Puerto Cabello (75.83 miles (122.04 km) from the capital)." .

lsd:Entity_49145 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 Grand Prix of Indianapolis, officially known as the 2016 Angie's List Grand Prix of Indianapolis for sponsorship reasons, was the fifth round of the 2016 IndyCar Series season." .

lsd:Entity_49172 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1969 UCI Track Cycling World Championships were the World Championship for track cycling. The events of the men's sprint and the individual pursuit for professionals were held in Antwerp, Belgium the other events took place in Brno, Czechoslovakia. Eleven events were contested, 9 for men (3 for professionals, 6 for amateurs) and 2 for women between 1969 and 09 August 1969." .

lsd:Entity_49207 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1982 World Rowing Championships were World Rowing Championships that were held from 28 to 29 August 1982 at Rotsee in Lucerne, Switzerland." .

lsd:Entity_49213 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Rhunahaorine Moss was a battle between Covenanters led by General David Leslie and Royalist forces led by Alasdair Mac Colla Chiotaich (Sir Alexander MacDonald) at Rhunahaorine Point, Kintyre, Scotland on 24 May 1647." .

lsd:Entity_49256 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The alpine skiing at the 2012 Winter Youth Olympics – girls' combined competition of the alpine skiing events at the 2012 Winter Youth Olympics in Innsbruck, Austria, was held on 15 January 2012, at the Patscherkofel." .

lsd:Entity_49261 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2001 Transnistrian presidential election were held in the breakaway republic of Transnistria on 09 December 2001." .

lsd:Entity_49300 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Action of 14 September 1779 was a minor naval engagement that occurred on 14 September 1779, off the Azores between the Royal Navy frigate HMS Pearl under the command of George Montagu and the Spanish Navy frigate Santa Mónica under the command of Miguel de Nunes, with the Pearl capturing the Santa Mónica after a brief engagement. Great Britain and Spanish naval forces engaged each other several times during the war, as the conflict spilled over into Europe with the Spanish laying siege to Gibraltar. In 14 September 1779, three years into the war, George Montagu set sail on his newly commissioned ship, HMS Pearl, on a cruise in the eastern fringes of the Atlantic Ocean. Since July 1779, the Spanish Navy had conducted naval patrols near the Azores to search for Great Britain ships in the area. On 14 September 1779, while Montagu was cruising off the Azores in the early hours of the morning, he spotted a large Spanish ship." .

lsd:Entity_49304 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Mixed Team tournament in judo at the 2014 Summer Youth Olympics – mixed team was held on 21 August 2014 at the Longjiang Gymnasium." .

lsd:Entity_49332 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1961 Omloop Het Volk was the 16th edition of the Omloop Het Nieuwsblad cycle race and was held on 04 March 1961." .

lsd:Entity_49334 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1986 World Rally Championship season was the 14th season of the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile (Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile) World Rally Championship (WRC). The season consisted of 13 rallying, including all twelve venues of the 1985 World Rally Championship season as well as the addition of the Olympus Rally. The 1986 season was notable for being the last World Rally Championship season driven with the popular Group B rally cars, which were banned after the fatal crashes at the Rally Portugal, where three spectators were killed and more than 30 injured, and at the Tour de Corse, where Henri Toivonen and his co_driver Sergio Cresto died in a fireball accident. 1986 marked the only season in which the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile issued the World Championship for Drivers of Group A Cars." .

lsd:Entity_49360 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Akasaka was one of the earlier battles of the Genkō War between the figurehead Emperor Godaigo and the largely Hōjō controlled Kamakura shogunate during the final years of the Kamakura period in Japan. The battle in question was fought at Shimo Akasaka_jō (下赤坂城), or (English: Lower Akasaka fortress), a fortress built upon Mount Yoshino near modern_day Ōsaka in the former Kawachi Province in Ōsaka Prefecture." .

lsd:Entity_49391 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Raid on Tabasco, Capture of Villahermosa or Newport's 2nd Expedition of 1599 was an English military expedition during the Anglo–Spanish War that captured the Spanish port settlement of Villahermosa in Viceroyalty of New Spain. Their target was the port of Villahermosa (then called San Juan Bautista) in the Bay of Viceroyalty of New Spain under governor Lázaro Suárez de Córdova. Newport arrived off the Viceroyalty of New Spain coast in late October; Villahermosa lay on the southeast of Viceroyalty of New Spain, with the Gulf of Mexico to the north." .

lsd:Entity_49415 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1942 Oregon gubernatorial election took place on 03 November 1942 to elect the governor of the U.S. state of Oregon. Republican candidate and Oregon Secretary of State Earl Snell defeated state senator Lew Wallace by a more than 3–1 margin, the largest margin of victory for any Oregon governor." .

lsd:Entity_49432 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The wrestling at the 1968 Summer Olympics – men's freestyle 52 kg as part of the wrestling at the 1968 Summer Olympics were held at the Insurgentes Ice Rink." .

lsd:Entity_49444 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Emirates Cup was a pre_season association football friendly tournament hosted by Arsenal F.C. at its Emirates Stadium, the Emirates Stadium in London. Held on the weekend of 2011–2011, the participants were Arsenal F.C., Boca Juniors, Paris Saint_Germain, and New York Red Bulls. For this event Arsenal F.C. and Paris Saint_Germain did not play each other, nor did Boca Juniors face New York Red Bulls. The Emirates Cup began in July 2007 once Arsenal F.C. finalised plans to stage a pre_season competition at its Emirates Stadium. Argentine club Boca Juniors, French side Paris Saint_Germain and American club New York Red Bulls were confirmed as participants for the 2011 edition, alongside hosts Arsenal F.C.. The involvement of New York Red Bulls had added significance because Thierry Henry, who formerly played for Arsenal F.C., faced his old club. The opening match of the 2011 Emirates Cup saw New York Red Bulls taking on Paris Saint_Germain. Gervinho assisted Robin van Persie's goal in the first half a minute before the half_hour, and substitute Aaron Ramsey scored Arsenal F.C.'s second, a long_range strike in the 46th minute. The final match of the 2011 tournament was between Arsenal F.C. and New York Red Bulls." .

lsd:Entity_49463 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hoengsong was a battle during the Korean War that took place between 11 February 1951 _ 15, 1951. As predicted, the XIII Army Group commander opened an attack on the night of 11 February 1951 toward Hoengseong County." .

lsd:Entity_49469 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Duke–Michigan basketball rivalry is a college basketball rivalry between the Duke Blue Devils men's basketball team of Duke University and Michigan Wolverines men's basketball team of the University of Michigan." .

lsd:Entity_49504 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Nanchang (simplified Chinese: 南昌会战; traditional Chinese: 南昌會戰) was a military campaign fought around Nanchang, Jiangxi between the Chinese National Revolutionary Army and the Japanese Imperial Japanese Army in the Second Sino_Japanese War." .

lsd:Entity_49510 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Central Coast Massacre was a shooting spree killing that occurred on the evening of 27 October 1992 on the Central Coast, New South Wales, Australia." .

lsd:Entity_4952 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2005 Fukuoka earthquake struck Fukuoka Prefecture, Japan at 10:53 am JST on 20 March 2005, and lasted for approximately 1 minute. The Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA) measured it as peaking at a magnitude of 7.0 (6.6) and named it and its subsequent aftershocks the Fukuoka Prefecture western offshore earthquakes (福岡県西方沖地震, Fukuoka_ken Seihō Oki Jishin). Fukuoka is not as seismically active as many other parts of Japan, and was known prior to the earthquake as one of Japan's safest locations in terms of natural disasters; the previous earthquake, a magnitude 5, had occurred over a hundred years ago and it had been centuries since the city had experienced a serious earthquake. Kyodo news agency, citing Japan's meteorological agency, said it was the strongest earthquake to hit kyushu since May 1997, and the first to exceed magnitude 6 since 1898. Earthquake experts in Japan said it is rare for a strong earthquake to strike the area. When a center is located at a depth of 10 km, it would cause an earthquake of a lower_6 magnitude (similar to the 20 March 2005 earthquake) in downtown Fukuoka. The probability of an earthquake along the known length of the Kego fault occurring within 30 years was estimated at 0.4% prior to the 20 March 2005 earthquake, but this probability has been revised upwards since. Following reports that the city has only prepared for earthquakes up to a magnitude of 6.5, the aftershock renewed fears that the quakes might cause the Kego fault to become active again beneath Fukuoka, leading to an earthquake as big as, or bigger than, the 20 March 2005 quake." .

lsd:Entity_49545 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 5th Tony Awards were held on 1951, at the Waldorf_Astoria Hotel Grand Ballroom and broadcast on radio station WOR and the Mutual Network." .

lsd:Entity_49581 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The swimming at the 1988 Summer Olympics – men's 4 × 100 metre freestyle relay event at the 1988 Summer Olympics took place on 23 September 1988 at the Jamsil Indoor Swimming Pool in Seoul, South Korea." .

lsd:Entity_4965 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Slammiversary XI was a professional wrestling pay_per_view (PPV) event produced by the Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) promotion, which took place on 02 June 2013 at the Agganis Arena in Boston. During the Lockdown Fanfest held in San Antonio, Texas on March 9, 2013, TNA President Dixie Carter announced that this year's Slammiversary would take place at the Agganis Arena in Boston on 02 June 2013. In the press release that followed, Carter stated, \"Slammiversary is our biggest show of the summer, and we're so excited to bring it to Boston for the first time. Slammiversary featured nine professional wrestling matches that involved different wrestlers from pre_existing scripted feuds and storylines." .

lsd:Entity_49657 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1949 Australian federal election was held in Australia on 10 December 1949. Robert Menzies became Prime Minister for the second time, and the Liberal Party of Australia won government federally for the first time." .

lsd:Entity_49693 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Åsta accident was a railway accident that occurred at 13:12:25 on 4 January 2000 at Åsta in Åmot, south of Rena in Østerdalen, Norway." .

lsd:Entity_49709 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018–19 figure skating season began on 01 July 2018, and ended on 30 June 2019." .

lsd:Entity_49754 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 African Cross Country Championships was the fourth edition of the international cross country running competition for African athletes organised by the Confederation of African Athletics. It was held on 12 March at the Yaounde Golf Club in Yaounde, Cameroon – the first time a West African nation had hosted the event since its re_launch in 2011." .

lsd:Entity_49757 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 DFS Classic was a women's tennis tournament played on grass court at the Edgbaston Priory Club in Birmingham in the United Kingdom that was part of WTA Tier III tournaments of the 1999 WTA Tour. The tournament was held from 07 June 1999 until 13 June 1999." .

lsd:Entity_49777 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Six_red World Championship (often styled the 2012 SangSom 6_red World Championship for sponsorship and marketing purposes) was a six_red snooker tournament held between 02 July 2012 and 07 July 2012 at the Montien Riverside Hotel in Bangkok, Thailand." .

lsd:Entity_4978 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The M+M's Tour was the sixth concert tour by American recording artist Britney Spears,in support upcoming fifth studio album Blackout (2007). On 01 May 2007, a front_page story on The San Diego Union_Tribune fueled the speculation." .

lsd:Entity_49795 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The best team who isn't playing on Campeonato Brasileiro Série A, Série B or Série C qualifies to the 2013 Campeonato Brasileiro Série D. The Federal District Football Federation allows teams from neighbouring states to play in its competition, with the condition that they are sited in cities no farther than 200km from Brasília. Brasiliense Futebol Clube won the 2013 Campeonato Brasiliense." .

lsd:Entity_49799 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1890 World Series was an end_of_the_year baseball playoff series between the National League champion Brooklyn Bridegrooms (later known as the Dodgers) and the American Association champion Louisville Colonels. After losing the 1889 World Series to their \"cross_town\" rivals, the New York Giants (Brooklyn was actually a separate city until 1898), the Bridegrooms came back strong and won the National League pennant in 1890, the first major league club to win consecutive pennants in two different leagues (the only other being the Boston Reds (1890–91)). The first four were played in Louisville (including a tie in Game 3), and the remainder of the Series was scheduled for Brooklyn." .

lsd:Entity_498 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Copa San Juan Gobierno was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in San Juan, Argentina between 08 October 2012 and 14 October 2012." .

lsd:Entity_49818 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Cricket World Cup Final was a One Day International (ODI) match played on 2003 at the Wanderers Stadium in Johannesburg, South Africa. The second semi_final was played between India and Kenya on 2003 at Kingsmead, Durban. The final was played on 2003 at the Wanderers Stadium, Johannesburg." .

lsd:Entity_4983 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Tauragė Revolt (Lithuanian: Tauragės sukilimas) was an anti_government revolt that took place in Tauragė, Lithuania on 09 September 1927. The rebels took control of Tauragė, the revolt spread to neighboring villages and their forces grew to 200 men. In the local press, the rebels printed 5,000 copies of a proclamation, signed by reserve captain Antanas Majus as the new head of the Tauragė District, informing locals about the revolt and ordering to surrender all weapons to the new commandant. Antanas Majus was not present in Tauragė and later claimed that he knew nothing of the revolt." .

lsd:Entity_49837 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Battle of Kachhi was fought between His Highness The Khan of Kalat Mir Abdullah Khan Baloch and Main Noor Mohammad Kalhoro Amir of Sindh to establish their rule in Kachhi District. In the year 1142 AH (1729 AD) Murad Kaleri Baloch was also known as Ganjah Baloch, was appointed by Main Noor Mohammad Kalhoro as an agent in charge of Siwí, and brought into subjection powerful chiefs like Jafar Khan Magsí, the land owner of Ganjobah, Ali Mardan Abro and Ibrahim Khan Abro chiefs of Nausharo, Kachhi District, Mahyan Eri and Lahná Machhi, big land owners of Bhag Nari, Kala Khan and other chiefs and owners of Dhadhar." .

lsd:Entity_49865 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Individual event for badminton at the Badminton at the 2017 Southeast Asian Games – Individual Event was held at the Axiata Arena, Kuala Lumpur from 26 to 29 August 2017." .

