lsd:Entity_51343 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Miss World Puerto Rico 2009 pageant was held on 2009 in Puerto Rico. Ivonne Orsini, who won the title of Miss World Puerto Rico 2008 and classified as one of the semi_finalists at Miss World 2008, crowned her successor, Jennifer Colón as Miss World Puerto Rico 2009, Jennifer represented Puerto Rico at Miss World 2009." .

lsd:Entity_51389 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Polish Figure Skating Championships (Polish: Mistrzostwa Polski w łyżwiarstwie figurowym 2002/2003) were held in Sosnowiec between 13 December 2002 and 15, 2002." .

lsd:Entity_51436 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Women's Rugby World Cup (officially IRB Rugby World Cup 2006 Canada) took place in Edmonton, Alberta, Canada. The tournament began on 31 August 2006 and ended on 17 September 2006." .

lsd:Entity_51522 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In 1148, a Council of Reims was called by Pope Eugene III to consider a number of regulations, or canons, for the Church, as well as to debate some other issues. Originally the summons for the council went out in October 1147 and it was supposed to be held in Trier, which is now in Germany, but conditions in Trier were such that it was moved to Reims, in France, for 1148. The papal entourage arrived in Trier on 30 November 1147, but shortly after arrival the pope decided to move the proceedings because of complaints from the residents of Trier, and announced in 1148 that the council would move to Reims, but still on the date given before. The Italian bishops, however, were mostly excused from attendance, as Eugene held a council at Cremona in 1148 where the Reims decrees were announced. The attendees were from what were later the countries of France, Germany, England, and Spain, and in keeping with the times, would have included not just the prelates who were summoned, but also their servants and officials, making the true number of people in Reims impossible to know. The opening of the council took place on 1148 at Reims Cathedral on a Sunday." .

lsd:Entity_51528 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Missouri lieutenant gubernatorial election was held on 06 November 2012. Incumbent lieutenant governor Peter Kinder won the 2008 Missouri lieutenant gubernatorial election with 49.9% of the vote against Democratic candidate Sam Page. Kinder had been considered the front_runner in the 2012 Republican Gubernatorial primary, however after Peter Kinder emerged, he decided to run for re_election." .

lsd:Entity_51534 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Women's 200 metres at the athletics at the 1988 Summer Olympics – women's 200 metres in Seoul, South Korea had an entry list of 60 competitors, with eight qualifying heats (60), four second_round races (32) and two semi_finals (16), before the final (8) took off on Thursday 29 September 1988. At the 1988 Olympic Trials, her 21.77 American record already showed Florence Griffith Joyner was going to be a contender against the East Germans who had dominated the sprints for the previous decade." .

lsd:Entity_51557 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Garnock Court fire was a fire that took place on 11 June 1999 at Garnock Court, a 14_storey block of flats in Irvine, Scotland, which resulted in one fatality." .

lsd:Entity_51584 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2004 Senior League World Series took place from 15 August 2004–21 in Bangor, Maine, United States." .

