lsd:Entity_51624 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2002 All_Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final was the 115th All_Ireland Hurling Final and the culmination of the All_Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 2002, a tournament for the top hurling counties. The match was held at Croke Park, Dublin, on 2002, between Kilkenny and Clare GAA." .

lsd:Entity_51646 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Crystal Skate of Romania was the 3rd edition of an annual senior_level international figure skating competition held in Romania. It was held between 22 November 2001 and 25, 2001 in Bucharest." .

lsd:Entity_51658 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2009 was the seventh edition of the annual Junior Eurovision Song Contest and took place in Kiev, Ukraine. Both Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko and President of Ukraine Viktor Yushchenko were present during the final; Tymoshenko was also present and speeched during the opening ceremony on 2009. The European Broadcasting Union (EBU) invited broadcasters to bid for the rights to host the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2009; three bids were received from Belarus, Serbia, and Ukraine. On 6 June 2008, after deliberations by the EBU, the National Television Company of Ukraine (NTU) was granted the rights to the 2009 contest and confirmed they would host it in Kiev. On 2009, Ukrainian Deputy Prime Minister Ivan Vasiunyk declared that the contest would not be postponed; (earlier) Party of Regions member of parliament Hanna Herman had called on Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko to cancel the song contest because of the 2009 flu pandemic in Ukraine. Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2009 _ KYIV _ Ukraine _ All The Songs From The Show, is a compilation album put together by the European Broadcasting Union, and was released by Universal Music Group on 21 November 2009." .

lsd:Entity_5170 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Samsung 500, the seventh race of the 2007 NASCAR Nextel Cup Series Series, was held on Sunday, 15 April 2007 of that year at the 1.5_mile Texas Motor Speedway in Fort Worth. In the end, the race came down to former Texas Motor Speedway winners and ex_teammates Matt Kenseth and Jeff Burton. While Burton won his second race, being the first repeat winner, still the past twelve races have been won by twelve different drivers, and it was the fourth different winning team at Texas Motor Speedway in the past four races (Roush, Evernham, Gibbs, Childress), with the past three teams winning at Texas winning for the first time." .

lsd:Entity_51709 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "United Nations Security Council Resolution 687, adopted on 03 April 1991, after reaffirming resolutions 660, 661, 662, 664, 665, 666, 667, 669, 670, 674, 677, 678 (all 1990) and United Nations Security Council Resolution 686 (1991), the Council set the terms, in a comprehensive resolution, with which Iraq was to comply after losing the Gulf War." .

lsd:Entity_51712 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Dance of the Forty_One or the Ball of the Forty_One (Spanish: El baile de los cuarenta y uno) was a society scandal in early 20th_century Mexico, during the presidency of Porfirio Díaz. The incident revolved around an illegal police raid carried out on 17 November 1901 against a private home on Calle de la Paz (since renamed Calle Ezequiel Montes) in Colonia Tabacalera of Mexico City, the site of a dance attended by a group of men, of whom 19 were dressed in women's clothing. The party began the night of 17 November 1901 secretly in a house rented for that purpose in what were the limits of Mexico City, the Colonia Tabacalera." .

lsd:Entity_51747 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1952 Summer Olympics – men's 50 kilometres walk at the 1952 Summer Olympics took place on 21 July 1952 at the Helsinki Olympic Stadium." .

lsd:Entity_51750 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2017 ESPY Awards were presented at the 25th annual ESPY Awards show, held on 2017 at 5 pm Pacific at the Microsoft Theater in Los Angeles, California and on television nationwide in the United States of America on American Broadcasting Company at 8 pm Eastern/7 PM Central. On 2017, it was announced by ESPN.com that Peyton Manning would host the show." .

lsd:Entity_51754 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1968 United States presidential election in Hawaii took place on 05 November 1968. Hawaii voters chose 4 electors to the Electoral College, which selected the President of the United States and vice President of the United States." .

lsd:Entity_51797 a lsd:Context_narration ;
