lsd:Entity_53504 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Korea Open Badminton Championships in badminton was held in Seoul, from 21 August 2006 to 27 August 2006." .

lsd:Entity_53510 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Monmouth Stakes is an American thoroughbred horse race on turf at Monmouth Park Racetrack in Oceanport. Monmouth Park Racetrack created the Monmouth Stakes when IEAH Stables said they wanted their Dual Classic winner, Big Brown, to compete in a turf race in the middle of September." .

lsd:Entity_53514 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 HEW Cyclassics was the fourth edition of the EuroEyes Cyclassics cycle race and was held on 15 August 1999." .

lsd:Entity_53524 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Bunkhouse Stampede was the third Bunkhouse Stampede professional wrestling event produced by Jim Crockett Promotions under the National Wrestling Alliance (NWA) banner. It was the only Bunkhouse Stampede event to air as a pay_per_view (PPV) event. The event took place on 24 January 1988 from the Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum in Uniondale, New York. In the main event, Dusty Rhodes won a Steel Cage Bunkhouse Stampede. The event comprised four professional wrestling matches that involved wrestlers from pre_existing rivalries, plots and storylines that were played out on Worldwide, Pro and World Championship Wrestling–Jim Crockett Promotions (JCP)'s television programs. The main match heading into the event was the Steel Cage Bunkhouse Stampede. On 24 January 1988 episode of World Championship Wrestling, Flair was scheduled to defend the title against Hawk at Bunkhouse Stampede. Before the event aired live on PPV, Sting and Jimmy Garvin defeated The Sheepherders (Butch Miller and Luke Williams) by professional wrestling in a non_televised tag team match. The main event was a Steel Cage Bunkhouse Stampede. The Bunkhouse Stampede event met little success and was badly criticized." .

lsd:Entity_53529 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Hudson River derby, also known as the New York derby, is the name given to the soccer local derby between the two teams based in the New York metropolitan area, New York Red Bulls and New York City FC." .

lsd:Entity_53535 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The triathlon at the 2004 Summer Olympics – men's was part of the triathlon at the 2004 Summer Olympics programme. The competition was held on Thursday, 2004 at the Vouliagmeni Olympic Centre in Athens." .

