lsd:Entity_53900 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of the Lippe was a cavalry action fought on 2 03 September 1595 on the banks of the Lippe river, in Germany, between a corps of Spanish cavalry led by Juan de Córdoba and a corps of Dutch cavalry, supported by English troops, led by Philip of Nassau. Maurice awaited them with 5,000 infantry and the rest of his cavalry arranged for the battle in the hills near Wesel, along the opposite riverbank." .

