    rdfs:label "The men's coxless pair competition at the 2017 World Rowing Championships – men's coxless pair in Sarasota took place in Nathan Benderson Park." .

lsd:Entity_55931 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Transbrasil Flight 801 (TR801/TBA801) was a scheduled cargo flight from Eduardo Gomes International Airport to São Paulo_Guarulhos International Airport that crashed on 21 March 1989." .

lsd:Entity_55964 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 FIBA Europe Under_18 Championship was the 28th edition of the FIBA Europe Under_18 Championship. 16 teams featured the competition, held in Poland from 21 July 2011–31." .

lsd:Entity_56019 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 World Single Distance Speed Skating Championships – women's 1000 metres race of the 2016 World Single Distance Speed Skating Championships was held on 12 February 2016." .

lsd:Entity_56048 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Music as a Weapon is a series of concert tours created by the American metal band Disturbed. The name of the tour is from the lyrics of \"Droppin' Plates\" on Disturbed's first album, The Sickness. This was the first time Music as a Weapon had co_headliners, Disturbed and Korn. Music as a Weapon II was recorded as a live album and DVD, created by Disturbed." .

lsd:Entity_56053 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The January 2010 attack in central Kabul was a suicide bombing and gun attack which occurred in central Kabul, Afghanistan for several hours on 18 January 2010." .

lsd:Entity_56081 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2001 Nabisco Championship was a women's professional golf tournament, held 22 March 2001–25 at Mission Hills Country Club in Rancho Mirage, California. She won eight times on tour in 2001 and this was the third in a streak of four consecutive; she successfully defended this title the 2002 Kraft Nabisco Championship." .

lsd:Entity_56092 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Perast (Serbian: Перашка битка) was a battle for control over Republic of Venice held Perast (modern day Montenegro) fought in 1654 between defending forces of Republic of Venice Republic from Perast accompanied by hajduks and attacking forces of Ottoman Empire from Sanjak of Herzegovina. Republic of Venice forces from Perast were victorious and successfully repelled Ottoman attack in the battle which is in some sources referred to as most glorious victory in their history. On the other hand, Perast had important strategic importance for the Republic of Venice Republic because it protected important Republic of Venice_held city of Kotor. Battle of Perast followed an unsuccessful attempt of Republic of Venice forces to capture Knin in early 1654. Around 1,500 refugees fled eastern Herzegovina in early 1654 and settled Republic of Venice_held territories in Kotor Bay, near Perast. Although they were of Orthodox faith, hajduks were treated well by Republic of Venice authorities in Perast who granted them some land, creating some kind of Military Frontier between Republic of Venice and Ottoman territories in Kotor Bay. The Ottoman forces that attacked Perast were from Sanjak of Herzegovina governed by Čengić, a secret Republic of Venice agent. Republic of Venice forces of 43 men from Perast were under command of Krsto Vickov Visković. Substantial number of hajduks, who migrated from eastern Herzegovina to Perast in the first half of 15 May 1654, participated in defence of Perast. About 30 Republic of Venice warships from Perast were unable to participate in defence of Perast because they were far away, on the open sea, together with their crews. During this battle mother of Perast captain Vicko Mažarević was kidnapped by the Ottomans and taken to Trebinje where she soon died. Eight days after the battle Petar Zrinski, thrilled with the victory, visited Perast for three days and presented a sword of Vukša Stepanović to the town. Another poem (Spjevanje događaja boja peraškoga) about this battle was written by Perast Catholic friar Ivan Krušala." .

lsd:Entity_56108 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Hill 731 (Greek: Μάχη του υψώματος 731), was a fierce battle fought during World War II in southern Albania, part of the Greco_Italian War. It began in the early morning of 9 24 March 1941, when Fascist Italy launched an assault (Italian Spring Offensive) against Greece, aimed at capturing the critical mountain pass leading into the Kalpaki valley." .

lsd:Entity_56125 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1951 Volta a Catalunya was the 31st edition of the Volta a Catalunya cycle race and was held from 13 September 1951 to 23 September 1951." .

lsd:Entity_5613 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Whose Line is it Anyway? (abbreviated to Whose Line? or WLIIA) is a short_form improvisational comedy radio programme." .

lsd:Entity_56173 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Pontins Professional was the twenty_fourth edition of the professional invitational snooker tournament which took place in 01 May 1997 in Prestatyn, Wales." .

lsd:Entity_56238 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's marathon event at the athletics at the 1928 Summer Olympics – men's marathon took place in Amsterdam, Netherlands on Sunday, 05 August 1928." .

lsd:Entity_56244 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1983 Cypriot presidential election were held in Cyprus on 13 February 1983. The result was a victory for Spiros Kyprianou of the Democratic Party (and also supported by AKEL), who received 56.5% of the vote." .

lsd:Entity_56254 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2021 Central American Games, the XII edition of the Central American Games, will be hosted in Santa Tecla." .

lsd:Entity_56277 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Tuska Open Air Metal Festival, commonly shortened to Tuska (Finnish: pain, agony), is a Finnish heavy metal festival taking place annually in Helsinki. The first Tuska took place in 1998 and the festival has since grown larger every year. However, since 2011, Tuska has taken place at the Suvilahti event field in the Kalasatama neighbourhood of the Sörnäinen district." .

lsd:Entity_56285 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Gerrie Coetzee vs. Michael Dokes, billed as \"The Buckeye Homecoming\", was a professional boxing match that took place on September 23, 1983, at the Coliseum at Richfield in Richfield Township, Ohio, United States of America for Dokes' WBA heavyweight title. The fight came off on September 23, 1983, at Coliseum at Richfield in Richfield Township, Ohio, about halfway between Dokes' hometown of Akron and the much larger city of Cleveland." .

lsd:Entity_5630 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kilmacrennan was a skirmish fought near Kilmacrenan, County Donegal in 1608 during O'Doherty's Rebellion." .

lsd:Entity_56302 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Open Seguros Bolívar was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Bogotá, Colombia between 04 November 2013 and 10 November 2013." .

lsd:Entity_56317 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Kor Royal Cup was the 80th Kor Royal Cup, an annual association football match contested by the winners of the previous season's Thai Premier League and Thai FA Cup competitions. The match was played at Suphachalasai Stadium, Bangkok, on 2015, and contested by 2014 Thai Premier League champions Buriram United F.C., and BG Pathum United F.C. as the winner of the 2014 Thai FA Cup." .

lsd:Entity_56330 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Jewish American Heritage Month (JAHM) is an annual recognition and celebration of Jewish American achievements in and contributions to the United States of America during the month of May. In April 2006, President George W. Bush announced that May would be considered Jewish American Heritage Month. According to Library of Congress hosted website, JewishHeritageMonth.gov, May was chosen as the month of Jewish American Heritage Month because of the successful 350th Anniversary Celebration of Jews in America marking the Jewish arrival in New Amsterdam. In addition to signing the proclamation marking May as the annual Jewish American Heritage Month, the White House shared plans for an address by President Obama on May at Adas Israel Congregation, a large Washington, D.C. synagogue." .

lsd:Entity_56335 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Louisbourg was a pivotal operation of the Seven Years' War (known in the United States as the French and Indian War) in 1758 that ended the French colonial era in Atlantic Canada and led to the subsequent British campaign to capture Quebec in 1759 and the remainder of French North America the following year. The chief engineer was John Henry Bastide who had been present at the first siege of Louisbourg in 1745 and was chief engineer at Fort St Philip, Minorca, in 1756 when the British had surrendered the fort and island to the French after a long siege." .

lsd:Entity_56354 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "dancesport at the dancesport at the 2007 Asian Indoor Games was held in Macau Forum, Macau, China from 27 October to 2007." .

lsd:Entity_5636 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Gap Fire was a fire that burned 9,443 acres (38.21 km2) of the Santa Ynez Mountains above Goleta, California between July 1 and July 28, 2008." .

lsd:Entity_56368 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Festival da Canção or Festival RTP da Canção is the name given to the national festival, produced and broadcast by Rádio e Televisão de Portugal (RTP) to choose the Portuguese entry for the Eurovision Song Contest." .

lsd:Entity_56374 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2008 Samsung Super League was the 2008 edition of the Samsung Super League, the premier international team show jumping competition run by the International Federation for Equestrian Sports and sponsored by Samsung Electronics. The emerging nations to the 2009 Meydan International Federation for Equestrian Sports Nations Cup were Sweden, France and Canada." .

lsd:Entity_56399 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1933 Copa del Presidente de la República (President of the Republic's Cup) was the 33rd staging of the Copa del Rey, the Spain association football cup competition. The competition started on 09 April 1933, and concluded on 25 June 1933, with the final, held at the Montjuïc Stadium in Barcelona." .

lsd:Entity_56408 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Western Air Express Flight 7, a domestic scheduled passenger flight from Salt Lake City to Burbank, crashed on 12 January 1937 near Newhall, California. The off_course Boeing 247D, en route from Salt Lake City, was on approach to the Union Air Terminal at Burbank in severely lowered visibility due to heavy rain and fog." .

lsd:Entity_56412 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Washington Park Handicap is an American Thoroughbred horse race held annually during the first week of September at Arlington Park in Arlington Heights, Illinois." .

lsd:Entity_56451 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Pikes Peak Marathon is a trail running competition that begins at the base of Pikes Peak, in Manitou Springs, Colorado, and climbs over 7,815 feet (2382 m) to the top of the 14,115 foot (4302 m) peak. On Aug. 10, 1956, Dr. Arne Suominen of Del Ray Beach, Fla., challenged smokers and nonsmokers to race up and down Pikes Peak, a 26_mile (42 km) race, in conjunction with the 150th anniversary of the discovery of America's most famous mountain by Zebulon Montgomery Pike. The Pikes Peak Marathon was the first American marathon to allow female competitors, allowing them from the beginning of the marathon in 1956, although no woman entered until 1958. The Pikes Peak Ascent race has twice incorporated the World Long Distance Mountain Running Challenge competition, first in 2006 then again in 2010." .

lsd:Entity_56520 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2018 Thomas & Uber Cup (officially known as the 2018 BWF Thomas & Uber Cup) was the 30th edition of the Thomas Cup and the 27th edition of the Uber Cup, the biennial international badminton championship contested by the men and women's national teams of the member associations of Badminton World Federation (BWF). The tournament was hosted by Bangkok, Thailand. It was the second time that Thailand hosted the Thomas Cup and the first time hosted the Uber Cup tournament and the first time this event was held in Southeast Asia since 2010 in Malaysia. Bangkok was named as the host in March 2017 during BWF Council meeting in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, where BWF also decided the host for 2018 BWF World Championships, 2019 Sudirman Cup and 2019 BWF World Championships. The draw for the tournament was conducted on 2018, at 18:00 ICT, at Arnoma Grand Hotel in Bangkok. For the Thomas Cup draw, the teams were allocated to three pots based on the World Team Rankings of 2018. A similar procedure was applied for Uber Cup draw, where top seed Japan (which were assigned to position A1), the second seed China (which were assigned to position D1), Korea and Thailand were in Pot 1." .

lsd:Entity_56532 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Early 2012 European cold wave was a deadly cold wave that started on 27 January 2012, and brought snow and freezing temperatures to much of the European continent." .

lsd:Entity_56539 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Treaty of Huế, concluded on 1883 between France and Vietnam, recognised a French protectorate over Annam and Tonkin. The treaty was dictated to the Vietnamese in the wake of the French victory at the Battle of Thuận An (1883) by Jules Harmand, the French civil commissioner_general for Tonkin. Cowed by the French appeal to naked force, the Vietnamese court gave way immediately, and on 1883 Vietnamese plenipotentiaries signed a treaty whose terms were dictated by Harmand. The Harmand treaty was eventually replaced by a new Treaty of Huế, signed on 6 June 1884." .

lsd:Entity_5654 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2008 Egypt Cup Final, was the final match of 2007–08 Egypt Cup, when Zamalek SC played ENPPI Club at Cairo International Stadium in Cairo." .

lsd:Entity_56552 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "From 2003 to 2010, it took place annually at Easter in Bingen am Rhein. Breakpoint 2003 proved to be an unmatched success among demosceners who attended. Breakpoint 2005 caused some sad moments to the demoscene when it was announced that the military depot was scheduled for condemnation by the German government, and the next edition was scheduled to be held in the city's gym in the middle of Bingen am Rhein. Breakpoint 2010 was the final Breakpoint event. After a series of viral teaser videos, the invitation to the official follow_up demoparty called Revision was released, and the party took place in Saarbrücken, largely sharing the same organizing crew as Breakpoint." .

lsd:Entity_56568 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Exciter Tour was a 2001 concert tour by the English electronic band Depeche Mode in support of the group's tenth studio album, Exciter, which was released in May 2001." .

lsd:Entity_56612 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1959 Milan–San Remo was the 50th edition of the Milan – San Remo cycle race and was held on 19 March 1959. The race started in Milan and finished in Sanremo." .

lsd:Entity_56640 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1931 Cork Senior Hurling Championship was the 43rd staging of the Cork Senior Hurling Championship since its establishment by the Cork County Board in 1887. The championship began on 1931 and ended on 13 December 1931." .

lsd:Entity_56651 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1946 Philippine presidential election were held on 23 April 1946 (pursuant to Commonwealth Act No. Soon after the reconstitution of the Commonwealth government in 1945, Senators Manuel Roxas, Elpidio Quirino and their allies called for an early national election to choose the president and vice president of the Philippines, as well as the members of Congress." .

lsd:Entity_56659 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 suicide air raid on Colombo was an unsuccessful kamikaze_style suicide attack launched by the air wing of the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam on 20 February 2009, targeting military locations in and around Colombo, Sri Lanka. However the attacks failed as the Sri Lanka Air Force detected the two explosive packed aircraft and shot them down before they reached their presumed targets, although one crashed into a government building in Colombo. However the LTTE did not use aircraft as offensive weapons until March 2007, when they launched a surprise attack against Colombo using light aircraft to drop a bomb on the main base of the Sri Lanka Air Force." .

lsd:Entity_56669 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Condorism (in Portuguese: Condorismo or Condoreirismo) was a Brazilian literary movement that lasted from the mid_1860s until the early 1880s. The name \"Condorism\" comes from the condor, a bird of solitary and high flight, said to be capable of seeing things from a great distance." .

lsd:Entity_56708 a lsd:Context_narration ;
