lsd:Entity_57108 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The athletics at the 1904 Summer Olympics – men's long jump was a track and field athletics event held as part of the athletics at the 1904 Summer Olympics programme. Myer Prinstein of the United States, who took silver in 1900, was the only jumper from Paris to return in 1904." .

lsd:Entity_57121 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1912 United States presidential election in Virginia took place on 05 November 1912. Virginia voted for the Democratic nominee, New Jersey Governor Woodrow Wilson, over the Republican nominee, incumbent President of the United States William Howard Taft, and the Progressive nominee, former President of the United States Theodore Roosevelt." .

lsd:Entity_57132 a lsd:Context_narration ;
