lsd:Entity_57759 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Guamanian gubernatorial election took place on 04 November 2014, to elect the Governor of Guam." .

lsd:Entity_57765 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1932 FA Cup Final was contested by Newcastle United F.C. and Arsenal F.C. at Wembley Stadium in what became known as the \"Over The Line\" final. Newcastle won 2–1, both of their goals scored by Jack Allen. Arsenal F.C. had led 1–0 with a Bob John goal, but Newcastle's equaliser came after a long ball that had appeared to foul over the goal line, and was put back into action for a goal kick. Allen scored again in the second half to win the match 2–1." .

lsd:Entity_57780 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 All_Ireland Senior Hurling Championship Final took place in Croke Park, Dublin on Sunday, 2011. Prior to the senior final, Galway claimed the 2011 Minor Hurling Championship after a 1–21 to 1–12 win against Dublin. Offaly_based referee Brian Gavin was named as the referee for the 2011 All_Ireland final on 16 August." .

lsd:Entity_57812 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sinking of Prince of Wales and Repulse was a naval engagement in World War II, as part of the war in the Pacific, that took place on 10 December 1941 in the South China Sea off the east coast of the British colony of Malaya (present_day Malaysia), 70 miles (61 nautical miles; 110 kilometres) east of Kuantan, Pahang." .

lsd:Entity_57819 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The wrestling at the 1996 Summer Olympics – men's Greco_Roman 62 kg as part of the wrestling at the 1996 Summer Olympics were held at the Georgia World Congress Center from July 22 to July 23." .

lsd:Entity_57821 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1973 Nauruan parliamentary election were held in Nauru on 15 December 1973." .

lsd:Entity_57852 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Open du Pays d'Aix was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Aix_en_Provence, France between 04 May 2015 and 10 May 2015." .

lsd:Entity_57855 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Nabisco Dinah Shore was a women's professional golf tournament, held 27 March 1997–30 at Mission Hills Country Club in Rancho Mirage, California." .

lsd:Entity_57873 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1954 Italian Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 05 September 1954 at Autodromo Nazionale Monza. It was race 8 of 9 in the 1954 Formula One season. The 80_lap race was won by Mercedes driver Juan Manuel Fangio after he started from pole position." .

lsd:Entity_57897 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1989 Men's World Open Squash Championship is the men's edition of the 1989 World Squash Championships, which serves as the individual world championship for squash players. The event took place in Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia from 1989_1989. Jansher Khan won his second World Squash Championships title, defeating Chris Dittmar in the final." .

lsd:Entity_57936 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 The Hague Open was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Scheveningen, Netherlands between 25 July 2016 and 31 July 2016." .

lsd:Entity_57958 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Kathmandu (Nepali: काठमाडौंको युद्ध) or Siege of Kathmandu or Siege of Kantipur occurred during the Gorkhali conquest of Nepal. It was fought in Kathmandu in 1768, and resulted in the defeat of its king Jaya Prakash Malla by Prithvi Narayan Shah, king of the adjoining Gorkha Kingdom. (26th 1768), the Gorkhali forces commanded by Vamsharaj Pande, Surapratap Shah and Tularam Pande attacked Kathmandu and captured the royal palace in the night. After a brief battle, Jaya Prakash Malla realized that he had been betrayed by the nobles, and that Kathmandu was lost." .

lsd:Entity_57972 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Studio Gigante was a Chicago_based video game developer established in 2000 by John Tobias, Dave Michicich, and Joshua Tsui, several developers of Midway's popular Mortal Kombat fighting game series." .

lsd:Entity_57986 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1976 Puerto Rican general election were held in Puerto Rico on 02 November 1976." .

lsd:Entity_58020 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Cahuenga Pass of 1831 was fought at Cahuenga Pass near Los Angeles between the unpopular Mexican Governor of California (Manuel Victoria), and a force assembled by wealthy local landowners. The forces met on 05 December 1831, at Cahuenga Pass, with Captain Portilla in charge of the rebels. This battle should not be confused with the Battle of Providencia (also known as the Second Battle of Cahuenga Pass)." .

lsd:Entity_58026 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Colonial Athletic Association (CAA) is a collegiate athletic conference affiliated with the NCAA's NCAA Division I whose full members are located in East Coast states from Massachusetts to South Carolina." .

lsd:Entity_58029 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A Corsican autonomy referendum, 2003 was held on 06 July 2003. The question asked was: Do you approve of the proposed suggestions to change the institutional organisation of Corsica represented in law 2003_486 of 2003?" .

lsd:Entity_58039 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Cambodia is participating at the Cambodia at the 2011 Southeast Asian Games which are being held in the cities of Palembang and Jakarta, Indonesia from 2011 to 2011." .

lsd:Entity_58053 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Sandro Girgvliani Murder Case is one of the most notorious criminal cases in the modern history of Georgia. Sandro Girgvliani was found dead on 28 January 2006 on the outskirts of Tbilisi with multiple injuries inflicted as a result of physical abuse. According to an Imedi Television investigation on February 12, the murder of the 28_year_old head of the United Georgian Bank's Foreign Department, can be traced to a series of events which developed in Tbilisi's elite Sharden Bar. At this point the influential former Foreign Minister and leader of the Georgia's Way political party, Salome Zourabichvili, announced her intention to work with the opposition parties regarding Girgvliani's murder. Tbilisi City Court launched on June 27 hearings into the murder case. The Tbilisi City Court sentenced Gia Alania, ex_chief of the first unit of the Interior Ministry's Department for Constitutional Security (DCS), to eight_years imprisonment for Sandro Girgvliani's murder. During the scandal the group held a series of protest rallies in Tbilisi demanding a fair investigation into Girgvliani's murder. If the testimony by Bukhaidze were to be confirmed , it would undermine the entire official motives behind the crime _ that the murder occurred as a result of a spontaneous row between the victim and four former police officials outside the Sheredan café in downtown Tbilisi. Patrol Policeman Grigol Bashaleishvili was found guilty and sentenced to four_years imprisonment on August 10 by the Tbilisi City Court of the negligent murder of 19_year_old Amiran Robakidze on 23 November 2004." .

lsd:Entity_58072 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Hall of Fame Tennis Championships (also known as 2000 Miller Lite Hall of Fame Championships for sponsorship reasons) was a tennis tournament played on grass courts at the International Tennis Hall of Fame in Newport, Rhode Island in the United States of America and was part of the ATP International Series of the 2000 ATP Tour." .

lsd:Entity_58084 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1965 LPGA Championship was the eleventh Women's PGA Championship, held September 23–26 at Stardust Country Club in Las Vegas, Nevada. Sandra Haynie, age 22, won the first of her two Women's PGA Championship titles, one stroke ahead of runner_up Clifford Ann Creed." .

lsd:Entity_5810 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2013 Philippine Senate election was the 31st election to the Senate of the Philippines. The senators elected in 2010 Philippine Senate election will serve until June 30, 2016 Philippine Senate election, while the senators elected in this election will serve up to June 30, 2019. Team PNoy campaign manager and senator Franklin Drilon was elected Senate President upon the convening of the 16th Congress of the Philippines on late July, after emerging as the frontrunner in the Senate Presidency, at the expense of incumbent Juan Ponce Enrile of UNA. Poe broke the record of Bong Revilla in 2010 Philippine Senate election for the most votes received in any election in the Philippines, by winning more than 20 million votes. As early in April, Miriam Defensor Santiago said that the Senate President for the 16th Congress of the Philippines will come from Team PNoy, and that it will shall come from its oldest members; she tightened the contenders to Sergio Osmeña III, Franklin Drilon, TG Guingona and Cynthia Villar." .

lsd:Entity_58105 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2012 Food City 500 was the fourth stock car race of the 2012 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series. It was held on 18 March 2012 at Bristol Motor Speedway in Bristol, Tennessee before a crowd of 102,000. The 2012 Food City 500 was the fourth of thirty_six scheduled stock car races of the 2012 NASCAR Sprint Cup Series. It took place on 18 March 2012, in Bristol, Tennessee, at Bristol Motor Speedway, a short track which holds NASCAR races." .

lsd:Entity_58116 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1880 United Kingdom general election was a general election in the United Kingdom held from 31 March 1880 to 27 April 1880." .

lsd:Entity_58159 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2006 Hong Kong Open Badminton Championships was held from 28 August 2006 to 02 September 2006." .

lsd:Entity_58185 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Typhoon Durian, known in the Philippines as Typhoon Reming, was a violent tropical cyclone that wreaked havoc in the Philippines in late 25 November 2006, causing massive loss of life when mudflows from the Mayon Volcano buried many villages." .

lsd:Entity_58194 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2009 Camping World Grand Prix at the Glen was the ninth round of the 2009 IndyCar Series season. It took place on 05 July 2009 at the 3.370_mile (5.423 km) Watkins Glen International road course in Watkins Glen, New York." .

lsd:Entity_58206 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000 Senior League World Series took place from 13 August 2000–19 in Kissimmee, Florida, United States." .

lsd:Entity_58223 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Alhandic (Spanish: Batalla de Alhandic), also known as Zamora's trench Battle (Batalla del Foso de Zamora), was a battle that occurred on 05 August 0939, 939 in the city of Zamora, Spain. The battle occurred when the troops of Abd_ar_Rahman III assaulted the walls of Zamora. This battle should not be confused with the Day of Zamora (Día de Zamora or Jornada del Foso de Zamora) which took place a few decades before in the year 901. This bloodthirsty strategy lends its name to the battle which is sometimes known as the Batalla del Foso de Zamora (Zamora's trench Battle)." .

lsd:Entity_58245 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Nordic Figure Skating Championships were the Nordic Figure Skating Championships of the 2016–2017 season. Skaters competed in two disciplines, ladies singles and men's singles, across three levels: senior (Olympic_level), junior, and novice. The 2017 Nordics were held at the Egilshöll in Reykjavik, Iceland from March 2nd through 5th, 2017." .

lsd:Entity_58255 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Keio Challenger was a professional tennis tournament played on hard courts. It took place in Yokohama, Japan between 27 February 2017 and 05 March 2017 for the men's edition and between 2017 and 12 for the women's." .

lsd:Entity_58285 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "National Astronaut Day is an American commemorative day held on May 5 since 2017. It commemorates the first United States human spaceflight, on May 5, 1961, piloted by astronaut Alan Shepard." .

lsd:Entity_58322 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "At the diving at the 1984 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles, four diving events (2 for men and 2 for women) were contested during a competition that took place at the McDonald's Olympic Swim Stadium of the University of Southern California (USC), from 5 to 12 August, comprising 80 divers from 29 nations." .

lsd:Entity_58391 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The murder of George Harry Storrs occurred on 01 November 1909 in Stalybridge, Cheshire, England." .

lsd:Entity_58403 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Animation Kobe (Japanese: アニメーション神戸) was an event established by Kōbe in 1996 to promote anime and other visual media. The Animation Kobe Awards (アニメーション神戸賞) are given annually by Kōbe and the Organising Committee to creators and creations. Animation Kobe has been held annually in Kōbe since 1996. Animation films released in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates. The TV animations broadcast in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year, excluding rebroadcasts, become candidates. The packaged media distributed in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates. Re_created in 2000 as Network Media Award, the anime_related media making the best use of interactive distribution in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates. The theme songs of either anime or other forms of animated media distributed in Japan from September of the previous year to August of the event year become candidates." .

lsd:Entity_58414 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1933 UCI Road World Championships took place in Montlhéry, France between 14 August 1933 and 1933." .

lsd:Entity_5842 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "During the Siege of Mantua, which lasted from 4 July 1796 to 02 February 1797 with a short break, French forces under the overall command of Napoleon Bonaparte besieged and blockaded a large Austrian garrison at Mantua for many months until it surrendered. The siege occurred during the War of the First Coalition, which is part of the French Revolutionary Wars. Mantua, a city in the Lombardy region of Italy, lies on the Mincio River. After driving the Austrian army out of northwest and north_central Italy, the French invested the fortress of Mantua starting in early June 1796. Mantua was reached and the French were forced to abandon the siege. By requisitioning cannon from all over northern Italy, Bonaparte assembled a siege train of 179 heavy guns. Bonaparte, who had only 44,000 soldiers, posted his divisions in an arc to protect his siege of Mantua. Wurmser pushed Masséna back and Quosdanovich quickly seized Brescia, forcing Bonaparte to lift the siege on 01 August 1796." .

lsd:Entity_58420 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 British Grand Prix (formally the 2007 Formula 1 Santander British Grand Prix) was the ninth race of the 2007 Formula One World Championship. It was held on 08 July 2007 at the Silverstone Circuit. The race was won by Kimi Räikkönen after overtaking pole position driver Lewis Hamilton during the first round of pit stops. Following United Kingdom driver Lewis Hamilton's win at the 2007 Canadian Grand Prix, circuit director Richard Phillips reported that ticket sales had \"gone through the roof\"." .

lsd:Entity_58426 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2010 Guamanian legislative election also known as Senatorial election for the Legislature of Guam took place on 02 November 2010, coinciding with the 2010 United States general elections and the Guam gubernatorial election." .

lsd:Entity_58431 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Star Awards 2003 was an awards ceremony part of the annual Star Awards held by MediaCorp Channel 8 on 2003." .

lsd:Entity_58438 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1984 Greenlandic general election were held in Greenland on 06 June 1984." .

lsd:Entity_58442 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A novel strain of 2011 Germany E. coli O104:H4 outbreak caused a serious outbreak of foodborne illness focused in northern Germany in May through June 2011. In all, 3,950 people were affected and 53 died, 51 of whom were in Germany. Essentially all affected people had been in Germany or France shortly before becoming ill. The most substantial outbreak outside of Germany was in Bordeaux, France where 15 cases of EHEC gastroenteritis were associated with the same strain of E. coli which caused the outbreak in Germany. The French cases had not previously travelled to Germany, suggesting they acquired the bacteria from contaminated sprouts grown in France. Most or all victims were believed to have become infected in Germany or France. A joint risk_assessment by EFSA/ECDC, issued 29 01 June 2011, made a connection between the German outbreak and a HUS outbreak in the Bordeaux area of France, first reported on 24 June, in which infection with E. coli O104:H4 has been confirmed in several patients." .

lsd:Entity_58453 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "2010 Anguillan general election were held in Anguilla on 15 February 2010. Retiring Chief Minister Osbourne Fleming officially set 15 February 2010, as the date for the election during a public meeting of the ruling Anguilla United Front (AUF) in Blowing Point held on 5 January 2010. In his announcement, Fleming told supporters, \"Tonight, I take great pleasure in advising you that by the help of God, because we don't know what could happen, elections in Anguilla will be on the 15th of 15 February 2010.\"" .

lsd:Entity_58476 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Spengler Cup was a men's ice hockey competition being held in Davos, Switzerland between 2017 and 2017. All matches were being played at HC Davos's home known as Vaillant Arena." .

lsd:Entity_58486 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "A sweep is either of two categories of martial arts techniques. A sweep can be used to take the opponent to the ground or it can simply disrupt the opponent's balance long enough to make an opening for a punch or kick." .

lsd:Entity_58507 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011–12 Montenegrin Second League (Serbian: Druga Crnogorska Liga / Друга црногорска лига) was the sixth season of the competition as the second top association football league in Montenegro. The league played its first games of the season on 14 August 2011 and its final matches were played on 30 May 2012." .

lsd:Entity_58512 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Big E is inclusive of all six of the New England states: Connecticut, Maine, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, Rhode Island, and Vermont. Located in the Pioneer Valley of Western Massachusetts, a short distance from the Memorial Bridge spanning the Connecticut River, The Big E is held every autumn in West Springfield, Massachusetts. The first Eastern States Exposition occurred in October 1916 in Springfield, Massachusetts and was called the Eastern States Agricultural and Industrial Exposition." .

lsd:Entity_58527 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1956 Democratic Party presidential primaries were the selection process by which voters of the Democratic Party chose its nominee for President of the United States in the 1956 U.S. presidential election. Former Illinois Governor Adlai Stevenson II was selected as the nominee through a series of primary election and caucuses culminating in the 1956 Democratic National Convention held from August 13 to 1956, in Chicago, Illinois." .

lsd:Entity_58540 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Producers Guild of America Awards 2008 (also known as 2009 Producers Guild Awards), honoring the best film and television producers of 2008, were held at Hollywood Palladium in Hollywood, California on 24 January 2009." .

lsd:Entity_58563 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Hamburg state election was held on 21 September 1997 to elect the members of the 16th Hamburg Parliament. Summary of the 21 September 1997 election results for the Hamburg Parliament." .

lsd:Entity_58599 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Eurymedon vase is an Attic red_figure pottery oenochoe, a wine jug attributed to the circle of the Triptolemos Painter made ca." .

lsd:Entity_58606 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1988–89 Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball team represented the US University of Oklahoma in competitive college basketball during the 1988–89 NCAA Division I season. The Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball team played its home games in the Lloyd Noble Center and was a member of the National Collegiate Athletic Association's (NCAA) former Big Eight Conference at that time. Mookie Blaylock established the current Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball single_season minutes played (1359) and career steals (281) records." .

lsd:Entity_58630 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999 Sparkassen Cup – doubles was the tennis doubles event of the tenth edition of the Sparkassen Cup; a WTA Tier II tournament held in Leipzig, Germany. Elena Likhovtseva and Ai Sugiyama were the defending champions but were defeated in this year's final by Larisa Neiland and Mary Pierce, 6–1, 6–3." .

lsd:Entity_58673 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "In culture of Wales, an eisteddfod (/aɪˈstɛðvɒd/ (listen) eye_STEDH_vod, also US: /eɪˈ_/ ay_, UK: /aɪˈstɛdvəd, _fəd, _vɒd, _fɒd/ eye_STED_vəd, _fəd, _vod, _fod, Welsh:  (listen); plural eisteddfods or eisteddfodau ) is, according to Martha A. Davies, \"a Welsh festival with adjudicated competitions for poets, musicians, and others.\" The revival proved enormously successful and is credited as the primary reason for the continued survival of the Welsh, literature, poetry, and culture of Wales. In some countries, the term eisteddfod is used for performing arts competitions that have nothing to do with culture of Wales or the Welsh. But interest in the Welsh arts declined during the 17th and 18th centuries, leading to the standard of the main eisteddfod deteriorating. By the 1850s people began to talk of a national eisteddfod to showcase Wales's culture of Wales. Eisteddfods (Australian plural) in the traditional Welsh sense have also been adopted into Australian culture of Wales. At least 20 years earlier, as described in the diaries of Joseph Jenkins, Ballarat's Welsh community was conducting an annual eisteddfod each St David's Day (1 March). The largest U.S. eisteddfod was held In 1893 at the World Columbian Exposition in Chicago, featuring visiting Welsh choirs invited by The Cymmrodorion Society of Chicago. The eisteddfod idea was retained by some subsequent world's fairs, and helped to link the Welsh Eisteddfod community to its American offshoot. The Jackson School Eisteddfod in Jackson, Ohio, is the result of an historically strong Welsh business community, who funded the Southern Ohio Eisteddfod Association and a 4,000_seat auditorium that was the only dedicated eisteddfod venue in the United States. Welsh Heritage Week and Cwrs Cymraeg, two ambulatory Welsh language and culture of Wales courses held annually, usually in the United States, also each feature a mini_eisteddfod. The North American Festival of Wales held by the Welsh North American Association also includes an eisteddfod. Since it was founded as part of the Gaelic Revival by Conradh na Gaeilge in 1902, Seachtain na Gaeilge, which is similar to the eisteddfod, has celebrated Irish traditional music, Gaelic games, and Irish culture of Wales and promoted the Irish language." .

lsd:Entity_58678 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Toyota Grand Prix of Long Beach was the 40th annual running of the Grand Prix of Long Beach and the second race of the 2014 IndyCar Series season." .

lsd:Entity_58694 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1977 Egypt Cup Final, was the final match of 1976–77 Egypt Cup, when Zamalek SC played Ismaily SC, Zamalek SC won the game 3–1." .

lsd:Entity_58702 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2011 Internationaler Apano Cup was a professional tennis tournament played on clay courts. It took place in Dortmund, Germany between 25 July 2011 and 31 July 2011." .

lsd:Entity_58718 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2000–01 Umaglesi Liga was the twelfth season of top_tier football in Georgia. It began on 19 August 2000 and ended on 23 May 2001." .

lsd:Entity_58736 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Curling was a Olympic demonstration sport competition at the curling at the 1992 Winter Olympics. The 1992 Winter Olympics was the third time curling was a Olympic demonstration sport competition at the Winter Olympics. The women's curling event at the curling at the 1992 Winter Olympics had eight countries in two groups." .

lsd:Entity_58739 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Action of 26 June 1625 is the battle which took place on 26 June 1625 near Syracuse, Sicily, when 6 Bizertan vessels defeated 5 Maltese galleys." .

lsd:Entity_58762 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2003 Asian Women's Volleyball Championship was the 12th Asian Women's Volleyball Championship, which took place from 20 September 2003 to 2003 in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam." .

lsd:Entity_58785 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 ICF Canoe Sprint World Championships were held in Duisburg, Germany on August 9–12, 2007 for the record_tying fourth time. The Germany city had hosted the ICF Canoe Sprint World Championships previously in 1979, 1987, and 1995." .

lsd:Entity_58809 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2017 Boston Marathon was the 121st running of the Boston Athletic Association's Boston Marathon." .

lsd:Entity_58816 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Senior men's race at the 1991 IAAF World Cross Country Championships – senior men's race was held in Antwerp, Belgium, at the Linkeroever Racecourse on 1991." .

lsd:Entity_5883 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1986 Cerritos mid_air collision was a scheduled commercial flight from Mexico City, Mexico, to Los Angeles, California, United States, with several intermediate stops. On Sunday, 31 August 1986, the McDonnell Douglas DC_9 operating the flight was clipped in the tail section by N4891F, a Piper PA_28_181 Archer owned by the Kramer family, and crashed into the Los Angeles suburb of Cerritos, killing all 67 on both aircraft and an additional fifteen on the ground. On Sunday, 31 August 1986 at about 11:46 am PDT, Flight 498 began its descent into Los Angeles with 58 passengers and six crew members on board." .

lsd:Entity_58860 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Operation Shahi Tandar, also called Operation Atal, was a series of operations by Coalition troops from the British 42 Commando Royal Marines, Royal Canadian Regiment, 2nd Battalion 2nd Infantry Regiment (United States), and the Afghan national military in central Helmand province and the Western Panjwayi and Western Zhari districts of Kandahar, Afghanistan from 07 January 2009–31, 2009. One raid targeted a Taliban bomb_making factory in the Khakrez and Shah Wali Khot districts of Kandahar, Afghanistan, 07 January 2009–9, 2009." .

lsd:Entity_58880 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1913 FEF Copa del Rey Final (FEF) was the 13th final of the Spanish cup competition, the Copa del Rey. The final was played at Campo de O'Donnell in Madrid on 22 March 1913." .

lsd:Entity_58897 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Internazionali Femminili di Palermo – doubles took place between 16 July and 22 July on outdoor clay courts in Palermo, Italy. Mariya Koryttseva and Darya Kustova won the title, defeating Alice Canepa and Karin Knapp in the final." .

lsd:Entity_58919 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The AFF Women's Championship is the competition in women's association football organised by the ASEAN Football Federation, contested by the national teams of nations in Southeast Asia. A 2017 edition was planned in Thailand but was later cancelled by the ASEAN Football Federation in February 2017 citing the big amount of major women's association football tournament already scheduled in Asia for the year." .

lsd:Entity_58938 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 34th Tony Awards was broadcast by CBS television on 1980, from the Mark Hellinger Theatre." .

lsd:Entity_58985 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2016 IAAF Diamond League was the seventh season of the annual series of outdoor track and field meetings, organised by the World Athletics (IAAF). The following fourteen meetings are scheduled to be included in the 2016 season: Events not included in the Diamond League are marked in grey background. There were twelve world leads set at the opening meet of the season in Doha, as well as 4 meeting records at an event which has begun the Diamond League season each of the past 7 years. The best performance of the 2016 Bislett Games was by Dafne Schippers, whose run of 21.93 seconds in the women's 200 m was a Diamond League record, meet record and a world lead." .

lsd:Entity_59003 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The men's ice hockey tournament at the ice hockey at the 1956 Winter Olympics in Cortina d'Ampezzo, Italy, was the 8th ice hockey at the Olympic Games, also serving as the 23rd World Championships and the 34th European Championships." .

lsd:Entity_59039 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1997 Toshiba Classic was a women's tennis tournament played on outdoor hard courts at the La Costa Resort and Spa in San Diego, California in the United States that was part of Tier II of the 1997 WTA Tour. It was the 19th edition of the tournament and was held from 28 July 1997 through 03 August 1997." .

lsd:Entity_59062 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014 Norwegian Football Cup Final was the 109th final of the Norwegian Football Cup. It was played on 23 November 2014 at Ullevaal Stadion, in Oslo, Norway. In the final Odds BK lost 2_0 to Molde FK, securing Molde FK's second cup title in a row and the double for the 2014 season. This was Molde FK's 7th cup final, while Odds BK traveled to Ullevaal for the 21st time. In the recent years, the two clubs has received 13,000 of the 25,500 tickets to the final, but after the expansion of Ullevaal Stadion the two clubs received 15,250 of the 27,000 tickets to the final." .

lsd:Entity_59116 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010 Queen's Club Championships (also known traditionally as the Queen's Club Championships) was a tennis tournament played on outdoor grass courts. It was the 108Th edition of the Queen's Club Championships and was part of the ATP World Tour 250 series of the 2010 ATP World Tour. It took place at the Queen's Club in London, United Kingdom, from 7 to 13 June 2010." .

lsd:Entity_59132 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Saudia Flight 162 was a scheduled flight from King Abdulaziz Air Base, Saudi Arabia to Jinnah International Airport, Pakistan that suffered a high_altitude uncontrolled decompression, above international waters off Qatar, killing 2 children who were among the 271 passengers." .

lsd:Entity_59138 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "WEC 50 was a mixed martial arts event held by World Extreme Cagefighting that took place on August 18, 2010 at Palms Casino Resort in Las Vegas." .

