lsd:Entity_61471 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Formosa Air Battle (Japanese: 台湾沖航空戦, Chinese: 臺灣空戰), 1944–1944, was a series of large_scale aerial engagements between carrier air groups of the United States Navy Fast Carrier Task Force (TF 38), and Japanese land_based air forces of the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN) and Imperial Japanese Army (IJA). Organized kamikaze attacks had been proposed after the First Battle of the Philippine Sea but were rejected by Imperial Japanese Navy leaders through 1944." .

