lsd:Entity_617 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Winter Campaign of 1941–1942 from 05 December 1941 to 07 May 1942 was the name given by Soviet military command to the period that marked the commencement of the Moscow Strategic Offensive Operation (better known as the Battle of Moscow). The campaign began with the Moscow Strategic Offensive Operation (05 December 1941 – 7 January 1942) with the simultaneous Kerch_Feodosia Amphibious Operation (25 05 December 1941 – 2 January 1942) The operations in central and northern European Russia began with the conclusion of the Moscow counter_offensive almost simultaneously with the Oboyan–Kursk Offensive Operation (3 January 1942 – 26 January 1942), the Lyuban Offensive Operation (7 January 1942 – 30 April 1942), the Demyansk Offensive Operation (7 January 1942 – 20 07 May 1942), the Orel–Bolkhov Offensive Operation (8 January 1942 – 28 April 1942), and the Rzhev_Vyazma Strategic Offensive Operation (8 January 1942 – 20 April 1942)." .

lsd:Entity_61706 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1980 Tooth Cup was the 7th edition of the NSWRFL Midweek Cup, a NSWRFL_organised national club rugby league tournament between the leading clubs and representative teams from the NSWRFL, the BRL, the CRL, the QRL and the NZRL. A total of 16 teams from across Australia and New Zealand played 23 matches in a round_robin format with teams playing 2 games each with the top 8 teams advanced to a knockout stage, with the matches being held midweek during the premiership season." .

lsd:Entity_61738 a lsd:Context_narration ;
