lsd:Entity_62248 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1953 National Invitation Tournament was the 1953 edition of the annual National Collegiate Athletic Association college basketball competition." .

lsd:Entity_62264 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2007 Belgian federal election took place on Sunday 10 June 2007. The previous 2003 Belgian federal election had resulted in a coalition between the socialist parties SP.a/Spirit (Flemish) and the Parti Socialiste (Francophone), and the centrist liberal_democratic parties VLD/Vivant (Flemish) and MR (Francophone), with Guy Verhofstadt of the VLD to retaining his position of Prime Minister of Belgium until 2007." .

lsd:Entity_62341 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Tour de Pakistan is a cycle sport held in Pakistan roughly every two years over more than 1,648 kilometres (1,024 mi). The 15th Tour de Pakistan started on March 1, 2010 participated by cyclists from different teams of Pakistan and Afghanistan." .

lsd:Entity_62393 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The May Bumps 2009 were a series of rowing races held in Cambridge UK. The 2009 May Bumps Getting_on Race took place on 2009." .

lsd:Entity_62401 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Siege of Naxos (499 BC) was a failed attempt by the Miletus tyrant Aristagoras, operating with support from, and in the name of the Persian Empire of Darius the Great, to conquer the island of Naxos Island. Seeing an opportunity to bolster his position in Miletus, Aristagoras sought the help of his overlord, the Persian king Darius the Great, and the local satrap, Artaphernes to conquer Naxos Island. About 40 years after the Persian conquest of Ionia, and in the reign of the fourth Persian king, Darius the Great, the stand_in Miletus tyrant Aristagoras found himself in this familiar predicament. The island of Naxos Island, part of the Cyclades group in the Aegean Sea, was also in this period affected by political turmoil. Seeing an opportunity to strengthen his position in Miletus by conquering Naxos Island, Aristagoras approached the satrap of Lydia, Artaphernes, with a proposal. Furthermore, Aristagoras suggested that once Naxos Island fell, the other Cyclades would also quickly follow, and he even suggested that Euboea could be attacked on the same expedition." .

lsd:Entity_62434 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2015 Swedish Open was a tennis tournament played on outdoor clay courts as part of the ATP World Tour 250 Series of the 2015 ATP World Tour and as part of the International Series on the 2015 WTA Tour. It took place in Båstad, Sweden, from 13 through 2015 for the women's tournament, and from 20 through 2015 for the men's tournament. It was also known as the 2015 SkiStar Swedish Open for the men and the 2015 Collector Swedish Open for the women for sponsorship reasons." .

lsd:Entity_62445 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Santiago Files, directed by Cetywa Powell, is a feature_length documentary film about Salvador Allende's topple from Chile's unstable government and the players in his downfall: the CIA, Chile's military, and Allende himself. Malcolm McDowell narrates the film, which premiered in 2011." .

lsd:Entity_62448 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "1993 Japanese general election were held in Japan on 18 July 1993 to elect the House of Representatives. An eight_party coalition government was formed and headed by Morihiro Hosokawa, the leader of the Japan New Party (JNP). Additionally, the Japan New Party (JNP, Nihon Shinto), the oldest of the new parties, was formed in May 1992 by Morihiro Hosokawa, formerly an upper house member from the Tanaka faction and governor (1983–91) of Kumamoto prefecture. The coalition partners, meanwhile, unanimously settled on JNP Chairman Morihiro Hosokawa as Japan's new Prime Minister, although the more experienced Tsutomu Hata was initially preferred by the SDPJ and Komeito." .

