lsd:Entity_62794 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "Wrestling Dontaku 2016 was a professional wrestling event promoted by New Japan Pro_Wrestling (NJPW). The event took place on 2016, in Fukuoka, Fukuoka at Fukuoka Kokusai Center and featured ten matches, six of which were contested for championships. Wrestling Dontaku 2016 featured ten professional wrestling matches that involved different wrestlers from pre_existing scripted feuds and storylines. NJPW announced the first matches for Wrestling Dontaku 2016 on 2016, the day after Invasion Attack 2016. More recently the two had met in the second round of the 2016 New Japan Cup, where Naito was victorious en route to winning the entire tournament. At Invasion Attack 2016, former All Japan Pro Wrestling (AJPW), Wrestle_1 and Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) worker Seiya Sanada made his surprise debut for NJPW, attacking Kazuchika Okada during the main event and costing him the IWGP Heavyweight Championship in his match against Naito, setting up a match between Okada and the man now simply known as \"Sanada\" for Wrestling Dontaku 2016. On April 19, the day after the Wrestling Hinokuni 2016 show had been canceled due to the 2016 Kumamoto earthquakes, two matches previously announced for the show were moved to Wrestling Dontaku 2016." .

lsd:Entity_62799 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2014–15 Russian Football National League was the 23rd season of Russia's second_tier football league since the dissolution of the Soviet Union. The season began on 06 July 2014 and ended on 30 May 2015." .

lsd:Entity_62803 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The Second Battle of Fort Wagner, also known as the Second Assault on Morris Island or the Battle of Fort Wagner, Morris Island, was fought on 18 July 1863, during the American Civil War. Gen Hagood wrote a book titled Memoirs of the War of Secession, in which he states that the constant bombardment from the Union guns in the weeks following the second battle had unearthed such large numbers of the Union dead buried after the assault of 18 July 1863, and the air was so sickening with the smell of death, that one could no longer stand to be in the fort." .

