lsd:Entity_62969 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 1999–2000 A.S. Roma season saw A.S. Roma continue its long drought of titles, finishing a frustrating 6th place in Serie A. Reward for Capello's new 3–4–1–2 system would come in 2000–01 A.S. Roma season, however, when summer signings Gabriel Batistuta, Walter Samuel and Emerson completed the thin squad of the 1999–2000 A.S. Roma season, and Roma was able to claim the title." .

lsd:Entity_62987 a lsd:Context_narration ;
    rdfs:label "The 2010–11 Lega Pro Seconda Divisione season was the thirty_third association football league season of Italy Lega Pro Seconda Divisione since its establishment in 1978, and the third since the renaming from Serie C to Lega Pro. Due to twenty_one bankruptcies and non_admissions in the Serie B (one vacancy), Lega Pro Prima Divisione (seven vacancies) and Lega Pro Seconda Divisione (thirteen vacancies) the 2010–11 season was to feature only 3 teams that played in 2009–10 Lega Pro Prima Divisione, 20 teams that played in 2009_10 Serie D, 1 team that played in Eccellenza and 25 teams that played in 2009–10 Lega Pro Seconda Divisione." .

